window.UDFOP_SHARD("2026-10",[{"id":"0.1.5201-001","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Swimming","t":"Rework","x":"Running out of fatigue in the water no longer kills you on the spot. It used to, whatever your health. Now you lose a tenth of your health every few seconds while you stay in the water with no fatigue left, and the screen says \"You are too exhausted to swim - get out of the water!\" From full health that's about 50 seconds to reach the shore, where you collapse and rest as you would anywhere on land.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-002","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Fishing","t":"Rework","x":"Fishing stops before you're worn out. In a lake you fish while swimming, and treading water tires you as swimming does. Once you are down to the last quarter of your fatigue, the net won't cast in the water, and a cast already out ends. The prompt says \"too tired to fish in the water - get out and rest\". On a pier or a boat's deck nothing changes: fish as long as you like.","g":["fishing","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-003","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Gathering Tools","t":"Fix","x":"Your gathering tools work from the hotbar. Use the Wood-Axe at a tree, the Pick-Axe at an ore vein or a boulder (in the wilderness or a dungeon), the Sickle at an herb patch, the Basket at a patch, or the Fishing-Net in water, from your hotbar or a quick slot, and it does exactly what pressing E there does: the gathering starts, and the goods go to your Stores with the profession's XP. The Sickle always picks the herbs and the Basket always searches for food, whichever one the patch's prompt is showing. With the Sickle, keep still until it's done - you don't need to hold E. The Fishing-Net makes a short cast; hold E instead for a longer one. If the spot needs something first, such as a higher rank, or you've already gathered it today, the tool says so.","g":["professions","quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-004","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Gathering Tools","t":"Fix","x":"Anywhere else, a tool no longer fills your pack. Used away from its spot, or from the open pack, the Wood-Axe, Pick-Axe, Sickle, Basket and Fishing-Net no longer make Wood Bundles, fish or other finds, start Foraging's quests or wear down. Instead the tool tells you where its profession is done, for example: *\"Logging is done at a tree in the wilderness: walk up to one until the prompt shows, then press E (or use the Wood-Axe).\"* Offline, and for guests without the professions, the tools work as they always have. The Spade still robs graves.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-005","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Professions","t":"Rework","x":"The Professions page explains how to gather Herbalism, Mining and Logging, as it already did for Hunting and Fishing, including using the tool from your hotbar at the spot. The empty Stores say where their goods come from.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-006","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Bank","t":"Rework","x":"The bank window names the region whose account it shows (\"Account in Wayrest\"), and lists the gold you've banked in other regions beneath it. Every bank online is the Bank of the Empire, but each region still keeps its own account: gold deposited in Daggerfall is in Daggerfall's account.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-007","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed the overworld frame rate sinking over time. An enemy from a camp you had left behind could be restored by a load over ground that wasn't there yet, and fall forever, each second of the fall costing more. Enemies over ground that hasn't loaded now wait for it, then stand on it.","g":["overworld","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-008","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A townsperson who knows where a quest's own building is always marks it on your map when you ask them outdoors (it used to be about one answer in four; the rest said \"north of here\").","g":["quests","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-009","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Town Map","t":"Rework","x":"A house a townsperson marked for a quest is ringed on the town map. On the Enhanced town map it looked like any other house.","g":["quests","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-010","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Houses","t":"Rework","x":"Houses' doors say \"Residence\" and list Go in and Buy it when you point at them, and a click goes in. Clicking any house used to ask \"This house can be your home ... Buy it?\". The quest's house reads by its own name, \"The <name> Residence\", and is never for sale.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-011","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Houses","t":"Rework","x":"Houses' doors say \"Residence\" and list Go in and Buy it when you point at them, and a click goes in. Clicking any house used to ask \"This house can be your home ... Buy it?\". The quest's house reads by its own name, \"The <name> Residence\", and is never for sale.","g":["homes","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5201-012","v":"0.1.5201","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"No more light-blue rectangles on the sea in the Overworld view. The surf along the coast was drawn from high above, where it showed as flat sheets over the water. It now shows only at ground level, as it should.","g":["overworld","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5204-001","v":"0.1.5204","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Bank","t":"Rework","x":"Your bank account is the same at every bank. Online, the Bank of the Empire now keeps one account for you. Gold and letters of credit paid in at any bank can be drawn at any other. Before, each region kept its own account, so money deposited in one region was missing from every other region's bank.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5204-002","v":"0.1.5204","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Bank","t":"Rework","x":"Nothing to do on your side. The next time you play an online character, the gold in all your regional accounts is moved into the one account, and the game tells you how much came in. No gold is lost or added.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5204-003","v":"0.1.5204","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Bank","t":"Rework","x":"Houses, ships, guild deposits, the market, homes, decor, rent and the Marks all pay from and into the one account.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5204-004","v":"0.1.5204","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Bank","t":"Other","x":"A loan still belongs to the region where you took it. Its due date, its default and the reputation a default costs stay in that region. The account pays it back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5204-005","v":"0.1.5204","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Bank","t":"New","x":"The Empire tells you when it takes your gold for a default. If a loan goes into default, the Empire pays it from your account, and now says how much it took. Before, the gold left without a word.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-001","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"When the Warden falls, a damage chart ranks everyone in the fight by the damage they dealt. It shows on the right side of the screen for a minute and fades out.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-002","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Each row shows your rank, name and level, a bar of your damage next to the top fighter's, the number, your share of the court's total, the hits you landed on him and your biggest one, the damage you put into the Crystals of Oblivion, and how many times you fell.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-003","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Your own row is outlined and marked \"(you)\". In a big court the top ten are listed, and if you're further down your own row shows underneath at your rank, with the rest counted.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-004","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Other","x":"The numbers come from the server's own count of the fight, the same count that decides who earns a receipt.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-005","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The Warden's Marks card no longer covers the middle of the screen when you step into the court. It sits low on the right, clear of your crosshair, and still fades after a few seconds.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-006","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Rework","x":"The phase name is gone from under his health bar. The marks on the bar still show where each phase turns, and each turn is still announced when it happens. The fighter count, the Reckoning countdown and Dagon's Wrath countdown stay.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5209-007","v":"0.1.5209","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Walking over a piece of loot no longer picks it up. Look at a piece and press activate to take it, like any loot pile, so crossing the court for the piece you want doesn't sweep up the rest. Anything you leave on the floor still goes into your pack when you leave the court.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5214-001","v":"0.1.5214","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A quest monster killed by a party member now counts for your quest, wherever you are. When you share a quest with your party and then die or leave while its monster is still standing, the monster passes to the party member nearest it. If that member hadn't taken the quest themselves and killed the monster with nobody on the quest nearby, the kill counted for nobody, and the monster was back when you returned. Now the kill reaches your quest, and the quest of every party member who shares it, as it happens.","g":["quests","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5214-002","v":"0.1.5214","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Your quest's monsters are yours. Players outside your party can't see them, hit them or be attacked by them, so someone else clearing a dungeon never takes your quest's target. A dungeon's own monsters, a cave's tigers included, are everyone's, and come back an hour after they die.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-001","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Rework","x":"Resting gives magicka back up to half your pool. Resting, collapsing from exhaustion, and arriving from a cautious journey all refill magicka to 50% of your maximum and no further. \"Rest until healed\" stops there. If you're already above half, for example after a potion, resting never takes any back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-002","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Economy","x":"Restore Power potions top up the rest. Each potion restores 5 magicka plus 4 per level. It now costs what it restores at your level, 1 gold per point of magicka, before haggling: about 9 gold at level 1, 45 at level 10 and 85 at level 20.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-003","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"New","x":"Every alchemist sells them. Each alchemist has 20 Restore Power potions on the shelf every day.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-004","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"New","x":"The Mages Guild sells them to anyone. Use the guild's magic-items merchant. Members of rank 3 and up see the potions next to the usual magic items. Everyone else, members or not, can buy the potions there instead of being turned away.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-005","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Economy","x":"Selling a Restore Power potion back is priced the same way, so buying potions to resell never pays.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-006","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"New","x":"Sell anything from your pack. Under My listings, choose A piece from your pack (gold) and set a price in gold. The piece leaves your pack at once. If you cancel, or it doesn't sell within 72 hours, it comes back. The new Goods view lists everyone's pieces.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-007","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"New","x":"A piece bought at a board in its seller's region reaches your pack at once. From another region it comes by courier.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-008","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Other","x":"bound pieces (Sigil Stones and the Sigil Broker's wares)","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-009","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Other","x":"anything you're wearing, locked pieces, quest items and summoned items","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-010","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Other","x":"gold, letters of credit, boat deeds and boat parts","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-011","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Other","x":"arrows","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-012","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Other","x":"Pieces from your pack sell for gold only, not Drakes.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-013","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Other","x":"A crafted piece someone else made can't be sold as a crafted piece; only its maker can do that. It sells from your pack, for gold.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-014","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: listing a crafted piece someone had traded you made it vanish from your pack. It now stays.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-015","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"Yard pieces stay off the road. A piece could be set down on the street, on its edges or on a track running past town, and the blue lot edge ran across the road. A piece on the road is now refused with a message, and the lot edge runs along the side of the road. Pieces can still touch the road's edge.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-016","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"No more furniture through your walls outside. A long piece turned at an angle could be placed cutting through the corner of your house. It's now refused until it's clear of the wall.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-017","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"Yard changes stick. A piece you had just placed could vanish, or one you had removed could come back, for about a minute. Your changes now stay put.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-018","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"Yards don't blink at map edges. Walking across a map boundary near decorated yards made their pieces disappear for a moment. They now stay in place.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-019","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Exterior","t":"Fix","x":"You can paint your house's outside again. In the Decorate panel's Exterior tab, the \"Paint it\", \"Put back\" and \"The town's own\" buttons were hidden. A look you tried disappeared as soon as you left the tab. Press \"Paint it\" to keep a look for everyone.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-020","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Exterior","t":"Fix","x":"A look you just painted no longer flips back to the old one for up to a minute. That could happen when the town's list of homes refreshed at the same moment, or when you painted twice in a row.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-021","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Exterior","t":"Fix","x":"Closing the decorator after trying a look you didn't paint now reopens the Exterior tab on your house's real look, not on the one you put away.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-022","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"Tenants can rest. If you rent a room in someone's home, you can now rest there. Before, it said \"You have not rented a room here.\"","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-023","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"Renewing only offers the days you can buy. A room can be paid at most 30 days ahead. When you renew, the door now lists only the day counts that fit, and tells you when your room is already paid that far. Before, it offered 30 days anyway, refused the rent, and moved the cost from your purse to the bank.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-024","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"Rent paid while you're home shows up. The \"Rooms to rent\" tab checks again each time you open the Decorate panel, and every half minute while it's open.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-025","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"Offers in a house that is one room again stay listed. You can still see your tenants and stop offering a room. Before, visitors could rent a room you could no longer see. While your rooms are still being found, the tab says \"Finding the rooms of your house...\" instead of \"A house of one room...\".","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-026","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"Room numbers match. A room you offer as \"Room 2\" is \"Room 2\" at the door, not \"Room 1\".","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-027","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"The door opens right after you rent. Before, it could stay locked for up to a minute.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-028","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Rooms to Rent","t":"Fix","x":"If the owner stops offering your room, the door now says your room can't be renewed and how many days you have left.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-029","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Skill Training","t":"Fix","x":"Running keeps every step past 100. A mastered skill past 100 stopped counting after about an hour and a half of running between rests, and the extra progress from a long run was thrown away. Now all of it counts, and whatever a rest doesn't turn into a point is kept for the next rest.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5233-030","v":"0.1.5233","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Climbing past 100 does something now. Climbing is already a sure thing at 95, so a mastered Climbing gained nothing past 100. Now each point past 100 makes you climb faster: about 8% faster at 125, 17% at 150 and 40% at 200.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5235-001","v":"0.1.5235","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Rework","x":"The change to magic is undone. The last update made resting refill magicka only to half your pool, and changed how Restore Power potions are sold and priced. That's reverted.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5235-002","v":"0.1.5235","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Rework","x":"Restore Power potions are back to their old price and shops. Alchemists and the Mages Guild no longer carry them; temples and the Dark Brotherhood sell potions to their members as before.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-001","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Weather","t":"Fix","x":"Rain no longer vanishes when you sink into a puddle. Standing in a puddle or other shallow water hid the rain and the sand while you could still hear it. Now the falling weather is only hidden when your eyes are actually under the water.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-002","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Weather","t":"Rework","x":"Rain isn't always a downpour any more. A rainstorm now drizzles at its edges and only pours at its heart, so a light sprinkle or a gentle shower is common, and snow falls lightly more often. A light rain also looks light, with thinner fog and more daylight. The dark, foggy look comes in with the heavy rain.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-003","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Weather","t":"Rework","x":"Rain isn't always a downpour any more. A rainstorm now drizzles at its edges and only pours at its heart, so a light sprinkle or a gentle shower is common, and snow falls lightly more often. A light rain also looks light, with thinner fog and more daylight. The dark, foggy look comes in with the heavy rain.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-004","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Weather","t":"Fix","x":"Distant clouds no longer look square. Far-off clouds near the horizon could show blocky, square edges, worst on the lower cloud quality setting. They're smooth now.","g":["weather","sky"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-005","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Underwater","t":"Rework","x":"The sea looks like water from underneath. Underwater is murkier now: the water is a blue-green that swallows reds first, gets darker the deeper you dive and at night, and closes off the distance sooner.","g":["water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-006","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Underwater","t":"New","x":"Sunbeams shine down through the water. On a sunny day, shafts of light reach down from the surface. They lean with the sun, shift as the waves pass, and fade as you go deeper, under clouds and at night.","g":["water","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-007","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"Weather fills the Overworld view. Rain, snow, sand and wind used to show only as a small patch around your character. Now they fill the air in front of the camera, as they do on the ground.","g":["overworld","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-008","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Your character faces the way you're going. In the Overworld, the movement keys turn your character toward the direction you press, so you see them walk off to the side or come toward the camera instead of always seeing their back.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-009","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"Other players show up in the Overworld. Other players were drawn at normal size from high up, so all you could see was their name over a tiny speck. They're now drawn as large as your own character, whether they're on foot, riding or in a Morrowind body.","g":["overworld","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-010","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Performance","x":"Smoother turning in a crowd with the Morrowind model. Turning to face a group of players could stall a frame while every body that came into view was posed at once. Bodies about to come into view are now prepared a little ahead of the turn, a few at a time.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-011","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Performance","x":"Fewer rebuilds of other players' Morrowind bodies. Another player drawing a different weapon, mounting a horse or stepping out of sight for a moment no longer makes their whole body load again; the weapon simply changes in their hand.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-012","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Coasts","t":"Performance","x":"No more stalls along the coast. Walking or sailing along a coastline could stall the game for a moment each time you crossed into a new area, while the surf along the shore was rebuilt. The rebuild now takes a few milliseconds instead.","g":["water","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5244-013","v":"0.1.5244","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ships","t":"Performance","x":"Ships in the distance cost less. The small details on far-off ships, such as lanterns, are no longer drawn once they're smaller than a pixel, just like the ships' own fittings, and ships' flags take less work to draw every frame.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-001","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"Every gathering spot near you is now marked on the compass: herb patches, ore veins, boulders, trees, fishing schools and bodies you can skin. You no longer need a specialisation for this. Each profession's marks have their own colour:","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-002","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"Rework","x":"Every gathering spot near you is now marked on the compass: herb patches, ore veins, boulders, trees, fishing schools and bodies you can skin. You no longer need a specialisation for this. Each profession's marks have their own colour:","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-003","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"Herbalism: orchid","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-004","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"Fishing: blue Spots within 150 m are marked, and the nearer a spot is, the brighter its mark. Marks work on both the Classic and Enhanced compass, in the wilderness, in dungeons (where ore veins grow on the walls) and in the Overworld view. They sit underneath your party's marks, Detect markers and every other compass mark, so they never hide them.","g":["professions","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-005","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Gathering Spots","t":"New","x":"Gathering spots glow. Each spot gives off a faint glow in its profession's colour, with motes of light drifting up out of it, so you can pick it out from the grass and rocks around it. The glow appears as a spot comes within about 120 m and fades with distance. If your system is set to reduce motion, the glow holds still. It isn't drawn in the Overworld view.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-006","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Gathering Spots","t":"Rework","x":"Spots you've used up stop showing. A vein you mined, a tree you felled, a patch where you took both the herbs and the food, or a body you skinned no longer has a mark or a glow. A patch with one harvest left keeps both.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-007","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Prospector","t":"Other","x":"The Prospector still sees further. A Prospector's ore veins are marked from 200 m away, where everyone else's show from 150 m. A Tracker's animals are still marked within 100 m, now in Hunting's rose rather than copper.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5249-008","v":"0.1.5249","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Tracker","t":"Fix","x":"The Prospector still sees further. A Prospector's ore veins are marked from 200 m away, where everyone else's show from 150 m. A Tracker's animals are still marked within 100 m, now in Hunting's rose rather than copper.","g":["hunting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-001","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Climbing now knows what a ledge is. Face a ledge and press Jump, and you pull yourself up onto it instead of jumping.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-002","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"From the ground: you can reach a ledge up to about shoulder height at Climbing 0, and a little above your head at Climbing 100.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-003","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Narrow tops: you can stand on a wall top only about a foot wide. You land in the middle of it.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-004","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Tables and shelves: thin tops count too, even with nothing but legs underneath.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-005","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Pitched roofs: you can climb onto a roof from its eave, up to a 45° pitch.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-006","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Low ceilings: if there's only room to crouch on top, you end up crouched. Pressing Crouch during the climb won't stand you up into the ceiling.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-007","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"No ledge in reach: Jump is an ordinary jump, the same as before. That includes on stairs, where Jump no longer turns into a climb two steps up.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-008","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Holding Jump: the Jump that climbed a ledge is used up. You won't hop when you arrive; press Jump again to jump.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-009","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Press Jump at a top too thin to stand on, such as a fence, a railing's top rail, or a roof's parapet, and you climb over it and step down onto the floor behind. This only happens when the floor behind is no more than about 1.5 m below.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-010","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Other","x":"Press Jump at a top too thin to stand on, such as a fence, a railing's top rail, or a roof's parapet, and you climb over it and step down onto the floor behind. This only happens when the floor behind is no more than about 1.5 m below.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-011","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Vault","t":"New","x":"Press Jump while moving forward at a wall or fence with a thin top, no higher than about 1.2 m, and you vault over it and keep going. The pace of the vault comes from your Jumping skill.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-012","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Vault","t":"New","x":"Press Jump while moving forward at a wall or fence with a thin top, no higher than about 1.2 m, and you vault over it and keep going. The pace of the vault comes from your Jumping skill.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-013","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Vault","t":"New","x":"A vault never throws you into a fall that would hurt. Over a railing above a long drop, the press is an ordinary jump.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-014","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Vault","t":"Other","x":"A top deep enough to stand on is climbed onto rather than vaulted.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-015","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ledge Catch","t":"New","x":"Jump at a ledge that's out of reach from the ground, or press Jump while falling past one, and you grab it as it comes within reach of your hands. A tap is enough: the press lasts until you land.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-016","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ledge Catch","t":"New","x":"Holding Jump through the jump does more: it also steps you onto a low ledge in mid-air, and with Forward held it grabs a bare wall. A tap only catches ledges at chest height or higher, so jumping up stairs or about a room still just jumps.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-017","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ledge Catch","t":"Other","x":"Holding Jump through the jump does more: it also steps you onto a low ledge in mid-air, and with Forward held it grabs a bare wall. A tap only catches ledges at chest height or higher, so jumping up stairs or about a room still just jumps.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-018","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"Hanging: a ledge at chest height or higher (about 1.2 m above your feet) is held. You hang under it with your eyes just below the edge. A roof's eave counts, up to a 45° pitch.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-019","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ledge Catch","t":"New","x":"A lower ledge (below your chest) is stepped straight onto.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-020","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ledge Catch","t":"New","x":"Hard catches depend on skill. At Climbing 0 you can only hold a ledge after a fall that wouldn't have hurt you anyway. At Climbing 100 you can hold one after a fall of about 15 m. Fall further than your skill can hold and you don't catch it; you keep falling and take the fall.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-021","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Ledge Catch","t":"Other","x":"Hard catches depend on skill. At Climbing 0 you can only hold a ledge after a fall that wouldn't have hurt you anyway. At Climbing 100 you can hold one after a fall of about 15 m. Fall further than your skill can hold and you don't catch it; you keep falling and take the fall.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-022","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"Forward, or a fresh press of Jump, climbs up onto the top, or over it if it's thin. A ledge with no room above it, such as a window sill, just keeps you hanging.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-023","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"Left and Right move you along the ledge (a shimmy). The hands follow the ledge as it rises, falls and bends. You stop where it ends or breaks.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-024","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"Corners: the shimmy goes round the corners of a building, inside and out, and round towers and rooms of any shape: square, eight-sided or round. Keep the key held and you carry on round. Going round a corner uses your grip like the rest of the shimmy.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-025","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"Back climbs down the wall under you.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-026","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"Crouch lets go. You fall from where you were hanging, so the drop is shorter than it looks from the top.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-027","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"Rework","x":"Hold Forward against a wall for a moment and you climb it. There's no dice roll any more and no random slipping.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-028","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"New","x":"Forward climbs up, Back climbs down, Left and Right move across. Let go of the keys and you stay where you are.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-029","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"New","x":"Jump with Forward held at a sheer wall grabs it straight from the jump.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-030","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"New","x":"Climbing down to the floor sets you back on your feet. A ledge too narrow to stand on, such as a window sill, stops you on the wall above it. Crouch lets go.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-031","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"Other","x":"If you're crouched under something low, you can't start a climb until there's room to stand up.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-032","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"New","x":"At the top, with Forward held, you pull yourself over the edge as soon as it's within reach. If there's no room up there, you climb on until the edge is at your hands and hang from it. Under a cornice that sticks out, you reach round it and hang from its edge.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-033","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Climbing","t":"Rework","x":"Your Climbing skill sets how fast you climb: slower than before at Climbing 0, faster at 100.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-034","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"Hanging and climbing wear out your grip. When it runs out, you let go.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-035","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"A fresh grip lasts about 6 seconds at Climbing 0 and 30 seconds at Climbing 100.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-036","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"It lasts less when you're tired: at no Fatigue, about a third as long.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-037","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"Holding still on a wall with your feet on it tires you half as fast as hanging or moving.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-038","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"It comes back in a couple of seconds once you're standing on something, or treading water.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-039","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"A Grip meter shows with the breath bar while you hold on, and while it comes back. It turns red, and you're told \"Your grip is failing.\", when it's nearly gone.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-040","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Grip","t":"New","x":"With no grip left you can't catch or grab anything until it comes back.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-041","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Saving","t":"New","x":"Save while you hang or climb and the load puts you back on the wall where you were, with the grip you had left. Save in the middle of a climb onto a ledge and you load at the end of it.","g":["climbing","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-042","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Carrying more than half of what you can carry shortens your reach. With a full pack, a ledge has to be about 30 cm lower to reach.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-043","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Climbing sets how high you can reach, how fast you pull yourself up, climb and shimmy, how long your grip lasts, and how long a fall you can still catch.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-044","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Past 100, Climbing still makes you climb and shimmy faster, up to 1.4 times as fast at 200, just as it does for ordinary climbing.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-045","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Climbing onto or over something, and catching a ledge or a wall, each cost about as much fatigue as a jump and train Climbing. A vault trains Jumping. Time on a wall costs fatigue as climbing always has, and trains Climbing as often as the old climb did.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-046","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Vault","t":"New","x":"Climbing onto or over something, and catching a ledge or a wall, each cost about as much fatigue as a jump and train Climbing. A vault trains Jumping. Time on a wall costs fatigue as climbing always has, and trains Climbing as often as the old climb did.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-047","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Other","x":"Khajiit and the Climbing spell help here too.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-048","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Rework","x":"With Roleplay & Realism on, you can't climb, catch or hang while holding a weapon, just as with ordinary climbing. Drawing one on a wall makes you let go. You can still vault. Sheathe your weapon (or use bare hands) to climb.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-049","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Vault","t":"Other","x":"With Roleplay & Realism on, you can't climb, catch or hang while holding a weapon, just as with ordinary climbing. Drawing one on a wall makes you let go. You can still vault. Sheathe your weapon (or use bare hands) to climb.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-050","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Enhanced Climbing","t":"New","x":"Enhanced climbing is under *The world* in Features. It's on by default. Turn it off to keep Daggerfall's own climbing.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-051","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Enhanced Climbing","t":"Other","x":"Offline, the classic UI always uses classic climbing.","g":["climbing","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5270-052","v":"0.1.5270","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Enhanced Climbing","t":"New","x":"Online it's on for everyone, whichever UI they use, so every player can reach the same places.","g":["climbing","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-001","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Bring up to two hands with you. In your boat's menu, choose Companions and pick a hand to Take ashore. They walk with you everywhere: through towns and the wilds, into shops and houses, and down into dungeons. Pick them again from your boat's menu to Send back aboard. While you sail, they're aboard with the rest of the crew, and step ashore with you again.","g":["companions","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-002","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"They fight at your side. Companions attack anything hostile near you, quest monsters included, and enemies fight them back, even with monster infighting switched off. Your own blows, arrows, spells and thrown torches never hurt them, and each one shows a green health bar over their head.","g":["companions","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-003","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"They fight at your side. Companions attack anything hostile near you, quest monsters included, and enemies fight them back, even with monster infighting switched off. Your own blows, arrows, spells and thrown torches never hurt them, and each one shows a green health bar over their head.","g":["companions","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-004","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"In co-op too. Companions fight your friends' monsters as well as your own, and your friends' monsters fight them back. Everyone in the game sees your companions as allies, in dungeons as well.","g":["companions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-005","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"They keep up. With nothing to fight, a companion follows a few steps behind and finds a way round walls. They won't chase an enemy far from you: drawn too far off, they come back to your side. If you leave one far behind, or drop down a floor, they catch up to you. Fast travel, doors and loading a save all bring them along, wounds as they were.","g":["companions","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-006","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"They keep up. With nothing to fight, a companion follows a few steps behind and finds a way round walls. They won't chase an enemy far from you: drawn too far off, they come back to your side. If you leave one far behind, or drop down a floor, they catch up to you. Fast travel, doors and loading a save all bring them along, wounds as they were.","g":["companions","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5286-007","v":"0.1.5286","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Knocked out, never killed. A companion who runs out of health is carried back to the ship to rest for eight hours before they can come ashore again, and their crewmates' spirits take a small knock. While ashore, a companion's place on deck stands empty, and the crew card says who is ashore with you.","g":["companions","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5289-001","v":"0.1.5289","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"Your boats are marked on the compass. Every boat you've put in the water shows as a little teal boat on the compass, pointing the way to her from anywhere outdoors, however far off she is - in another town, across the bay, or in another region. If she's behind you, the mark waits at the end of the compass on the side to turn toward.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5289-002","v":"0.1.5289","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"Find a boat you've lost track of. A Large Boat's deed and a Rowboat's parts are used up when you put the boat in the water, so if you died aboard and woke at a temple, or simply forgot where you left her, follow the mark back to her.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5289-003","v":"0.1.5289","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"Other","x":"The boat you're steering isn't marked, and neither is one you're standing on or right beside.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5289-004","v":"0.1.5289","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"A boat you left in a dungeon's water points you to that dungeon.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5289-005","v":"0.1.5289","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Compass","t":"Other","x":"Works on both the Classic and Enhanced compass, and in the Overworld view.","g":["naval","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-001","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"New","x":"Link your Patreon. Open your account card (the profile mark on the main menu). Under Patreon, press Link Patreon. It opens Patreon in your browser: press Allow, then press Link to (your username) on the page that follows.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-002","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"New","x":"Your tier is your title. Disciples and Heralds get their tier's title and glyph beside their name while their pledge is active. Wear the title from Title on the account card, as any other.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-003","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"New","x":"It keeps up by itself. Change tier on Patreon and your title changes with it. End your pledge and the title goes. Nobody has to hand anything out.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-004","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"Other","x":"Back in the game, the card reads your account again, so you see your new title as soon as you return.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-005","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"New","x":"Refresh asks Patreon again if your title looks out of date. Unlink takes your Patreon off this account.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-006","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Herald Title","t":"New","x":"Herald is new: the Patreon tier between Disciple and Hierophant. The title is in azure, and its glyph is a herald's trumpet with a banner hanging from it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-007","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Herald Title","t":"New","x":"Herald patrons get it as soon as they link their Patreon.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-008","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"Other","x":"Linking needs a registered account (a username and a password). A guest account can't link.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-009","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"Other","x":"One Patreon account links to one game account. Linking it to a different game account moves it there - the page tells you which account had it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-010","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"Other","x":"The page after Patreon always names the game account you're linking. If it isn't yours, close the page and nothing is linked.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-011","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"Other","x":"If your card is declined, the title pauses until Patreon says the payment went through.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5294-012","v":"0.1.5294","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Patreon Link","t":"Other","x":"Titles already given by name stay as they are. Hierophant is custom and is still given by name.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5308-001","v":"0.1.5308","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5317-001","v":"0.1.5317","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5325-001","v":"0.1.5325","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5333-001","v":"0.1.5333","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-001","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"You can no longer get stuck on a roof.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-002","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Over a parapet: press Jump at a parapet or rail with a long drop behind it, and you climb over it and hang from its far side. Then climb down with Back, or let go.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-003","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Off an edge: crouch and walk to the edge of a roof or a wall top, and you lower yourself over it and hang from the edge. Pitched eaves count, up to 45°. Walking off without crouching still just walks off.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-004","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Holding Forward as you lower yourself doesn't climb you straight back up. Press it again when you want to climb.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-005","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Low parapets over a short drop can be climbed over too.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-006","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Rework","x":"With Roleplay & Realism stopping you from climbing, you stay crouched at the edge instead of walking off it.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-007","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"New","x":"Leaps have their own longer, flatter arc, set by your Jumping skill. The ordinary jump hasn't changed.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-008","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"New","x":"with Left or Right to leap sideways to the next handhold along the wall (1.5 m to 2.5 m);","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-009","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"New","x":"with nothing else held, where there's nothing to climb onto, to leap up to a ledge above you (1 m to 1.8 m);","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-010","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"New","x":"with Back to push off the wall and jump away from it. You can catch a ledge on the way. A leap uses a tenth of your grip.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-011","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"Other","x":"with Back to push off the wall and jump away from it. You can catch a ledge on the way. A leap uses a tenth of your grip.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-012","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Running Leap","t":"New","x":"Running leap: run at an edge and press Jump to leap 4 m to 7 m. It always carries you at least as far as an ordinary jump would. Pressing a moment after you run off the edge still works, and you leap the way you were running. In the air you reach a little further for ledges.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-013","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Running Leap","t":"Other","x":"A running leap needs a real drop: running down stairs or off a low step, Jump is an ordinary jump. There's no leap while crouched, under Slowfall, or wading.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-014","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Wall Run","t":"New","x":"Wall run: run at a wall at full pace and press Jump to run 1 m to 2 m up it and grab the ledge at the top, or keep climbing the wall.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-015","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Past a window sill: from a hang on a sill with more wall above it, Forward climbs on up past it.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-016","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"Other","x":"A leap trains Jumping; a wall run trains Climbing.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-017","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing Feel","t":"New","x":"The view moves with you. A catch jolts the view down, harder after a long fall. Hanging sways a little. Shimmying and climbing rock from one hand to the other. Pulling up, you look up at the edge and then over it. A vault dips over the top, lowering yourself looks down over the edge, and corners turn the view with the wall. Leaps kick the view outward. A failing grip shakes. The jolts, sways and tilts are first person only; the turns (a corner's, a leap's) turn your view in third person too.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-018","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing Sound","t":"New","x":"You can hear it. Hands slap onto stone, boots scrape for footholds, you haul yourself over edges, and grit crumbles away when your grip starts to go. Every hand and foot hold is heard, never the same sound twice in a row. Hard pulls, leaps and long catches can make your character grunt (with combat voices on). These are part of Enhanced sounds.","g":["climbing","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-019","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Your weapon goes down while your hands are on the wall, and comes back up when you let go. You can't swing while climbing, as in Daggerfall. With the Morrowind-style arms, your weapon is put away and you see your own hands on the stone instead.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-020","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Hanging: both hands grip the ledge, palms down, elbows out, with the feet against the wall below.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-021","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Shimmying: hand over hand. The leading hand reaches out first and the other closes up behind it, one hand off the ledge at a time. Stop part-way through a reach and the hand settles on the nearer handhold.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-022","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Climbing a wall: hands reach up in turn, with the opposite foot following each hand.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-023","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Moves: you reach for the ledge you leap at, push up and over when you pull yourself onto a ledge, tuck your knees when you vault, squat and lower yourself over an edge, and run your feet up a wall.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-024","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"A failing grip makes the hands tremble and the feet scrabble. A hard catch swings the body under the hands.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-025","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"In first person the hands reach the ledge you see.","g":["climbing","morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-026","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Other players see your body climb the same way, including the moves.","g":["climbing","morrowind","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-027","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Third-Person View","t":"New","x":"In third person your character turns to face the wall while climbing and turns back after, even if you are still turning the view.","g":["climbing","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-028","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Online, other players see you facing the wall you're climbing, posed off the ground rather than walking in the air, and hear you climb. (This needs the updated server.)","g":["climbing","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5381-029","v":"0.1.5381","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Performance","x":"Climbing over very detailed walls is faster, and so is every collision check in the game that finds nothing to push against.","g":["climbing","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-001","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Rework","x":"Pitched roofs: you can climb onto a roof from its eave, up to a 50° pitch. That takes in Daggerfall's steep roofs, which are a little over 45°.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-002","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Overhanging roofs: most of Daggerfall's roofs stand out past their walls. Jump at one from under it or from just outside it and you catch the roof's edge and hang there, clear of the wall. Its edge can be up to about 0.8 m out from the wall.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-003","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Under a roof that overhangs, you reach out to the roof's edge and hang from it, then Forward pulls you up onto the roof. A roof that stands out more than about 0.8 m, such as the deep overhang over a gable end, is out of reach. So is one steeper than 50°.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-004","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Other","x":"Under a roof that overhangs, you reach out to the roof's edge and hang from it, then Forward pulls you up onto the roof. A roof that stands out more than about 0.8 m, such as the deep overhang over a gable end, is out of reach. So is one steeper than 50°.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-005","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"Rework","x":"Jump always gets you off a wall. If there's nothing to leap to that way, Jump pushes you off the wall, as Jump with Back does. Near the top of a wall you're climbing, Jump pulls you up onto it, as Forward does. Only a grip too weak to leap keeps you holding on.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-006","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Leaps","t":"Rework","x":"Jump always gets you off a wall. If there's nothing to leap to that way, Jump pushes you off the wall, as Jump with Back does. Near the top of a wall you're climbing, Jump pulls you up onto it, as Forward does. Only a grip too weak to leap keeps you holding on.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-007","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Jumping or falling against a roof or a parapet too steep to stand on no longer leaves you hanging in the air. You slide down it.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5384-008","v":"0.1.5384","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Jumping into the edge of a low roof no longer leaves you standing in mid-air on the edge.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5386-001","v":"0.1.5386","d":"2026-10-01","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-001","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Gear wears at about Daggerfall's own rate. Two of the combat mods made weapons wear several times faster than the original game, and armour many times faster. Their wear options are now off by default, online and offline.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-002","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Only the damage that gets through wears your gear. Under the combat overhaul, armour soaks up part of a blow instead of turning it aside, so a blow wears your weapon and the piece it hits by what got past the armour. Good armour wears slower.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-003","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Claws and bites no longer wear your armour. Only blows from weapons do, as in the original game.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-004","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Fix","x":"Broken enchanted gear is no longer destroyed. It breaks and stays in your pack, and a smith can repair it.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-005","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Repairs","t":"Economy","x":"Repairs cost half as much. Every smith and guild now charges a third of Daggerfall's repair price, down from two thirds. With the slower wear, keeping a Daedric longsword in shape costs between a seventh and a tenth of what it did, and Daedric armour far less.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-006","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Repair Kits","t":"Rework","x":"Repair kits mend up to three quarters. Field Repair Kits and smith-made Repair Kits now restore a piece to about three quarters of its condition at most. That keeps your gear working in the field; a smith restores it fully, and a freshly sharpened blade hits harder than a worn one.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-007","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Repair Kits","t":"Fix","x":"A kit isn't wasted. If everything it could mend is already at three quarters or more, it tells you so and isn't used up, from your pack or from the hotbar. It won't spend itself on a piece that's only a sliver below three quarters.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-008","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"A kit asks before it goes on the wrong piece. If your worn gear is past three quarters and the only piece the kit can mend is something else you're carrying, it asks first, and you can keep the kit.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-009","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Shops","t":"Rework","x":"Shops pay for worn loot as you found it. A weapon or piece of armour you loot, or buy worn from a shop, sells for no more than the condition it was in when you got it, even after a repair. Repairs are for using your gear, not for selling it. Gear that came to you whole sells at its own condition, as before. Offline, nothing changes.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-010","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Healing Potions","t":"New","x":"Alchemists always stock Potions of Healing. Every alchemist has a few each day (more in a better shop), and general stores keep one to three. Online they're half price, like every potion.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-011","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Healing Potions","t":"New","x":"You'll find more of them. Enemies that carry loot sometimes have one, and the treasure piles in most dungeons hold one more often than before.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-012","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Your crew companions carry what a person of their strength can. A companion's pack now has a weight limit based on their strength: from about 67 kg to about 97 kg, depending on their class. A strength spell you cast on them raises it. The pack window shows how much they're carrying.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-013","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"When a pack is full, the companion says they can't carry any more. If you store gold, they take only what they can carry.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5393-014","v":"0.1.5393","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Other","x":"Offline, you can turn the combat overhaul's own wear back on, on Physical Combat And Armor Overhaul's tile on the Features page. It wears gear the way that mod does, a little faster than the old default. If you had changed these options before, they've been reset once.","g":["equipment","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-001","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"Rework","x":"Herb patches, ore veins, boulders, trees, bodies and fishing water now use the loot list. Look at one and the same box that lists a body's loot shows its name, your profession, and what you can do there: \"Pick Red Rose\", \"Quarry the stone\", \"Skin the Grizzly Bear\", \"Search the Grizzly Bear\", and so on.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-002","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Pick an action the way you take loot. Click it, press your activate key, or tap it. The Up arrow moves to the next action; you can rebind it in Controls.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-003","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"An action you can't do yet says why, right on its row: no tool, rank too low, or the day's limit reached.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-004","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Starting a hold action (kneeling, steadying, skinning) from the list holds it for you, the same as using the tool from the hotbar.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-005","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"On the Classic skin and on touch screens, where the loot box isn't shown, the same choices come up as a small list window.","g":["professions","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-006","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"Rework","x":"The gathering minigames no longer open a panel over the screen. Each one is drawn on and around your crosshair, so you can see the world while you work. The rules and timings haven't changed.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-007","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Mining","t":"Rework","x":"Mining: the rock's five strike points are marked where they are on the rock and move as you look around. The glinting point shows the circle a blow must land in to count double. A blow flashes on the crosshair, gold when it hits the glint.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-008","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Logging","t":"Rework","x":"Logging: a ring closes on the notch around your crosshair. It lights up in the band where a strike is a Clean Cut.","g":["logging","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-009","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Herbalism","t":"Rework","x":"Herbs: your hold fills as an arc around the crosshair. It turns orange if you bruise the plant by moving.","g":["herbalism","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-010","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Basket","t":"Rework","x":"The Basket: the glint appears near the crosshair with a ring showing how long it has left. Your three finds show as small diamonds.","g":["foraging","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-011","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Hunting","t":"Rework","x":"Skinning: the cutting line is laid on the body itself, with a faint band showing how far off it you can stray. The first point shows where to start, and points light up as you pass them.","g":["hunting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-012","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fishing","t":"Rework","x":"Fishing: winding the net fills an arc, with the throw distance beside it. While you wait, a float sits under the crosshair, and a gold ring flashes at a tug. Hauling is a small upright bar beside the crosshair; keep the weight inside the band.","g":["fishing","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-013","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"One line of help. A short hint sits under the crosshair and fades after a couple of seconds. Your progress shows as small diamonds above it.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-014","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Every strike, find, slip, splash and tug also has a sound.","g":["professions","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-015","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"With reduced motion turned on in your system, nothing pulses. Logging uses a short still bar instead of the closing ring.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-016","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"Rework","x":"The anvil's heat, the loom's beat and the workbench's plane use the Enhanced Plus look: the same dark stone frame as the loot box, with your strikes shown as diamonds. They work exactly as before.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-017","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pickups","t":"New","x":"On the Enhanced skin, what you pick up shows at the centre of the screen. Each item gets a card with its picture, its name in its rarity colour, and how many you took. Gold shows as \"+N Gold\".","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-018","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pickups","t":"New","x":"Take more of the same item while its card is up and the count goes up instead of adding another card.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-019","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pickups","t":"New","x":"Up to four cards show at a time. Each stays about two and a half seconds, then fades. They stay clear of the crosshair, the loot box, the hotbar and the HUD.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-020","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pickups","t":"New","x":"Works for every quick-loot take, one item or Take All, from a body, a dropped pile or a catch of fish.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-021","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"The bushes around bandit camps and other World of Daggerfall sites no longer float in the air or sink into the hillside. Each one now stands on the ground under it. Tents, fires, walls and rocks are where they were.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-022","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Party Travel","t":"Fix","x":"The leader keeps the Party tab while the party readies up. Choosing a destination on the travel map used to close the Party tab, taking the ready count and Call off with it. It now comes back when the map closes.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-023","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Party Travel","t":"Fix","x":"The leader's \"Waiting for the party to ready up (n/m ready)\" message stays up for the whole round and updates as people answer.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5406-024","v":"0.1.5406","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Party Travel","t":"Fix","x":"A member who has the Party tab open answers there with Ready or Stay behind. The pop-up question only appears if the tab is closed.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5409-001","v":"0.1.5409","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Every blow wears your weapon and armour twice as much as before. A steel longsword now loses about an eighth of its condition over a hundred swings (it was about a sixteenth). Armour wears faster too, though good armour still lasts.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5409-002","v":"0.1.5409","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Other","x":"Still far gentler than before the last update. Armour wears a fraction of what it did then, and a monster's claws still don't wear it at all.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-001","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Boulders","t":"Fix","x":"More boulders, and at the rock. A rock field's boulders mostly never appeared, and the few that did often had their loose stones out on open ground, well away from any rock. Now each boulder's stones sit at the foot of a rock you can see, and a large rock can hold more than one boulder or vein on its different sides.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-002","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Boulders","t":"Rework","x":"More boulders each day. Each map square now holds up to 3 boulders a day in woodlands, haunted woodlands and subtropical land (was 1), 4 in mountain woods (was 2), and 5 in mountains and deserts (was 3). Swamps and rainforests still have none. Ore veins sit at the rocks more often too.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-003","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Boulders","t":"Rework","x":"More boulders each day. Each map square now holds up to 3 boulders a day in woodlands, haunted woodlands and subtropical land (was 1), 4 in mountain woods (was 2), and 5 in mountains and deserts (was 3). Swamps and rainforests still have none. Ore veins sit at the rocks more often too.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-004","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Boulders","t":"Rework","x":"More boulders each day. Each map square now holds up to 3 boulders a day in woodlands, haunted woodlands and subtropical land (was 1), 4 in mountain woods (was 2), and 5 in mountains and deserts (was 3). Swamps and rainforests still have none. Ore veins sit at the rocks more often too.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-005","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Settlements","t":"Rework","x":"Settlements. Mining, quarrying, herb gathering and logging don't work in a town, farm, temple, tavern or wealthy home, or within a city block of one. Veins, boulders, herb patches and trees no longer appear there, so nothing glows or shows on the compass that you can't work. At the edge of that area, the node's action now says \"not in a settlement\" on its row, rather than offering an action that E then refuses. Dungeon veins aren't affected.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-006","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Settlements","t":"Rework","x":"Settlements. Mining, quarrying, herb gathering and logging don't work in a town, farm, temple, tavern or wealthy home, or within a city block of one. Veins, boulders, herb patches and trees no longer appear there, so nothing glows or shows on the compass that you can't work. At the edge of that area, the node's action now says \"not in a settlement\" on its row, rather than offering an action that E then refuses. Dungeon veins aren't affected.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-007","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fishing","t":"Fix","x":"Fishing: cast at any angle. Casting the net was only offered while you looked level or down at the water. It's now offered whether you look down, level or up, up to about 55 degrees either way. An herb patch or other spot you look at directly still comes first, and so does a door, a person or a chest you're looking at: E only casts when nothing else under your look takes it.","g":["fishing","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-008","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Boulders","t":"Other","x":"The boulders you can quarry glow and show on the compass. Walk up to one until \"Quarry the stone\" shows in the loot box, then press E, click it, or use the Pick-Axe.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-009","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Rework","x":"Twice as many nodes. Every map square now holds twice the herb patches, trees and ore veins each day, in every climate (woodlands: 8 herb patches, 12 trees, 4 veins). The daily limit per profession is unchanged, so you gather the same amount in a day, with less walking between nodes.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-010","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Other","x":"Twice as many nodes. Every map square now holds twice the herb patches, trees and ore veins each day, in every climate (woodlands: 8 herb patches, 12 trees, 4 veins). The daily limit per profession is unchanged, so you gather the same amount in a day, with less walking between nodes.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-011","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Gathering groups. On the Overworld, each profession's nodes on a nearby map square show as one diamond in that profession's compass colour, with how many are left today - for example \"Mining ×6\" or \"Herbalism ×7\". Only the nearest twelve within about 3 km are shown, and a group you've worked out disappears.","g":["overworld","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-012","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Gathering filter. The Overworld's filters have a new Gathering switch to hide or show them.","g":["overworld","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-013","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Clicking a group walks you to that spot, as clicking open ground does.","g":["overworld","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-014","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"Players standing close together on screen show as one larger dot, such as \"5 travellers\".","g":["overworld","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-015","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"Players off the edge of your screen in roughly the same direction share one arrow.","g":["overworld","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-016","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"Only the six players nearest you on screen show their full title, Renown, guild tag and glyphs; others, and players off the edge of the screen, show just their name.","g":["overworld","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5420-017","v":"0.1.5420","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overworld","t":"Other","x":"Your party is always shown in full.","g":["overworld","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-001","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Friends","t":"Rework","x":"One friend list on every device. Your friends, requests and party were tied to the browser you played in, so a laptop and a desktop each had their own list. They now belong to your account: the same list wherever you sign in. The first time each of your devices connects after this update, the friends it knew are added to your list, so nobody is lost.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-002","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Friends","t":"Fix","x":"A friend list can't be taken over. A friend list that someone else had set up under your account before this update is thrown away, not given to you.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-003","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Friends","t":"New","x":"An old copy of the game says so. If a tab or the desktop app is still running an older build, it now tells you to update the game to see your friends and party, instead of showing an empty list.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-004","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cast When Used","t":"Fix","x":"Cast when used items work in dungeons. A bracer of Ice Storm, a scarab of Fireball, or any item that casts a spell when used now casts it underground. Before, the click just swung your weapon, the item still lost condition, and the spell went off the next time you clicked outside.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-005","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cast When Used","t":"Fix","x":"A spell readied from an item goes through doors with you. Use an item, then step into or out of a dungeon, and the spell is still ready to cast. It no longer fires by itself once you're back outside, or vanishes.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-006","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cast When Used","t":"Fix","x":"The right cost underground. The readied-spell line in a dungeon showed an item's spell at its full spell-point cost. An item's spell costs you nothing, and now it says so.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-007","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Slowfall","t":"Fix","x":"Slowfall no longer sticks you to walls. A slow fall that drifted into a wall could catch onto it, or hang on a steep cliff face, before you reached the ground. Now you slide down and land.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-008","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Slowfall","t":"Fix","x":"No more hard landing after a slow fall. Slipping off a wall you were climbing while Slowfall was on used to drop you at full speed and hurt. Now you come down gently.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-009","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Jump Spell","t":"Fix","x":"Steep slopes while Jump is active. With the Jump spell's air control, holding Forward into a steep face no longer holds you up on it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-010","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Slowfall","t":"Fix","x":"Gliding onto a roof. A slow glide that reaches a lower roof's edge still steps up onto it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-011","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"Rework","x":"Turn and tilt the 3D map together. Holding the right mouse button now turns and tilts the dungeon map at the same time. A small wobble while you turn still doesn't tilt it, but a real move up or down does, for the rest of that drag.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-012","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"World of Daggerfall's mountains look like rock. The big rock formations and mountains had their texture stretched across hundreds of metres, so they looked like smeared ground reaching into the sky. Their rock now repeats at a natural scale, so it shows as rock from up close to about a kilometre away. Their size and shape haven't changed.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-013","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"Planks and stone stay straight. Fort palisades and dock stonework keep their planks and blocks running the right way.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-014","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cursor","t":"Fix","x":"The game's cursor stays the game's cursor. Hovering over a menu's scrollbar, or moving close to the right or bottom edge of the screen, no longer swaps the custom cursor for your system's arrow. This works with both the classic and the enhanced look.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-015","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Scrollbars","t":"Rework","x":"Tidier scrollbars. Menu scrollbars use the game's slim stone style. On a phone or tablet, scrollbars stay hidden as before.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5433-016","v":"0.1.5433","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Area Spells","t":"Other","x":"Area spells of buffs reach you. An Area at Range or Area Around Caster spell made only of buffs, such as Regenerate with Fortify, also lands on you when you cast it. This came in the previous update.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-001","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Day Length","t":"Rework","x":"A day online is now 30 minutes. Nights, full moons and quest hours come round four times as often. Midnight falls on the hour and the half hour, real time, and dusk at :22:30 and :52:30 (the Online page gives your own clock's times).","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-002","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Day Length","t":"Rework","x":"A day online is now 30 minutes. Nights, full moons and quest hours come round four times as often. Midnight falls on the hour and the half hour, real time, and dusk at :22:30 and :52:30 (the Online page gives your own clock's times).","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-003","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Sky","t":"Rework","x":"The sun, moons, stars, seasons and calendar all run on the faster sky.","g":["clock","sky","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-004","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Sky","t":"Other","x":"The switch happens once, a little after this update arrives, at a moment when both schedules show the same hour. The sky never jumps. Until then the Online page says when it turns.","g":["clock","sky","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-005","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Vampirism","t":"Rework","x":"A vampire waits at most 15 real minutes for nightfall, and the message counts it right.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-006","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"World Clock","t":"Other","x":"The world's business keeps its pace: shops, prices, guild shelves, weather fronts, gates and raids. The weather follows the sky's season and time of day.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-007","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gate Messages","t":"Rework","x":"Gate and raid messages now give your local time only.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-008","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Werewolf","t":"Rework","x":"Online, the full moon forces the change for its night only, from dusk to dawn: 15 real minutes. At dawn you can change back.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-009","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Werewolf","t":"Rework","x":"Full-moon nights come two real hours apart, then none for fourteen.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-010","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quest Timers","t":"Rework","x":"Quest timers now run on your own clock. Resting, waiting and travel spend them, as in Daggerfall: \"come back in 3 days\" is a 72-hour rest, about half a minute.","g":["clock","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-011","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quest Timers","t":"Rework","x":"Time away is still never charged. A closed or hidden tab costs a quest timer half an hour of game time at most.","g":["clock","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-012","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quests","t":"Rework","x":"A quest's hours (\"daily from 12:00 to 13:00\"), the date and the season follow the sky. A daily window comes round every 30 real minutes.","g":["clock","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-013","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quest Journal","t":"Fix","x":"Journal dates match the calendar you see.","g":["clock","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-014","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quest Timers","t":"Rework","x":"In a party, each member's copy of a shared quest runs on that member's clock. When a timer runs out on one copy, it runs out for the whole party.","g":["clock","quests","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-015","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quest Timers","t":"Fix","x":"Quest timers ran a fifth to a third slow while you played, offline too. They count every second now.","g":["clock","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5446-016","v":"0.1.5446","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quest Timers","t":"Other","x":"Online saves made before this update move their quest timers onto your clock the first time they load. Older saves otherwise load as before.","g":["clock","quests","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5448-001","v":"0.1.5448","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5451-001","v":"0.1.5451","d":"2026-10-02","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"No more giant dark shards hanging in the sky. The last update's fix for floating bushes around bandit camps also lifted the big boulders that World of Daggerfall's rock fields are built from. They stuck up out of their rock piles as huge dark slabs, some hundreds of metres tall, around Hadus and near rock fields everywhere. The boulders are back where the mod sets them, down in the rock.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-001","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Tall dungeon walls can be climbed again. Dungeon walls are built from stacked sections. Where the section above sticks out a little, such as the edge of a doorway or a pillar, your climb used to stop about 1.4 m up, under it. That's how a \"two blocks\" wall left you stuck in a pit. Now you shift along the wall past it, up to about half a metre, and keep climbing.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-002","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Low Climbing skill gets you off the ground. Some large dungeon walls stopped a climber with low Climbing skill right at the floor. You now climb them at your normal pace.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-003","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"No more falling off at gaps in a wall. Some dungeon walls have a thin gap between two sections. The climb used to treat the gap as a ledge, grab it, then let go and drop you to the floor, again and again. It now climbs straight past it.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-004","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Climbing past a step in a wall. Where the upper part of a wall sits a little further back than the lower part, you used to stop at the step, or grab it and fall off. Now you climb past it and carry on to the top. Climbing back down, you stop on the wall above the step, as you do above a window sill.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-005","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Climbing in a corner. In a narrow shaft you can end up on the side wall instead of the one you're facing. When the wall you're turned towards has a top within reach, you now climb onto it, instead of carrying on up the side wall.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-006","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Climbing down from just over a step or a recess in a wall no longer freezes you or makes you let go. You climb down to the floor.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-007","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"No more letting go near a sloping top. Where a wall's top leans back at a corner, you could let go and fall from high up. You now hold on.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-008","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Turning your view while you climb no longer pulls you sideways onto a crate, a low wall or a fence beside the wall.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-009","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Travel","t":"Rework","x":"Enemies near you end a hunt. When you're offered a hunt on the road (\"You spot a set of animal tracks...\"), an enemy that comes near (or a duel opponent) now closes the offer, or ends the search if you've already started, so you can turn and fight. Nothing is searched and no time passes. The result page itself stays until you close it, so close it quickly if an enemy is coming.","g":["hunting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-010","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"No ambush while you read the result. The time a hunt takes now passes when you close the result, not while it's on screen. Before, a wandering enemy could appear and walk up while you were still reading.","g":["hunting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-011","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"A hunt is no longer offered while an enemy nearby is still on its way in.","g":["hunting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-012","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"Loading a save with a hunt open no longer charges the loaded game the hunt's time or puts its animal there.","g":["hunting","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-013","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"No fishing prompt at the helm. At sea, the \"Open Water / Cast the net\" prompt sat in the middle of the screen while you steered, and got in the way when you aimed the bow guns. It no longer appears while you're at the helm, aiming the guns or boarding. You can still fish from a deck you're standing on.","g":["naval","fishing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-014","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"The ship's sound no longer cuts out. Taking the helm and getting under way, or slowing down, used to restart the boat's sound from the beginning, so it cut out. The sound now carries on smoothly as you speed up and slow down.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5461-015","v":"0.1.5461","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"No more silent boats. With more than one boat nearby, one could be left silent until it started moving. Every boat can be heard now.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-001","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"The enhanced pack's paperdoll card now has a Stats button at the bottom centre of the card, in the figure's own column (it no longer sits on the right weapon's slot). Pressing it turns the card over on a 3D hinge (lift, shadow, content rising in) to a combat page; the button then reads Paperdoll and turns it back.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-002","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"Damage (min-max and average), hit chance, critical chance and what a critical does, backstab chance, and the expected damage of an average swing.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-003","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"A table per swing direction (sideways, thrust, down-right, down-left, overhead; a bow shows its release).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-004","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"Breakdown: weapon roll, material, Strength, proficiency, race, your attack term, the foe's armour and dodging.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-005","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"Defence (overall armour, the seven part numbers, dodging, biography, health), attributes with their effects, and the skills in play.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-006","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"The hit and damage are scored against a foe of your level in four real armour classes (chips at the top): Soft / Tough / Armoured monster (armour value 6 / 0 / -10, as the bestiary stores them) and a Human foe in mail.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-007","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"Other","x":"Enhanced skin only; the classic canvas window is untouched.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-008","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"prefers-reduced-motion gets a crossfade instead of the turn.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-009","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"Fix","x":"The page wears the window's pixel face (PIXEL_STACK: Pixelify Sans, Silkscreen's 5), not Barlow / Cormorant.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-010","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"Fix","x":"The shimmer is gone: the light sweep across the card while it turns is removed (the turn, lift, shadow and rising content stay).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5465-011","v":"0.1.5465","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Stats Card","t":"Fix","x":"The hit chances were far too high. The old reference foes were a hybrid: a class (human) foe's armour numbers (100 = unarmoured) with a monster's +40 (overhaul +50) bonus to be hit, so a bare foe read 97% whatever your skill. They are now the real thing: monsters carry armorValue x 5 (the bestiary runs -12..7, so 30 / 0 / -50 on each part) with the monster bonus; the human is a class foe with no bonus, and the overhaul reads the flat 60 it reads off every class foe (pcaaoArmorToHit). Damage figures were right and are unchanged.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-001","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"Grass is no longer dark. Up close, tufts of grass used to look almost black against the ground they grew from, and darker still at dusk, in rain and in storms. Grass is now painted in the ground's own colours: the base of each tuft matches the ground under it, and the blades get lighter towards their sunlit tips.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-002","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Grass blends into the land. Grass takes its colour from whatever ground it grows on, so it matches in every climate and season: the lush green of the woodlands, the grey-green of the mountains, the deep green of the swamps.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-003","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"No more yellow band. The grass a little way off used to show as a yellowish stripe across the field. Now the far grass fades into the ground's own colour.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-004","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Grass is lit like the ground. At dawn, at dusk, under clouds and by moonlight, the grass now takes exactly the same light as the ground under it, with Enhanced lighting on or off.","g":["grass","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-005","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Shade falls on the grass. Grass in the shade of a tree, a wall or a passing cloud is now shaded like the ground around it, instead of staying in full sun.","g":["grass","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-006","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"Rain doesn't darken the grass twice. Grass used to be darkened for bad weather on top of the dimmer light the weather already brings. Now it's darkened once, like everything else.","g":["grass","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-007","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Lanterns and torches light the grass. At night, grass near a lantern, a campfire or the torch in your hand now glows along with the ground under it, instead of staying dark beside the lit ground.","g":["grass","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-008","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Grass on hillsides. Grass on a slope facing away from the sun is now shaded like the slope, instead of staying as bright as grass on level ground.","g":["grass","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-009","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Texture mods. With a texture mod that replaces the ground, grass now takes its colours from the mod's ground.","g":["grass","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-010","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"Classic lighting. With Enhanced lighting off, grass is no longer brighter and greener than it is with Enhanced lighting on.","g":["grass","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-011","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Grass","t":"Other","x":"The grass is under *Sight* in Features: Grass sets how much grass grows and its style (Pixel or Smooth). Both styles get the new colours and light.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-012","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"Trees grow together in forests. Trees used to be spread evenly over the whole map, one every few steps, all lined up in rows. Now they gather into woods, from small copses to forests a few kilometres across, with open grassland between them dotted with bushes, flowers, rocks and the odd lone tree.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-013","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"Forests run on from one area to the next. A forest doesn't stop where the land around you finishes loading.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-014","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"Fix","x":"No more rows. Every tree and bush stands at its own spot, so a wood looks like a wood.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-015","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"Dungeons hide in the woods. Dungeons, ruins, shrines, graveyards, covens and World of Daggerfall's camps, forts and ruins are usually surrounded by forest, with a clearing round them big enough for their tents and walls. Towns, farms and taverns stand in cleared fields. World of Daggerfall's rock fields and mountains are scenery: the woods grow round them as anywhere else, but never through the rocks.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-016","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"Paths stay clear. No tree or bush grows on a road or a track.","g":["terrain","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-017","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"The Oblivion Gate keeps its clearing. No tree stands through the gate, its plinth or the Sigil Broker.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-018","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"Other","x":"Deserts are unchanged. The Desert and Subtropical lands keep Daggerfall's own scattered plants.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-019","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Logging","t":"Rework","x":"Loggers chop in the woods. The day's trees to fell stand in the forests whenever there's a forest nearby. The lone trees of open land are only used where there's no wood at all.","g":["logging","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-020","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"Real forests is under *The world* in Features. It's on by default and takes effect when the world next loads. Turn it off to spread the trees evenly, as Daggerfall does.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-021","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"Other","x":"Forests hold more trees than Daggerfall's even scatter, about two and a half times as many on average. If the outdoors runs slowly on your machine, turning Real forests off is one more way to lighten it.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5476-022","v":"0.1.5476","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Real Forests","t":"New","x":"Online, Real forests is on for everyone, so everyone in a room walks the same woods and chops the same trees.","g":["terrain","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-001","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Seats. Every town with a palace is a seat: a town a guild will one day hold. Daggerfall, Wayrest and Sentinel are the three crown seats, the largest prizes.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-002","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Arriving. Walking into a seat town tells you whose it is: \"Anticlere, held by the Silver Hand <SH>.\" or \"Anticlere. Its Charter is unheld.\" In a week with a siege called there, the line says when: \"A siege is called for Wednesday at 20:00 UTC.\"","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-003","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Arriving. Walking into a seat town tells you whose it is: \"Anticlere, held by the Silver Hand <SH>.\" or \"Anticlere. Its Charter is unheld.\" In a week with a siege called there, the line says when: \"A siege is called for Wednesday at 20:00 UTC.\"","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-004","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"a grey ring around the town;","g":["seats","map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-005","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"a crown above the three capitals, in their kingdom's colour (Daggerfall blue, Wayrest crimson, Sentinel gold);","g":["seats","map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-006","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"a thin second ring on the Marches (half in each claiming kingdom's colour) and a green one on the Free Lands.","g":["seats","map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-007","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Selecting a seat shows its Charter.","g":["seats","map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-008","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Banners. A seat town flies its kingdom's plain banner at its palace door, its city gates and above its notice boards. The Free Lands fly none.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-009","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"The pledge. Each week a guild chooses one seat in a region to work toward, in up to five regions. An Officer or the guildmaster sets it from the Seat tab of that town's Notice Board, until Friday 18:00 UTC. Influence earned in a region where your guild pledged nothing doesn't count.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-010","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"The pledge. Each week a guild chooses one seat in a region to work toward, in up to five regions. An Officer or the guildmaster sets it from the Seat tab of that town's Notice Board, until Friday 18:00 UTC. Influence earned in a region where your guild pledged nothing doesn't count.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-011","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"The Watch. Walking the streets of the seat town: 1 every 2 minutes, up to 60 a day. Standing still doesn't count.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-012","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"Gate kills. A gate you helped close in the seat's region: 300, up to 900 a week.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-013","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"Renown. Renown XP you earn in the seat's region: 1 for every 20, up to 400 a week.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-014","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"Homes. A member's home in the seat town: 25 a day, up to five homes a guild.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-015","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"Tribute. The guildmaster can burn silver from the guild's treasury: 1 for every 10 silver, up to a fifth of the guild's week at that seat.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-016","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"The limits. One account counts for at most 2,000 a seat a week. The first guild any of your characters contributes to in a week is your account's guild for that week's seats. A character counts after 7 days in its guild.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-017","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Tab","t":"New","x":"The Seat tab. A seat town's Notice Board has a new Seat tab: the week's standings, every pledged guild under its banner, your guild's pledge and your own week there. Officers pledge from it, and the guildmaster pays Tribute.","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-018","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Turning","t":"New","x":"Every Sunday at 18:00 UTC the week's influence is counted.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-019","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Turning","t":"New","x":"An unheld seat. The guild with the most influence takes the town's Charter if it has at least 6,000 (a crown seat: 30,000) and its treasury can pay the fee: 8,000 silver (a crown: 80,000), which is burnt. If it can't pay, the next guild past the line can.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-020","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Turning","t":"Economy","x":"An unheld seat. The guild with the most influence takes the town's Charter if it has at least 6,000 (a crown seat: 30,000) and its treasury can pay the fee: 8,000 silver (a crown: 80,000), which is burnt. If it can't pay, the next guild past the line can.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-021","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Turning","t":"New","x":"Contested. If the second guild is within 10% of the first, nobody takes it this week. The two will meet in a Tourney.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-022","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Turning","t":"New","x":"A held seat. The holder's defence is its own week of influence, raised or lowered by the town's Standing, plus what it carried over. A guild past the line and the defence wins a Right of Siege. A guild wins at most one a week, at its strongest seat. A new Charter can't be challenged at its first Turning.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-023","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Turning","t":"New","x":"A held seat. The holder's defence is its own week of influence, raised or lowered by the town's Standing, plus what it carried over. A guild past the line and the defence wins a Right of Siege. A guild wins at most one a week, at its strongest seat. A new Charter can't be challenged at its first Turning.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-024","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charters","t":"New","x":"Holding a Charter. The town's banners fly your guild's heraldry, its ring on the map is filled in your colours, and the gate names your guild. Your guild counts at its seat without pledging, and can't pledge elsewhere in that region. A seat held without a challenge gains Standing.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-025","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Legacy","t":"New","x":"Legacy. A tenth of each guild's influence at a seat carries into the next week.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-026","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charters","t":"New","x":"Titles and glyphs. Every member of a guild holding a town's Charter wears a tower beside their name; a crown's members wear their kingdom's crown. The guildmaster can wear the title Warden of <Town> (a crown: Protector of <Kingdom>) from their account card.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-027","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Tab","t":"New","x":"The Seat tab now shows the holder, this week's siege or Tourney, what it takes to claim or challenge, and the town's Chronicle. The guildmaster can give the Charter up there. A guild holding a Charter can't disband until it does.","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-028","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charters","t":"New","x":"The Seat tab now shows the holder, this week's siege or Tourney, what it takes to claim or challenge, and the town's Chronicle. The guildmaster can give the Charter up there. A guild holding a Charter can't disband until it does.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-029","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Upkeep","t":"Economy","x":"Upkeep. Each Sunday's Turning takes a held seat's upkeep from the guild's silver treasury: 2,500 for a palace, 15,000 for a crown (scaled to how many players played that week, from 0.4x to 1.5x).","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-030","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Upkeep","t":"Economy","x":"Upkeep. Each Sunday's Turning takes a held seat's upkeep from the guild's silver treasury: 2,500 for a palace, 15,000 for a crown (scaled to how many players played that week, from 0.4x to 1.5x).","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-031","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overreach","t":"New","x":"Holding more than one seat costs more. A crown counts as 3 and a palace as 1. Everything past your biggest seat is your Overreach: each point adds 25% to every seat's upkeep and takes 5% off every seat's defence. A crown plus a palace is 1 point; two crowns are 3.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-032","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Overreach","t":"New","x":"Holding more than one seat costs more. A crown counts as 3 and a palace as 1. Everything past your biggest seat is your Overreach: each point adds 25% to every seat's upkeep and takes 5% off every seat's defence. A crown plus a palace is 1 point; two crowns are 3.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-033","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Neglect","t":"New","x":"Neglect. If the treasury can't pay, the seat falls into Neglect: Standing drops 10 and the week is owed. Next Sunday both weeks are due. Pay them and you're back (Standing -5 for paying late). Miss again and the Charter lapses.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-034","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Neglect","t":"New","x":"Neglect. If the treasury can't pay, the seat falls into Neglect: Standing drops 10 and the week is owed. Next Sunday both weeks are due. Pay them and you're back (Standing -5 for paying late). Miss again and the Charter lapses.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-035","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Tithe","t":"New","x":"The Tithe. Your guildmaster or an Officer sets it at the town's board, 0-10% (a crown 0-15%), once a week. It comes out of the seller's proceeds on every sale at the boards your seat covers: its own town and every town in the region nearer to it than to another seat. It also takes the same cut of courier fees paid there. It goes into your guild's silver treasury. Sales for gold pay no Tithe.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-036","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Tithe","t":"New","x":"The Tithe. Your guildmaster or an Officer sets it at the town's board, 0-10% (a crown 0-15%), once a week. It comes out of the seller's proceeds on every sale at the boards your seat covers: its own town and every town in the region nearer to it than to another seat. It also takes the same cut of courier fees paid there. It goes into your guild's silver treasury. Sales for gold pay no Tithe.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-037","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Shops","t":"Economy","x":"Members shop cheaper. Members of the holding guild pay 10% less at the seat town's shops (15% at a crown) for buying and repairs, and 5% more off while Standing is 80 or higher.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-038","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Shops","t":"Economy","x":"Members shop cheaper. Members of the holding guild pay 10% less at the seat town's shops (15% at a crown) for buying and repairs, and 5% more off while Standing is 80 or higher.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-039","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Standing, the town's favour, now moves each week: | Change | Standing | |---|---| | A low Tithe (half the cap or less) | +2 | | A high Tithe (over three quarters of the cap) | -3 | | Held without a challenge | +5 | | Each gate felled in the region | +2 (up to +6) | | Each of your writs filled there | +1 (up to +5) | | No member of yours kept the Watch | -5 | | Neglect | -10 | | Paying late | -5 | Below 20 the town is in Unrest: challengers earn a quarter more influence there, and visitors are told so when they arrive.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-040","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Standing, the town's favour, now moves each week: | Change | Standing | |---|---| | A low Tithe (half the cap or less) | +2 | | A high Tithe (over three quarters of the cap) | -3 | | Held without a challenge | +5 | | Each gate felled in the region | +2 (up to +6) | | Each of your writs filled there | +1 (up to +5) | | No member of yours kept the Watch | -5 | | Neglect | -10 | | Paying late | -5 | Below 20 the town is in Unrest: challengers earn a quarter more influence there, and visitors are told so when they arrive.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-041","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Standing, the town's favour, now moves each week: | Change | Standing | |---|---| | A low Tithe (half the cap or less) | +2 | | A high Tithe (over three quarters of the cap) | -3 | | Held without a challenge | +5 | | Each gate felled in the region | +2 (up to +6) | | Each of your writs filled there | +1 (up to +5) | | No member of yours kept the Watch | -5 | | Neglect | -10 | | Paying late | -5 | Below 20 the town is in Unrest: challengers earn a quarter more influence there, and visitors are told so when they arrive.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-042","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Edicts","t":"New","x":"Edicts. Each week the guildmaster or an Officer proclaims an Edict for the next week at the board. It takes effect at the Turning. Only Market Day can be proclaimed two weeks running. | Edict | Effect | Cost | |---|---|---| | Market Day | A tenth off at the town's shops, for everyone | - | | Open Gates | Every home in town is open to all | Standing +3 | | Curfew | Guards are much tougher at night, and crimes there cost double reputation | Standing -2 | | Festival | Everyone who comes to town gets +5 to every attribute for a game day (two real hours) | Standing +10; 2,500 silver (a crown 10,000) | | Levy | A tenth of what's gathered near the town goes to its stockpile | Standing -2 | | Bounty | World of Daggerfall camps near the town drop double loot, and the treasury pays 20 silver for each camp you clear, up to 5 a day, from what you set aside | the set-aside |","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-043","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Edicts","t":"Other","x":"Edicts. Each week the guildmaster or an Officer proclaims an Edict for the next week at the board. It takes effect at the Turning. Only Market Day can be proclaimed two weeks running. | Edict | Effect | Cost | |---|---|---| | Market Day | A tenth off at the town's shops, for everyone | - | | Open Gates | Every home in town is open to all | Standing +3 | | Curfew | Guards are much tougher at night, and crimes there cost double reputation | Standing -2 | | Festival | Everyone who comes to town gets +5 to every attribute for a game day (two real hours) | Standing +10; 2,500 silver (a crown 10,000) | | Levy | A tenth of what's gathered near the town goes to its stockpile | Standing -2 | | Bounty | World of Daggerfall camps near the town drop double loot, and the treasury pays 20 silver for each camp you clear, up to 5 a day, from what you set aside | the set-aside |","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-044","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Tab","t":"New","x":"The Seat tab shows everyone the Tithe and this week's Edict. Members also see next week's Edict, the upkeep due and any debt. The guildmaster and Officers set the Tithe and proclaim Edicts there.","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-045","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"The window. A seat's guildmaster or an Officer sets when its battles are fought, at the town's board: a day from Wednesday to Saturday and a start from 16:00 to 02:00 UTC. A start after midnight is the night after the day you pick. If you never set one, it's Wednesday 20:00.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-046","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"The schedule. At each Sunday Turning, every Right of Siege and every Tourney is placed in the coming week: a siege in the holder's window, a crown siege on Saturday (Daggerfall 20:00, Wayrest 21:00, Sentinel 22:00), a Tourney on Wednesday at 20:00. If a guild would have to fight two battles at once, the second moves two hours on, and the Seat tab says so.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-047","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"The schedule. At each Sunday Turning, every Right of Siege and every Tourney is placed in the coming week: a siege in the holder's window, a crown siege on Saturday (Daggerfall 20:00, Wayrest 21:00, Sentinel 22:00), a Tourney on Wednesday at 20:00. If a guild would have to fight two battles at once, the second moves two hours on, and the Seat tab says so.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-048","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"Signing up. The Seat tab shows who has won the Right, who holds the Charter and when battle is joined, and how many have signed for each side. Members who were in the guild for 7 days at the Turning, and whose account counted for the guild that week, sign themselves: 10 a side at a palace, 20 at a crown. Signing closes 10 minutes before the battle, and you can give your place back until then.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-049","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Sellswords","t":"New","x":"Sellswords. A side's guildmaster can hire up to 2 Sellswords (4 at a crown) by username, for a fee of up to 5,000 silver held from the treasury. The Sellsword signs from the same Seat tab. A Sellsword can't be in either guild and can't fight for both sides within four weeks. A contract nobody has signed can be withdrawn, and the fee goes back.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-050","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Sellswords","t":"Economy","x":"Sellswords. A side's guildmaster can hire up to 2 Sellswords (4 at a crown) by username, for a fee of up to 5,000 silver held from the treasury. The Sellsword signs from the same Seat tab. A Sellsword can't be in either guild and can't fight for both sides within four weeks. A contract nobody has signed can be withdrawn, and the fee goes back.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-051","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Battlefield","t":"New","x":"The battlefield. A siege's room lets in only the fighters signed for each side, plus up to 60 spectators. You start at your side's camp and rise there after a fall, every 20 seconds (30 at a crown). You can't strike or harm your own side, and you can only heal your own side.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-052","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Battlefield","t":"New","x":"The battlefield. A siege's room lets in only the fighters signed for each side, plus up to 60 spectators. You start at your side's camp and rise there after a fall, every 20 seconds (30 at a crown). You can't strike or harm your own side, and you can only heal your own side.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-053","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Banners. Stand at a banner point (the Gate, the Market, the Temple) with no living enemy within 8 m for 20 seconds to raise it. A contested banner freezes, and a half-raised one falls back if you leave it.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-054","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Banners. Stand at a banner point (the Gate, the Market, the Temple) with no living enemy within 8 m for 20 seconds to raise it. A contested banner freezes, and a half-raised one falls back if you leave it.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-055","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Throne","t":"New","x":"The Throne. It opens to the attackers once they hold 2 of the 3 banners (3 of 4 at a crown). Holding it uncontested for 2 minutes (3 at a crown) takes the seat.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-056","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Throne","t":"New","x":"The Throne. It opens to the attackers once they hold 2 of the 3 banners (3 of 4 at a crown). Holding it uncontested for 2 minutes (3 at a crown) takes the seat.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-057","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Clock","t":"New","x":"The clock. A siege lasts 30 minutes (45 at a crown); at time the holder keeps the seat. A Tourney lasts 20 minutes and goes to the side holding more banners.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-058","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Clock","t":"New","x":"The clock. A siege lasts 30 minutes (45 at a crown); at time the holder keeps the seat. A Tourney lasts 20 minutes and goes to the side holding more banners.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-059","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"No-shows. If no attacker comes within 10 minutes, the attackers forfeit.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-060","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Receipt","t":"New","x":"Your receipt. At the end every fighter gets a receipt signed by the server: the result, and whether you earned Honours (you stood for half the battle or felled a foe). Lost your connection at the end? Come back within the battle's window and it's waiting for you.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-061","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"Attackers win: the Charter is theirs, at Standing 50, and it can't be challenged at the next Turning. The old holder's carried-over influence there is gone.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-062","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"The holder holds: +15 Standing (+10 if the attackers ever reached the Throne) and a fifth more defence at the next Turning - but only if the attackers raised at least one banner. The attackers lose their influence there that week and can't challenge the seat at the next Turning.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-063","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"A forfeit: +10 Standing (once a Season against the same challenger) and the same fifth more defence; the challenger is shut out the same way.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-064","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tourney","t":"New","x":"A Tourney: the side holding more banners takes the Charter and pays the claim fee. If it can't pay, the other side may; if neither can, the seat stays unheld. A dead heat goes to the guild with more influence there that week.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-065","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Sellswords","t":"Economy","x":"Sellswords are paid their fee when the battle ends; an unsigned contract's fee goes back to the guild.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-066","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"New","x":"Fighting it. From ten minutes before the battle until its window closes, the town's Notice Board offers Enter the battle (or Watch the battle if you didn't sign). You fight in the town's own streets. The bar across the top shows each banner (^ attackers, o defenders, ~ being raised), the Throne, the clock and each side's fighters; your vitality and your next wave sit at the lower right. When it ends, a result card shows who holds the seat, and your Honours once your receipt is claimed (the game claims it for you, and keeps it to try again if the server can't answer).","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-067","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Honours","t":"Economy","x":"Honours. Fight on the winning side and earn 50 silver and 2,000 Renown XP; on the losing side 25 silver and 1,000. Every honoured fighter also rolls on the Spoils of War: a Warforged Steel Ingot, a Standard-bearer's Silk or a Siege-cracked Gem (a third each), into your Stores. The same two guilds earn Honours from each other once a Season (8 weeks).","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-068","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Honours","t":"New","x":"Honours. Fight on the winning side and earn 50 silver and 2,000 Renown XP; on the losing side 25 silver and 1,000. Every honoured fighter also rolls on the Spoils of War: a Warforged Steel Ingot, a Standard-bearer's Silk or a Siege-cracked Gem (a third each), into your Stores. The same two guilds earn Honours from each other once a Season (8 weeks).","g":["seats","siege","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-069","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crowns","t":"New","x":"Kingdom reach. A guild holding a crown - Daggerfall, Wayrest or Sentinel - earns a quarter more influence from every source but Tribute at that kingdom's palace seats, its own included, so a crown defends its realm better.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-070","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Marches","t":"New","x":"The Marches. Betony, Anticlere and Lainlyn are each claimed by two crowns. Each claiming crown's holder earns an eighth more there; a guild holding both claiming crowns, a quarter.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-071","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Free Lands","t":"New","x":"The Free Lands. No crown reaches Balfiera, Orsinium or the Wrothgarian Mountains. Instead, every guild's Watch there counts a tenth more.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-072","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Conscription","t":"New","x":"Conscription. A new Edict, for a crown alone. While it rules, the kingdom's palace seats held by other guilds pay the crown 2% of their Tithe for that week (a March's seats 1% to each claiming crown that proclaims it). It's paid at the Turning, after the guild's own upkeep, from whatever its treasury holds; each seat that pays loses 5 Standing, and both Chronicles say so. A guild's Tithe for the week is shared evenly across all its seats, and a guild that took no Tithe pays nothing. The Free Lands never pay.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-073","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"A crown's Edict. A crown's guild can proclaim a Royal Tourney for the coming week. It costs 5,000 silver, set aside as the week's prize.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-074","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"The ring. All that week a duel ring stands in the crown city's palace square, before the palace door. It moves to the castle's entrance in a later update. Open the town's Notice Board, go to its Seat tab and choose Enter the Royal Tourney (or Watch).","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-075","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"Bouts. To challenge a contender, open their card and press Challenge. To accept a challenge made to you, press Challenge on the challenger's card within 30 seconds. One bout fights at a time: both fighters start whole on their marks, and after a three-second countdown only the two of them can strike each other.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-076","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"The server referees every blow, and you can't leave the ring during a bout.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-077","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"A fall ends the bout. Five minutes with no fall is a draw, and a fighter who leaves the room loses.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-078","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"The ladder. Each bout won counts on the ladder, which is shown on the Seat tab and on screen. The same two players count at most three bouts a day against each other.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-079","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"The champion. When the week ends, the ladder's leader wins the 5,000 silver and the title \"Champion of <Kingdom>, Season N\" for good. Ties go to fewer losses, then to whoever reached their wins first. If no bout was won, the prize goes back to the crown.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-080","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"New","x":"Fealty. A guild holding a palace seat in a crown's kingdom, or in a March that crown claims, can swear fealty to the guild holding the crown. Either side's Guildmaster or an Officer offers it on the Seat tab, by the other guild's tag, and the other side accepts it there. The Free Lands swear to no one, and a guild holding a crown is no one's vassal.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-081","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"Economy","x":"The vassal pays its liege 5% of its Tithe each week, at the Turning, after its own upkeep.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-082","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"New","x":"The liege adds half its reach to the vassal's defence: an eighth of the vassal's own influence at a seat in the crown's kingdom, a sixteenth at a March.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-083","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"New","x":"Never against each other. A liege and its vassal can't pledge against each other's seats, and Conscription never takes from a vassal.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-084","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"New","x":"Breaking it. Either side can break it at any time. It ends at the next Turning, and the side that broke it loses 10 Standing at every seat it holds. If the two no longer fit (the liege loses its crown, say), the fealty simply ends at the Turning, at no cost.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-085","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pacts","t":"New","x":"Pacts. Any two guilds can sign a Pact of non-aggression. One side offers it on the Seat tab, and the other offers it back to sign it. It lasts to the end of the Season. Neither guild can pledge against a seat the other holds. A Pact can be broken early, but the whole server is told in red.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-086","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pacts","t":"New","x":"Pacts. Any two guilds can sign a Pact of non-aggression. One side offers it on the Seat tab, and the other offers it back to sign it. It lasts to the end of the Season. Neither guild can pledge against a seat the other holds. A Pact can be broken early, but the whole server is told in red.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-087","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"Other","x":"None of this can be sworn or signed while either guild is pledged against the other's seat that week.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-088","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"The Seasons. The war runs in Seasons of 8 weeks, after a four-week Season 0 (the open beta). They are named for the months: the Season of Morning Star, of Sun's Dawn, and on through the year. The Seat tab shows the week of the Season you're in.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-089","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"every guild holding a crown earns \"Crowned in Season N\", and every guild that held a seat for the whole Season earns \"Keeper of <Town>, Season N\". The titles go to the Guildmaster and are kept for good.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-090","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"every member of a Keeper's guild wears the Season's banner ribbon through the next Season: a thin band in the guild's colours under their name, which everyone online sees. A member who joins after that Turning doesn't wear it.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-091","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Legacy is cleared, and every seat's Standing moves halfway back toward 50.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-092","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"Other","x":"The Charters stand, and every seat's Chronicle records who held it at the Season's end.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-093","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Season 0's end wipes the seats, influence, Chronicles, fealty and Pacts. Your silver, Stores, profession tracks, titles and Honours are kept.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-094","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Hall of Records","t":"New","x":"The Hall of Records. Every seat's palace keeps its whole Chronicle as a book: press a shelf in the palace to read it, one chapter a Season. The Chronicle now dates each line by its Season - \"In the third week of the Season of Morning Star...\" - on the Seat tab too. The three castles keep theirs on their shelves, and every seat's board has a \"Read the Hall of Records\" button.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-095","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"Rework","x":"Once a Season now means the Season itself. A Pact lasts to the Season's end, and the same two guilds earn Honours from each other once a Season.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-096","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"The world moves under the war. Each week, each kingdom, the Marches and the Free Lands have a Tide. The Seat tab shows this week's and next week's for the seat's land, so you can plan for the next Turning. Tides run only while a Season is counted.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-097","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Plague: the Watch counts half, and Festivals cost double.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-098","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Daedric Incursion: gate kills give double influence and double silver.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-099","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Royal Wedding: Festivals cost half, and every held seat gains 3 Standing.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-100","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Tax Revolt: a Tithe above 5% costs 3 more Standing.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-101","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Harvest: gathering yields a quarter more (herbs, foraging, wood, ore and stone).","g":["seats","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-102","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Blight: herbs and wood yield a quarter less.","g":["seats","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-103","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Storm Season: fishing yields half again.","g":["seats","fishing","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-104","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Bandit Summer: couriers into the land take twice as long. These count where the witnesses have confirmed the ground, as the Marches' bonus does.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-105","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Orc Raids: World of Daggerfall camps in the land hold twice the foes. Each camp you clear gives your guild 50 influence at its seat in the region, up to 5 camps a day and 250 influence a week.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-106","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"New","x":"Storm Season also slows the sea: a voyage into the land takes half again as long on the water.","g":["seats","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-107","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"New","x":"The works. A held seat can raise ten works, each in tiers: the Walls, the Gatehouse (at a crown, or once a palace's Walls reach tier 3), the Watchtowers, the Barracks, the Market Hall, the Shrine, the Forge, the Workshop, the Apothecary and, in a port town, the Harbour.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-108","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"New","x":"Beginning a work. The holder's guildmaster or an Officer begins the next tier of a work from the Seat tab at the town's board, for example *\"Raise the Walls to tier 2 (3,000 silver)\"*. The silver is spent from the guild treasury. One tier of each work can be building at a time.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-109","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"New","x":"The stockpile. A work also needs materials (Cut Stone, planks, ingots and more). They come from the seat's stockpile: the Levy's tenth, and seat writs. Each delivery moves straight into the works being built, in the table's order. When the last need is met, the tier stands 2, 4 or 7 days later. The Seat tab shows each work, what it still needs, the day it stands, and the stockpile.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-110","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Writs","t":"New","x":"Seat writs. On the Work tab, a writ's new For choice sends its units to a seat your guild holds (its stockpile), or to a seat it's pledged to this week (its Siege Camp). A seat writ only asks for a material a work needs. The card says where the units go and shows the guild's banner. A guild member of 7 days who delivers their own units also raises the guild's influence at the seat by the units' value.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-111","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Camp","t":"New","x":"The Siege Camp. At the Turning, a camp whose guild won the Right of Siege sends its Ram Kits to the coming battle if the seat has a Gatehouse. Everything else in every camp is burnt.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-112","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"New","x":"Losing them. A captured seat's works each drop a tier, and anything being built is lost (its materials go back to the stockpile). A Fortifier on the defending side keeps the Walls from dropping, once a Season at each seat. At a Season's end every work drops a tier. A relinquished Charter keeps its works.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-113","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"New","x":"Losing them. A captured seat's works each drop a tier, and anything being built is lost (its materials go back to the stockpile). A Fortifier on the defending side keeps the Walls from dropping, once a Season at each seat. At a Season's end every work drops a tier. A relinquished Charter keeps its works.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-114","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Market Hall","t":"New","x":"The Market Hall works at once: the holder's Tithe can go a point higher for each tier, and anyone listing at a board in its town may hold a quarter more listings for each tier.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-115","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Market Hall","t":"New","x":"The Market Hall works at once: the holder's Tithe can go a point higher for each tier, and anyone listing at a board in its town may hold a quarter more listings for each tier.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-116","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Shrine","t":"New","x":"The Shrine. Each tier of a seat's Shrine gives its holder +1 Standing every week. It also gives the holder 50 influence a tier for every gate felled in the seat's region that week, which counts toward its defence. The Seat tab shows the Shrine's share of the holder's influence.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-117","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Shrine","t":"New","x":"The Shrine. Each tier of a seat's Shrine gives its holder +1 Standing every week. It also gives the holder 50 influence a tier for every gate felled in the seat's region that week, which counts toward its defence. The Seat tab shows the Shrine's share of the holder's influence.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-118","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Watchtowers","t":"New","x":"The Watchtowers. The holder's members are told when a challenger reaches half of their defence (tier 1) or a quarter of it (tier 2), for example *\"The Watchtowers of Anticlere see the Iron Circle <IC> past half of our defence.\"* Each warning comes once in chat, and the Seat tab lists them under the standings.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-119","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crafting Halls","t":"New","x":"The crafting halls. The holder's members crafting in the seat's town get a better quality roll: a step for each tier of the Forge (Smithing) and of the Workshop (Carpentry, Outfitting and Masonry). The Apothecary's step waits for the professions it serves.","g":["seats","crafting","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-120","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Harbours","t":"New","x":"The Harbour. A Harbour can be raised at any seat on the coast, where the sea touches the town. Once it stands, the town is a port for the holder's members: the travel map's ports, ship travel's port rules, and the boat deed all count it.","g":["seats","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-121","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siegewright","t":"New","x":"The Siegewright. Carpentry's master choice is open now. A work begun by a Siegewright stands a day sooner. Its +50% to a Ram's health comes with the battle update.","g":["seats","carpentry","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-122","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ram Kit","t":"New","x":"The Ram Kit. Carpenters can make the Ram Kit at Carpentry 60 from 40 Oak Planks, 20 Iron Ingots and 4 Bear Hides. It goes to your Stores and never to your pack. A guild pledged to a seat posts a writ for Ram Kits to fill its Siege Camp; each kit counts as 108 silver's worth of materials. A seat's own stockpile and the guild Stores don't take them.","g":["seats","carpentry","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-123","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ram Kit","t":"Other","x":"The Ram Kit. Carpenters can make the Ram Kit at Carpentry 60 from 40 Oak Planks, 20 Iron Ingots and 4 Bear Hides. It goes to your Stores and never to your pack. A guild pledged to a seat posts a writ for Ram Kits to fill its Siege Camp; each kit counts as 108 silver's worth of materials. A seat's own stockpile and the guild Stores don't take them.","g":["seats","carpentry","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-124","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gatehouse","t":"New","x":"The Gatehouse. A crown always has a Gatehouse, and a palace gains one once its holder raises it. It stands at the Throne, the palace door, with 20,000 health, half again for each tier. While it stands, the attackers cannot take the Throne, however many banners they hold. Attackers break it with their weapons, each blow dealing a tenth of its damage, and with Rams. When it falls, it is breached and the Throne is open. At a crown, the Gatehouse and the Throne move to the castle's entrance in a later update.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-125","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gatehouse","t":"New","x":"The Gatehouse. A crown always has a Gatehouse, and a palace gains one once its holder raises it. It stands at the Throne, the palace door, with 20,000 health, half again for each tier. While it stands, the attackers cannot take the Throne, however many banners they hold. Attackers break it with their weapons, each blow dealing a tenth of its damage, and with Rams. When it falls, it is breached and the Throne is open. At a crown, the Gatehouse and the Throne move to the castle's entrance in a later update.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-126","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Rams","t":"New","x":"The Rams. The Ram Kits a guild's Siege Camp sent become Rams at the gate, one at a time. A Ram has 3,000 health (4,500 if a Siegewright fights for the attackers). While two attackers stand within 3 m of it, it strikes the Gatehouse for 500 every ten seconds. Defenders can hack it apart with their weapons. When one is destroyed, the next arrives with the attackers' next wave.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-127","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Walls","t":"New","x":"The Walls. Each tier of the Walls brings the defenders back 3 seconds sooner after they fall.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-128","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Bar","t":"New","x":"On your screen. The siege bar shows the Gatehouse's and the Ram's health, the Ram's next stroke, the Rams still in the camp and the Walls' tier. A swing near the gate strikes the Gatehouse (attackers) or the Ram (defenders) when no enemy is in reach.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-129","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Barracks","t":"New","x":"The Barracks' guards. A seat's Barracks sends 2, 4 or 6 town guards (City Watch) to fight for the holder. Each stands at a post: the Throne first, then the banners. A guard attacks the nearest attacker within 12 m and chases no further than 24 m from its post. Its blow lands a second after it starts, for 20, so stepping away dodges it. A guard counts as a defender where it stands, so attackers can't raise a banner or hold the Throne past it. A felled guard returns with the defenders' next wave at their camp and walks back to its post. Only attackers can strike guards, and felling one counts toward your Honours.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-130","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revolts","t":"New","x":"When a town revolts. A seat whose Standing falls to 0 at the Turning revolts in its holder's siege window the next week (a crown's at its Saturday slot). If a Right of Siege is won there that week, the siege takes the window instead.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-131","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revolts","t":"New","x":"The rising. A Rebel Captain (400 health) and 12 rebels hold the palace door. They attack the holder's fighters who come near. A felled rebel stays down.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-132","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revolts","t":"New","x":"Putting it down. The holder's members sign to defend, as for a siege, and have two hours to fell the Captain. If they do, the seat's Standing returns to 20. If he still stands at the end, or nobody comes, the Charter lapses and the seat is unheld.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-133","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revolts","t":"New","x":"Putting it down. The holder's members sign to defend, as for a siege, and have two hours to fell the Captain. If they do, the seat's Standing returns to 20. If he still stands at the end, or nobody comes, the Charter lapses and the seat is unheld.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-134","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revolts","t":"Other","x":"Honours. A revolt earns no Honours. Putting it down is its own reward.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-135","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Bar","t":"New","x":"The siege bar shows the Captain's health and the rebels still standing, and the Chronicle records how it ended.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-136","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Palace Hall","t":"New","x":"Your guild's palace. A guild holding a palace seat now has that palace as a guild hall. Its members can open the guild's Stores from any cupboard there and rest in its beds. The court stays where it always stood.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-137","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Palace Hall","t":"New","x":"Your guild's palace. A guild holding a palace seat now has that palace as a guild hall. Its members can open the guild's Stores from any cupboard there and rest in its beds. The court stays where it always stood.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-138","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charter Room","t":"New","x":"The Charter Room. The holder's Officers and guildmaster can decorate the palace's largest room from the decorator's catalogue, up to 100 pieces. Each piece costs what it costs in a home, paid by the Officer placing it. Half of a piece's cost goes back to the guild's treasury when it is taken down.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-139","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charter Room","t":"New","x":"The board. A board placed in the Charter Room is the guild's own board, as in a guild hall.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-140","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charter Room","t":"Other","x":"Keep clear of the court. No piece can stand within 2 m of anyone in the palace or of a quest's spot.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-141","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charter Room","t":"Other","x":"Lost with the Charter. When the seat changes hands or its Charter lapses, everything in the Charter Room goes. Nothing is refunded.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-142","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crown Castle","t":"New","x":"The crown's castle. A guild holding a crown seat has its castle's throne room as its hall. The guild's two banners hang on the wall behind the throne. A roster board and a Stores chest stand a few paces into the room: members open the guild's notes and Stores there. The throne room takes no decorations.","g":["seats","guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-143","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Battle","t":"Fix","x":"Leaving a battle. You can now leave a siege or a Royal Tourney: the bar's Leave button, the result card's Close, /leave in chat, walking out of the seat's town, or dying.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-144","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Battle","t":"New","x":"Battle announcements. Each battle at a seat is announced in red at the Turning, a day before, an hour before and five minutes before.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-145","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"Arrows and spells in a siege now count: an arrow or a harmful spell on a foe goes to the referee, and a heal on your own side. Teleport, Recall and Levitate don't work in a siege.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-146","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"Spectators get a free camera while they watch, and no longer stand on the field.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-147","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"A dropped fighter's place is held for five minutes. Back in time, you return at your side's camp.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-148","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fealty","t":"Fix","x":"Declining an offer. An offer of fealty or a Pact made to your guild can now be declined from the Seat tab.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-149","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Chronicle","t":"Fix","x":"The Chronicle now says how long a captured seat's siege lasted, and what Conscription and fealty actually paid.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-150","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Hall of Records","t":"Fix","x":"The Hall of Records can be read from every seat's board, and from the shelves in the three crown castles.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-151","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"A battle nobody finished is void at the Turning: the Sellswords' fees go home, and the challenger keeps its Right for next week.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-152","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"Fix","x":"A seat struck from the registry returns its holder's claim fee, if the Charter was won this Season and the guild's treasury has room for it.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-153","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"Fix","x":"Season 1's Keepers. A Charter won at Season 1's first Turning now counts as held for the whole Season.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-154","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Tithe","t":"Fix","x":"The Tithe on a split sale is now taken on the whole sale, as the market tax is.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-155","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Tab","t":"Fix","x":"The Seat tab reloads after every act, and the Relinquish button resets itself after four seconds.","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-156","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Market Hall","t":"Fix","x":"The Market Hall's Tithe. The extra Tithe points a Market Hall gives can now be set at the board.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-157","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revolts","t":"Fix","x":"Revolts. A revolt's defenders no longer need to have contributed to the guild the week before.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-158","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gatehouse","t":"Fix","x":"A crown's Gatehouse stands from the start, and the Seat tab now shows it.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-159","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Edicts","t":"Fix","x":"The Bounty Edict's words now say \"near the town\".","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-160","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Apothecary","t":"Fix","x":"The Apothecary can't be raised until the professions it serves are in.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-161","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tides","t":"Fix","x":"The Daedric Incursion's words now say gate kills give double silver too.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-162","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"Fix","x":"A captured seat's works. A project whose day had come now counts when its seat is captured, as it did in the battle. The works drop from that tier, and its materials stay with the seat.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-163","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Tithe","t":"Fix","x":"A crown's Tithe can now be set above 15% with a Market Hall, instead of failing.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-164","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seasons","t":"Fix","x":"A Season's end now lowers a project under way with its work. Its materials go back to the stockpile.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-165","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifications","t":"Fix","x":"A Charter lost (given up, Neglect, a revolt, a strike) now stops its works' projects. Their materials go back to the stockpile.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-166","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Writs","t":"Fix","x":"Seat writs can only be delivered while the guild still holds the seat, or is still pledged there for a Siege Camp.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-167","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"Guards, rebels and the Rebel Captain can't be shot from beyond their reach any more. One struck comes for whoever struck it.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-168","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Palace Hall","t":"Fix","x":"Loading into a palace or a crown castle now finds its guild hall, a moment after the seats are read.","g":["seats","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-169","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"A fallen guard or rebel no longer replays its fall every second.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-170","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Bar","t":"Fix","x":"The siege bar is hidden when you die or another window takes your seat.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-171","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Charter Room","t":"Fix","x":"A Charter Room chest pressed by a visitor now says whose it is.","g":["seats","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-172","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"Siege and Royal Tourney results now reach the server. Your client had been checking receipts against the wrong account id, so no result was ever claimed.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-173","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Edicts","t":"Fix","x":"Edicts at the Turning. An Edict changed while the Turning was being settled could pay out more than was set aside. The Turning now settles it again.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-174","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"Flying and sinking in battle. A fighter can no longer climb above the field or sink under it. Blows and spells from high up don't count, and a Tourney bout won't start unless both contenders are level.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-175","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege","t":"Fix","x":"Back from a drop. A fighter who reconnects returns to their side's camp straight away.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-176","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"Fix","x":"The Tourney's 48 now counts a returning contender too.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-177","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Receipt","t":"Fix","x":"Your receipt can be collected as soon as a battle ends, even if your place was taken while you were away.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-178","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Honours","t":"Fix","x":"Honours go to the character who signed for the battle.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-179","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Upkeep","t":"Fix","x":"A crown's upkeep shown in the Seat tab now uses the same week the Turning uses.","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-180","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Market Hall","t":"Fix","x":"A Market Hall's extra listings can now be used from the market tab, and listing hints include the seat's Tithe.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-181","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"The Tithe","t":"Fix","x":"A Tithe above its cap after a Season's wear lowers the Market Hall comes down with it.","g":["seats","market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-182","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pledges","t":"Fix","x":"Five regions now counts the regions your guild holds as well as those it pledged.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-183","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Tab","t":"Fix","x":"A crown's Seat tab shows its Saturday siege slot instead of the holder's window.","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-184","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Palace Hall","t":"Fix","x":"A palace hall lost while you're inside no longer leaves its furniture in your save.","g":["seats","homes","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-185","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seats","t":"Fix","x":"The seats are read again a minute after a failed read, instead of waiting until you travel.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-186","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Titles","t":"Fix","x":"Titles. Changing your aura, buying an insignia or unlinking Patreon no longer hides a Charter's title.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-187","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Curfew","t":"Fix","x":"The Curfew's night watch comes out at the sky's night.","g":["seats","sky"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-188","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Pacts","t":"Fix","x":"Pact breaks are limited per guild, and the day's red announcements are capped at 20.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-189","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Seat Registry","t":"New","x":"The registry. Each client works out the seats from its own game files. When you stand in a seat town, your game reports it to the server once a day. The server trusts a seat once three players whose accounts are at least a week old agree on it exactly.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-190","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fair Sieges","t":"New","x":"Fair sieges. In a siege the server keeps every fighter's health and checks every blow, spell and step: a blow lands only if the weapon you carry can reach and deal it, nobody heals or strikes faster than the game allows, and nobody runs faster than the fastest legal runner. A siege's health is its own (300, more with your Renown) and never touches your character's health, items or gold. A siege room lets in only the fighters each side signed, and spectators.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-191","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Buy a hall for your guild. A guildmaster whose guild has no hall can buy any house as the guild's hall. At the house's door, choose Buy it for <your guild>. Press it twice to buy it. On a touch screen, or where the door shows no list, the house's buy box offers the same choice.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-192","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Economy","x":"The guild treasury pays the house's price plus half again. Only gold that realm characters put into the treasury counts.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-193","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"A guild has one hall. The hall belongs to the guild, not to any character.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-194","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Who may walk in: the guild's members, or anyone. The guildmaster and Officers choose, at the hall's door or on the Guild tab.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-195","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Every cupboard is the guild's chest. For members it opens the guild Stores on the Guild tab.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-196","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Members may rest in its beds, use its crafting stations (forge, workbench and loom included) and cast spells in it.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-197","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"The guildmaster and Officers can decorate the hall with pieces from the catalogue. Each piece is paid for from the gold of whoever places it. When a piece is removed or shrunk, half of what it cost goes into the guild treasury.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-198","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Other","x":"Your own items can't be placed in a hall, and nothing dropped in a hall stays there. Its yard and outside can't be customised yet.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-199","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Economy","x":"Selling the hall: on the Guild tab, the guildmaster presses Sell the hall twice. 85% of what the hall cost, plus half of what its pieces cost, goes back into the treasury.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-200","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Other","x":"A guild with a hall can't be disbanded, and its last member can't leave or delete their character, until the hall is sold.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-201","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"The treasury ledger now shows what the hall's gold was for: bought, sold, or a piece's half back.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-202","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Board","t":"New","x":"Notes for your guild only. Every Notice Board has a new Guilds tab. It shows your guild's own board, which only its members can read.","g":["guild","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-203","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Board","t":"New","x":"Any member can pin a note for the guild. You can have 3 up at a time, apart from your notes on town boards.","g":["guild","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-204","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Board","t":"New","x":"You can take down your own notes. The guildmaster and Officers can take down anyone's.","g":["guild","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-205","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Board","t":"New","x":"Recruitment posters. The Guilds tab also shows the guilds recruiting in that town, each under its banner.","g":["guild","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-206","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Board","t":"New","x":"A board in your hall. Officers can place a Notice Board in the guild's hall from the decorator. For members it opens the guild's board.","g":["guild","notice-board","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-207","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Homes","t":"New","x":"Homes have a new setting under Who may enter: My guild. Members of your character's guild can then walk in.","g":["homes","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-208","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Heraldry","t":"New","x":"Every guild can raise a banner: a field colour, a border colour and a device. There are 16 colours and 24 devices (wolf, bear, stag, dragon, tower, crown, sword, sun, rose and more).","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-209","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Heraldry","t":"Other","x":"Ash can only be used as the border.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-210","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Heraldry","t":"New","x":"The guildmaster chooses on the Guild tab, which shows the banner as you choose it.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-211","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Heraldry","t":"Economy","x":"The first choice is free. Each change after that costs 500 silver from the guild's silver treasury, and the silver ledger shows it as a heraldry change.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-212","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Heraldry","t":"New","x":"Banners at the hall: once your guild has heraldry, two banners hang either side of its hall's door, swaying in the wind.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-213","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Rented Rooms","t":"Fix","x":"Rented rooms: a tenant can now sleep in the home they rent. They were told \"You have not rented a room here.\"","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-214","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Silver","t":"Rework","x":"Drakes are now called silver, everywhere you see them: your account card, the Bank (\"Sell silver\", \"8 gold for each silver\"), the Market and Work tabs, writs, the professions' prices, the Seat tab and your guild's silver treasury.","g":["marks","online"],"n":"Nothing else changed. Your balance is exactly what it was, just under the new name."},{"id":"0.1.5580-215","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Silver","t":"Other","x":"The metal is unchanged: Silver ore and the Silver Ingot are still materials, as before.","g":["mining","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-216","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Masonry","t":"New","x":"The mason's bench. Work stone at a General Store's bench (50 gold a work), or at a mason's bench in your own home (a new home station, 50,000 gold).","g":["masonry","crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-217","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Masonry","t":"New","x":"Cut Stone: 2 Rough Stone make 1 Cut Stone. From rank 0.","g":["masonry","crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-218","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Masonry","t":"New","x":"Mortar: 1 Sulphur, 1 Lead and 5 Rough Stone make 10 Mortar. From rank 10.","g":["masonry","crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-219","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Masonry","t":"New","x":"The chisel. Each work is a few strikes. Five lines are scored on the stone and one is marked: strike the marked line before it moves (the arrow keys, a number key, Space, or a tap on the line). Four strikes make a work, seven a carving. Strike every one true for a clean work and half again the XP.","g":["masonry","crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-220","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Masonry","t":"New","x":"XP follows your rank. Each unit gives XP at your rank's own tier, and +500 the first time you make it.","g":["masonry","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-221","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Mortar","t":"New","x":"Mortar is a new Stores material: withdraw it as an item, or sell it on the market.","g":["masonry","crafting","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-222","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Quarryman","t":"New","x":"Quarryman (50): Rough Stone cuts 1:1, not 2:1.","g":["masonry","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-223","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Builder","t":"New","x":"Builder (50): a seat's fortification projects you begin need 10% less stone.","g":["masonry","professions","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-224","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Fortifier","t":"New","x":"Fortifier (100): standing on a seat's defending side in a siege, you keep its Walls from dropping when it's captured, once a Season at each seat.","g":["masonry","professions","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-225","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Sculptor","t":"New","x":"Sculptor (100): carve stone furniture for your home - a column, a bench, a font and a statue plinth, from Cut Stone and Mortar. They arrive among your home's things, and can be sold on the market.","g":["masonry","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-226","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"The Professions page lists Masonry as practised, and the Stores page has the Mason's Bench.","g":["masonry","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5580-227","v":"0.1.5580","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Masonry","t":"Fix","x":"A stone work's XP is now said as Masonry's, not Smithing's.","g":["masonry","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5595-001","v":"0.1.5595","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5616-001","v":"0.1.5616","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-001","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crown Sieges","t":"Rework","x":"Crown sieges at the castle. At Daggerfall, Wayrest and Sentinel, the Throne, the Gatehouse, the defenders' camp and the Palace square now stand at the castle's entrance in the city, not the palace door.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-002","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"Rework","x":"The Royal Tourney's ring stands in the castle's square.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-003","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crown Sieges","t":"New","x":"Two more banners hang either side of the castle's entrance, in the holder's colours.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-004","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Tags","t":"New","x":"Guild tags in their colours. A player's <TAG> over their head now sits in a frame edged in their guild's colour, with the guild's shield beside it - for your own guild and every guild that holds or fights for a seat.","g":["guild","seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-005","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Siege Bar","t":"New","x":"The siege HUD shows both banners. The defenders' shield stands at the left of the battle bar and the challengers' at the right.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-006","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Chronicle","t":"New","x":"The Chronicle wears its arms. Each line of a seat's Chronicle on the Notice Board sits under the shield of the guild it is about, and the Hall of Records book now ends with a Roll of Arms naming each guild's heraldry.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-007","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"/siege void <seat>. A Moderator can now void a seat's battle of the week when it was won by an exploit found after it - a siege, a Tourney or a revolt. The Chronicle says so: \"The siege of X was voided by the Moderators.\"","g":["seats","siege","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-008","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"Before its result: the battle is called off and every Sellsword's fee goes home to the guild that offered it. The challenger's Right of Siege is spent - it does not carry to next week.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-009","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"After a capture: the Charter goes back to the guild that held it, at the Standing, Tithe and Legacy it had before the battle; the walls and works the capture knocked down stand again, and anything the capturer started building falls.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-010","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"After a hold: the holder keeps the seat but loses the Standing and the next-defence bonus the battle gave it, and the challenger's bar from the seat is lifted.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-011","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"Other","x":"Rewards already claimed stay claimed - Honours, silver, Renown and Spoils are never taken back - but no new ones can be claimed from a voided battle.","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-012","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Standing's trend. A seat's board now says which way its holder's Standing moved since the last Turning - \"Standing 55, up 7 since the last Turning.\"","g":["seats","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5625-013","v":"0.1.5625","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Festival","t":"New","x":"A Festival you can hear and see. While a Festival rules in a town, its streets play the tavern's songs, the holder's banners hang at the taverns' doors and over the bounty boards too, and a lantern glows before every banner after dusk.","g":["seats","audio","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5630-001","v":"0.1.5630","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5637-001","v":"0.1.5637","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Glyphs","t":"New","x":"You can now hide your glyphs. Press a glyph on the account card to hide it, and press it again to show it. Other players see the change the next time you enter a new place.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5637-002","v":"0.1.5637","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Glyphs","t":"Other","x":"Hiding a glyph only hides the icon. Anything the glyph lets you do still works.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5637-003","v":"0.1.5637","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"tabbyvish and Starempire42 are now moderators, with the blue shield and /mute and /unmute.","g":["online","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5637-004","v":"0.1.5637","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Mode","t":"Other","x":"Everyone online is disconnected once when this update goes live, and reconnects.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-001","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Text","t":"Rework","x":"Text is easier to read across the Enhanced interface. Letters are drawn slightly heavier and a little further apart, so small text no longer blurs into grey at the edges.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-002","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Text","t":"Rework","x":"No more tiny text. Labels, counts, key hints and badges that were drawn at 9 or 10 pixels are now at least 11, the smallest size the pixel font draws cleanly. That covers the hotbar's key letters (and its stack counts on a phone), the inventory's quickslot marks, the Features rail, the party frames, the chat's tags and times, and the naval HUD.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-003","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Text","t":"Rework","x":"Grey text is brighter. The dim grey used for secondary text (hints, notes, labels, counts) was too dark to read comfortably on the dark panels. It is lighter now, and still clearly quieter than the main text.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-004","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"Every Enhanced screen now uses the Enhanced pixel font (three exceptions below). Several places were still using older fonts:","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-005","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the Features, Overhauls and About pages","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-006","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"character creation's skills and questions","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-007","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the detail lines on an inventory item's card","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-008","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the controller bindings headings and the controller prompt bar","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-009","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the death screen","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-010","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the burning-ground warning at Dagon's Breach","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-011","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the opening film's credits and buttons","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-012","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Rework","x":"the asset pickers (music, sounds, lighting, Morrowind bodies)","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-013","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Fix","x":"Text that was still drawn in the 1996 font under Enhanced is now in the Enhanced font:","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-014","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: in dungeons, a readied spell was named twice, once by the HUD and once by an old line in the classic font. Only the HUD names it now.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-015","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Other","x":"the account recovery code, which has to be copied onto paper exactly - the pixel font draws B and 8, G and 6, and S and 5 too much alike","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-016","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Other","x":"the pages of books, which stay in the readable book serif","g":["books"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-017","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Other","x":"the place names lettered on the map","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-018","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Enhanced Font","t":"Fix","x":"Long labels that had to squeeze into small boxes (the ship's battery counts, party members' locations, the hotbar's key letters on a phone, the accessory shelves) were fitted so the bigger text still fits.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-019","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"A new Timers window, online. An hourglass now sits next to your profile icon on the pause menu. Press it to see every shared event in the world with a live countdown:","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-020","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"Dagon's Breach - when the next one opens, and while one stands, when it seals and when it collapses","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-021","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"Town raids - every raid in your own region, when it starts and when the raiders withdraw, plus the next raid anywhere else and how many more are coming today","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-022","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"The Sunday Turning - the seat week's settlement at Sunday 18:00 UTC, and the Reckoning on Friday 18:00 UTC when pledges lock (for players the guild seats are open to)","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-023","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"This week's battles - every scheduled siege, tourney and revolt, with who is fighting whom, and the Royal Tourney while one runs","g":["seats","siege","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-024","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"The Season's end, when one is under way","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-025","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"The resets - when new bounty hunts and raids roll, and the daily reset at 00:00 UTC","g":["bounty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-026","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"Events running now are listed first with the time until they end; everything else follows, soonest first.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-027","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"Times are shown in your own clock, and the countdowns tick live while the window is open.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5646-028","v":"0.1.5646","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"Tap outside the window or press Escape (or B on a controller) to close it and return to the pause menu.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5656-001","v":"0.1.5656","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"Fix","x":"Voiding a revolt before it is fought no longer saves the Charter. It now lapses, exactly as it would have at the Turning had nobody put the revolt down.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5656-002","v":"0.1.5656","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"Fix","x":"A voided capture gives back the holder's building projects. Anything the defenders were building when their seat fell starts again where it was, with the materials it held taken back from the seat's stockpile - the silver they spent on it is no longer lost. A voided revolt that stood does the same, and brings back the holder's Edict for next week.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5656-003","v":"0.1.5656","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"Fix","x":"A guild that gave up its seat before the siege no longer gets it back from a void. The capturer loses the seat, and it stands unheld, as it did before the battle.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5656-004","v":"0.1.5656","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"Fix","x":"Voiding a held siege fought before this update leaves the holder's Standing alone instead of taking off more than the battle gave.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5656-005","v":"0.1.5656","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Moderation","t":"Fix","x":"A void can no longer land after the Turning. Once a battle's week has been reckoned, /siege void says so: \"That battle's week is settled - its Turning has reckoned it, and it can no longer be voided.\"","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-001","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"New","x":"Friendly ships have green health bars. A merchantman or a crown's ship that isn't after you shows a green bar over her name, and her card reads \"Friendly\" in green. Fire on her, or become wanted enough that her crown's navy hunts you, and she turns hostile - red, as before. Once the blow is forgotten, she's friendly again. A pirate who isn't after you is neither, and a ship that has struck her colours is neither.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-002","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"New","x":"Thousands of ship names. Every ship is named for her trade and her waters: a crown's ships for their kings and queens, their gods and their towns (\"Eadwyre's Fury\", \"The Eagle of Cybiades\"); pirates for beasts, Daedric princes and deeds (\"The Blind Gale\", \"Azura's Grin\", \"The Goldreaver\"); merchantmen for their ports, wares and luck (\"The Menevia Mead\", \"The Patient Wren\"). Every player sees the same ship under the same name.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-003","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ship Tags","t":"New","x":"Where a ship is bound. Within 400 m, a ship's tag shows her class and where she's going - moored at a harbour, leaving it, patrolling off it, bound for the next port, or coming to your aid. The ship card shows the same line, kept to one line.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-004","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Rework","x":"Ships fade in and out. A ship sails into view fading in over a few seconds, and one heading out of range fades away as she sails on, instead of popping in and out. Her shadow, lanterns, deck fires, smoke, wake and flag fade with her.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-005","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Sea","t":"Fix","x":"Online, a ship never blinks. When the player who was sailing a ship moves away, another player near her takes her over where she lies - no fading out and back in on anyone's screen. The same goes for raiders and a port's moored ships.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-006","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"New","x":"Ships sail between the Bay's ports. Packets - merchantmen, and some crown ships - sail lanes between neighbouring port towns, berth, wait a while, and sail on. They keep one shared schedule, so every player meets the same ship in the same water, and the ship you watch leave one port is the one that berths at the next.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-007","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"New","x":"They follow the water round headlands, take a free berth at the harbour, and lie off the port when there's no room. A packet running late sails on as soon as she arrives; one running early waits for her time.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-008","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Other","x":"A packet that is sunk or taken is gone for everyone until her next voyage.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-009","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Other","x":"The Ships at sea setting decides how many are out near you (none when it's off).","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-010","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Fix","x":"Ships no longer stick on World of Daggerfall's ocean rocks. A rock now only stops you sailing into it: you can always sail away from it, rocks behind you no longer hold you to a crawl, and a ship inside a rock pile can get out.","g":["naval","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-011","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Fix","x":"Ships no longer get stuck in place at sea, and the sails work there again. World of Daggerfall's levelling of the ground near a town could lift the sea above the waterline there, leaving a ship beached in open water with her sails refusing to move. The sea now stays at its level. With Iliac Puddle No More on, a boat can't be put in water that is still too high, and you're told why.","g":["naval","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-012","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Fix","x":"A ship run aground can float off again, and backing off a shore now works.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5664-013","v":"0.1.5664","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Crew","t":"Fix","x":"Your crew no longer talks over each other. Lines the whole crew sings or shouts show once; everything else shows under the speaker's name, stacked neatly, never covering a mate's name.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5671-001","v":"0.1.5671","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Basket","t":"Fix","x":"The mouse cursor now appears for the Basket's search. The glints show around the crosshair, not on it. Before, moving the mouse toward one turned your view, and the glint moved with it, so you couldn't click it. Now the cursor is free while you search, and your view stays still. Click a glint while it shows to find it. The hint under the crosshair now says \"click the glint\".","g":["foraging","herbalism"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5671-002","v":"0.1.5671","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Basket","t":"Fix","x":"When the search ends, however it ends, the mouse goes back to looking around. If you end it with Escape, the look comes back when you let go of the key, and holding Escape no longer opens the pause menu as well.","g":["foraging","herbalism"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5671-003","v":"0.1.5671","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Basket","t":"Other","x":"Clicking anywhere while a glint shows still counts, so your attack key, a controller's trigger and a tap on a phone work as before. With a controller in hand, the mouse pointer stays hidden.","g":["foraging","herbalism"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5671-004","v":"0.1.5671","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Basket","t":"Other","x":"With Gentle acts on, the search has nothing to press, so the cursor isn't freed and the hint says \"searching...\".","g":["foraging","herbalism"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5671-005","v":"0.1.5671","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Basket","t":"Fix","x":"No second harvest after the search. Letting go of the click that found the last glint could start picking the same patch's herbs straight away, and wear your Sickle. It doesn't any more.","g":["foraging","herbalism"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5671-006","v":"0.1.5671","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gathering","t":"Fix","x":"Mining, Skinning and Fishing take the look back. You aim these with the crosshair: the rock's strike points, the cutting line on the body, and where your net lands (a school of fish under it means a bigger catch). If you had freed the mouse (the Free Mouse key, Y by default; offline, Enter too) before you started, the look now comes back so you can aim, and stays back afterwards.","g":["mining","hunting","fishing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-001","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Elite and Champion foes (level 3+) that kill you become your revenant. They get a name of their own and an epithet for what they did, e.g. \"Grushnak the Butcher\" or \"Varis, Bane of Ayla\".","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-002","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"They can also run. Below 20% health, a special foe has a small chance (5%) to break and flee. If it gets away, it becomes a revenant too (\"the Scarred\", \"Who Ran\").","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-003","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"They come back. One to three in-game days later, a revenant can turn up in place of a wilderness encounter. Only one comes at a time, the strongest first.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-004","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Stronger every time. Each time a revenant kills you or escapes, it ranks up (up to rank 5) and earns a new epithet. Each rank adds health (+25%) and damage (+10%). Human foes also gain levels.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-005","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Stronger every time. Each time a revenant kills you or escapes, it ranks up (up to rank 5) and earns a new epithet. Each rank adds health (+25%) and damage (+10%). Human foes also gain levels.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-006","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Spells and poison count. A foe whose spell, lingering effect or poisoned blade finishes you becomes your revenant just like one that cuts you down.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-007","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"They remember even if you reload. Revenants are tied to your character and survive an offline death or loading an older save. Up to 5 can hunt you at once.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-008","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Other","x":"Revenants follow the Loot rarity setting. Turn it off and no new ones are made.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-009","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Every revenant has a personality that shapes everything it says: Brutal, Witty, Humorous, Arrogant, Cold, Zealous, Unhinged, Honourable, Craven or Weary.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-010","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A revenant keeps its personality for good. What it is leans who it is: orcs tend brutal, liches cold, daedra arrogant, and a person can be anything.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-011","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Every moment has its own lines in each voice: the taunt when it returns (different if it killed you, if it ran from you, or if it has come back three times), breaking to flee, being cornered, escaping, its last words, its gloat after killing you, begging or defying you when beaten, its last words before an execution, its oath when spared, and its words as your companion.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-012","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Beasts don't talk. Their temperament shows in what they do instead (\"Sinks low before you with a nervous whine, beaten\").","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-013","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"The card and the Revenants page show each revenant's personality.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-014","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A beaten revenant yields instead of dying. It drops to its knees at the edge of death, says its piece in its own voice, and waits for your judgement. Nothing can hurt it while it kneels, and other foes leave it alone.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-015","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Walk up to it and use it to choose its fate. The choice opens in the loot window, with its name, its plea and two choices:","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-016","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Kill. This shows the exact weapon it will drop.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-017","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Spare. This says where it will go: to your side, or away if your companion slots are full.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-018","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Click a choice, then confirm it. You can also press K or S, then K/S again or Enter. Esc backs out of a pick, or closes the window and leaves it kneeling.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-019","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Don't take too long. If you leave it kneeling for 90 seconds, or walk away, it slips away. That counts as an escape: it ranks up, and it remembers your hesitation. The wait pauses while its window is open.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-020","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Other","x":"A flying revenant kneels on the ground, so you can always reach it.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-021","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Choosing Kill plays an execution. 1. It says its last words and the blow lands. 2. Blood bursts out with a flash and the screen shakes. 3. Its body burns away in embers from the feet up until nothing is left.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-022","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"It counts as your kill: Renown, and a soul for a Soul Trap or Azura's Star.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-023","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"It drops a unique weapon of its own, plus everything it carried, in a pile where it knelt:","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-024","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"The right weapon for it. It's the weapon it fought with, or one that fits what it was: an orc's axe, a lich's staff, a vampire's saber, a barbarian's claymore, an assassin's tanto.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-025","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Named for it, e.g. \"Grushnak's Reaver\" or \"Varis' Requiem\".","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-026","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A random rarity, never Common: Magic, Rare or Legendary. The higher its rank, the better the odds.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-027","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"An executed revenant is gone for good. The Revenants page lists it among the Fallen as \"Executed\".","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-028","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Choosing Spare frees it and swears it to you. It rises, steps into a portal and joins you as a companion. It never hunts you again.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-029","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Sworn revenants use the same companion system as your crew. They follow you through every door and into buildings and dungeons, fight at your side, and keep up with you. Their health and spells carry over between places.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-030","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"They fight with the strength of their rank and go by their own names.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-031","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Use one to open its pack and store items.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-032","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Each has a card on the party panel and a green health bar overhead.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-033","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Companion slots are limited: 3 at your side, shared between sworn revenants and any ship's crew you've brought ashore. If your slots are full when you spare one, it waits away until you call it. If loading a game ever puts more than 3 at your side, the most recently sworn steps away. You can have up to 6 sworn revenants in total.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-034","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"Other","x":"Companion slots are limited: 3 at your side, shared between sworn revenants and any ship's crew you've brought ashore. If your slots are full when you spare one, it waits away until you call it. If loading a game ever puts more than 3 at your side, the most recently sworn steps away. You can have up to 6 sworn revenants in total.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-035","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Knocked out, not killed. A companion that falls is carried off through a portal to recover for 8 hours, then waits for your call.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-036","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"A new Companions page (pause menu, Stats rail):","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-037","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"At your side. Each companion's portrait, rank, personality and health, with Send away.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-038","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Away. Companions waiting or recovering, with Call. If it can't come yet (your slots are full, or it's still hurt), it tells you why.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-039","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Release frees a companion for good and hands you back its pack. It asks you to confirm first.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-040","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"They talk in their own voice: when they arrive, when sent away or released, when they fall, and now and then when they charge into a fight or finish a foe.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-041","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Companions no longer pop in and out. They step through a swirling violet portal:","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-042","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"when they catch up to you after falling behind, through a pair of portals (one where they were, one where they reappear).","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-043","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"The figure gathers out of the light as it arrives and burns into it as it leaves. This applies to your ship's crew ashore too.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-044","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"In online play, other players see your beaten revenant kneel, burn away when you execute it, or step into its portal when you spare it. The choice is yours alone.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-045","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Other players see your revenant by its name.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-046","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Nothing can hit a kneeling revenant: no weapon, arrow or spell. Before, your weapon's poison and life drain still applied, and it trained your skills.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-047","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A revenant you've judged can't come back. If its poison killed you after you executed or spared it, it no longer rose again or ranked up.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-048","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Saving while a revenant stands no longer leaves a nameless copy of it behind.","g":["revenants","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-049","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Dungeon saves: a revenant that escaped, was executed or was spared no longer leaves a lootable corpse after a load.","g":["revenants","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-050","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Companion packs follow your save: loading no longer duplicates or loses the items you gave them.","g":["companions","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-051","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A spared revenant no longer appears twice for a moment while it steps into its portal.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-052","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Spells a companion carried (like a poison) no longer come back with it after it recovers, is sent away, or you load.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-053","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"The Execute button and confirmed Release are edged in red. The kill choice shows the weapon's card on hover. The window fits on phones.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-054","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Rendering: fixed a bug where every sprite could vanish after an execution in a dungeon. Elite glow no longer hangs in the air while an elite revenant burns away. A burning or arriving body no longer casts a full shadow.","g":["revenants","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-055","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Words: a revenant that only ever ran no longer boasts about how often it killed you. Skeletons, zombies and atronachs are no longer \"Witty\". Every personality has more lines.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-056","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"Elites are rarer. In the open world, 2% of foes (was 5%), and only one at a time: none while another elite is nearby, and none for about 15 minutes of play (3 in-game hours) after the last. A camp or a pack never brings more than one. Ordinary dungeons hold one 10% of the time (was 20%). Elite Dungeons keep their 3 to 4.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-057","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"Elites no longer appear below foe level 3, and never as city watch or allies (same rules as Champions).","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-058","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"Elites are named everywhere: on hover, in death notices and on their corpses, not just the target bar. Champions, elites and revenants are now named on hover even while hostile.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-059","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Other","x":"The cards, the kill-or-spare window and the Companions page are Enhanced UI. On the Classic skin, the cards appear as text and the choice is a keyed box (K, S, Esc).","g":["revenants","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-060","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Revenants","t":"Other","x":"The revenant card is a HUD piece like any other: unlock the UI (Alt+U) to move it.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5689-061","v":"0.1.5689","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Paperdoll","t":"Fix","x":"Firefox no longer shows the paperdoll mirrored over the stats. Under the pack's blurred backdrop Firefox could lose the card's 3D turn and draw both faces at once. In Firefox alone, the face turned away is now hidden at the exact moment the card is edge-on (about a quarter of a second into the turn), so you never see either side from behind. Other browsers are unchanged, and reduced motion keeps its crossfade.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-001","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"No quest fails because time ran out online. \"You have 14 days\", travel-time limits, \"return before the time is up\" - none of them run out. Take as long as you like; the quest waits for you.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-002","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"No more waiting days for the story to move. A step that would make you wait days - a letter that arrives later, a contact who will see you in a few days, a reward paid after a wait - now moves on after about two minutes of play. This includes Lady Brisienna's invitation and every main quest letter.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-003","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Finished quests close sooner. A quest that wraps up a while after you finish it (once you are paid, or once the next part of the story begins) now closes within a couple of minutes.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-004","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Quest text no longer counts days online. Lines like \"you have 7 days\" now read \"you have a few days\".","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-005","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"No countdowns online. The journal, the quest tracker, the quest rail and the map markers no longer show \"Time remains\", and you no longer get \"running out of time\" warnings.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-006","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Quest letters reach you any time of day online. They still wait until you are in a town, but no longer wait for morning.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-007","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Bounties","t":"Rework","x":"Bounties never lapse online. A bounty you take stays yours until you finish it or drop it.","g":["bounty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-008","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Vampire and werewolf quests come sooner online. Clan quests and the cure quests no longer wait 38 or 84 game days. Online they come after a few minutes of play (a cure can take ten or so), one at a time.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-009","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"The Thieves Guild and Dark Brotherhood invitations come sooner online. They now arrive a couple of minutes after you earn them, not three days later.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-010","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Quests","t":"Other","x":"A few quests still follow day and night online. They have someone at a certain place at night or during the day, or guard a hall for a few hours. The day and night cycle online lasts about an hour.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-011","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Weapons and armour last twice as long. Wear per hit is back to Daggerfall's own rate. The last update doubled wear, and a dagger or short bow broke after about 25 hits; it now lasts about 50, and every other piece lasts twice as long as it did. Repairs cost the same.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5694-012","v":"0.1.5694","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Weapons and armour last twice as long. Wear per hit is back to Daggerfall's own rate. The last update doubled wear, and a dagger or short bow broke after about 25 hits; it now lasts about 50, and every other piece lasts twice as long as it did. Repairs cost the same.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5698-001","v":"0.1.5698","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Paint your hall. A guild's Officers and its guildmaster can now choose the hall's outside - its walls, windows, roof and door - from the Exterior tab of the yard's decorator, just as you paint your own home. It costs nothing, and everyone walking past sees it.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5698-002","v":"0.1.5698","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Furnish its yard. Stand on the hall's lot and press Decorate: the same catalogue as a home's yard, up to sixty pieces, each paid in gold by whoever places it (from their purse, then the region's bank).","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5698-003","v":"0.1.5698","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"The guild gets the half back. Take a yard piece down, or shrink it, and half of what it cost goes into the guild's treasury - never into the pocket of whoever took it down. Sell the hall and its yard goes with it, half of each piece's cost paid back to the treasury along with the hall's own share.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5698-004","v":"0.1.5698","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Other","x":"Members and visitors look, they don't touch. Ranks below Officer, and anyone outside the guild, see the hall's colours and its yard but cannot change them.","g":["guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5701-001","v":"0.1.5701","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-001","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Door Griefing","t":"Fix","x":"Foes no longer stand in doorways. Guards and enemies step off a door's threshold and out of its mouth, so a crowd can't seal a building or a dungeon door.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-002","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Door Griefing","t":"Fix","x":"Clicking a door works even with a guard in front of it. If you're aiming at a door, a peaceful guard standing in the way no longer eats the click. Hostile foes still take it, so you can always swing at someone attacking you.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-003","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Door Griefing","t":"Fix","x":"The indoor watch spawns inside, spread out. Guards called into an interior appear past the threshold and spaced apart, instead of stacked on the door.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-004","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Foes","t":"Fix","x":"Foes are aware of each other. Guards, bandits, dungeon foes and wilderness encounters now push apart across groups, so mixed crowds no longer stand inside one another.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-005","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cover","t":"New","x":"Trees, crates, barrels, statues and solid decor block sight. A foe can't see you through a tree trunk or a stack of crates.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-006","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cover","t":"New","x":"They also stop missiles, both ways. Your arrows and bolts hit the cover, and so do theirs. Area spells still burst where they land.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-007","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Cover","t":"Other","x":"Grass, flowers, small clutter and see-through props aren't cover. Felled trees stop being cover.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-008","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tactics","t":"New","x":"Attack turns. At most two melee foes and two ranged foes attack you at once. The rest hold a ring around you, circle and wait their turn.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-009","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tactics","t":"New","x":"Knowing when to strike. Melee foes step in when you're open (after your swing, while casting, drinking, turned away or staggered) and back out after their own blow. A patience clock means nobody waits forever.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-010","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tactics","t":"New","x":"Backing off. A hurt foe gives ground and circles before coming back.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-011","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tactics","t":"New","x":"Fleeing. Animals and cowardly people run at low health. Guards, undead, daedra and constructs never do.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-012","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tactics","t":"New","x":"Archers and casters keep their distance. They back away from a closing melee fighter, fight when cornered, and look for a clear shot instead of firing into a crate.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-013","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Tactics","t":"Other","x":"Applies everywhere (dungeons, streets, interiors and guards) when Enhanced AI is on. With it off, foes behave exactly as in classic Daggerfall.","g":["enhanced-ai","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-014","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Tougher foes have a special attack with a wind-up, like the world boss's but smaller: level 10 and up, or elite foes.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-015","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Lunge: a long lane ahead (beasts, swordsmen).","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-016","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Sweep: a wide cone in front (brutes, blades).","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-017","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Slam: a disc just ahead (giants, atronachs, daedra lords).","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-018","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Readable and dodgeable. The shape glows dim on the ground through a short wind-up (0.7 to 0.9 s) and flashes when it lands. Step out of it and it misses. A hit does 1.25x to 1.75x a normal blow.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-019","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Readable and dodgeable. The shape glows dim on the ground through a short wind-up (0.7 to 0.9 s) and flashes when it lands. Step out of it and it misses. A hit does 1.25x to 1.75x a normal blow.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-020","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Used sparingly. Each foe has a cooldown of 8 to 15 seconds, and only one foe near you winds up at a time. Casters, spirits, small and flying foes don't use them.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-021","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"The ground marks follow slopes and fade into fog.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-022","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Sigil Broker is now held prisoner by Dagon's Faithful. She waits in a cage at the faithful's rite circle, near the breach, from the omen at 17:00.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-023","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Kill every one of the faithful, including the Summoner, to free her. You have to do it before the breach opens at 20:00. When the last of them falls, her cage door swings open for everyone online.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-024","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"If someone else already killed the Summoner, killing the rest still frees her.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-025","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"You can talk to her from any side of the cage.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-026","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"If the faithful are still standing when the breach opens, they pass into it and she stays caged for the night.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-027","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Once freed, she trades until midnight, even if the Warden falls early and the breach collapses.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5719-028","v":"0.1.5719","d":"2026-10-02","e":"Online Mode","t":"Other","x":"Everyone online is disconnected once when this update goes live, and reconnects.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-001","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Ship Tags","t":"Fix","x":"Ship name tags no longer pile up. Off a busy harbour, every ship's tag used to sit on top of the others. Now no tag is drawn over another: the ship you're looking at, then hostile ships, then the nearest ones get their tags first, and a tag with no room waits until there's space for it.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-002","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Fix","x":"Other players' AI ships sail smoothly. Online, ships run by another player's game jumped forward, sped up to more than twice their real speed and sometimes slid backwards, whenever the network was a little slow or quick. They now keep sailing at their own speed and catch up gently.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-003","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Ship Tags","t":"Rework","x":"Only one ship shows its second line (its class and where it's headed). That's the ship whose card is up, or else the one nearest your crosshair. Look at a ship to read it; the rest show just their name and health bar.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-004","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Travel Options","t":"Fix","x":"Changing the Travel Options settings now takes effect straight away. You no longer need to relog. Turn off the first dial, Player Controlled Cautious Travel, and a trip with Cautiously picked uses Daggerfall's fast travel the next time you open the map. The same goes for Only From Ports, Location Pause, Avoid Obstacles and the Acceleration Limit. A few things still wait for the next load: turning the whole mod on or off, its roads and junction-map options, and paid teleportation.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-005","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Travel Options","t":"New","x":"New dial: Player Controlled Inns Travel. It sits under the cautious one in Features > Travel Options. With it on (the default), any trip that stops at inns is a journey you travel, including reckless ones. Turn it off and a trip that stops at inns uses fast travel. Reckless trips where you camp out are always journeys you travel, as in the original mod.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-006","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"HUD","t":"Fix","x":"The lost part of the fatigue, health and magicka bars is faint now. When a bar drops, the part you just lost used to show as a pale, almost white strip. On the fatigue bar it looked like fatigue you still had. Now it's a dim strip of the bar's own colour.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-007","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"HUD","t":"Fix","x":"That strip no longer gets stuck. If a bar kept dropping a little at a time, such as fatigue during a long fight, the strip stayed at your starting level for the whole fight. Now it stays for at most about a second before catching up.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-008","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Loading","t":"Fix","x":"Pressing a key while the world loads no longer shows a red crash message. A volume key, F11, a gamepad button or anything else pressed during the loading screen used to put up an error that stayed for the whole session. Keys pressed during loading are now ignored until the world is ready.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-009","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Swimming","t":"Fix","x":"Sinking into water no longer puts your view under the ground. In water your view was only 0.2 m above your feet, and the bobbing while swimming took it lower still. In a moat, at a dock or by the shore you could end up looking at the underside of the ground, with the sky showing beneath you. Your view now sits where Daggerfall puts it, about half a metre above your feet.","g":["water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5723-010","v":"0.1.5723","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Sprites","t":"Fix","x":"Likely fix for dark boxes around sprites on Macs with Apple chips. A change in the last update could draw a dark outline around people, enemies and other sprites on some graphics chips, and the texture filter setting didn't help. The sprite shader now reads its textures in a way every graphics chip handles the same. We couldn't test on an Apple chip ourselves, so if you still see the boxes, please tell us on the Discord.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-001","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Fix","x":"Walk up to a foe and it fights you. A foe waiting for its turn used to back away as you came closer, so you could chase it around the room. Now it turns and fights.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-002","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Rework","x":"The step back after a blow is short. A foe that just hit you steps back for a moment (under half a second) and then holds its ground. Chase it and it fights back.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-003","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Fix","x":"Retreating foes walk away facing the way they're going. A hurt foe backing off, or an archer making room, turns around and walks off, then turns back to fight. No more moonwalking.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-004","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Rework","x":"Hurt foes back off less often. At most once every 10 seconds.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-005","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Fix","x":"No more circling. An archer waiting for its turn to shoot stands still and faces you. It doesn't strafe around you.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-006","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Rework","x":"One retreat, then it fights. An archer you close in on walks back once, for up to 2 seconds. If you catch it, or it backs into a wall, it fights you hand to hand. It won't retreat again for 8 seconds.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5727-007","v":"0.1.5727","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Rework","x":"Once you're more than about 6 m away again, it goes back to shooting.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-001","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Champions","t":"Rework","x":"Champions are a little more common. About 7% of foes of level 3 or more now stand as a champion (it was 5%) - roughly one in fourteen, up from one in twenty. Every champion that stood before still stands where it did; this only adds more.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-002","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Crosshair","t":"Rework","x":"Special foes are no longer named at the crosshair. A hostile champion, elite or revenant shows no tooltip when you look at it, the same as any other foe. Its name and its trait (\"Mighty Orc\", \"Elite Orc\") appear on its health bar once you strike it.","g":["elites","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-003","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Crosshair","t":"Other","x":"A special foe that isn't fighting you is still named at the crosshair as before: a sworn companion by its own name, and a beaten revenant still reads \"- beaten\" so you know to go and judge it.","g":["elites","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-004","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"Elites are back to their old numbers. The last change made them rarer; that's undone.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-005","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"In the open world, 5% of foes stand as elites again (it had been cut to 2%). There's no longer a limit of one at a time or a wait after the last one, so a camp or a pack can bring more than one, and a summoned squad can too.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-006","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"Ordinary dungeons hold an elite 20% of the time again (it had been cut to 10%). Elite Dungeons keep their 3 to 4.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5732-007","v":"0.1.5732","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Champions","t":"Other","x":"Champions are unchanged (they were never made rarer): about one foe in twenty of level 3 or more.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-001","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"New","x":"The alchemy station. Brew potions at any Alchemist's shop (50 gold a brew), or at the alchemy station in your own home. Open your Stores page: The Alchemy Station lists Daggerfall's own twenty potions and what each needs. Your potions go to your pack, and they are Daggerfall's own potions - they stack, drink and sell as any other.","g":["alchemy","crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-002","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"New","x":"Your ingredients come from your Stores: herbs you picked, metals and gems from the veins, the Pearl from the sea, a body's parts from Hunting. The rest - Werewolf's Blood, Fairy Dragon's Scales, Unicorn Horn, Ectoplasm, Troll's Blood, Snake Venom, Mummy Wrappings, Saint's Hair, Small Tooth, Pure Water, Rain Water, Orc's Blood, Elixir Vitae, Nectar, Ichor and Ivory - are sold at the new Apothecaries' counter on the Notice Board's Market tab, beside the Weavers', and at the station whenever a recipe is short of one (1 to 40 silver a measure).","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-003","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy","t":"New","x":"Ranks by price: the cheapest potions (Orc Strength, Stamina, Healing, Water Walking) from rank 0, the resistances and Restore Power from 10, up to Invisibility at 70 and Purification at 90.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-004","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"New","x":"More potions as you rise: one a brew, two from Journeyman, three as a Master. A potion made only of the Apothecaries' goods (Water Breathing, Levitation) brews one at any rank, and the station says so.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-005","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"New","x":"Potent potions. A brew may come out Potent, and named so (\"Potent Potion of Healing\"). A healing, stamina, strength or power potion gets +25% to its magnitude; every other potion - the resistances, Slow Falling, Water Breathing, Chameleon Form, Invisibility, Shadow Form, Free Action, Levitation and Water Walking - lasts 25% longer instead (and a resistance is that much likelier to take). Cure Disease and Cure Poison are never Potent - they act at once, and the station says so; Purification can be. Your rank's own chance starts at Expert - 10% at Expert, 20% at Master - and at any rank +5% for each herb you picked unbruised with the Sickle's steady hand (an unbruised herb you withdraw, sell or spend elsewhere takes its +5% with it), +10% for a Distiller, and +10% for each tier of the Apothecary in the town you brew in, where your guild holds it - the station's chance counts it. A Potent potion stacks only with Potent ones, keeps its own quick slot apart from the plain ones, and is worth a quarter more.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-006","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy","t":"New","x":"XP comes with every brew by the potion's rank, and +500 the first time you brew each one (not for a potion made only of the Apothecaries' goods).","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-007","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"Other","x":"Daggerfall's potion maker (with the ingredients in your pack) is unchanged, and still earns nothing toward Alchemy.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-008","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Brewer","t":"New","x":"Brewer (50): three potions a brew at Journeyman.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-009","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Distiller","t":"New","x":"Distiller (50): +10% Potent chance.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-010","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Master Alchemist","t":"New","x":"Master Alchemist (100): Potent potions are +40% (stronger or longer), not +25%.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-011","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Transmuter","t":"New","x":"Transmuter (100): at the alchemy station, turn two of a metal and a Mercury into one of the next up - Tin to Copper, Copper to Silver, Silver to Gold, Gold to Platinum.","g":["alchemy","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-012","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enchanting","t":"Economy","x":"Cheaper enchanting. The item maker now costs less gold as your Enchanting rises: 10% off from Journeyman, 20% as a Master, and the Efficient specialisation takes 5% more.","g":["enchanting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-013","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Efficient","t":"New","x":"Cheaper enchanting. The item maker now costs less gold as your Enchanting rises: 10% off from Journeyman, 20% as a Master, and the Efficient specialisation takes 5% more.","g":["enchanting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-014","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Disenchanting","t":"New","x":"Disenchanting. At an enchanting station - a Mages Guild hall (50 gold a piece) or the enchanting station in your own home - a crafted piece in your pack comes apart into Arcane Essence in your Stores: one for every 100 enchantment points it carried (a Gold Ruby Ring gives 21). Press twice: the piece is gone. Only a piece a crafter made online can be disenchanted - never loot, nor arrows. A Disenchanter gets twice the Essence. The button stays shut when your Stores have no room for the Essence. A piece made with goods bought at a counter is a bought piece: its Essence is bought too.","g":["enchanting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-015","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enchanting","t":"New","x":"Enchanting XP comes from every piece you disenchant, by the piece's own tier - a quarter for a piece far below your rank, and none for a piece made only of the Weavers' Linen and Wool.","g":["enchanting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-016","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arcane Essence","t":"New","x":"Arcane Essence stays in your Stores - it never goes to your pack - and sells on the market like any Stores material.","g":["enchanting","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-017","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Market","t":"Rework","x":"A crafted piece made with any goods bought at a counter with silver now sells only for silver, as those goods do - from another player's pack too.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-018","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"A piece you auctioned, or bid on, stays in My listings after its owner disenchants it.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-019","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Market","t":"Rework","x":"Alchemy's reagents no longer list on the market from your pack. The sixteen reagents the Apothecaries sell - Unicorn Horn, Saint's Hair, Ectoplasm and the rest - are Stores materials now, and the market's \"goods from your pack\" refuses a Stores material, as it always has: one taken out of the Stores cannot be told from one you looted, so a looted Unicorn Horn is refused too. Daggerfall's own shops still buy them.","g":["market","alchemy"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-020","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"Cook at any fire. Stand by a lit fire - a campfire (yours or anyone's), a hearth or a brazier, in the wilds, a town, a building or a dungeon - and open your Stores page: The Fire lists what you can cook. No fee. Your dishes go to your pack.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-021","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"Hunter's Stew (from rank 0): 2 Raw Meat, 1 Mushroom, 1 Root Bulb. Endurance +5 for 2 hours.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-022","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"Fisherman's Supper (from rank 0): 2 Raw Fish, 1 Egg, 1 Green Leaves. Agility +5 for 2 hours.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-023","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"Orchard Tart (from rank 10): 2 Apples, 1 Egg, 1 Yellow Berries. Your stamina lasts a fifth longer for 4 hours.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-024","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"Feast of the Hearth (from rank 70): 4 Raw Meat, 4 Raw Fish, 2 Apples, 2 Oranges, 2 Mushrooms, 2 Eggs. Strength, Endurance and Willpower +5 for a whole day - for you and every party member in your area.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-025","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"Other","x":"Northern and southern herbs both work.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-026","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"The pan. Each dish is cooked in three pans (a feast five). Each pan heats from raw to burnt - take it off while it is in the window (Space, Enter or the button). Take every pan off at the right moment for a clean dish and half again the XP. A Skillet in your pack widens the window. Quick cook skips it.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-027","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"Eating a dish fills you up like a meal (with Climates & Calories on) and gives its bonus. Eating the same dish again refreshes the bonus - it does not stack. Dishes spoil like other food.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-028","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"New","x":"XP follows your rank, and you get +500 the first time you cook each dish - once a dish, whichever herb (northern or southern) you cook it with.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-029","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Market","t":"New","x":"Dishes sell on the market (a new Dishes category) and can be asked for in commissions.","g":["cooking","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-030","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cook","t":"New","x":"Cook (50): every dish makes two servings.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-031","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Field Cook","t":"New","x":"Field Cook (50): lighting a Campfire Kit uses none of its charges.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-032","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Chef","t":"New","x":"Chef (100): your feasts last half again - a day and a half, for whoever eats them.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-033","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Provisioner","t":"New","x":"Provisioner (100): your dishes, and the food you take out of your Stores, never spoil.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-034","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"The Professions page lists Cooking as practised.","g":["cooking","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-035","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"Other","x":"Cooking a Raw Fish over a fire from your pack still works as before - it is a plain meal and gives no Cooking XP.","g":["cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-036","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Feast","t":"Fix","x":"A feast shared by a party member now refreshes yours instead of stacking. If you've eaten a feast, one shared with you replaces its bonus, the same as eating it again.","g":["cooking","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-037","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Provisioner","t":"Fix","x":"Food that is both a Butcher's and a Provisioner's never spoils. It used to spoil at the Butcher's half pace.","g":["cooking","hunting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-038","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Apothecary","t":"Fix","x":"The Apothecary's line on the Seat tab now says what each tier does: jewellery a quality step better, dishes half again the XP, and brews +10% Potent chance (at tier 2: two steps, twice the XP, +20%).","g":["seats","cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-039","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Feast","t":"Fix","x":"A feast only comes from your party. A feast cast at you by a player outside your party is ignored - it used to add its whole day onto the one you had.","g":["cooking","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-040","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Feast","t":"Fix","x":"A shorter feast never cuts a longer one short. If the feast you have has more time left (a Chef's day and a half), eating or being shared a plain one leaves it as it is.","g":["cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-041","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Feast","t":"Fix","x":"A feast is shared with the party members at the table, the ones you can see - not party members elsewhere in the town.","g":["cooking","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-042","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Orchard Tart","t":"Fix","x":"The Orchard Tart's stamina can be ended from the buff row, like every other dish.","g":["cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-043","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Cooking","t":"Fix","x":"The fire's XP line counts the town's Apothecary where your guild holds the town, so it shows the XP you actually get.","g":["cooking","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-044","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Crafting","t":"Fix","x":"Pressing Brew while another craft is under way now says your hands are busy with another craft (it said your last brew was still in the cauldron).","g":["alchemy","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-045","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Feast","t":"Fix","x":"Only a real feast counts as a feast. A spell that is merely named \"Feast of the Hearth\" - one a party member cast at you, or one of your own - no longer replaces your feast or stops you from eating one.","g":["cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-046","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Feast","t":"Fix","x":"Eating a feast while a longer one is still on you now says so (\"The feast you already enjoy lasts longer.\") - your party still gets it.","g":["cooking","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-047","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"The jeweller's bench. Make jewellery at any Pawn Shop or Gem Store (50 gold a piece), or at a jeweller's bench in your own home (a new home station, 50,000 gold). Open your Stores page: The Jeweller's Bench lists what you can make. Your pieces go to your pack.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-048","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Eight pieces - Daggerfall's own rings, marks, bracelets, bracers, amulets, torcs, cloth amulets and wands:","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-049","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Ring: 1 Silver, Gold or Platinum, and a gem if you like.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-050","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Mark: 1 metal and 1 gem.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-051","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Bracelet: 2 metal.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-052","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Bracer: 2 metal and 1 Cured Leather.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-053","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Amulet: 2 metal and 1 gem.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-054","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Torc: 3 metal.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-055","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Cloth Amulet: 1 Linen and 1 gem.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-056","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Wand: 2 Ironwood or Ghostwood Planks and 1 gem.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-057","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"The gems are the eight a vein gives (Ruby, Emerald, Sapphire, Diamond, Jade, Turquoise, Malachite, Amber) and the sea's Pearl.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-058","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Ranks: Silver pieces and Cloth Amulets from rank 0, Gold from 25, Platinum from 55, Wands from 70.","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-059","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Enchantment points. A crafted piece holds more than a found one: Gold +10%, Platinum +20%, and +10% for a set gem. The item maker reads them when you enchant it. A gemmed piece is worth its gem as well.","g":["jewelcrafting","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-060","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"Quality. Pieces come Crude to Masterwork, as smithing does - a Superior or a Masterwork rolls a magic property, and a Masterwork carries your name.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-061","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"The facet. Each piece is cut in three facets (five with a gem). The stone turns slowly along the dial - stop it where it catches the light (Space, Enter or the button). Catch every facet for a clean piece, one quality step better. Willpower and Luck widen the window; so does your rank. Quick craft skips it.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-062","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"The facet. Each piece is cut in three facets (five with a gem). The stone turns slowly along the dial - stop it where it catches the light (Space, Enter or the button). Catch every facet for a clean piece, one quality step better. Willpower and Luck widen the window; so does your rank. Quick craft skips it.","g":["jewelcrafting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-063","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"New","x":"XP comes with every piece by its tier, and +500 the first time you make each piece of each metal or wood (a Gold Ring once, whichever gem you set).","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-064","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Market","t":"New","x":"Jewellery sells on the market (a new Jewellery category), goes to auction as a Masterwork, and can be asked for in commissions.","g":["jewelcrafting","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-065","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gemcutter","t":"New","x":"Gemcutter (50): a set gem adds +20% enchantment points, not +10%.","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-066","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Goldsmith","t":"New","x":"Goldsmith (50): your Silver pieces hold Gold's points and worth.","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-067","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Master Jeweller","t":"New","x":"Master Jeweller (100): Masterwork chance +5%.","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-068","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Lapidary","t":"New","x":"Lapidary (100): set a Siege-cracked Gem (a Spoil of War) as any gem the piece asks for.","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-069","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"Other","x":"What a Gemcutter or a Goldsmith gave a piece stays with it, whoever owns it.","g":["jewelcrafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-070","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"The Professions page lists Jewelcrafting as practised.","g":["jewelcrafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-071","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enchanting","t":"Fix","x":"A Masterwork piece can now be enchanted further. Its magic property used to keep it out of the item maker, so its points went unused. The item maker now takes any piece you crafted along with the enchantment it already has. That enchantment stays on the piece and cannot be removed, and its cost counts against the piece's points. You can add more enchantments while the total fits. Other enchanted items are still refused, as in Daggerfall.","g":["jewelcrafting","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-072","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enchanting","t":"Fix","x":"A piece's enchantment points can't go past what its recipe makes. A tampered piece no longer brings an impossible budget to the item maker.","g":["jewelcrafting","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-073","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"Fix","x":"A Masterwork piece's own enchantment now always fits its points. A small piece (a Cloth Amulet, a Mark) could roll an enchantment that cost more than the piece holds, leaving nothing to spend - it now rolls one that fits.","g":["jewelcrafting","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-074","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Enchanting","t":"Fix","x":"The Enhanced+ item maker shows a crafted piece's own enchantment at the top of its list, greyed out, as the classic window does. Before, it was invisible though its cost still counted.","g":["jewelcrafting","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-075","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"Fix","x":"The bench no longer promises a Wand a Masterwork enchantment - Wands do not roll one.","g":["jewelcrafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-076","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Jewelcrafting","t":"Fix","x":"A piece remembers the jeweller's hand that made it (a Goldsmith's Silver, a Gemcutter's gem), so its points are capped at its own recipe's, not at the most any jeweller could have given it.","g":["jewelcrafting","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-077","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Apothecary","t":"New","x":"The Apothecary can be raised. A seat's holder can now build the Apothecary from the seat's board, as any other work (tier 1: 100 Cut Stone, 100 Oak Planks and 1,000 silver from the treasury; tier 2: 200 Cut Stone, 20 Pearls and 2,500 silver). It waited on Alchemy, Cooking and Jewelcrafting - all three are open now.","g":["seats","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-078","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Apothecary","t":"New","x":"Jewelcrafting: a piece comes one quality step better - as the Forge does for a smith.","g":["seats","jewelcrafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-079","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Apothecary","t":"New","x":"Cooking: a dish takes no quality, so the step is in the cooking: half again the Cooking XP of the dish (a clean pan in a tier 2 Apothecary's town earns two and a half times the plain dish's).","g":["seats","cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-080","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Apothecary","t":"New","x":"Alchemy: +10% chance a brew comes out Potent.","g":["seats","alchemy"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-081","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Apothecary","t":"Other","x":"Only the holding guild's members get it, and only in that town.","g":["seats","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-082","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"Your home beside your guild's hall opens the right yard. If you own a home and keep the guild hall next door, Decorate now opens the yard you are standing in - the one whose building is nearest - instead of whichever the town happened to list first.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-083","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"\"Your guild's hall is painted.\" Painting the hall and walking off before the answer came back no longer says \"Your house\"; and if the paint fails, it says the hall could not be painted.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-084","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"A promotion or demotion reaches the hall sooner. Made an Officer (or no longer one), the hall's decorator follows as soon as the game next reads your guild - opening the Guild tab, for one, or walking up to the hall's door - instead of up to a minute after that.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-085","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"Only characters who can decorate the hall get its decorator. An Officer playing a local (offline) character is no longer shown a hall's yard decorator whose every piece would be refused.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-086","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Other","x":"...but they still choose who may enter. That Officer's hall door still offers Who may enter, as it did before - only decorating needs a realm character.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5760-087","v":"0.1.5760","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"The hall's yard speaks of the hall. A piece placed inside the building now says \"That is inside the hall\", and a full yard says \"The hall's yard already holds 60 pieces.\" - not \"your house\" or \"your yard\".","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-001","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Combat Silver","t":"Economy","x":"A town you defend now pays silver. When a raid you fought in is counted, 30 silver is struck to your account, beside its Renown and the town's thanks. Your chat says so.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-002","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Combat Silver","t":"Economy","x":"One daily limit for fighting. Oblivion Gates and raids now share 150 silver a day: three gates, five raids, or any mix. The gate used to stop at two a day. If a gate or raid would go past the limit, you are paid what is left of it, and anything after that pays no silver (it still counts on your record).","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-003","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bank","t":"New","x":"The Bank's card shows how much combat silver you have earned today.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-004","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Deeds","t":"New","x":"When three members of a guild defend the same town, or close the same gate, the guild's silver treasury earns 25. Each must have been in the guild for 7 days.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-005","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Deeds","t":"Other","x":"When three members of a guild defend the same town, or close the same gate, the guild's silver treasury earns 25. Each must have been in the guild for 7 days.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-006","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Deeds","t":"New","x":"A guild earns at most 4 deeds a day. The member whose claim completes a deed is told in the chat, and the Guild tab's treasury list shows it. The Guild tab's silver treasury says how many deeds the guild has earned today.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-007","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Deeds","t":"Other","x":"Each account counts once for each town or gate, for the guild of the character it claimed with.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-008","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Contracts","t":"New","x":"A guild can pay fighters to defend a region. On a Notice Board's Work tab, a Guildmaster (or an Officer, within the week's writ budget) can post a guild contract: 1 to 50 silver for each defender of a raid in that region, for up to 500 defenders. The whole amount is held from the guild's silver treasury.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-009","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Contracts","t":"New","x":"Anyone who defends a town in that region is paid as their raid is counted, less the market's 5% tax - every member of a party, however close together their claims arrive. Your chat says which guild paid you. A guild's own Officers and Guildmaster are not paid by its contracts. Its other members are.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-010","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Contracts","t":"New","x":"A contract stands for 7 days. A guild can have 5 at once. Withdraw one on the Work tab, and what is left of its silver goes back to the treasury. The same happens when it runs out.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-011","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Contracts","t":"Other","x":"Officers' contracts and writs share one weekly writ budget.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-012","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Contracts","t":"Other","x":"A guild with a contract standing can't be disbanded until it is withdrawn.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-013","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"New","x":"Three Motherlodes break ground every day, each in its own part of the day, on ground players have explored. Each stands for two hours, or until 20 miners have struck it.","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-014","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"New","x":"You are warned in the chat 10 minutes before one rises, with its region and its ore. With the Motherlode Sense specialisation (Mining 100), the warning comes 30 minutes ahead. Motherlode Sense can now be chosen.","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-015","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"New","x":"Find it on your compass from anywhere in the open world, in Mining's colour. Close up it is a large, glowing heap of ore at a rock (where a town covers the middle of its ground, it stands at the nearest open spot outside the town).","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-016","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"New","x":"Strike it with your Pick-Axe like a vein, at its tier-6 difficulty. It needs Mining 25. The Watch must have seen you on its ground in the last few minutes - it marks those who move about, every two minutes. If it hasn't, you are told to walk about on it a moment.","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-017","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Other","x":"If its twenty miners have struck it, or it has gone, your first try tells you and the Motherlode is gone from your world - no more wasted swings.","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-018","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"New","x":"Each strike gives 4 to 6 of its ore (Adamantium, Ebony or Orichalcum - half again for a clean strike), Mining XP and 10 silver. Each account can strike one Motherlode a day. It does not count against your 60 harvests.","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-019","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Other","x":"Each strike gives 4 to 6 of its ore (Adamantium, Ebony or Orichalcum - half again for a clean strike), Mining XP and 10 silver. Each account can strike one Motherlode a day. It does not count against your 60 harvests.","g":["mining","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5767-020","v":"0.1.5767","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Renown","t":"Other","x":"Renown stays separate from silver: it still raises your health and magicka, opens sigil stages, founds guilds and counts toward a seat's influence.","g":["renown","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5769-001","v":"0.1.5769","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-001","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Retro Mode","t":"Fix","x":"The HUD, your weapon and your horse now stay inside the picture. With Retro Picture Mode on and Retro Aspect set to 4:3 or 16:10, only the world used to be framed by the black bars. The health bars sat in the left bar, the compass and your weapon hugged the screen's right edge, and the docked large HUD stretched across the whole screen. Now the HUD, the large HUD, your weapon (and the Weapon and Shield Widget sprites), the spellcasting hands and the horse all sit inside the picture, as in Daggerfall Unity. The docked large HUD is the picture's width, so the view above it keeps Daggerfall Unity's shape. On the Enhanced Plus UI, the HUD, notifications, quest tracker and status line stay inside the bars too.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-002","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"HUD","t":"Fix","x":"Notifications you've moved now fade in where you put them. If you dragged the notifications to a new spot (Alt+U), each new notification first appeared at its old place on the right and then jumped. Now it shows up at your spot from the first frame, and fades in and out there instead of sliding in from the side. Notifications you haven't moved still slide in from the right as before. Revenant taunt cards you've moved fade the same way.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-003","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Classic UI","t":"Rework","x":"The classic UI now uses Daggerfall Unity's classic blue arrow cursor. It shows from the very first screen, over every window and panel, and the gamepad cursor uses the same arrow. Text boxes still show the text cursor. Enhanced Plus keeps its gauntlet.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-004","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Performance","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed a GPU memory leak in long sessions. Each time you opened the map inside a dungeon or a building, the game created a new graphics context of 30 to 40 MB (more on a 4K screen) and never freed it. The map now reuses one. The game also releases all its graphics memory as soon as you close the tab, instead of waiting for the browser to get round to it. This mattered most on Firefox.","g":["map","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-005","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bounties","t":"Fix","x":"Bounty packs no longer spawn inside rocks. A bounty's pack, a wilderness camp or a roaming band could stand inside one of the World of Daggerfall rock formations or mountains, where you couldn't reach them. They now always stand on open ground.","g":["bounty","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-006","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"The Bodyguard now finishes online once you're paid. After you saved Evelara from the assassins and were paid, the quest stayed in your journal forever when playing online. It now closes a couple of minutes after the reward, like other finished quests. If it's already stuck in your journal, it closes on its own the next time you play. Offline, it closes the next day, as it always has.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-007","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Weapon Widget","t":"Fix","x":"Inertia now sways the sprites when you look around. The Inertia module was getting your mouse look in the wrong units, so the sway from turning was about a fourteenth of what the mods intend. Walking and strafing swayed them, but looking around barely did. Turning now sways the weapon, shield and torch as in Daggerfall Unity. Turn the Inertia dials down if it's too much for your taste.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-008","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Shield Widget","t":"Fix","x":"The Shield Widget's Recoil now kicks when an attack lands on your shield. With the default armor rules (Physical Combat and Armor Overhaul), the game never told the shield which part of you was hit, so its default \"Attack On Shield\" recoil never fired. The Weapon Widget's Recoil already worked once its module is switched on.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-009","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Rework","x":"Clearer words when the guild treasury can't pay for a hall. Buying a hall for your guild takes the house's price plus half again, paid from the guild's gold treasury (Social > Guild > Treasury). Only gold that realm characters put into the treasury counts. Gold in a bank account never pays for a hall. The old message (\"put in by realm characters\") didn't say which of these was the problem, and \"realm\" read like a place. There are now two separate messages: one when the treasury is short of the price, and one when it holds enough but not enough of that gold counts.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-010","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"The Guild tab shows how much of the treasury can buy a hall.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-011","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guild Treasury","t":"Rework","x":"Deposit and Withdraw say \"at most 1,000,000 at a time\" if you type more than one move allows, instead of failing after you press. A 1,274,880 gold hall takes two deposits.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-012","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gather Cards","t":"New","x":"A harvest is one card under your crosshair, in the same place loot cards appear. It shows:","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-013","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gather Cards","t":"New","x":"Gather the same thing again while its card is up and the card adds to itself (+3, then +5), instead of stacking new lines.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-014","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gather Cards","t":"New","x":"A gem, a Heartwood, a resin or a hide's extra find shows as its own card under the first, with its own Stores count. Fish show their species.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-015","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gather Cards","t":"New","x":"A Motherlode strike is one bigger card showing the ore, the 10 silver, your purse and how many of its twenty miners have struck it.","g":["professions","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-016","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gather Cards","t":"New","x":"Silver gets a card wherever you earn it:","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5778-017","v":"0.1.5778","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Gather Cards","t":"Other","x":"When you have reached the day's combat limit, a muted card says so.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5781-001","v":"0.1.5781","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-001","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"The Arena of Daggerfall now stands in the heart of Daggerfall city, in the block just east of the centre, facing the market. The building is Kamer's Daggerfall Arena (used with his permission): high walls, tiers of seats, torches and braziers around a sand floor.","g":["arena","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-002","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Other","x":"It stands in every game, whether you use Daggerfall's own city layout or Beautiful Cities. It is part of the city, not a switch.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-003","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Other","x":"It is drawn with your own copy of Daggerfall's textures, and the stone passages under it are built from your own game's dungeon pieces.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-004","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"You can walk the tiers and the floor. The walls are solid.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-005","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Removal","x":"The tavern, the two gem stores and the houses that stood on that block are gone. Every other building in the city keeps its name, its owner and its guild. The Palace, the temple, the guilds and the banks are where they were.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-006","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Gate","t":"New","x":"At the north gate you'll find the Herald of the Arena, two gate wardens of the Royal Guard, recruiters for the Red Banner and the Blue Banner, and a bookmaker.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-007","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Gate","t":"New","x":"Talk to the Herald and he gives you a choice: watch the exhibition, fight on the ladder, open the Arena window, go down to the fighters' hall (the undercroft), or leave. If a choice isn't open, he tells you why.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-008","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"The arena's two companies take fighters at the gate. Talk to the Red Banner Recruiter or the Blue Banner Recruiter to join. Joining is free.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-009","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Every ladder bout you win is a point for your banner. Beating a Tier Champion is worth 3, and the Grand Champion 10.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-010","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"A season lasts a year of the game's calendar. When it ends, the banner with more points wins, and its fighters wear the laurel all the next year: the crowd is on your side from the first bell.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-011","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"You can quit your banner whenever you like (the recruiter asks you twice), but you can't join the other one until the next season. You can go back to the banner you quit at any time.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-012","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Each banner fields 24 fighters of its own, who climb the same ladder you do over the season. You'll see them on the leaderboards.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-013","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Your banner's pennant shows beside your name on the versus bar. In an exhibition, the Red Banner's fighter faces the Blue Banner's.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-014","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Your colours on the sand: fight a ladder bout under a banner and the banners around your side of the ring hang in its colour, and your half of the crowd takes on its colour too. At an exhibition, the Red Banner's half of the stands faces the Blue's.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-015","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"One window for everything at the arena, opened by the Herald, the recruiters and the bookmaker, and once you've joined a banner, from the Arena button on the character page of the pause menu.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-016","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"Bouts: the hour's exhibition with both fighters' records and odds (Watch, Wager), and your next ladder bout with its purse (Fight). Watching, wagering and fighting are done at the arena's gate; the window tells you why when you can't.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-017","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"Ladder: the ten tiers, where you stand, every opponent and champion, the purses and the title each tier gives.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-018","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"Team: your banner, the season's standing against the other, the laurel, your points, and your banner's top ten.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-019","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"Leaderboards: the highest tier, the fastest Grand Champion and the banners season by season, with your own row pinned below the top ten. Online, the realm's boards and its Hall of Champions (see Online below).","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-020","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"Records: your wins, losses, yields, falls, streaks and purses, your last twenty bouts and your wagers. Offline, your last three ladder bouts can be watched again from here (see Replays below).","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-021","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"New","x":"Rules: the arena's rules in plain words.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-022","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bookmaker","t":"New","x":"The Bookmaker at the gate takes wagers on the hour's exhibition, from 10 to 1000 gold, until the fight begins. One wager a bout.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-023","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bookmaker","t":"Economy","x":"His odds come from the fighters' records, less the house's tenth. A winning wager pays your stake back plus the odds he gave; a draw gives you your stake back.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-024","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bookmaker","t":"Economy","x":"He lays no price shorter than 1 to 5: a fighter more likely to win than that is not taken.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-025","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bookmaker","t":"Other","x":"If you don't stay to watch, the bout is still fought and your wager is still settled once the hour is over. But leave once the fight has begun and he keeps your stake, whoever was ahead.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-026","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bookmaker","t":"Other","x":"He takes no wager on an hour whose bout you have already seen, and the Herald won't stage an hour's exhibition again once its fight has begun.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-027","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bookmaker","t":"New","x":"Collect your winnings at his stall. He pays in person.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-028","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Titles","t":"New","x":"The Herald calls you by your arena title when you step onto the sand.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-029","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Hall of Champions","t":"New","x":"The Hall of Champions in the undercroft names every Grand Champion your character has seen: yours first, then each banner fighter who took the title, season by season. Their names hang on a wall of plaques beside the Keeper of the Hall. Click a plaque to read whose it is.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-030","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Titles","t":"New","x":"Your banner shows on the character sheet beside your arena title and record.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-031","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Exhibitions","t":"New","x":"Exhibitions: every hour from 8 in the morning to 9 at night, two fighters meet on the arena's sand. Stand near the colosseum and you'll see the bout, hear the crowd and see the fight on your screen. The same hour always brings the same two fighters.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-032","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"New","x":"The Ladder: ten tiers, from The Pit to The Grand Melee. Win three bouts in a tier and you face its Tier Champion; beat the champion and you climb, and the arena gives you a title. Tier 5's champion is two Warriors at once, Tier 6 throws you to the beasts, Tier 9 is two against one, and Tier 10 is a free-for-all melee before the Grand Champion.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-033","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Other","x":"Your opponents don't grow with you. The ladder is a fixed mountain.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-034","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"New","x":"Nobody dies on the sand. At 1 health you go down and the bout is over. Badly hurt (15% health or less)? Sheathe your weapon to yield. Fighters can also be carried out of the ring, and after three minutes the judges decide: damage dealt, then hits landed, then fewer misses.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-035","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"New","x":"After every bout the arena's healers make you whole again.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-036","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Economy","x":"Purses run from 50 gold for a first-tier win to 10,000 gold for the Grand Champion. The crowd's favour raises or cuts your purse. Losing costs you only the purse.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-037","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Other","x":"While your bout is on, you can't rest, travel or leave through the gates.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-038","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"New","x":"Your progress, titles and record are saved with your character. Your arena title and record show on the character sheet.","g":["arena","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-039","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Other","x":"Strike an exhibition fighter and the Herald will warn you once. Do it again and the watch comes for you.","g":["arena","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-040","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"New","x":"Replays: your last three ladder bouts are kept with your character. Ask the Herald (R - Watch your last bout again) or press Watch the replay on the Records page, at the arena's gate, and you watch the bout again from the terrace, with the crowd, the Herald and the verdict. A replay pays and counts nothing, and you can leave it whenever you like. (In a replay you appear as a fighter of your class.) Replays are kept offline only: online the realm keeps its own records.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-041","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"New","x":"The tiers fill with Daggerfall's own people: the gesturing man, dancers and musicians, courtiers and nobles. Big bouts draw hundreds.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-042","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"New","x":"The crowd cheers a great blow, gasps at a telling one, groans at a knockdown and roars at a comeback. It boos stalling, running away and an early yield. A fighter it hates is booed every time they strike.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-043","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"New","x":"Each fighter has the crowd's favour, for good or ill. Its darling and its villain are marked on the screen.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-044","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"New","x":"The crowd shouts, too: \"Blood on the sand!\", \"Get up, you dog!\", and the name of a favourite's home town.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-045","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"New","x":"At the verdict the crowd throws flowers for a winner it loves, and something worse for one it doesn't.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-046","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"New","x":"The crowd's voices are built while you play from Daggerfall's own crowd recordings. Drums, the bell and the old Arena fanfares are Daggerfall's own sounds. The arena also has its own march and victory fanfare.","g":["arena","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-047","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Versus Bar","t":"New","x":"A versus bar shows both fighters' names and health, your stamina, the crowd's mood and the time left. It takes no keys and never pauses the game. It moves aside for the target frame and the quest card, keeps clear of the crosshair on a short screen, and hides with the rest of the HUD (F10).","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-048","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"The bout's clock stops while the game is paused, so a pause never runs out a bout's time.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-049","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"New","x":"The Herald calls each fighter by name, counts down \"3 - 2 - 1 - Fight!\" and gives the verdict in the middle of the screen.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-050","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Undercroft","t":"New","x":"A stair inside the colosseum leads down to The Arena Undercroft: Kamer's own 32-block dungeon under the arena, now the fighters' hall.","g":["arena","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-051","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Undercroft","t":"New","x":"Nothing down there attacks you, and nothing breaks your rest. You'll find fighters at rest, the arena's keepers, the armourer at his anvil, and the beasts of the beast tier on their chains.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-052","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Undercroft","t":"New","x":"Talk to the Pit Master at the training pit to spar: a practice bout against a fighter of your own tier. No purse, no crowd, no step on the ladder - just practice.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-053","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Undercroft","t":"New","x":"The Keeper of the Hall reads you the Hall of Champions: the tier champions you have beaten, and your name as Grand Champion once you earn it.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-054","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Undercroft","t":"Other","x":"The Smaller Dungeons setting never shrinks the undercroft, so the fighters' hall, the training pit and the Hall of Champions are always where they belong.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-055","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Rework","x":"A house: the Daggerfall Bank moves your deed to a house of the same kind elsewhere in the city, the first time you load. Your own furniture goes back to your furnishings, ready to set down again, and anything you bought from the decorator is paid back in full to your Daggerfall bank account. Everything that was in your chests and on your floor waits for you in a chest in the new house (or in a crate by the door if the house has no chest). You'll get a letter, and a note in your notebook.","g":["arena","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-056","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Rework","x":"A rented room at the old tavern is honoured at any inn in the city.","g":["arena","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-057","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Rework","x":"A quest building on that block is chosen again in the city, so the quest can still be finished.","g":["arena","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-058","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Rework","x":"A save made inside one of those buildings, or a Recall anchor set there, puts you outside instead.","g":["arena","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-059","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Rework","x":"An online home on that block moves too (see Online below).","g":["arena","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-060","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"Other","x":"Online play needs a relay update (a single reconnect) and a registered account. Guests can watch, but they can't queue, join a banner or keep a result.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-061","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"Find a match: from the Arena window's Bouts page, look for a real opponent at your season rating. Ratings start at 1,000. The search widens every 10 seconds until someone is found. You both have 20 seconds to accept. A fighter who declines isn't offered to you again for a minute.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-062","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"Casual bouts: choose Casual bout instead and you're matched only with other players who want one. It's refereed the same way, but nothing is counted: no rating, no points, no record.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-063","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"Refereed bouts: a bout between players is fought on its own copy of the arena floor, and the server referees it. It holds both fighters' health (the same for every fighter of a level) and only counts a blow that could really have landed: in reach, at a believable pace, no harder than your weapon can hit.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-064","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"Other","x":"Leave a fight for more than 15 seconds and you forfeit it. A matched bout that nobody turns up to is called off.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-065","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"A win or loss moves your rating. More than five rated bouts in a day against the same fighter are kept, but don't move it.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-066","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"The ladder online is your account's own climb, with opponents the server runs. Wins count only in order, and your purse is paid once the realm has counted the win. Ladder wins (and rated wins against players) also earn Renown for the character who fought, within the usual hourly limit.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-067","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"The hour's exhibition is the same bout for everyone: online, the server fights it, so every player at the arena sees the same blows and the same winner. The bookmaker settles your wager by that result.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-068","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"The stands: watch any bout from the Bouts page (exhibitions, players' bouts, ladder bouts; a private session's bouts are watched by joining it), up to 60 watchers a bout. You're seated in the tiers with no body. Cheer and Boo from the stands (buttons on screen, or the = and - keys), and the whole crowd hears it.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-069","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"Banners online are your account's, not your character's. Seasons last eight weeks. You earn points for your banner: 1 for a ladder win, 3 for a Tier Champion, 10 for the Grand Champion and 2 for a rated win against a player. Last season's winners wear the laurel, and the crowd favours them from the first bell. Every fighter's banner shows on the versus bar.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-070","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"Realm leaderboards: the highest climb, the fastest Grand Champions, the season's player ratings and the banners, with your own row pinned under the top ten. The Hall of Champions online names every Grand Champion of the realm, in the window and when the Keeper of the Hall reads it.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-071","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Online","t":"New","x":"Records online shows your account's record and your last twenty bouts, with whom you fought and how.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-072","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Titles","t":"New","x":"Titles: your arena title shows on your letters and notices too. Grand Champion is yours for good once the realm has counted all forty ladder wins. The season's #1 player (with at least three rated bouts) wears the title Arena Champion and the laurel beside their name, until someone else takes the top.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-073","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"New","x":"Host your own session: open the Arena window (from the Herald, a recruiter or the bookmaker at the arena's gate in Daggerfall, or the pause menu's Arena button once you've joined a banner) and, on the Bouts page, press Host a session (you need a registered account). You get a six-character code to share on stream or in chat. Codes leave out I, L, O, 0 and 1, so a code read off the screen is typed right, and upper or lower case both work.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-074","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"New","x":"Join one: type the code into the Session code box on the Bouts page and press Join (or Enter). You're taken to the arena floor and seated in the stands. Guests can join to watch; fighting needs a registered account. Press Host or Join while outdoors.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-075","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"New","x":"The host decides who fights. The session's card lists everyone in it. The host presses Make Red or Make Blue beside a name to pick the two fighters, then Start bout: the two are brought down to the sand and everyone else watches from the stands. The host can also End bout (no result) while the bout has no result yet, Remove someone from the session, Lock session so nobody new can join (members who step away can still come back), or Close session.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-076","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"New","x":"Every fighter is equal: in a session's bout both fighters have the same health, whatever their level. The server referees every blow, as in any bout between players, and the Herald calls it a friendly bout. However a bout ends, its fighters are healed and sent back to the stands.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-077","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"Other","x":"Nothing is counted: no rating, no banner points, no records, no Renown. The session keeps its own last 20 results, shown on its card.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-078","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"New","x":"A session holds up to 62 people: 60 in the stands and two on the sand. It ends when its host closes it, 15 minutes after the host leaves, or 8 hours after it opened. A host or member who steps out can come back within that time with Rejoin session on the card (Host a session always starts a new one).","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-079","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"The stairs: every stair in the colosseum now walks smoothly up and down, including the stair from the gate courtyard to the ring. You no longer catch on the steps or start climbing them.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-080","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"Paving: the streets that meet the arena now lead onto paved squares instead of ending in snow, and the gate passage and the courtyard inside the walls are paved too. Lamps, benches, crates and signposts mark the three sides away from the gate.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-081","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Gate","t":"Rework","x":"The gate's people are known by what they do: the Herald of the Arena, the Red Banner Recruiter, the Blue Banner Recruiter, the Bookmaker and the Arena Wardens.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-082","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"New","x":"The entrance: fighters now walk out from the gates under the stands to their marks as the Herald calls their names.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-083","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"The judges now count missed swings (yours and your opponent's), so \"fewer misses\" can settle a close bout.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-084","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"Fix","x":"The crowd gasps at a real critical strike now, not just at any big hit.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-085","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"Fix","x":"The stands: the noble lords and ladies in the crowd are their proper size.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-086","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"Your character now faces the way you do when you arrive somewhere (on the sand, through a door), instead of turning to face the camera.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-087","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"Thin lines of sky that showed through some of the colosseum's walls, and flickering streaks on an inner wall, are gone.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-088","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"A torch left burning in a house that was moved for the arena now waits for you in the new house's chest.","g":["arena","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-089","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Performance","x":"The colosseum draws faster, and building it for the first time no longer stalls the game.","g":["arena","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-090","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Beautiful Villages of Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"Beautiful Villages of Daggerfall (by carademono) lays out every village, hamlet, farm, manor and temple in the Iliac Bay again, and rebuilds the roadside taverns.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-091","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Beautiful Cities of Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"Beautiful Cities of Daggerfall (by carademono) lays out all 410 cities again, with districts, walls, gates, markets and docks.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-092","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Beautiful Cities","t":"New","x":"Both are on by default. Each has its own switch in the Features pane (under Mods). A change takes effect the next time the game starts, so a town never changes around you. Offline, the new towns also need Replace Game Artwork switched on.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-093","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Beautiful Villages of Daggerfall","t":"Other","x":"Roadside taverns keep their inn. A few of the new village blocks have no tavern in them, so those 274 roadside taverns stay as they were in Daggerfall.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-094","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Other","x":"Your houses, rented rooms, quest buildings, items left with a smith, Recall anchors set indoors, and saves made inside a building all keep the town layout they were made in. If you switch either mod on or off later, that town keeps its old layout, so your furniture, chests and decorations stay where you left them.","g":["mod","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-095","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Other","x":"If a town can't be shown in the layout your house was bought in (for example, Replace Game Artwork is switched off), the house isn't treated as yours there, so you never walk into a stranger's home or a shop as its owner. It comes back when the town does.","g":["mod","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-096","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Other","x":"The first time you load after this update, the game forgets which buildings you had found in towns that changed. The towns themselves stay on your map.","g":["mod","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-097","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Rework","x":"Online, a home can't be bought until the game has loaded the towns as the other players see them. An out-of-date copy of the game is asked to reload before buying.","g":["mod","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-098","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Rework","x":"Online, players who see a town differently are never put in the same building together.","g":["mod","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-099","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Rework","x":"Online, both mods are set for the whole room. Every online home keeps the layout its town had when it was bought, and everyone sees the same town around it.","g":["mod","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-100","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Homes","t":"Fix","x":"You can take any of a room's own furniture out of your house, including the new towns' food, tableware and clutter. Before this fix, some of those pieces couldn't be taken out online, and came back after a load offline. Some cabin pieces on Detailed Ships' ships had the same problem.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-101","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Furnishings","t":"New","x":"The two mods place pieces from other mods that this game doesn't include. This game draws its own versions instead of leaving gaps: coloured beds, framed paintings, tapestries and banners for the regions and the Eight Divines, beams, mantels and chimneys, food, animals and tools, rocks and hills, market stalls, docks with their ramps and steps, temple gardens, and crop fields that change with the climate and turn to stubble in winter.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-102","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Detailed Ships","t":"Rework","x":"Detailed Ships' bottles and other items now also appear in the towns, even with Detailed Ships switched off.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-103","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Furnishings","t":"Other","x":"A few pieces are left out because they're effects, or because nothing is known of their shape, the same as in Daggerfall Unity without those mods. These include some bridges, chimney smoke, and the temples' deity statues.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-104","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"Fix","x":"Roleplay & Realism: you can rest in the towns' coloured beds.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-105","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"Fix","x":"Roleplay & Realism: the Master Armorer quest finds the armorer's shop in the new towns, instead of naming a neighbour's house.","g":["mod","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-106","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Bank","t":"Fix","x":"The bank no longer offers a house that has no door.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-107","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town People","t":"Fix","x":"Lamps, food and animals in the new towns are no longer mistaken for people you can talk to.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-108","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Guilds","t":"Fix","x":"The Mages Guild in Bubandanis and both guilds in Tulaedax work properly.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-109","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"Buildings in a few new villages now use the right colours and materials for their climate.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-110","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"Loading a save made inside a building in the new towns puts you back inside it, even after changing which mods are on.","g":["mod","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-111","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"Windmills stand on the new farms when Windmills of Daggerfall is on, and the Order of the Raven's guild halls work in the new cities.","g":["mod","windmill"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-112","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"You can enter the castles of Daggerfall, Sentinel and Wayrest in the new cities.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-113","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"The temples in two village layouts no longer have their front doors blocked by their foundations.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5875-114","v":"0.1.5875","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"A building no longer fails to load when it holds something the game has no picture for. Nothing is drawn there instead.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5879-001","v":"0.1.5879","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Login","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed a crash some online players hit right after logging in (\"can't access lexical declaration before initialization\").","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5883-001","v":"0.1.5883","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Homes","t":"Fix","x":"Online homes and guild halls on the block in Daggerfall city where the Arena now stands move to a new house on their owner's next login. Before, the move could miss and the home looked deleted. Nothing was lost; the homes were never deleted.","g":["arena","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5883-002","v":"0.1.5883","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"Fix","x":"The arena crowd sounds like people now instead of static.","g":["arena","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5883-003","v":"0.1.5883","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed the crackle and pop at the end of a match, after the victory celebration.","g":["arena","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5885-001","v":"0.1.5885","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"Rework","x":"When you host or join a private session, chat now confirms you're in it and how many others are there. Players watching from the stands aren't drawn, so the arena can look empty. Open Bouts in the Arena window to see who has joined; the host calls fighters to the sand.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5889-001","v":"0.1.5889","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"New","x":"An Arena button appears on screen during a private session, and the / key does the same. Both open the session's Bouts page, so the host can pick fighters and start bouts without going through the pause menu.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5889-002","v":"0.1.5889","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"Fix","x":"Removed the static under the crowd's cheers and boos.","g":["arena","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5889-003","v":"0.1.5889","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed the crackling after a bout ends. The crowd now roars at the result instead.","g":["arena","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5889-004","v":"0.1.5889","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"Losing a bout no longer kills you or throws you out of the arena. You fall, the healers come, and both fighters go back to the stands.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5894-001","v":"0.1.5894","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Stands","t":"Rework","x":"Watchers in the arena's stands can no longer jump down onto the sand during bouts. A private session's host can still go down, and fighters called to the sand are unaffected.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5894-002","v":"0.1.5894","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Stands","t":"Fix","x":"Players in the arena's stands are now visible to each other and to the fighters, in private sessions, player bouts and the hourly exhibition. In a private session, only its members see each other.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5894-003","v":"0.1.5894","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"Fix","x":"Host and Join now ask you to sign in and be online first, instead of putting you in an empty arena.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5896-001","v":"0.1.5896","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"Blows in player-versus-player arena bouts land again. Since spectators became visible, your hits could aim at someone in the stands instead of your opponent.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5898-001","v":"0.1.5898","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"Hits in player-versus-player arena bouts now land every time. They could still go to a nearby spectator instead of your opponent.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5900-001","v":"0.1.5900","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"The arena floor (bouts and private sessions) now shows the sky above the stands, instead of black.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5902-001","v":"0.1.5902","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Town Map","t":"Fix","x":"The Arena of Daggerfall now appears on Daggerfall's town map, drawn as a ring around its sand and labelled \"Arena\".","g":["arena","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5905-001","v":"0.1.5905","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Window","t":"Rework","x":"Arena buttons and messages are shorter and easier to read: Bet, Find match, Host, Join, Cancel bout, Replay.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5905-002","v":"0.1.5905","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Arena Gate","t":"Rework","x":"The Herald, recruiters and bookmaker offer short, plain choices.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5905-003","v":"0.1.5905","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Private Sessions","t":"Rework","x":"Private session messages say plainly what happened and what to do.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5908-001","v":"0.1.5908","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Staff Teleport","t":"Fix","x":"Staff teleport takes you to the right interior in towns with the new layouts.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5908-002","v":"0.1.5908","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Staff Teleport","t":"Fix","x":"Teleporting to a boat or cabin keeps you on the right boat and in your own cabin.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5908-003","v":"0.1.5908","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Staff Teleport","t":"Other","x":"Private rooms and homes still check ownership when you teleport or visit.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5908-004","v":"0.1.5908","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Save Screen","t":"Fix","x":"The save screen no longer leaks memory from its screenshots.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-001","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Searchables","t":"New","x":"Search things in dungeons and graveyards. Coffins, sarcophagi, shelves, chests, crates and graveyard headstones can be searched. You find gold and items, wake undead (sometimes an elite), or find nothing. Each one can be searched again after five game hours. Some chests and crates are locked; pick them in Steal mode.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-002","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Searchables","t":"New","x":"Searching in a party. You get two foes per player, and a search counts for the whole party: everyone sees the same find and waits the same five hours.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-003","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Travel Panel","t":"New","x":"Pace near enemies. The travel panel has a second speed setting that shows up when enemies slow the clock. It sets how slow travel gets near them. It starts at ×5, so travel no longer drops to walking pace when an enemy is near; set it to ×1 for the old behaviour.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-004","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Spellbook","t":"New","x":"Spell icons. In the spellbook, the Icon button lets you pick any icon for a spell. You can also choose no icon; the spell then shows its initials.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-005","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"New","x":"Steady shadows switch in the Enhanced lighting tile (Settings, Features). It's on by default. There's also a shadow debug log switch, off by default.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-006","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Nerf","x":"Normal enemies drop at most 3 items, gold included (5 in an Elite Dungeon). Their drops are mostly white, blue is rare, yellow very rare and orange almost never.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-007","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Nerf","x":"Champions no longer always drop a Rare. Their Magic and Rare chances are half a normal enemy's, and their Legendary chance is the same as before.","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-008","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Rework","x":"An elite's extra Rare chance is half a champion's at its level.","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-009","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Fix","x":"Shadows no longer pop on and off with Enhanced Lighting. Every shadow is redrawn every frame.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-010","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Rework","x":"The nearest twelve lamps keep full shadows (it was eight), so your shadow and the townsfolk's don't vanish when a lamp swaps in.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-011","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Fix","x":"Lamps at almost the same distance no longer trade shadows back and forth.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-012","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Fix","x":"Your own shadow no longer jumps from lamp to lamp.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-013","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Rework","x":"While Steady shadows is on, your eyes adjust to light changes more slowly, so a brief shadow pop doesn't make the whole screen brighten and dim.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5910-014","v":"0.1.5910","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Other","x":"Steady shadows costs more graphics card work and about 48 MB more graphics memory. Turn it off if your frame rate drops.","g":["lighting","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5913-001","v":"0.1.5913","d":"2026-10-03","e":"Game","t":"Other","x":"Fixes and improvements.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-001","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"Rest at a rest point. Online you rest at a lit fire (your Campfire, a friend's, a tent's, a brazier or a dungeon's campfire), at a bed (a rented room, your house, a ship's cabin) or in a guild hall that lets you rest. Out in the open with none of these, the rest window says \"Find a fire or a bed to rest.\" In town, resting outside is still illegal: the window says so, and no guard is called.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-002","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"Hold still for six seconds. The rest window shows a short bar instead of the hours. Press Esc (or Stop in the enhanced window) and nothing happens. The rest is broken the moment an enemy comes, you are hurt, or the fire you rest by goes out.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-003","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Other","x":"Monsters can still find you in the night. If one turns up while you sleep, you wake at once to fight it, with only the hours you slept behind you - even in the night's last minutes.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-004","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"A night passes at once. When the bar fills you sleep a whole night: eight hours on your character's own clock, in one step. Spells wear off, hunger and sleep work as they did for eight hours of rest, and a rented room's night is used.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-005","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"One night every ten minutes of play. Resting again sooner is a short rest: it heals you, and no time passes. The enhanced HUD's status bar shows a Rested tile with the minutes left until the next night.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-006","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"New","x":"One night every ten minutes of play. Resting again sooner is a short rest: it heals you, and no time passes. The enhanced HUD's status bar shows a Rested tile with the minutes left until the next night.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-007","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"A night at a fire, a tent or a bed heals you fully. A guild hall's floor is a rough night with Climates & Calories: in Hard it heals less and you wake stiff.","g":["camping","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-008","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Rented Rooms","t":"Rework","x":"Rooms count nights. A room rented for three days gives three nights, and playing between them no longer uses them up. It still ends once three days have passed for your character, and if it runs out partway through a night you only get the hours you slept.","g":["camping","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-009","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"Rework","x":"A Campfire you leave in a dungeon, lit or cold, comes out with you with the fuel it has left - when you walk out, are teleported out, or log off down there (offline too).","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-010","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Removal","x":"The loiter option is gone online. The sky runs on real time, so waiting for it does nothing.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-011","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"New","x":"Online, every new character starts with a Campfire, and General Stores sell two to four, whether or not Climates & Calories is on. Pawn Shops have up to two. A Campfire costs 40 gold, half that online, as a potion does. (Offline the Campfire is part of Climates & Calories: a new character with it starts with a full one, and a General Store has two to four on its counter, where it had one to three Campfire Kits on every shelf.)","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-012","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"Economy","x":"Online, every new character starts with a Campfire, and General Stores sell two to four, whether or not Climates & Calories is on. Pawn Shops have up to two. A Campfire costs 40 gold, half that online, as a potion does. (Offline the Campfire is part of Climates & Calories: a new character with it starts with a full one, and a General Store has two to four on its counter, where it had one to three Campfire Kits on every shelf.)","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-013","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"New","x":"It has eight nights of fuel. Placing it costs nothing. A night you sleep at your own Campfire uses one night of fuel; a friend sleeping at your fire costs you nothing. Firewood refuels it - a smith won't. (Online, until Firewood arrives, a Campfire that has burned its last night is replaced by buying another.)","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-014","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Firewood","t":"New","x":"It has eight nights of fuel. Placing it costs nothing. A night you sleep at your own Campfire uses one night of fuel; a friend sleeping at your fire costs you nothing. Firewood refuels it - a smith won't. (Online, until Firewood arrives, a Campfire that has burned its last night is replaced by buying another.)","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-015","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Field Cook","t":"Rework","x":"Field Cook (Cooking's choice at rank 50): a night you sleep at your own Campfire uses none of its fuel. (It used to light a Campfire Kit without using a charge; placing a Campfire is free for everyone now.)","g":["camping","cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-016","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"Rework","x":"It doesn't burn away. When it burns down it goes cold and stays where it is. Relight it while it has fuel, or pick it up: it goes back in your pack with the fuel it has left.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-017","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Tents","t":"Rework","x":"Tents work the same way. Pitching one is free; a night you sleep at your own tent uses one of its uses.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-018","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"New","x":"Use the loot window's list on a fire. Look at a fire or a tent and the item list shows what you can do: Rest here, Cook food, Relight the fire (Stoke the fire for a tent), Pick up the Campfire (Pack up the camp for a tent). The highlighted row is what a click does. Online a cold fire offers no rest - relight it first. A brazier's or a hearth's list is Rest here and Cook food, indoors too.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-019","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Dungeon Campfires","t":"New","x":"Dungeons have campfires of their own: one near the entrance, one deep inside, and more in between, at least 80 metres apart. A small dungeon has one or two, a large one up to seven. An elite dungeon has half as many. A palace, the Burning Court and the Arena's sand have none. A brazier already by the entrance counts as its fire.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-020","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Dungeon Campfires","t":"New","x":"They are the same in every player's game, never go out and can't be picked up. They stand clear of loot piles and the way in, light the room around them, you can cook at them, and online you can rest at them.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-021","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Dungeon Campfires","t":"New","x":"Online, no wandering monster appears within 15 metres of one - for everyone resting there, not only the dungeon's host. A monster that was already in the dungeon can still walk up. (Offline, resting is as in Daggerfall, so monsters can still find you there.)","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-022","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Dungeon Campfires","t":"New","x":"They show on the compass in yellow, and on the held dungeon map (the enhanced map) once you've seen the spot.","g":["camping","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-023","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Dungeon Campfires","t":"Other","x":"They appear offline too, as places to cook and warm up with Climates & Calories.","g":["camping","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-024","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Rework","x":"No more votes. Online, when a party member sleeps a night at a rest point, everyone in the party within 15 metres (indoors, in the same building) who has \"Rest with my party\" on sleeps that night too, each with their own healing. Only the player who rested can be ambushed, and a rester with \"Rest with my party\" off carries nobody.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-025","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"New","x":"You sleep by their fire. Standing near the party member who rested is enough: you sleep as well as they do, not as if you were on the bare ground.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-026","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Other","x":"If you're fighting, swimming, in a menu or already resting, you're skipped, and told so - and so are you if you stand in town, where camping is illegal. If you're in the same place but further than 15 metres away, you're told that you missed the night. A night cut short says so.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-027","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Fix","x":"A party member's night carries you once, however their connection behaves; it can't be repeated to keep you asleep.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-028","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Other","x":"In taverns, temples and guild halls everyone rests for themselves, as before - nobody is pulled into another member's night there.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-029","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Rework","x":"/ready now just says how a party rests online.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-030","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Fix","x":"Other players never stop you resting at a fire or a bed.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-031","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Bedroll","t":"New","x":"Bedroll (10 nights): online, once the supplies arrive, a rough rest point wherever you could place a camp, dungeons included - you lay it down and the rest starts after ten seconds; other players nearby still stop you. (Offline every rest is already possible anywhere, so it isn't sold offline.)","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-032","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ember Jar","t":"New","x":"Ember Jar: lights a fire for one night (about three hours of the world's time). You can rest and cook at it. It can't be picked up.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-033","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Firewood","t":"New","x":"Firewood: adds three nights of fuel to your Campfire, up to eight. It feeds the emptiest of your own Campfires you're standing by, relighting it if it has gone cold; otherwise the emptiest one in your pack that has room.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-034","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Restorative Tonic","t":"New","x":"Restorative Tonic: restores 40% of your fatigue at once. With Climates & Calories it also takes four hours off your need for sleep.","g":["camping","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-035","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Meditation Candle","t":"New","x":"Meditation Candle (3 uses): light it from your pack, then rest. You kneel for six seconds and get half your magicka back.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-036","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Waking Salts","t":"New","x":"Waking Salts (3 uses): for an hour, being tired, drowsy or exhausted has no effect. You still get more tired, and two more hours of tiredness hit you when it wears off. You can't take another dose until the first wears off.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-037","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sleeping Draught","t":"New","x":"Sleeping Draught: your next night sleeps as well as a bed, even on the ground.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-038","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Supplies","t":"Other","x":"Offline (with Climates & Calories) General Stores and Alchemists sell them (all but the Bedroll), dungeon piles sometimes hold an Ember Jar or a Tonic, and enemies an Ember Jar. Online they arrive in a later update. This update teaches every game what they are first, so nobody on an older version loses one in a trade or a shared chest. A character you bring online keeps these supplies on the offline copy for now, and the realm says so.","g":["camping","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-039","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quest Waits","t":"Rework","x":"Online, a quest that only makes you wait moves on after a couple of minutes of play: a letter, a meeting, a \"come back in three days\". Deadlines still run on the world's clock while you play, as the quest timer notes say.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-040","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"a knightly order's artifact hunt (it no longer ends a couple of minutes after the knight's reward);","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-041","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"the scholar's errand (\"Please be prompt\") and the banker's lead to the guard;","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-042","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"a noble's daedra heart: you have the chemist's days to come back for your reward (the quest had failed a couple of minutes after you delivered the heart);","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-043","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"the main quest's chapter in Orsinium: it stays there for its six days of play before the Necromancers steal it (it was stolen a couple of minutes after you took the quest);","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-044","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"a thief's delivery \"as soon as possible\": the contact waits its time for you.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-045","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Quest time limits are back online. \"You have 14 days\", travel-time limits and the rest work as they do in Daggerfall again: a deadline can run out. This undoes the update that made online quests time-free.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-046","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"A quest that only makes you wait moves on after a couple of minutes of play. A letter, a meeting, a \"come back in three days\" arrives about two real minutes later online, and its text says \"a few days\". Only a quest's deadlines keep their days.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-047","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Quest timers run while you play. A quest day is about two real hours of play (the sky's day is one).","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-048","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Resting, waiting and travelling don't use up a quest's timers online. An eight-hour rest, a long wait or a fast-travel journey takes nothing off a quest's clock. Only time you spend playing counts.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-049","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Other","x":"Time logged off never counts, and a tab left in the background counts only its first couple of minutes.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-050","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Countdowns are back for a quest's deadlines in the journal, the quest tracker, the quest rail and the map markers, along with the \"running out of time\" warnings. Quest text says a deadline's real number of days again.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-051","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Bounties","t":"Rework","x":"Bounties lapse again a day after you take them: about two real hours, whether you rest, play or log off. A bounty you held before this update gets a fresh day from your first moment online, kills kept, and one you bring online from offline keeps the time it had left.","g":["bounty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-052","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Quest letters wait for morning again, as well as for you to be in town.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-053","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Other","x":"Vampire, werewolf, Thieves Guild and Dark Brotherhood quests still come after a few minutes of play online, one at a time (a cure can take ten or so), as they have since quests went time-free.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-054","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Quests","t":"Other","x":"A failed quest online still doesn't cost its faction the standing Daggerfall takes for any unfinished quest - but now that deadlines can run out, a quest's own penalty for failing it (some cost standing with someone) applies.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-055","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Nerf","x":"Ordinary foes drop half as much. A foe that is not an elite, an Elite Dungeon foe or a champion now leaves each item it would have dropped only half the time, online and offline. Its gold is untouched, and elites and champions drop everything as before.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5976-056","v":"0.1.5976","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"New","x":"A need's tile says how bad it is. On the enhanced HUD each Climates & Calories need tile shows its stage at its foot (\"2/3\" is Hungry, of Peckish, Hungry, Starving).","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-001","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Strength","t":"Rework","x":"Every ship takes 60% more punishment. Hulls and sails are 1.6 times as strong, and cannon balls, fires and rams thin crews 1.6 times more slowly.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-002","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Strength","t":"Other","x":"This goes for your boats and for every pirate, merchantman and navy ship.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-003","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Strength","t":"Other","x":"Sea fights last longer and leave more time to manoeuvre, brace and board.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-004","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Strength","t":"Other","x":"The odds of a fight haven't changed. A ship that outguns another still does, by the same margin. A fight costs about as many men as before; it just takes longer.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-005","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Floating Casks","t":"Rework","x":"Floating casks last longer. Casks and wreckage now float about 4 minutes (it was 2½), so loot from the first ship you sink is still there after the second.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-006","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Pirates","t":"Rework","x":"Pirates break off at the same point in a fight. A beaten pirate tries to run for about as long as before she has to strike, instead of 1.6 times as long.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-007","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Saved Boats","t":"Fix","x":"A ship saved whole loads whole, and one saved half-holed loads half-holed.","g":["naval","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-008","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Saved Boats","t":"Fix","x":"A part-used Carpenter's Store keeps its work.","g":["naval","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-009","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Saved Boats","t":"Other","x":"A save made now loads in an older version with your boats as you left them, with one exception: the Fleet ledger (below) is new, so in an older version a laid-up ship is gone and a placed one can't be picked up.","g":["naval","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-010","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Rework","x":"Your crew gets to work sooner and works faster. The free patch-up starts 15 seconds after the last hit (it was 30) and runs twice as fast. Carpenter's Stores repairs run twice as fast too.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-011","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Rework","x":"Your crew gets to work sooner and works faster. The free patch-up starts 15 seconds after the last hit (it was 30) and runs twice as fast. Carpenter's Stores repairs run twice as fast too.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-012","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"New","x":"No orders needed. Once a fight is over, your crew uses the Carpenter's Stores in your hold to repair her to full on their own.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-013","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"New","x":"Your First Mate says when she's sound or when the stores run out.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-014","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Other","x":"Damage below half strength is left to the free patch-up, so no store is wasted on work the crew does for free.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-015","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Other","x":"A wrecked Small Ship is whole in about three minutes this way, on 7 stores.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-016","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"New","x":"To turn this off, go to Features > Naval Combat > Crew repairs on their own.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-017","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"New","x":"A crewed ship repairs even when you're not aboard. A boat with no crew (a Large Boat you sail alone) is only repaired with stores while you're on her.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-018","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Rework","x":"Make repairs is the fast option. Your crew uses stores from the first plank: a wrecked Small Ship's hull is whole in about a minute and her canvas half a minute later, on 12 stores.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-019","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"New","x":"Damage control. With an enemy close by, Make repairs keeps your crew working at an eighth of the usual pace.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-020","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Other","x":"That makes good about a third of the damage a ship your size deals you, at the cost of a store every minute or so.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-021","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Repairs","t":"Other","x":"Fires keep burning while they patch, and a wreck stays crippled until the fight is over.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-022","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Shipwright","t":"Economy","x":"The shipwright charges about the same. He charges less per point because hulls have more points.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-023","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Carpenter's Stores","t":"Economy","x":"Carpenter's Stores cost 314 gold (they were 336) and each one repairs more, so a wreck still takes thirteen (a Carrack now takes eighteen, up from seventeen).","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-024","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"A sunk ship leaves her wreckage afloat beside her floating casks. It's larger and paler than a cask.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-025","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"Sail through it to haul it aboard. It gives Carpenter's Stores for your hold (2 from a sloop, 4 from a brigantine or a cutter, up to 6 from a pirate flagship) and powder that fills your stern's fire barrels.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-026","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"Sink what you meet and you can keep sailing. Salvage lets you repair to full and refill your fire barrels without making port.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-027","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Salvage","t":"Other","x":"If you're swimming, the stores go into your pack one at a time (or straight aboard, if you're alongside your own boat). Whatever is too heavy to carry is lost, and you're told.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-028","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"If you fast travel or go through a door first, your crew stows wreckage from ships you sank, just as it does the casks.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-029","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"Online: everyone in the room sees the wreckage, and whoever reaches it first hauls it in. A ship sunk in a sea run by a player on an older version leaves no wreckage, and players on an older version don't see it.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-030","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Holdings","t":"New","x":"The pause menu has a fourth tab: Holdings, between Stats and System. It holds everything you own and everyone who follows you.","g":["holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-031","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Holdings","t":"Rework","x":"Stats is just your character sheet again (and your Professions, online). The Companions, Revenants and Stores pages moved to Holdings.","g":["holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-032","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Holdings","t":"Fix","x":"On a narrow window (a phone), the tabs shrink to fit instead of being cut off.","g":["holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-033","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Holdings","t":"New","x":"Two new pages: the Stable and the Fleet.","g":["holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-034","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"See your horse and wagon at a glance: whether you're riding, whether they're following you, or how far away they're parked or waiting.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-035","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"Summon brings them to your side, as the summon key does.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-036","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"Send away takes them back to the stable, out of the world. Mount them from the Transport window any time, or summon them again.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-037","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"Rename your horse right on the page. Renaming with an empty name tells you he keeps no name, not that you don't own a horse.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-038","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"Rework","x":"Ship deeds no longer sit in your pack. A ship's title goes into your Fleet ledger.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-039","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"A deed you buy at a shop goes there the moment you buy it, and she waits for you at that port.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-040","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"A ship you take as a prize goes there when you claim her.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-041","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"Rework","x":"Deeds already in your pack move into the ledger the first time you open the Fleet page.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-042","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"Rework","x":"Picking a ship up puts her parts in your pack, and her title goes with them. Her parts are her: sell them and you've sold her; drop them or chest them and that's where she is. Placing her parts puts her title back in the ledger. Parts can't be placed while that ship is already afloat.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-043","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"Each ship gets a card showing:","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-044","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"Summon: at any port (within Come Sail Away's port search range), she's brought round to a free berth at the quay. If the harbour has no free berth, click the water to place her, as a deed did. A Large Galley is too long for a quay, so she's always placed by clicking.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-045","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"Send away: she sails for the port nearest you and is laid up there, cargo and all. A boat with no crew has to be sent from close by. A Large Boat keeps the rig you gave her.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-046","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"Repair, even when you're away. If she has crew aboard, they mend her where she lies, at no cost up to half strength. Past that they use the Carpenter's Stores in her hold.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-047","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"Shipwright: at a port, open the shipwright's window for a ship that's laid up or lying there.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-048","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"New","x":"Hold: carries 20% more cargo per tier before she rides low.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-049","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"New","x":"Rigging: 4% faster under sail per tier.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-050","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"New","x":"Hull: 10% more hull and canvas per tier.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-051","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"New","x":"Guns: her cannon balls do 8% more damage per tier.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-052","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"Economy","x":"Refits cost gold and materials from the world, taken from your pack or her hold:","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-053","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"Other","x":"A ship bought on the bank's credit can't be refitted while that region's bank is owed anything (borrowing more, or the Empire calling the debt in, doesn't free her). Once it's repaid, she's free for good. This includes a Rowboat bought as parts.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-054","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Refits","t":"Economy","x":"Bigger ships cost more: half the price for a Rowboat, two and a half times for a Carrack.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-055","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Names","t":"New","x":"Give any ship a name (up to 24 printable characters). It shows on her hover plaque, for you and for every other player who sees her.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-056","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Names","t":"Other","x":"Names go through the same filter as player names.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-057","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"Give each named hand a post from his ship's card: First Mate, Bosun, Gunner, Carpenter, Lookout, Cook or Deckhand. A Bard can keep or return to his calling.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-058","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"Each post has a place on deck:","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-059","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"Hands keep to their posts most of the time, and still wander, work and talk now and then.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-060","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Crew Roles","t":"Other","x":"With no Lookout named, a hand with no post keeps the bow, or else a Gunner. A Bard never keeps the lookout.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-061","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Crew Roles","t":"Rework","x":"One First Mate per ship. Making a new one makes the old one a Deckhand. Your First Mate is the one who answers you.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-062","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quays","t":"New","x":"Port towns have quays. Every berth of a port's harbour now has a timber quay on piles, with:","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-063","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quays","t":"New","x":"They appear as you sail in. A port's quays stand from about 1.6 km out, so you see them before you reach the berth.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-064","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quays","t":"Rework","x":"The port's own ships lie alongside them, small and large, instead of out in open water.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-065","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docking","t":"New","x":"Dock your ship. Strike your sails and come in slowly beside a free quay, roughly along it. Your crew warps her in and makes her fast.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-066","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docking","t":"New","x":"A gangway runs out while she's made fast, square to her side: up to a ship's entry port, or down from the quay's edge onto a boat's gunwale. Use it from the quay to go aboard, or from her rail beside it to step ashore. Looking at her helm, hold or door, Activate uses those instead.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-067","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Fleet","t":"New","x":"The Fleet page knows where she's docked: \"Made fast at Wayrest's quay\", even from far away.","g":["holdings","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-068","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docking","t":"New","x":"Summoned ships arrive at a quay, made fast and ready to board.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-069","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docking","t":"New","x":"Set sail or take the oars to cast off.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-070","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docking","t":"Other","x":"Galleys don't dock. A Large Galley is too long for a quay.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.5995-071","v":"0.1.5995","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quays","t":"Other","x":"Online: every player sees the same quays, except that players with Iliac Puddle's Deep Waters set differently may find a harbour's berths in different places.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6002-001","v":"0.1.6002","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"New title: Aegis of Oblivion, in violet that rises out of the void into a pale lilac light. It belongs to Sureme: press it on the account card to wear it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6002-002","v":"0.1.6002","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"A new glyph comes with it: three pillars standing through a ring, with the void's tendrils spreading beneath them. It shows beside Sureme's name.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6002-003","v":"0.1.6002","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"New aura: Oblivion Ward, Sureme's own. A whole ring of violet light circles the ground where you stand, with two bright scribes running around it and a bezel of fine ticks outside it. Inside the ring, a circle of twelve runes turns slowly the other way and lights up one rune after another, as if it were being written. Four claws hang from the ring at the diagonals, a violet mist turns inside, and a low veil of light with rising motes stands up off the ring.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6002-004","v":"0.1.6002","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"Floating symbols: runes lift off the ring and float up to chest height, swaying and drifting outward and always turned toward you, then blur, break into dust and fade away. Each one rises again somewhere else round the ring with a new rune.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6002-005","v":"0.1.6002","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"When the ward is first put on, it draws itself round from behind you. Wear it or take it off from the account card. Every player near you sees it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6002-006","v":"0.1.6002","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Auras","t":"Other","x":"Dagon's Fire looks exactly as it did.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-001","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"New","x":"Online, every General Store now sells a Materials Bag for about 500 gold. It holds 300 kg of crafting materials.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-002","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"New","x":"On the enhanced inventory the bag opens beside your pack, like the cart. If nothing else is open beside your pack, use the Materials Bag button at the bottom of your pack. On the classic inventory, reach your bag from the Stores page.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-003","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"New","x":"Anything you gather goes into your bag first, then your pack. With no bag, it all goes into your pack. Anything that doesn't fit is left where you gathered it, and the game tells you what was left.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-004","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stores","t":"Rework","x":"Your Stores are now kept in town. In any town, open the Stores page (on the pause menu's Holdings tab) to put materials in (one material at a time, or Put everything in) or take them out into your bag or pack.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-005","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stores","t":"New","x":"Empty your bag into your pack from the Stores page, anywhere.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-006","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"Rework","x":"Crafting stations use what you carry, including what's in your wagon. If your Stores are short, the rest is moved in from your bag and pack. Goods bought with gold on the market are never moved in.","g":["professions","crafting","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-007","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"Other","x":"You can't sell or drop the bag while it has anything in it, and it can't be traded.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-008","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"Other","x":"Food in the bag spoils, just like food in your pack.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-009","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Guild Tab","t":"Rework","x":"The Guild tab is now split into pages: Overview, Members, Treasury, Vault, Arms and Settings, and Stores where professions are on.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-010","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Guild Rename","t":"New","x":"Rename your guild: the guildmaster can change the guild's name or tag for 25,000 gold. The gold comes from the treasury, from gold your members' online characters put in. Renames are limited to one every two weeks. You can't rename in a week your guild is in a siege or a Tourney. Your guild's past entries in the Chronicle keep its arms.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-011","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Guild Vault","t":"New","x":"The guild vault: 50 item slots, or 100 if your guild has bought a hall. Put items in and take them out in any town. By default, officers can take items out 10 times a day, and members and recruits can put items in. The guildmaster can grant or revoke each member's access and set their daily limit. The chest in your guild hall now opens the vault.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-012","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Heraldry","t":"New","x":"Richer arms: 16 new devices (40 in all), 7 ways to split the field into two colours, and a colour of its own for the device. Pick them from pictures on the Arms page. Guild banners, shields and tags all show them.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-013","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Heraldry","t":"Other","x":"Players who haven't reloaded the game since this update see no arms for a guild that uses a new device, and see split fields as plain.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6020-014","v":"0.1.6020","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Guild Rename","t":"Rework","x":"Guild names and tags now go through the name filter, and a refused name says which word was refused. Names with numbers in them, like \"The 22 Blades\", are allowed.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6039-001","v":"0.1.6039","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Beautiful Villages","t":"Fix","x":"Trees in Beautiful Villages towns no longer float. Some village and tavern blocks plant trees on hillsides, and those trees now stand on the hill or ground drawn beneath them.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6039-002","v":"0.1.6039","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quest-givers are back. You can hand in a quest you took from a shopkeeper, innkeeper or librarian before the town update. The quest-giver now stands in the building your journal names, as the town is laid out now, and answers to their own name. This also works for party members you shared the quest with.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6039-003","v":"0.1.6039","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Shared quests pick the same monsters. Every party member's copy of a shared quest now picks the same random monsters, so The Exterminator's vermin no longer switch kind partway through. A party member's quest monsters also no longer fail to appear in a building or dungeon just because the player who shared the quest is nearby. The spiders keep coming in the guild.","g":["quests","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6039-004","v":"0.1.6039","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"The Totem rises with its cage. The Totem of Tiber Septim now rises with its cage in Castle Daggerfall's treasury, so you can finish \"Who Gets the Totem\" again. This works even if another player raised the cage long before you arrived.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6039-005","v":"0.1.6039","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Enchanting","t":"Fix","x":"The item maker no longer accepts Aetheric pieces: Ruhn's Regalia, the Sigil Broker's Regalia and the raid sets. These pieces carry their own powers, and the maker was laying its enchantments on top of them. Pieces enchanted before this change keep what they have.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6039-006","v":"0.1.6039","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"Leaving your ship's cabin no longer strands you in a black void. Your ship stays outside while you are below deck, so her own decks no longer cut through the cabin floor and items no longer sink into the gaps. If a save already has you stuck, type /unstuck in chat to return to the deck.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6042-001","v":"0.1.6042","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Fix","x":"Resting again before the next night is allowed now clears lost sleep too. If a night was cut short (an ambush in its first hour), slept on rough ground, or started deep in sleep debt, you can rest again at the fire or bed straight away to shake off Tired, Drowsy or Exhausted. Before, you had to wait out the ten minutes. A rest between nights still moves no time.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-001","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Login","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: logging in sent you straight back to the title screen. After two server restarts on October 4, everyone reconnected at once and the account service fell over under the load: sign-in failed and dropped you on the title screen. The service now does far less database work on every request, so a full server of players can log in together again.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-002","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"World Map","t":"Fix","x":"Ports show on the Enhanced world map. Every port you've discovered has an anchor at every zoom, including the whole-bay view the map opens on. Before, anchors appeared only zoomed in, and only with Travel Options' \"Only From Ports\" on.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-003","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"World Map","t":"Rework","x":"Easier to spot. The anchor is drawn darker, with a light outline, so it stands out on a busy coast.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-004","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docked Ships","t":"Fix","x":"No more ships inside your ship. A ship you leave made fast at a port's quay keeps her berth while she's out of sight. Before, sailing back into that port could find one of the port's own ships moored right inside her.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-005","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docked Ships","t":"Fix","x":"Summon and docking agree. Neither brings a ship to a berth where one of yours lies unseen.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-006","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docked Ships","t":"Fix","x":"Online: another player's ship lying at a berth keeps it even while its captain is invisible at her helm.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-007","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Death Penalty","t":"Rework","x":"Dying online now costs a tenth of the gold you carry, down from a quarter.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-008","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Travel Options","t":"Rework","x":"Online, every trip over land on the travel map is travelled rather than instant. Travel Options, its Cautiously and Inns options, and \"ships only from ports\" are always on online. Ships from a port and travelling to your party leader work as before.","g":["online","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-009","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"With Climates & Calories on, rations in your pack are eaten automatically when you get Hungry, instead of waiting until you are Starving.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6068-010","v":"0.1.6068","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Beautiful Cities","t":"Fix","x":"City walls no longer have gaps next to their corner towers. With Beautiful Cities on, the walls of most cities (Alik'ra and Chesterwark among them) had a 3-metre opening on each side of every corner tower that you could see and walk through. These now hold a matching section of the wall.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6076-001","v":"0.1.6076","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Bank Ships","t":"Fix","x":"A bank ship's cabin goes to the right ship. If you own a bank ship and more than one sailing ship of its size, the game asks which ship gets the bank ship's cabin (Link existing bank cabin on the ship's menu). Before this fix, a ship laid up in your Fleet didn't count. The cabin and everything in it could move into whichever ship was afloat.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6076-002","v":"0.1.6076","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Bank Ships","t":"Fix","x":"When your linked ship isn't in the water, the message now tells you to summon her from Holdings > Fleet. It used to point to a deed that is no longer kept in your pack.","g":["naval","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6084-001","v":"0.1.6084","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Gathering","t":"Fix","x":"Gathering without a Materials Bag puts everything you gather in your pack, even if that takes it over its weight. Before this fix, anything that didn't fit was lost.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6084-002","v":"0.1.6084","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"When a harvest takes your pack over its weight, the message says so. To lighten it, put materials in your Stores in any town, or buy a Materials Bag at any General Store.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6084-003","v":"0.1.6084","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"Fix","x":"Every shelf in a General Store now sells the Materials Bag. Before, only one shelf per store had it, and it could vanish from that shelf for everyone in the store.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6084-004","v":"0.1.6084","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"Rework","x":"Materials Bags and Campfires never sell out: buy as many Campfires as you like.","g":["camping","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6084-005","v":"0.1.6084","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"Rework","x":"Shops no longer buy Materials Bags or Campfires back.","g":["camping","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6084-006","v":"0.1.6084","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Materials Bag","t":"Rework","x":"You can only carry one Materials Bag. Trying to buy or pick up a second says \"You already have a Materials Bag.\"","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-001","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Choosing a category (Weapons, Armour, crafted goods, auctions) no longer hides listings that sat behind 500 cheaper items of other kinds.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-002","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"Long journeys across the map are no longer refused as \"no way by land\" when a route exists.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-003","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"Fast travel remembers the speed you chose. A path's slower cap no longer overwrites it, and the speed panel and the actual clock now agree.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-004","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"A landfall with no safe shore stops the journey and keeps your boat in the water, instead of packing it away under you.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-005","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"After a mantle under a low ceiling, you stand up again once there is room, instead of staying crouched. A crouch you chose yourself is kept.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-006","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"Finishing a vault on a slow frame no longer leaves your hands gripping the air.","g":["climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-007","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Boats","t":"Fix","x":"Climbing a boat's ladder no longer carries your fall or momentum onto the deck, so you stop sliding off.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-008","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Plunder","t":"Fix","x":"Settling a captured ship returns you to your own deck, or to the boat of the player you rode in with. If there is no safe deck to return to, scuttling and casting adrift are refused rather than leaving you in the sea.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-009","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Plunder","t":"Fix","x":"\"Open her hold\" no longer flashes back to the plunder window; when the hold can't open, the window says so.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-010","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Travel Map","t":"Fix","x":"Players riding another's boat are marked on the travel map where their boat is.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-011","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Reputation","t":"Fix","x":"Guild and faction reputation now recovers over time away, even when the clock catches up before your faction data has loaded.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-012","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Fix","x":"Switching accounts no longer carries the last account's found Motherlode over to the next.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6087-013","v":"0.1.6087","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Weapons","t":"Fix","x":"Daedric (and other) weapons show their own model: a longsword is no longer drawn as a katana, or a mace as a club.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-001","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"Rework","x":"The Small Ship is a brand-new model by Mac. That is the galleon you can buy, and the hull the pirate brigantines, merchant galleons and navy cutters sail. She has a deep hull with a sharp bow, six oak beams carrying her main deck, and every texture at 64x64, the size of Daggerfall's own.","g":["naval","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-002","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"Doors and hatches that open and close. Both hatch covers on her main deck lift open, and a ladder runs down under each one to her gun deck. The door into her great cabin and the door in her gun deck's bulkhead swing open and shut. Use them like any boat door.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-003","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"A wheel at the helm. Her wheel stands on the castle roof, where you steer from, and turns with the rudder as you put the helm over under sail. Under oars the wheel and rudder stay centred.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-004","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"Sails and ropes. She carries five sails: a fore course, two topsails, a big gaff sail on the main, and a jib. They furl and set, fill with the wind and swing as you trim, and their sheets and braces follow them. Shrouds with ratlines, stays and backstays hold them up.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-005","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"Painted properly. A painted hull with gilt bands, a panelled castle, a glazed stern gallery that glows at night, planked decks, gratings, red gunport shutters and tarred rigging.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-006","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"Cannon fire from her gunports. She has five gunports a side. When you lay a broadside, that side's shutters swing up and the guns run out through the ports, even on a quick click. Each ball leaves from its own port, and each gun kicks back as it fires before it's hauled out again. Other players see your shutters open and your guns run out, and when you leave the helm her guns run in and her ports shut. Ships of hers at sea open their ports when they run their guns out.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-007","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"Her castle is part of her deck. Two staircases climb to the castle roof and the helm. Her crew and boarders can walk up them, so nobody at the wheel is out of reach. Her officer and coxswain keep their posts up there while the hands work the main deck.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-008","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"Shots tear the canvas that's there. A ball through her sails tears them wherever the canvas hangs, however you trim. Chain shot passes through where a furled or shot-away sail would hang. Battle damage takes her highest canvas first: main topsail, fore topsail, jib, gaff, then the fore course.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-009","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"New","x":"At a quay, her gangway climbs to the entry port in her waist. She stands tall, so it's a steeper climb than the Carrack's. Her carpenter keeps his post beside her hatch.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-010","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Harbours","t":"Rework","x":"Harbours sound for her keel. Where the sea floor shelves gently, berths and their quays lie a little further from the shore than before, so the ships that moor there can put out and come back in.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-011","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"Other","x":"If her model fails to load, the old galleon takes her place with its own guns, decks, sails, gangway and the shallower water it can reach.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-012","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Small Ship","t":"Nerf","x":"The new galleon carries five guns a side instead of the old one's six, so ships built on this hull hit a little lighter in a broadside. A cautious pirate brigantine is less eager to attack a boat on its own.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-013","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Pirates","t":"Rework","x":"That lighter broadside changes who picks a fight at sea. A cautious pirate brigantine no longer goes after merchant carracks, so from level 5 the brigantines' raids are on merchant galleons only. A cautious corsair galley now attacks merchant galleons, so from level 7 you can come across those fights. A cautious brigantine now runs from a navy war galley, and from a crewed Large Galley of yours.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-014","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"Standing in the water or on a quay right next to a moored galleon no longer counts as being aboard her.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-015","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Boarding","t":"Fix","x":"A pirate boarding a prize that lies close to land now comes alongside instead of circling off.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-016","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Fix","x":"Head to wind with her sails set, her gaff and jib are taken aback and drive her astern: about 4 m/s in a steady wind, nearly half her speed ahead. The helm now tells you you're in irons while she goes astern. Put the helm over or strike sail to come out of it.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-017","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sails","t":"Fix","x":"A gaff, jib or lateen sail on a ship at sea now bellies away from the wind, on either tack. Before, they always bellied to starboard.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6136-018","v":"0.1.6136","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Boarding","t":"Fix","x":"Boarders can cross the Carrack's shut cargo doors, and standing on them counts as being aboard. Boarders follow you through open doors into cabins: the galleon's great cabin and the Carrack's rooms. Bodies on the Carrack no longer drop through her forecastle stair or get lifted onto her forecastle.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6140-001","v":"0.1.6140","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Companions now follow the path you actually walked when they can't see you. They go through doorways and round corners instead of walking into the wall beside the door.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6140-002","v":"0.1.6140","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Companions keep walking while they turn, so they no longer stop and start on every bend.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6140-003","v":"0.1.6140","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Companions","t":"Rework","x":"A companion that has fallen behind speeds up to keep pace with a running player, so they warp in to catch up less often.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6140-004","v":"0.1.6140","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Companions","t":"Rework","x":"Companions growl and moan far less often: every 18 to 54 seconds instead of every 3 to 9.","g":["companions","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6140-005","v":"0.1.6140","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"When your whole party comes through a door, the portal sound now plays once instead of once per companion.","g":["companions","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6140-006","v":"0.1.6140","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Lysandus","t":"Rework","x":"The ghost of King Lysandus is quieter. His cry of \"Vengeance!\" plays at 40% volume and at most once a minute.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-001","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"New","x":"A carriage, its horses and a driver now wait outside the gates of the walled cities (Immersive Travel by kkgobkk). Talk to the driver and press Fast Travel to open the driver's map.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-002","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"New","x":"Pick a town or village and pay the fare to fast travel there. The fare is a small daily carriage fee on top of any inn nights, and the trip's days still pass for your character.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-003","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"Other","x":"Drivers won't take you everywhere. As shipped, a carriage goes to cities, hamlets and villages only, and never puts you on a ship. You can change where carriages go in Mods → Immersive Travel.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-004","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"Other","x":"Disable Normal Travel is off by default, so your own travel map works as before. Turn it on to make carriages the only way to fast travel, as the mod's author intended.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-005","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"Other","x":"Turning Immersive Travel on or off takes effect the next time you start the game.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-006","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"New","x":"A driver's carriage is the way to fast travel over land online (a ship from a port is the other fast travel). You pay the fare and arrive in the world's present, and the days pass on your own clock. Every trip you start from your own map is still travelled on foot or horseback, as before.","g":["mod","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-007","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"Other","x":"Online the carriages, the fares and the driver's rules are the same for everyone.","g":["mod","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6149-008","v":"0.1.6149","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Immersive Travel","t":"Other","x":"Online, vampires and characters hurt by sunlight can't take a carriage by day, just as they can't fast travel from their own map.","g":["mod","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6159-001","v":"0.1.6159","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Casting a heal or buff on or near a companion, or a party member, no longer floods the notification panel. \"Press button to fire spell.\", \"Aim at your companion...\" and \"You cast Heal on Hilda.\" now show once, then at most once every 10 seconds while you keep casting.","g":["companions","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6159-002","v":"0.1.6159","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"The aim hint always shows again when the spell starts waiting for a target after casting straight away, so an armed spell is never silent.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6159-003","v":"0.1.6159","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"A party member healing you no longer repeats \"Bran casts Heal on you.\" on every cast.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6159-004","v":"0.1.6159","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Professions","t":"Rework","x":"The Professions page descriptions are shorter and plainer.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6159-005","v":"0.1.6159","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Professions","t":"Rework","x":"Herbalism and Hunting now say the search is on the patch's or body's list, not the act-choice key.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6159-006","v":"0.1.6159","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Stores","t":"Rework","x":"With a Materials Bag, the empty Stores page now says gathered goods go into your bag or pack and are put into the Stores in any town.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-001","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Home Prices","t":"Economy","x":"A house's price now depends on how much ground it covers and how big its town is: 300 gold a square metre, multiplied by up to 2.75 in the largest cities.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-002","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Home Prices","t":"Economy","x":"Every home costs between 5,000 and 250,000 gold. For example, a 6 × 6 m cottage in a hamlet costs 10,800, and a 12 × 12 m house in Daggerfall costs 118,800.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-003","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Home Prices","t":"Economy","x":"Before, prices ran as high as 850,000, and a small house could cost more than a big one.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-004","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Economy","x":"A guild hall still costs the home's price and half again, so at most 375,000.","g":["homes","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-005","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Selling Homes","t":"Rework","x":"\"Sell your home for N gold?\" now shows what you will really get back: 85% of what you paid, plus any rent you haven't collected. A home bought before this change sells back for 85% of what it cost then.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-006","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Selling Homes","t":"Fix","x":"Online, the bank now buys back a knightly order's free house at 85% of the same online price the door uses. Before, the bank paid Daggerfall's old price, up to about a million.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-007","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Homes","t":"Fix","x":"The free house from a knightly order is never a building another player already owns.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-008","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Home Prices","t":"Fix","x":"Home and rent prices show thousands separators (45,000 gold, not 45000).","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6167-009","v":"0.1.6167","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Home Prices","t":"Rework","x":"Home and rent lines now say the gold comes from and goes to your account at the Bank of the Empire, which is where it moves online.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6172-001","v":"0.1.6172","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docks","t":"Fix","x":"Port towns' docks now appear even with Naval Combat or Come Sail Away turned off.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6172-002","v":"0.1.6172","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Docks","t":"Fix","x":"Docks now always connect to the town. With Deep Waters on, every dock used to stand alone out on the water about 80 m from shore; each one now has a pier running to land.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-001","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Fix","x":"Shadows no longer go too dark, and candles no longer blow out to white, with Steady shadows on.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-002","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Rework","x":"It now falls only from the two lamps nearest you, as with Steady shadows off. Those two are still redrawn every frame, so nothing flickers.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-003","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Calmer Eye","t":"Rework","x":"Calmer eye is now its own switch, off by default (Settings, Features, Enhanced lighting, beside Steady shadows). It used to come bundled with Steady shadows, so dark rooms stayed dark and candle glare lingered for seconds. Turn it on if the picture still seems to breathe brighter and darker.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-004","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Nearby Quests","t":"New","x":"New Nearby quests switch (Settings, Features, World), on by default. Quests from guilds, temples, nobles and townsfolk now send you to towns and dungeons near where you took them, not anywhere in the region.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-005","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Nearby Quests","t":"New","x":"At level 1, a quest stays within about 10 map squares, a day or two on foot.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-006","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Nearby Quests","t":"New","x":"Each level adds 4 squares. By level 15 or so, anywhere in the region can come up, as in Daggerfall.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-007","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Nearby Quests","t":"New","x":"If fewer than three dungeons of the right kind are close, it picks from the nearest three.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-008","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Nearby Quests","t":"New","x":"A town quest that needs a building no nearby town has looks twice as far, then anywhere in the region.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-009","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Nearby Quests","t":"Other","x":"Quests you already have keep their places. Off is Daggerfall's pick, unchanged. Online, each player's own switch decides their own quests.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-010","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loitering","t":"New","x":"You can loiter online again, with no camp, fire or bed. When the rest window can't let you rest (no fire or bed nearby, a town's street, or a building that won't let you sleep), it now offers Loiter.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-011","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loitering","t":"New","x":"You can loiter at a fire too: while settling in to rest, press 3 (or your Loiter key), or click Loiter Instead.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-012","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loitering","t":"Other","x":"Loitering works as in Daggerfall: choose the hours, up to your Loiter limit.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-013","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loitering","t":"Other","x":"It heals nothing and doesn't count as a night's sleep.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-014","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loitering","t":"Other","x":"Monsters can interrupt it, and it commits no crime.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-015","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Loitering","t":"Other","x":"Online it doesn't bring on night or shorten a quest's waits.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-016","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire Kit","t":"New","x":"General Stores and Pawn Shops always stock a Campfire Kit and a stack of 99 Rations, with Climates & Calories on or off. Online they never run out. Offline they sell out until the shop restocks the next day, like the rest of the shelf.","g":["camping","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-017","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Rations","t":"Rework","x":"Rations and other food can always be eaten, never refused as \"not hungry\". They give back stamina by how filling they are (rations about a quarter of your stamina). A putrid one is still refused.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6179-018","v":"0.1.6179","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire Kit","t":"Rework","x":"A Campfire Kit can be placed, rested at, cooked at, stoked and packed. Only a fire's warmth still needs Climates & Calories.","g":["camping","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-001","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quest items standing on beds, dressers and shelves inside houses can now be picked up. The furniture took the click meant for them, which blocked the Thieves Guild's \"The Qualifying Examination\": the robes you are sent to steal often stand on furniture.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-002","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Houses","t":"Fix","x":"Shelves in ordinary houses no longer swallow your clicks. They were never usable there.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-003","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quest items lying in the world now show their name when you look at them, and a quest letter reads as \"Letter: …\" rather than \"Parchment\".","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-004","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Taking a quest item with quick loot, the right-click / long-press menu, or the gamepad's X now counts as picking it up. Quests that react to the pickup now advance, such as the Thieves Guild's note tucked in the robes or a letter a foe carries.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-005","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"In a party with a shared quest, a sync that arrives just as you pick up a quest item, or click a quest character, no longer undoes it.","g":["quests","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-006","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hall of Records","t":"Fix","x":"In a castle while the seats are open, the shelves are always the Hall of Records; a click meant to read no longer sometimes searches the shelf.","g":["seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-007","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Decor","t":"Fix","x":"A candle or other piece standing on a decor dresser can be clicked past the dresser's mirror.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6190-008","v":"0.1.6190","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Roads","t":"Performance","x":"Roads are painted onto new terrain about five times faster.","g":["roads","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-001","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Primarch, a new title made for GA00250. It is drawn in the same light gold the pause menu uses for names.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-002","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"The Primarch glyph: GA00250's own three-barred cross, shown beside the name in the same gold.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-003","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"Golden Radiance, a new aura: a column of golden light around the character, brightest at the edges so the character stays clear inside it. Golden motes rise through it, and a ring of light with turning rays lies at the feet. The light rises from the feet when you put it on. In first person you see the light at your feet, but your view is never tinted gold.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-004","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Titles","t":"Other","x":"Wear the title and the aura from the account card.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-005","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Founder","t":"Fix","x":"Founder title: if you played before the Founder cutoff in one browser or on one device and made your account somewhere else (the desktop app especially), you now get Founder too, as long as at least one of your characters made it onto the new account (a cloud save, its Renown, or a realm character).","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-006","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Other players no longer jump backwards. Near the edge of an area you hear each player through two servers at once, and a late copy of their movement could pull them back a step. You now follow each player through one server at a time, and switch to whichever one is quicker.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-007","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"No more teleporting in sieges, Royal Tourneys, and player homes and ships. Running players there jumped forward on almost every step. Now they run.","g":["online","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-008","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Smoother players on a rough connection. After a lag spike, players catch up at no more than twice their speed instead of dashing ahead, and small hiccups no longer make them stop and start. They also no longer freeze for a moment every time their movement arrives.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-009","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"A player stepping into a new area no longer snaps back to where they stood when they first connected.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-010","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Players move at the pace they actually moved. Every movement update now carries the moment it was sent, so other players are drawn at their own pace rather than the pace their updates happened to arrive. After a hiccup they catch up more gently, and they are drawn a little closer to where they really are.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-011","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Server","t":"Performance","x":"A lighter server, ready for more players. The server now does much less work for each player: reconnecting no longer rewrites your details, moving no longer re-saves your connection, and busy areas pick who hears you without re-sorting everyone on every step. It also stops waiting on a stuck part of the server instead of hanging on it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6206-012","v":"0.1.6206","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Server","t":"Performance","x":"Empty areas go quiet. When nobody else is in your area, your game stops sending its enemies, its memory of the place and your ship's cabin to the server; the party map only updates while a party member is online; and the regular cloud checkpoint skips a save that hasn't changed. The enemies, the place and the cabin are sent in full the moment someone arrives.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6215-001","v":"0.1.6215","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Boarding","t":"Fix","x":"Enemies in the water no longer count as \"enemies nearby\" while you're aboard a boat. A fish under the hull no longer resets the time speed-up at the helm, stops a journey, slows overworld travel, or stops you resting or making camp aboard. Enemies on your deck or on shore still count, and so does anything while you're swimming.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6215-002","v":"0.1.6215","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Campfire","t":"Fix","x":"Campfires and tents placed on a boat's deck now stay on the boat as she sails. If the boat is packed away, put in storage, or its owner leaves, your camp goes back into your pack with its uses intact.","g":["camping","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6215-003","v":"0.1.6215","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Helm Controls","t":"Rework","x":"W/S and the up/down arrows now do the same thing at the helm. Each press moves you one step along a single ladder: rowing backward, stopped, rowing forward, sails up, then full sail on ships with square sails. Rowing is now a speed you set rather than a key you hold, and taking in the last sail leaves her rowing forward. A/D and the left/right arrows steer. End, and the helm panel's sails button, still raise or stow all sail at once.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6218-001","v":"0.1.6218","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"New","x":"Developers can now stage the Sun Baby for everyone online with /event sunbaby (end it with /event sunbaby off or /event off).","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6218-002","v":"0.1.6218","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"New","x":"The sky turns a bright nursery blue full of drifting flowers, and a big giggling baby-faced sun rises out of the east.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6218-003","v":"0.1.6218","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"New","x":"The weather clears while it lasts - no rain, snow or storms - and the land is lit like a sunny day at any hour.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-001","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"Quest people, foes and items no longer appear under floors, in attics, inside stairs or outside walls in some Beautiful Cities and Beautiful Villages buildings.","g":["mod","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-002","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"34 Arkay temples in Beautiful Villages that were left with no houses are back to their classic layout, so their quests can start again.","g":["mod","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-003","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"A quest whose building moved in the new towns no longer sends you to a tavern or a stranger's house.","g":["mod","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-004","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Houses","t":"Fix","x":"Entering some houses (Warvale Village among them) no longer drops you into the void or leaves you in the dark. If a room has nowhere to stand you stay outside (\"This house has nothing of value.\"), and if you ever fall below a room you are put back at its door.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-005","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Foes, quest foes included, no longer spawn stuck inside dungeon crates.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-006","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hall of Records","t":"Fix","x":"The Hall of Records book can always be closed.","g":["seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-007","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Camps","t":"Fix","x":"Placing a tent or Campfire when you already have four out now packs away your oldest camp and returns its gear, instead of refusing. Characters locked out of camping can camp again.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-008","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Houses","t":"Fix","x":"A house given by a Knightly Order no longer offers \"Buy it\" at your own door, and other players can no longer buy it.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-009","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"Crop fields no longer grow through walls and buildings, and the rooftop domes stand at their proper size.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-010","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Long sessions no longer pile up GPU memory: places you have left are released after a while.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6247-011","v":"0.1.6247","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Performance","t":"Fix","x":"People, guards and foes no longer pop out of view at the edges of the screen.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6251-001","v":"0.1.6251","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Rework","x":"Party members who rest together at the same camp now share one ambush roll instead of each spawning their own enemies.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6251-002","v":"0.1.6251","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"New","x":"While the camp's roll is decided you'll see \"Resting with <name>...\". Everyone then sleeps the same night, or wakes together if it's ambushed.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6251-003","v":"0.1.6251","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Rest","t":"Rework","x":"An ambush on a resting party tries to keep its distance from every sleeper, not just one.","g":["camping","social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6251-004","v":"0.1.6251","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Party Leader","t":"New","x":"Party leaders can hand the lead to another online member with Make leader in the Party tab. Everyone in the party is told.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-001","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hired Traders","t":"New","x":"Hire a trader for your home: place a figure from the decorator's new Vendors category and make it the Hired trader station (25,000 gold, online). Put pieces from your pack up for sale at it; they stay up for 30 days.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-002","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hired Traders","t":"New","x":"Visitors buy from your trader inside your house. The Vendors tab on any Notice Board lists the region's traders whose houses you can enter, searchable by item, owner or town.","g":["homes","notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-003","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hired Traders","t":"New","x":"Set waypoint on a trader's house: a gold coin marks its town on both world maps, the house is named on the town map, and the compass points the way.","g":["homes","map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-004","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Vendor Page","t":"New","x":"The new Vendor page (pause menu, under Professions) shows your traders, what is for sale, what has sold, and your takings to collect.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-005","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"The rest bar now heals health, stamina and magicka as it fills. If the rest is interrupted, you keep what it healed.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-006","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Weather","t":"Fix","x":"Rain and snow now fall in front of grass and banners instead of behind them.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6257-007","v":"0.1.6257","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Weather","t":"Fix","x":"Rain keeps falling while you travel on the Overworld map.","g":["weather","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6263-001","v":"0.1.6263","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"Your wagon stays attached to the horse. It no longer stretches out and snaps back when you speed up, stop, turn or cross a slope, whether you ride it or it follows you.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6263-002","v":"0.1.6263","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"On the Overworld your cart's wagon is drawn at your rider's size, attached behind the horse. Other players' wagons stay attached to their riders too.","g":["horse","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6263-003","v":"0.1.6263","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"The wagon, your storage and the Materials Bag now have a search box and a category menu (All, Materials and the nine pack pages).","g":["horse","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6263-004","v":"0.1.6263","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"Shift-click an item in your pack to put the whole stack into your wagon, storage or Materials Bag in one click, with no split popup. In the classic skin this works for the wagon and storage.","g":["horse","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6267-001","v":"0.1.6267","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hunting","t":"Removal","x":"The text hunting minigame (Climates & Calories) no longer runs. You won't get \"You spot a set of animal tracks...\" prompts in the wilderness any more, and no Yes/No search box, result page, or \"You are not the hunter, but the hunted!\" beast follows them.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6267-002","v":"0.1.6267","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Travel","t":"Fix","x":"Long journeys are no longer interrupted by hunting prompts.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6267-003","v":"0.1.6267","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hunting","t":"Other","x":"Hunting the profession (skinning a body you killed with the Skinning Knife) is untouched.","g":["hunting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-001","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Controller Bindings","t":"New","x":"Overworld and Quick dial can be bound in the Controller bindings window, and put on any d-pad tap or hold.","g":["gamepad","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-002","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hotbar","t":"New","x":"Arranging the hotbar on a controller: in any window, press LT to raise the hotbar. Press A on a slot to pick it up, then A on another slot to move or swap it. Y clears a slot. Press LT again when you are done.","g":["gamepad","quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-003","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hotbar","t":"New","x":"Add to hotbar asks which slot. With a controller in hand, the item card's and the spellbook's \"Add to hotbar\" picks the entry up and raises the bar. Press A on a slot, or hold LB/RB and press that slot's own button (X too). All 16 crossbar slots can be reached.","g":["gamepad","quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-004","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Hotbar","t":"Other","x":"Picking up the mouse while something is in hand drops it and lowers the bar.","g":["gamepad","quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-005","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Rework","x":"Arrows and pellets you shoot in a bout are handed back by the healers. Conjured arrows are not, and arrows you drop or sell during a bout are not either.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-006","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Arena of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"The Curse of Daggerfall's ghosts no longer come for you at the arena's gate, in its stands, on the floor or in the undercroft. They wait outside the grounds, and resting there is not interrupted.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-007","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"In two-against-one bouts, an enemy's area spell no longer hits its own partner. A Grand Melee's HUD now says \"each alone\", because every fighter there is on their own side.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-008","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Arena Undercroft","t":"Rework","x":"The undercroft has enemies again in its deep cellars, past the fighters' hall. The hall itself stays peaceful, and resting there is still never interrupted.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-009","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Node distance filter: a \"Nodes\" button picks how far away gathering groups still show: any distance, 0.5, 1 or 2 km.","g":["overworld","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-010","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Carriage towns: towns with a carriage driver at the gate show a wheel on both maps, and the Overworld edges their plate in brass.","g":["overworld","map","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-011","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Name colours: friends' names are blue and guild-mates' names are violet. Your party stays green.","g":["overworld","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-012","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Player filters on both maps: Friends, Guild, Others, and a minimum Renown. On the travel map they sit in the key.","g":["overworld","map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-013","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Town seats: hovering a town that can be captured shows who holds it and this week's battle (mouse only; on touch, the travel map's info box says it). The map's info box also names the holder now; before, it always said \"unheld\".","g":["overworld","map","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-014","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"On horseback in the Overworld, your sprite faces the way you are riding again.","g":["overworld","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6274-015","v":"0.1.6274","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Road Encounters","t":"New","x":"Encounters on the road (World settings, on by default): while you travel, an enemy far below your level (a rat for a level 3+, an imp for a level 6+, an orc for a level 15+) no longer stops you. Other encounters sometimes come as a small patrol. Resting is not travelling.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6279-001","v":"0.1.6279","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"New","x":"/event sunbaby now cycles: the laughing sun baby turns evil — a red, horned, grinning sun over a burning sky — and rains fireballs on Daggerfall, then calms down, then becomes Todd Howard over sixteen times the flowers. It just works.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6279-002","v":"0.1.6279","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"Other","x":"Everyone online sees the same phase at the same time. The fireballs are harmless.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6281-001","v":"0.1.6281","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"Fix","x":"The sun now snaps between its faces in a second instead of slowly melting.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6281-002","v":"0.1.6281","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sun Baby","t":"Fix","x":"Todd Howard's phase now shows Todd Howard himself.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-001","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Portal Stone","t":"New","x":"Every shop now sells the Portal Stone for 5 Welkynd Shards (the shards you get by salvaging Magic, Rare and Legendary gear). Find it on the shopkeeper's menu, under \"Portal Stone (5 shards)\", or press P on the classic interface. Shops never run out.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-002","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Portal Stone","t":"New","x":"Use a stone from your pack or hotbar while outdoors and pick any place on the map. A portal opens two metres in front of you and stays open for 30 seconds.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-003","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Portal Stone","t":"New","x":"Anyone who walks into it travels there instantly, including other players nearby when you are online. Bring your friends.","g":["portals","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-004","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Portal Stone","t":"Other","x":"One stone opens one portal. Stones are bound to you: they can't be sold, traded or dropped.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-005","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Portal Stone","t":"Other","x":"A portal won't open, and won't take you, while enemies are nearby, during a duel, in a siege, or while you are travelling a route. It needs open ground with room in front of you, and won't open in water or aboard a boat.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-006","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Portal Stone","t":"New","x":"Every existing character receives 10 Portal Stones, once, the next time it is loaded. They join any stones you already carry.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6289-007","v":"0.1.6289","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Welkynd Shards","t":"Fix","x":"Welkynd Shards you are wearing as a crystal are no longer spent by the Reforge or a shop.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-001","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"A new online world event. Every four hours a great sea serpent rises on one of the Iliac Bay's packet lanes, out in open sea.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-002","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Bells ring in the harbours fifteen minutes before it rises. The chat names the port it lies off and the local time it rises, the map rings its waters, and inside the ring your compass points the way.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-003","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Sail out and fight it from your deck with your ship's guns. Every ship that joins makes it tougher by the same measure as her own guns, so a fleet of any size fights it for about the same length of time. It is a fight to meet up for: one ship alone cannot bring it down, and a fleet of three or more can.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-004","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"The Hunt: it lashes with its tail, rams down a lane, bursts up under its mark and spits venom that pools on the decks.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-005","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"The Coil (from two-thirds health): it wraps a ship and crushes her if left alone. Focus fire on the coils to break them - every blow on a coil hurts the serpent too - and it lies stunned: every blow lands half again as hard, and its head takes double.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-006","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"The Maelstrom (from one-third health): a whirlpool drags ships toward its grinding eye while the serpent rears and roars. Its waters are marked on the sea as it forms, and every ship can sail out of it.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-007","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Its boss bar names each attack as it winds up, warns MOVE when one is aimed at your ship - all the way down a ram's lane - and counts down a coil's health.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-008","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Bracing your guns halves its blows on your hull and canvas, as it does a cannonball's. Your guns lead it as it swims.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-009","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"If your ship is wrecked, the serpent stops going at her, and she stops making it tougher.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-010","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Fifteen minutes after it rises, a storm closes its waters and no new ship can join. Ten minutes after that it dives and is gone.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-011","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Every ship whose guns did their share (a tenth of what she brought to the fight) earns a hoard: gold, a Rare-or-better piece and a Magic-or-better piece. A hand who stood the fight out aboard a ship, close to the serpent, earns gold and a Magic-or-better piece.","g":["events","naval","loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-012","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Each serpent slain is worth six quests of Renown (half for standing it out), and your account card and your inspect card count the serpents you've slain.","g":["events","renown","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-013","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Other","x":"If you were away from its waters when it fell, your share comes to you the next time you're online.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6299-014","v":"0.1.6299","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Other","x":"Guests receive the hoard; only registered accounts keep the count and the Renown.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6304-001","v":"0.1.6304","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"The Timers window (the hourglass on the pause menu) now counts down the sea serpent. You can see when Sethrakul rises, how long until the storm closes its waters, and when it dives. Once the bells ring, the row names the port it lies off.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6304-002","v":"0.1.6304","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Timers","t":"New","x":"The next serpent's rising is shown once the current one is under way.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6304-003","v":"0.1.6304","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Timers","t":"Rework","x":"The hourglass button no longer has the word \"Timers\" beside it; it is the hourglass alone.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6304-004","v":"0.1.6304","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Discord","t":"New","x":"The Discord channel that announces the Oblivion Gates now announces the sea serpent too. The harbour bells are posted 15 minutes before it rises, with where it was sighted, when it rises and when the storm closes its waters. The post pings the same opt-in role as the gate posts, and each time is shown in your own clock.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6304-005","v":"0.1.6304","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Discord","t":"New","x":"When Sethrakul is slain, the channel names the port and the top fighters.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6304-006","v":"0.1.6304","d":"2026-10-04","e":"Discord","t":"Other","x":"A kill is only posted for the site most players' games agree on. A faked fight never reaches Discord.","g":["events","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-001","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"The Market tab can see your Materials Bag and pack again. Since the bag arrived, everything you gathered went there, and the market only looked in your Stores, so it showed nothing to sell. Listing materials and filling buy orders now count what you carry and move it into your Stores first.","g":["market","professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-002","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"New","x":"Buy orders now show on every Notice Board, not just in their own region. You can fill an order from anywhere; if it's in another region, the courier fee comes out of your pay, and the board shows what you'll receive.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-003","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"The List form now says the truth: your listing stands on every board in the Bay, and buyers outside your region pay a courier.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-004","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"A gold purchase that's refused (because the listing sold or its price moved) now gives your gold back exactly as it was paid. It used to come back as coins in your purse, even if a letter of credit or your bank account had paid; a large letter could come back as more coin than you can carry.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-005","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"The same fix applies to founding a guild, guild deposits, renting a room, buying a home and paying for decor.","g":["market","guild","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-006","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Buying the 20th unit of a 1-silver listing no longer fails and retries forever.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-007","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Filling single units of a 1-silver order no longer gives a wrong reason, and the last unit can always be filled.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-008","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Pressing Buy again after a lost connection no longer buys twice.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-009","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"The market tab no longer goes blank while another action finishes.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-010","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Crafted pieces with the same name now show their quality and wear in the List form, and every piece you carry is offered, even past 64.","g":["market","crafting","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-011","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"A closed market says why instead of the tab vanishing. A failed load keeps its filters and the Weavers' and Apothecaries' counters.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-012","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Messages after an action no longer follow you to other views, and an open dropdown no longer snaps shut.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-013","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Hired Traders","t":"Fix","x":"Your home trader's stock has its own limit of 60 and no longer uses up your 30 board listings.","g":["market","homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6309-014","v":"0.1.6309","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"The Materials view always includes your own region's listings.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-001","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"SirMcMobdon's own aura, granted with the Shadow Fang title and glyph. Wear it from the account card's aura picker.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-002","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"A hooded cape of living shadow with crimson accents: a red lining, a stitched mantle, wolf's-teeth embroidery down its opening, and a hem that frays into trailing smoke.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-003","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"The wearer's wolf glyph is on its back and its clasp. Emblems of the glyph rise off the back and fade away.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-004","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"It casts a pool of shadow at the wearer's feet and kindles in from the hem when first worn.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-005","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"In third person the cape hangs from your body's own shoulders, head and knees as they animate. Crouching presses it down, and a striding knee pushes the cloth out.","g":["online","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-006","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"It trails behind a run or a strafe, swings past and settles when you stop, lags behind a turn, and lifts as you fall.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-007","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"It folds away while you ride. Other players see your cape hang and swing on your body the same way.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-008","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"Transforming into a werewolf tears the cloak apart along its seams, with embers along the tears. Its shreds float around the beast.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-009","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"It forms again when you turn back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6320-010","v":"0.1.6320","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"The account card said \"Wearing shadowcloak.\" (an aura's internal key). It now shows the aura's name, for every aura.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-001","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"SquidKamer's Low Poly Trees is in the game: the trees, bushes and stumps of the wilderness and of every town's gardens stand as real 3D models instead of flat pictures - 253 of them, across every climate and its winter.","g":["mod","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-002","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"Each wild tree has its own size and turn, so no two stretches of wood look alike. Trees in towns and gardens keep their size.","g":["mod","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-003","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"The view reaches as far as it always did. Up close you see the 3D tree; further out, a picture made from that same 3D tree stands in its place, and the two fade into each other as you walk. The distant woods draw exactly the trees they drew before, one picture a tree.","g":["mod","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-004","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"Performance","x":"The near trees are drawn only where you are looking, and the mod's pictures are kept only while trees near you use them.","g":["mod","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-005","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"Works with Seasons of the Iliac Bay. A tree takes autumn, spring and snow exactly when its flat would - in the climates the mod changes - and keeps its own colours in the ones it leaves alone. Without the mod, winter brings the trees' own snow-capped winter models.","g":["mod","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-006","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"Other","x":"On by default: Mods -> Low Poly Trees. Turning it off brings back the classic trees the next time the world loads.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-007","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"Other","x":"Felling a tree for Logging still works as before, and a tree still gives the same cover in a fight.","g":["mod","logging"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6330-008","v":"0.1.6330","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"Other","x":"The trees' leaves and bark are painted from your own Daggerfall files when the world loads, so nothing extra is downloaded beyond the mod's shapes (about 3 MB).","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-001","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"The developers' own aura. Wear it from the account card's aura picker.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-002","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"Wings of flowing golden light grow from the wearer's back. Each wing has long plumes and short inner feathers, with waves of light running out along them.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-003","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"The wings breathe slowly and beat once every eight seconds. Sparks streak out past their tips, and a soft glow with turning rays shines behind the shoulders.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-004","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"They cast a pool of gold at the wearer's feet and a gold light on the world around them.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-005","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"They sit on the wearer's back on both Morrowind bodies and Eye of the Beholder sprites, and they lean, turn and trail with the body.","g":["online","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-006","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Rework","x":"An aura you put on or take off now shows to everyone around you within a second or two. Before, they saw it only after you changed area.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-007","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Rework","x":"Up to 32 auras are drawn at once (was 16).","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-008","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"A player who drops out of sight for a moment no longer has their aura start over from nothing.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-009","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"The cloak and the wings now sit at the sprite's real shoulders. Before, they floated well above the head whenever a weapon, staff or spell was out.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-010","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"They face the way your sprite faces. Walking backward, the cloak no longer covers your sprite's face.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-011","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"The cloak is no longer drawn around your camera in first person.","g":["online","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-012","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Rework","x":"While you swim, the cloak folds away and the wings close.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-013","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"Players in beast form now carry the wings at the beast's own shoulders.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-014","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"The Golden Radiance no longer vanishes when you look down on its wearer from high above.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6337-015","v":"0.1.6337","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"The Seraph Wings' light stays gold in dungeons.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6339-001","v":"0.1.6339","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"In first person, looking down no longer washes your view in gold from the wings' backlight.","g":["online","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6339-002","v":"0.1.6339","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"After swimming, the Seraph Wings open again when you ride or crouch. Before, they stayed closed and unlit, and the Holo Shadow Cloak stayed folded.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6339-003","v":"0.1.6339","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"The tip of every wing strand no longer shows a faint twist.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6341-001","v":"0.1.6341","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"On Eye of the Beholder skins the wings now sit farther back and no longer clip through the body when seen from the side or at an angle.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6341-002","v":"0.1.6341","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"Before your first step, the wings now hang behind you instead of over your sprite's face.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6341-003","v":"0.1.6341","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Rework","x":"The wings are slimmer, shorter and much softer: fewer, thinner strands of pale gold, a smaller and fainter glow behind the shoulders, and a dimmer light on the ground and the world around you.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-001","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Rework","x":"Arena fighters now telegraph their heavy blows at each other, not just at you - step out of the marked ground.","g":["arena","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-002","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Rework","x":"Losing a ladder bout resets that tier's run; every tier's champion is an elite.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-003","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Rework","x":"No potions or cheese spells (Invisibility, Chameleon, Shadow, Levitate, Calm, Charm, Teleport) in ladder bouts, and a height ceiling over the sand. Bouts between players keep their kit.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-004","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Rework","x":"Winning a ladder bout you have won before pays no purse, points or Renown.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-005","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Rework","x":"The online ladder needs a registered account, and each ticket is good for one bout.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-006","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Rework","x":"Online, the champions run, look elite, and a time-out needs real damage on the judges' card; a tie is a draw.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-007","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Ladder","t":"Fix","x":"Fixes: a run that could get stuck for good, champions fleeing as revenants, a worn ring losing its effect after a bout, collapsing mid-bout resting an hour, Recall off the sand.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6350-008","v":"0.1.6350","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"A quest's foe that is not yet hostile now shows \"Quest: <title>\" under its name on the enhanced plaque.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6363-001","v":"0.1.6363","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Homes","t":"Fix","x":"Graveyard crypts are no longer sold as homes. The crypts in graveyards (Wayrest's, the Wickcroft Tombs' and 65 others) were for sale online, but they have no inside: entering one only said \"This house has nothing of value.\" They are no longer offered. If you already bought one, you can still sell it back at its door.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6363-002","v":"0.1.6363","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"The Possessed Child can be finished in Tigonus. In some houses Beautiful Cities builds a cellar and then lays a floor over its stairs. A quest person or item that was placed in such a cellar now stands upstairs, next to the covered stairs (128 buildings).","g":["quests","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6363-003","v":"0.1.6363","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Beautiful Villages","t":"Fix","x":"Houses and the stone gazebo no longer float. Beautiful Villages builds on hills, for example around Ipsham's temple and at the roadside taverns' gazebo. Those hills are now drawn at their real size and shape, so what stands on them is back on the ground.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6363-004","v":"0.1.6363","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Dying","t":"Fix","x":"Dying clears paralysis. After you respawn online, any paralysis from a ghost or spider is gone, and so are a wraith's silence and any fatigue or magicka drain. Diseases still carry over.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6363-005","v":"0.1.6363","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Fishing","t":"Fix","x":"\"Open Water\" only appears over water. The fishing net no longer offers a cast while you are looking at the beach, and a net you are still winding up can't be thrown onto the sand.","g":["fishing","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6363-006","v":"0.1.6363","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Resting","t":"Rework","x":"Dungeon beds count as beds. Online, you can now rest at a bed in a dungeon, the same way you rest at a campfire. The bed must be on your floor. Palace beds don't count, and resting at a bed doesn't use up a Bedroll lying next to it.","g":["camping","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-001","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Loading Screens","t":"New","x":"Loads now have a face. Starting or continuing a game, going online, a dungeon's door, a fast travel, a guild teleport, Recall, a respawn and a save loaded in play all show a loading screen: where you are headed, what the game is doing, and a running bar.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-002","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Loading Screens","t":"New","x":"The screen stands on one of your own screenshots, with where and when you took it - or, with none, on the main menu's night sky and a tip.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-003","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Loading Screens","t":"Other","x":"It never covers something you need to see: character creation, the pause menu, a level-up and the dream videos all come first, and the screen comes back only if the world is still loading.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-004","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Loading Screens","t":"New","x":"Choose Your screenshots, Night sky or Off on the new Loading screens tile under Features (Interface). The Classic UI is unchanged.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-005","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Screenshots","t":"New","x":"The screenshot key (F8 by default) now also keeps every shot in a gallery in your browser - up to 120, and nothing is ever uploaded.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-006","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Screenshots","t":"New","x":"A new Screenshots page: on the main menu (bottom right, beside About) and on the pause menu's System tab. Open a shot large, choose which ones appear on loading screens, save one to your files, delete one, or add pictures from your computer.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6368-007","v":"0.1.6368","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Screenshots","t":"New","x":"A switch on that page decides whether the key still downloads a PNG as well (on, as before).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-001","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"Rework","x":"An enemy winding up a telegraphed attack no longer drops it at the first scratch. Hits landed during the wind-up fill a poise meter (shown under its health bar on the Enhanced HUD); heavy weapons, hits to its back and hits to its weakness fill it faster. Fill it and the wind-up shatters: the enemy is staggered for about a second, helpless and taking 25% more damage.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-002","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Iron attacks (red and hatched - a giant's slam, an elite's heaviest, a revenant's signature) cannot be interrupted. Get out of the way.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-003","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Missing costs the enemy. An attack that hits nobody leaves its enemy open for about a second, taking 30% more - and your first hit staggers it. Step out of the attack in its last moment for a perfect dodge and a longer opening.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-004","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Missing costs the enemy. An attack that hits nobody leaves its enemy open for about a second, taking 30% more - and your first hit staggers it. Step out of the attack in its last moment for a perfect dodge and a longer opening.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-005","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"You can read it coming: the body glints as the wind-up begins and again just before it lands, with a sound for each, and the mark on the ground is easier to see.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-006","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Wind-ups vary in length, lunges track you for their first half, skilled blade-fighters sometimes feint (a feint never glints - the glint is the honest tell), and brutes chain two blows.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-007","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"New attacks: the ring (safe at its feet), the charge from range, the leap onto where you stand, and an archer's aimed shot you can step off. Landings now do something: a lunge pushes you back, a sweep makes you bleed, a slam rattles you, and an iron slam knocks you down.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-008","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"Rework","x":"Champions and revenants telegraph at any level; elites and revenants more often, and with their kind's whole set of attacks.","g":["enhanced-ai","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-009","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Telegraphed Attacks","t":"New","x":"Online, everyone sees an enemy's wind-up, and enemies wind up at other players too - each player dodging on their own screen.","g":["enhanced-ai","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-010","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A revenant learns from how you beat it and comes back adapted - mail against your blades, warded against your fire, arrow-wise against your bow, patient against your dodging. At most three adaptations, never immunity.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-011","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Every revenant has a hidden weakness - an element, a metal, a weapon or the daylight. Strike it to reveal it: it takes 50% more and staggers twice as easily. Its own flinches, and the townsfolk, hint at it.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-012","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"From rank 3 its will must be broken before it will kneel: strike its weakness, stagger it, or perfectly dodge its attack. If you don't, it escapes at the killing blow - stronger, and adapted again.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-013","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"The last stand: from rank 3, the first killing blow brings it roaring back instead (at 30%, 35% or 40% of its health by rank) - faster, harder, ember-lit, with a burst around it. Once a stand.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-014","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"From rank 2 it has a signature attack named for it (\"Grushnak's Skullsplitter\"), iron from rank 3, and a band of one to three of its kin, who scatter when it falls.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-015","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"The hunt: each revenant has a lair, a named dungeon near where it was made. Ask around (\"Any news?\") and townsfolk may tell you where - and sometimes its weakness. Once heard of, the lair is marked on your maps and in your journal; walk in and you will find it resting there.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-016","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"It takes something: online, a revenant that kills you takes one of your unlocked items. Kill it or spare it to get it back.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-017","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"It festers: left alone past its due day it grows stronger, and three times over it ranks up on its own.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-018","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"New ways to make one: a special enemy that knocks out your companion, or one you run from, becomes a revenant too.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-019","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Sworn companions have loyalty: kept well they are devoted (and warn you of an attack from behind); neglected, they desert; and a disloyal Unhinged, Craven or Brutal one may turn on you once your health falls under a quarter.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6410-020","v":"0.1.6410","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"The Revenants page (Holdings tab) and the revenant's card show everything you know - its habits, weakness, will, signature, band, lair, what it took and how long it has festered - and it speaks every new moment in its own voice.","g":["revenants","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-001","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk are no longer strangers who appear and vanish. Every town's people are residents with a name, a face, a home and a trade - the baker, the smith, the innkeeper, the priests, the watch - and they keep them for good.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-002","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Each has a day: they get up (early birds and night owls), go to work, run errands at the shops, meet friends in the square, spend the evening at the tavern or the temple, and go home to bed. The watch walks its beat in shifts.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-003","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Online, everyone sees the same people in the same places at the same time.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-004","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"They stop and talk among themselves, and greet you as you pass - by name, once they count you a friend.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-005","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Doors open: step into a tavern in the evening, a shop or a temple, or a house, and the people whose day has them there are inside - talking at the tables, and now and then getting up to cross the room. Nobody walks into your own home.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-006","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Merchants, pilgrims, couriers, pedlars and adventurers travel between towns by day and camp by night. Merchants hire sellswords and travel in caravans; anyone armed puts on their gear before they leave town.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-007","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Travellers meet the land's monsters. Come upon a party under attack and you can fight beside them - save them and they will remember it; arrive too late and the fallen stay dead, and a newcomer takes their place in time. The towns talk about what happened on their roads.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-008","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"In port towns, sailors crew the ships that call there, and travellers sail across the Bay - now and then one is lost at sea.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-009","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"On the Overworld, parties on the road are marked, and a party in trouble shows in red.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-010","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Adventurers dive the dungeons near their towns. Meet a company down there and they fight at your side.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-011","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Some never come up. Their remains lie where they fell for three days, with what they carried and a keepsake - bring it home to their family, and the town will talk of it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-012","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"What you do changes how each person feels about you: a kind word, help in a fight, a life saved - or a blow, a theft, a crime they saw.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-013","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"A friend greets you by name and comes to your aid on the road. An enemy will not speak to you, and an armed one will draw on you beyond the town walls.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-014","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Striking down a resident is permanent: their household turns against you, and every witness counts the crime.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-015","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Chronicle","t":"New","x":"The chronicle (L) has a new People page: your friends, your enemies, the people who know you, and the dead.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-016","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Travel Options","t":"Removal","x":"The Travel Options speed dials are gone: a journey runs at x100 on a road or track, and x60 off it.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-017","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Travel","t":"Rework","x":"Wilderness enemies only come for a fast traveller who fails a Stealth check. An enemy that has noticed you wears a \"!\" and slows the journey; one that has not leaves you be.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-018","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Travel","t":"Removal","x":"Online, the ship's time dial is gone - time at sea keeps the world's pace.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-019","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"Other","x":"Living world is on by default, on its tile under Features (World); a change takes effect when a town next loads. Off - or on the Classic UI - towns keep Daggerfall's own wandering townsfolk.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6444-020","v":"0.1.6444","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Living World","t":"Performance","x":"Tuned for big cities: the living world's work in the largest city was cut from up to 120 ms a frame to a few milliseconds, and arriving in a town no longer hitches.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-001","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Vanilla Enhanced","t":"New","x":"Vanilla Enhanced now ships with the game, and it is the default look. It is carademono's remaster of Daggerfall's own textures: the ground, the trees and rocks, the city walls and the dungeons. There is nothing to download.","g":["mod","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-002","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Overhaul","t":"New","x":"Prefer Daggerfall's own textures? Pick Classic on the Texture Overhaul card. Your choice is remembered, and Classic switches your texture mods off without removing them.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-003","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Overhaul","t":"New","x":"While Vanilla Enhanced is worn, the card offers its two add-ons as switches: Masked Roads (by carademono and Kokey) and Snowless Swamps and Jungles. The card remembers your add-ons when you switch back to Classic.","g":["mod","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-004","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Overhaul","t":"Performance","x":"The new textures are decoded in the background, so loading them doesn't stutter the game.","g":["mod","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-005","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Mods","t":"Rework","x":"Texture mods now load in Daggerfall Unity's order. A mod loads after the mods it is built on. Where two mods carry the same texture, the one loaded later is drawn.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-006","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Mods","t":"New","x":"Each texture mod can be switched off and on without removing it, on the Replacement packs card at the foot of Features. The built-in mods are listed there too.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-007","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Mods","t":"Fix","x":"Switching texture mods mid-game now applies to everything drawn after the switch. Before, a switch could leave a mix of classic and new textures until the page was reloaded. What is already on screen keeps its look until its area loads again.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-008","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Overhaul","t":"Fix","x":"The Texture Overhaul card on the main menu now sees the texture mods you attached. Before, it could show \"Classic\" while your mods were on.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-009","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Mods","t":"New","x":"A texture mod that can't be read is now listed on the Replacement packs card with the reason and a Remove button.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-010","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Overhaul","t":"New","x":"With a loose texture pack attached, the card explains why Classic can't be picked, and how to remove the pack.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-011","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Vanilla Enhanced","t":"Rework","x":"If you attach your own copy of Vanilla Enhanced (for example a newer version from Nexus Mods), it is used instead of the built-in one.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6453-012","v":"0.1.6453","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Texture Mods","t":"Fix","x":"Ground textures now appear on the terrain, as in Daggerfall Unity, when they come from a loose texture pack or from a mod that ships the ground tile by tile.","g":["mod","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-001","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Main Menu","t":"New","x":"Two new icons in the main menu's top-left corner: Patreon and Ko-fi. Each opens its page in your browser (from the desktop app, your system browser). Hover one and it lights up; it is reachable with the keyboard and a controller too.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-002","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Main Menu","t":"Fix","x":"The main menu no longer gets cut off on short windows, such as a 720p screen in a browser. The logo always shows in full, and the menu scrolls down to its last button.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-003","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Main Menu","t":"Fix","x":"On narrow and mid-size windows, the logo now sits below the corner icons and your profile picture instead of underneath them.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-004","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Website","t":"New","x":"The website now offers Ko-fi beside Patreon in its top-right corner (https://ko-fi.com/daggerfallonline).","g":["website"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-005","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Fire: a fireball bloom. Embers are thrown out and fall, land and smoulder. Flame licks up, and a scorch glow and a shock ring spread on the floor.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-006","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Frost: a splash crown of droplets that rain down and ripple where they land, ice glints winking on the floor, and cold mist.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-007","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Shock: jagged lightning arcs strike from the impact into the floor, flickering and re-striking, while fast sparks skitter away.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-008","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Poison: green globs are lobbed out and splat into small bubbling pools, under a sickly vapour.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-009","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Magic: motes spiral out over rune rings.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-010","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Heal: a still, soft green glow on the floor with thin lines of light rising out of it. There is no shockwave and no ring. It shows on yourself, a party mate, your companion, a touch, or an area heal.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-011","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Every element's burst takes its colour from that element's own spell art in your game files, so the light matches the missile you just watched fly. Heals keep their green. Touch spells now show a small burst where they land.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-012","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Area Spells","t":"New","x":"Area at Range and Area around Caster now show exactly what they catch. A person is caught out to about 4.45 m, and the world boss out to about 5.8 m. A shockwave and racing sparks run out to that edge, and the edge glows for a moment.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-013","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Area Spells","t":"New","x":"The shockwave spreads across whatever the spell hit. A fireball that strikes a wall at chest height bursts as a ring on the wall, and the same goes for ceilings.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-014","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Area Spells","t":"New","x":"Bigger areas show more. The element breaks out across the whole area as the shockwave passes. Area heals fill the circle with rising light.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-015","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"New","x":"Impacts briefly light up the walls and floor around them in the element's colour.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-016","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Sounds","t":"New","x":"Fire: a whumpf and crackle.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-017","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Sounds","t":"New","x":"Poison: a squelch and bubbles.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-018","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"Other","x":"The classic flash, the bloom and the camera kick stay. There are fewer element-art sparks now.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-019","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Spell Bursts","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: sparks no longer jump away when the world recentres mid-burst, and none are left behind after a load or a teleport.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-020","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Interface","t":"Fix","x":"Text and buttons in the client no longer light up with a blue selection highlight when you click or drag. Text fields can still be selected.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-021","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Decorator","t":"New","x":"The house decorator now offers the town mods' furnishings while those mods are on (Beautiful Villages, Beautiful Cities and Detailed Ships). That adds 297 pieces: the coloured beds, the paintings, tapestries and banners, rugs and hangings, set tables and stocked shelves, the captain's sea chest, the weapon rack, and more. Online, these mods are on for everyone.","g":["homes","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-022","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Decorator","t":"New","x":"Turning one of those mods on or off now changes what the decorator offers within a second. A mod turned on mid-game has its pieces offered and priced; a mod turned off stops offering them.","g":["homes","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-023","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Decorator","t":"New","x":"The decorator now offers what Daggerfall stands in its dungeons: thrones, cages, coffins, statues, chains, braziers, the knight's armour, weapons and wall hangings.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-024","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Decorator","t":"New","x":"A yard now offers Daggerfall's street pieces (fences, wells, fountains, carts, lamp posts) and the trees and plants of its own town's climate. They are drawn in the town's climate and season, Seasons of the Iliac Bay included, and so is the placement preview of a fence or a well.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-025","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Decorator","t":"New","x":"A tree or plant placed in a yard shows its own picture under \"In this yard\".","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-026","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"With Low Poly Trees on, a tree or plant placed in a yard now stands as the mod's 3D tree up close and as its picture far away, like the world's own trees. It is sized and turned the way you placed it, and the placement preview shows the same tree.","g":["mod","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-027","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"Fix","x":"A yard tree whose picture was still loading as you travelled no longer appears far from its yard.","g":["mod","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-028","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Hired Traders","t":"Rework","x":"With Show Nudity off, the house decorator's Vendors no longer offer nude figures. A figure already placed in a house, ship, yard or guild hall now stands, moves and shows in the decorator's lists as its clothed stand-in, like the world's own people. It stays the same trader with the same stock.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6480-029","v":"0.1.6480","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Arena Crowd","t":"Rework","x":"The Arena crowd no longer seats nude figures while Show Nudity is off.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-001","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Flylighter now holds the Crystal Fist title, shown in purple, with its own glyph beside the name: three purple slashes.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-002","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Titles","t":"Other","x":"Flylighter keeps the Disciple title too. Pick which title to wear from the account card.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-003","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"A ring of tiny purple squares about the feet, stacked into columns that rise and fall like a music visualiser's bars.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-004","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Other","x":"It comes with the Crystal Fist title. Wear it from the account card's Aura row.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-005","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"On an Eye of the Beholder character, the developers' wings now stay lined up with the sprite as it turns.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-006","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Auras","t":"Fix","x":"This holds on a key press, while the camera moves round, in the saddle, and on other players.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6491-007","v":"0.1.6491","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Developers","t":"New","x":"RookieG is now a developer.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6495-001","v":"0.1.6495","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"Fix","x":"Steep ramps in hallways now fill in on the 3D dungeon map once you have walked them, like the corridors around them.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6495-002","v":"0.1.6495","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Boats","t":"Fix","x":"A boat or ship whose hold is too heavy to carry packed can no longer be picked up into parts nobody could carry. \"Pick up\" now says \"her hold is too heavy\", and fast travel or a landfall leaves her moored. Lighten her hold to pack her.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6495-003","v":"0.1.6495","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Teleporters","t":"Fix","x":"Red brick teleporters you walk into now always send you on. Before, some only worked when clicked.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6495-004","v":"0.1.6495","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Sworn revenants and crew ashore now go after the enemy fighting you first, instead of standing still or wandering toward an idle enemy behind a wall.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6495-005","v":"0.1.6495","d":"2026-10-05","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"The Haunted House (and other quests SEALED-CELLAR fixed): if you saved inside the house while the foe was in the sealed cellar, it now stands by the hatch when you load.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-001","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Buff","x":"Regular (non-elite) enemies leave more of what they carry. Offline they keep 3 of every 4 items, up from half. Online it depends on your Renown: 5 of every 8 at Renown 1, 3 of every 4 at Renown 20, and 7 of every 8 at Renown 40.","g":["loot","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-002","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Buff","x":"Regular enemies drop blue, yellow and orange items more often, and online this boost also grows with your Renown. Blue is still rare, yellow is very rare, and orange is still almost impossible.","g":["loot","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-003","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Other","x":"The boost steps up at Renown 10, 20, 30 and 40, the same steps sigils use. Online, every step pays more than loot did before this update.","g":["loot","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-004","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Other","x":"The Renown that counts belongs to the player whose game rolls the loot. That is yours for the enemies you meet and for every treasure pile, and the host's for the enemies in a shared dungeon.","g":["loot","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-005","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Buff","x":"The weapons and armour an enemy was wearing can now drop as Magic, Rare or better. This covers every enemy, including champions, elites and bosses. Until now worn gear always dropped plain, so most humanoid enemies only ever left plain iron and steel.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-006","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: after you loaded a save, the worn gear of enemies already in the world dropped plain again.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-007","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Rework","x":"When a body is full, it now keeps a potion or rest supply ahead of a plain piece of gear.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-008","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Healing Potions","t":"Buff","x":"Potions of Healing drop more often: about 1 enemy in 13 carries one (it was about 1 in 33; animals never carry potions), and about 1 dungeon treasure pile in 5.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-009","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Restore Power Potions","t":"New","x":"Potions of Restore Power (magicka) now drop too: about 1 enemy in 20, and 1 treasure pile in 10.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-010","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Rest Supplies","t":"New","x":"Rest supplies now drop online (they never did before) and drop more often: about 1 enemy in 14 carries an Ember Jar, Restorative Tonic, Meditation Candle, Waking Salts or Sleeping Draught. Dungeon treasure piles can hold any of those, plus Firewood. Online, General Stores and Alchemists now sell rest supplies too.","g":["loot","camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-011","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Other","x":"These are the offline chances, and the online chances at Renown 20. Online at Renown 1 the boost is half that size, and at Renown 40 it is half again bigger.","g":["loot","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-012","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ember Jar","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: other players saw your Ember Jar's fire as a plain campfire.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-013","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Silver Finds","t":"New","x":"Gathering sometimes turns up silver now. About one harvest in ten (herbs, ore, stone, logs, hides or fish) finds 2–5 silver, up to 30 silver a day.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-014","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Silver Finds","t":"New","x":"Bodies, treasure piles and searches can hold silver: 1–4 silver from about 1 body in 20, 1 treasure pile in 8, and 1 search in 7 that turns something up. That includes dungeon treasure, tavern and guild hall treasure, World of Daggerfall's treasure piles and Deep Waters' chests. Up to 20 silver a day.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-015","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Silver Finds","t":"Other","x":"Each body or pile gets one chance, so leaving a dungeon and coming back doesn't roll it again.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-016","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Silver Finds","t":"Fix","x":"If a find can't reach your account (your connection drops, say), it is kept and sent later, even after a reload.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-017","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Silver Finds","t":"New","x":"Found silver shows as a card under the crosshair (Enhanced Plus), or as a line in chat. The Bank's silver panel shows how much you have found today.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-018","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Silver Finds","t":"Other","x":"Silver finds need you to be online and signed in with a registered account that is at least a week old.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-019","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Every sea serpent hoard now holds a Deadlands Ember, the Oblivion Gate's currency. It spends at the Sigil Broker's insignia counter like an ember from a breach.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-020","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Coilscale","t":"New","x":"A ship that fought the serpent has a 1 in 4 chance to find a piece of Sethrakul's Coilscale, the serpent's own Aetheric set:","g":["events","naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-021","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Coilscale","t":"New","x":"Sea-Scale (2 pieces): frost resistance and Endurance.","g":["events","naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-022","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Coilscale","t":"New","x":"Constrict (4 pieces): each weapon hit on an enemy makes your next hits on that enemy stronger, stacking up to 5 times (bows count). Every enemy has its own stacks, and they fade 6 seconds after your last hit on it.","g":["events","naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-023","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Coilscale","t":"New","x":"Shed Skin (6 pieces): when an enemy's hit takes you below 35% health, you heal part of your health at once. It then needs a few minutes to recover. It doesn't trigger when a death save, like Unbroken or Divine Grace, has already kept you alive.","g":["events","naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-024","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Slaying the serpent now pays 40 silver (20 for a ship that stood by). This counts toward the same 150 silver a day as closing breaches and defending towns.","g":["events","naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-025","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Rework","x":"Set bonuses, sigil weapon bonuses and Legendary powers now switch off in arena bouts against other players, the same way they always did in duels.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-026","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"New","x":"Every character now carries a Wallet. New characters start with one, and existing characters receive one the next time they load.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-027","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"New","x":"It holds your letters of credit, Deadlands Embers and Welkynd Shards, and shows your gold and, online, your silver.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-028","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"Rework","x":"In the Enhanced inventory, letters of credit, Deadlands Embers and Welkynd Shards move off the pages and into the Wallet (on the Valuables page). Pick the Wallet to see what it holds and what your letters are worth. Everything inside works just as it does on the pages: pick a piece to open its card, drag it, Shift-click to stow it, or right-click for its menu.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-029","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"Other","x":"In the classic inventory nothing moves. The Wallet is on the Clothing & Misc page: Use it to see what it holds.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-030","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"New","x":"On the hotbar, pressing the Wallet shows what it holds and fetches your silver for the next press. When it can't show your silver, it says why.","g":["quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-031","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"Other","x":"The Wallet weighs nothing and never leaves your pack. It can't be dropped, sold, traded, put in your wagon or storage, or set out as a home decoration, and revenants can't steal it.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6508-032","v":"0.1.6508","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Wallet","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: letters of credit now show on the Valuables page in the Enhanced inventory. They were filed under Misc.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6510-001","v":"0.1.6510","d":"2026-10-06","e":"City Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed a crash (\"Cannot set properties of null (setting 'conceal')\") that could happen when a city watchman died from his own attack. This could happen when the Ring of Namira turned his blow back on him, or when thorns, Spite of the Spurned or the Wrath of the Warden answered it.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6510-002","v":"0.1.6510","d":"2026-10-06","e":"City Watch","t":"Fix","x":"A watchman no longer flickers out of sight for a moment each time he lands a blow on a monster.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-001","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Rework","x":"The watch now keeps the town day and night. Three eight-hour shifts (from 06:00, 14:00 and 22:00) and a day off, so there are guards on the streets at night too.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-002","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"Patrols walk in pairs, side by side, around their own district of the town. In larger towns a watchman stands at each gate, facing the road.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-003","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"Off duty, a watchman wears his own clothes and is an ordinary townsperson. He changes at home, never in front of you. Larger towns keep a larger watch.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-004","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"A watchman on duty now greets you by your standing with the law of the region: by name if you are honoured, politely if you are respected, with a curt word for a common citizen, a warning if the law has its eye on you, and a reminder that the watch knows your face if you are a known criminal.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-005","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Rework","x":"A first minor offence in a region (picking a pocket, trying a locked door, trespassing or sleeping in the street) now draws a \"Hold!\" warning instead of an arrest. It still costs you standing with the law, and the next one in that region brings the arrest. Serious crimes and known criminals get no warning.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-006","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"A monster that gets into town can now attack townspeople, not just you: it goes for whoever is nearest, and one blow kills a townsperson. Archers, spellcasters and human enemies still leave townspeople alone.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-007","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"The watch now comes to defend townspeople a monster is attacking, just as it does when a monster attacks you.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-008","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Townspeople run from a monster that comes close, along the street rather than through walls, and keep their distance until it has gone. While frightened they don't stop for you, greet you or chat.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-009","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"The watch no longer shouts \"Halt!\" over and over. When it comes for you, the first watchman calls out at once; after that only one of them calls, at most once every 15 seconds, and nobody calls while a window is open.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-010","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Other","x":"All of this is in the living world (the enhanced skin with the living world switched on). Classic play keeps Daggerfall's own watch and townspeople.","g":["law","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-011","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Townspeople who stop to talk now turn to face each other instead of all facing you. Someone who stops for you still turns to you.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-012","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"A group waits until everyone has walked over before anyone speaks. Then they take turns, with pauses between exchanges, and you hear them only while the whole group is there, standing together.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-013","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"People keep the same company for about two minutes before moving on (it used to change every 40 seconds), and each square keeps its own rhythm. The town no longer falls silent all at once and then has ten people talking in the same moment.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-014","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"Much less repetition. The common trades, mornings, days, evenings and nights all have more to say, and nobody starts the same conversation twice in a row. Morning greetings are heard only in the morning, and talk of other places names real towns on the town's roads.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-015","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Indoors, people at a table start talking as soon as they sit down together. Someone who joins waits for the current exchange to end, and the group stays seated while they talk.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-016","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"A stranger who said nothing as you walked past now speaks when you stop in front of them.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-017","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Paying your fine no longer counts as killing the watchman who walked away: his household no longer turns against you, and he goes back to his rounds.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-018","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"A townsperson the watch turns into a guard keeps who they are, and returns to their day when the guard walks away. A watchman killed by a monster is mourned by the town instead of being counted against you.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-019","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Two crimes at the same moment no longer bring more guards than the limit, or turn the same townsperson into a guard twice.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-020","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Online, another player's watch no longer shows the same watchman twice (with the updated server).","g":["law","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-021","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"In the biggest cities the watch now reaches its post by the start of its shift and stays to the end of it.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-022","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Foe Health Bar","t":"Fix","x":"The large dark see-through box that hung under an enemy's health bar is gone. A foe at rest now shows only its thin wind-up track (the strip that fills amber as it winds up a blow), as it was meant to.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-023","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quick Slots","t":"Fix","x":"With the diamond quick-slot style, the status-effect icons that move beside the diamond (on a phone held sideways, or with the chat open) no longer sit on a dark box.","g":["quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-024","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quick Slots","t":"Fix","x":"An empty spell quick-slot no longer leaves a gap under it that pushed the quick block up.","g":["quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-025","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ship Plate","t":"Fix","x":"At sea, an empty fire-barrel battery no longer stretches the gun rose on the ship plate.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-026","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Townspeople no longer stand inside building walls or out over the harbour water. Wherever they stop to chat or wait is now open street, spread around the spot rather than bunched against a wall, and when they move between those places they go round corners instead of through them.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-027","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Townspeople no longer walk on the spot, running into whatever is in front of them, while the game works out their next route (this happened mostly in big cities). They now stand still, then set off from where they are.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6527-028","v":"0.1.6527","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Travellers","t":"Fix","x":"Travellers on the roads no longer camp for the night, fight, or leave their fallen out in the sea where a road runs along the coast. Caught on a wet stretch at dusk, a party walks on to the first dry ground and camps there, and picks up its journey from that camp in the morning. Where no dry ground lies ahead on its road, it walks on to the town it was heading for.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6540-001","v":"0.1.6540","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Other players no longer run in place. When a player's movement stops reaching you - they tabbed out, their connection hiccupped, or the server was restarting - their character used to keep running on the spot (for up to 80 seconds if they never came back). Now they stand still until they move again. That includes players who had already gone quiet before you arrived in their area.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6540-002","v":"0.1.6540","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Crowds","t":"Fix","x":"Distant players in a big crowd walk smoothly. A far-away player whose computer was running at a low frame rate used to stop and start every second or so; now they keep walking.","g":["rendering","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6540-003","v":"0.1.6540","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Performance","x":"Lantern shadows cost much less to prepare. With Steady shadows on (the default), every lantern near a walker or a swaying tree redraws its shadow every frame, and each of its six shadow views used to look over everything in the town to find what to draw. Now each lantern looks once, at what can actually reach it - and a still scene does not look at all. The shadows themselves are exactly what they were.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6540-004","v":"0.1.6540","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Chat Window","t":"Performance","x":"The chat's player list no longer rebuilds and re-sorts itself every frame while the chat is open. On a busy server that was costing the frame more the more players were online. The friends list sorts faster too.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6540-005","v":"0.1.6540","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Settings are read a little faster everywhere.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-001","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quests that wouldn't start in towns redesigned by Beautiful Villages and Beautiful Cities now start. When the mods took away a building a quest needs (a second tavern, enough houses, a weaponsmith, a pawnshop), the quest uses the nearest town that has one. This covers villages that lost a tavern, the Kynareth temples, manors, and Beautiful Cities' shops. A quest that never fit a town, even in Daggerfall's own layout, still isn't offered there.","g":["quests","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-002","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Pothago's Dark Brotherhood contract that needs a weaponsmith now starts, using the nearest one in the next region.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-003","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A quest character whose usual building is gone from their town lives in a house of that town, not in another town.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-004","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Thieves Guild and Dark Brotherhood contracts can be handed in again after a town's layout changes. A temple priest is always found in their own god's temple, and a questor still standing where you met them stays there.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-005","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Shared party quests no longer move their quest location to another building every time the party syncs, and party members see the same house name.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-006","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"An item or person placed in a quest building after it was shared now appears for every party member.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6546-007","v":"0.1.6546","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Temples","t":"Fix","x":"Every Beautiful Villages temple has its god's Daedra summoner again. The summoner stands apart from the priest, so clicking the priest always reaches the priest.","g":["mod","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-001","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Helm Panel","t":"New","x":"A speed readout. At the helm, your ship's speed through the water shows beside her name, in knots.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-002","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Rework","x":"No more tacking. Your ship sails on every heading. Pointed straight into the wind she makes a little over half her best speed; before, she stalled or was blown backwards. She is fastest with the wind behind her, off to one side.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-003","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Buff","x":"More speed. Ships are faster under sail. A galleon with the wind on her side is nearly two thirds faster than before.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-004","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Rework","x":"A storm still drives her harder, up to twice what a fair breeze does. In fog she keeps nearly a third of her speed instead of lying becalmed.","g":["naval","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-005","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Rework","x":"Every ship answers the helm as she did before: she gathers speed, loses it and turns at her new speed as she did at her old one. At her new speed she turns on a wider circle, as a faster ship does.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-006","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sails","t":"Fix","x":"Sails no longer flap uselessly or blow backwards when you point into the wind, and she can no longer get stuck \"in irons\".","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-007","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Helm Controls","t":"Removal","x":"The helm trims the sails itself, so the trim buttons and keys are gone under Responsive.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-008","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sailing","t":"Rework","x":"Overworld travel by sea sails straight for a port that lies upwind instead of zig-zagging. It steers well clear of islands at the new speeds, and sails through fog instead of rowing.","g":["naval","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-009","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Boarding","t":"Fix","x":"Heaving to beside a ship that has struck her colours stops you within boarding reach. At storm speeds it is offered as you come up on her, early enough to stop alongside.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-010","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Fix","x":"Rowing after you strike sail no longer holds your speed: she slows as fast as she does with no oars out, then rows on.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-011","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Online Sea","t":"Fix","x":"In a storm, a galleon or Carrack no longer vanishes from other players' screens.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-012","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Online Sea","t":"Fix","x":"A short hiccup in the connection no longer puts you off a friend's ship you are riding on.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-013","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"It no longer teleports. It swims every move it makes. For a Rising Maw or a coil it dashes at you under the water, and a wake on the surface shows where it is going. The Maelstrom now forms where the serpent is swimming, and always inside its waters.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-014","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"It aims where you are going. A Rising Maw, a coil, a spit or a ram is aimed where your ship will be when it lands. Turn or slow when you see it coming.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-015","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"It closes in on the surface. If you are too far away for it to reach in time, it surges at you above the water, where your guns can hit it, faster than you are sailing up to its own top speed. Outsail it for about 12 seconds and it gives up and picks again.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-016","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"Your hits count. A broadside is judged where the serpent was when the shot landed, so a volley fired just before it moves is no longer wasted.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-017","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Buff","x":"Two ships can win. While exactly two ships are fighting it, its attacks deal two thirds of their damage: blows, coils, the Maelstrom and venom alike, crew losses included. A rowboat or a friend riding on your deck is not a second ship. In fair weather one ship alone still cannot beat it. Three or more ships take full damage, as before.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-018","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"A coil wraps round your ship the way its body lies, and no longer sweeps across your deck as it closes and lets go.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-019","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"A short drop in your connection no longer throws the serpent back across the water when you reconnect. If everyone sails away and comes back later, it is where it was, not somewhere new.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-020","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"Its wake no longer crowds out the splashes of your own cannon fire.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-021","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"An older version of the game is told to reload, and cannot fight until it has. While it reloads, it no longer counts as a ship in the fight.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-022","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"It moves smoothly on every screen, even for players whose connection lags behind, and no longer jumps when a relay restarts.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6561-023","v":"0.1.6561","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"A ship that wrecks inside a coil is let go.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6566-001","v":"0.1.6566","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Login","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed logins failing for everyone. The account server was overwhelmed by every game checking every town's yard decorations each minute. Yards are now only fetched for towns near you, the server keeps a short copy instead of asking its database each time, and a failed fetch waits longer each time instead of retrying every 10 seconds.","g":["online","homes"],"n":""},{"id":"0.1.6566-002","v":"0.1.6566","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Crew","t":"Buff","x":"Your crew lasts twice as long. Cannon fire, fires on deck, rams and the sea serpent's blows all take half as many of your men. Against a ship of the line your hull now gives out before your crew does.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6566-003","v":"0.1.6566","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Crew","t":"Rework","x":"Swivel-gun boats (pirate sloops, coasting traders) still go for your crew first, but at half the old pace. Enemy crews are unchanged.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6566-004","v":"0.1.6566","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Small Ship","t":"Buff","x":"Your galleon's broadside hits like six guns. It has five gunports a side, one fewer than the old galleon, so each ball now does 20% more damage to hulls and sails. Pirates size your galleon up by it. Enemy captains' galleons are unchanged.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6570-001","v":"0.1.6570","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Cite Tool","t":"Other","x":"No gameplay changes in this update. The developers' notes and code comments that point at specific places in the game's code now name the code itself instead of a line number. Every update used to shift those numbers, and updates kept colliding over them, which slowed releases down. That no longer happens.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6570-002","v":"0.1.6570","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Cite Tool","t":"Fix","x":"Hundreds of those pointers were wrong, and are fixed. While rebuilding them, every pointer was checked against the code it was first written for. The ones that had drifted onto the wrong code were moved back, so the game's design notes describe the game accurately again.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6575-001","v":"0.1.6575","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Yard","t":"Nerf","x":"A yard decoration can now stand at most 4 m above the ground. Stacking pieces into towers is no longer possible. If you try to place or move a piece higher, the decorator says why.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6575-002","v":"0.1.6575","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Yard","t":"Other","x":"Pieces already standing higher than that stay where they are. You can still move them down or remove them.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6575-003","v":"0.1.6575","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Decorate","t":"New","x":"Turn placed pieces in place. In the Decorate panel's \"In this room\" and \"In this yard\" views, choose a piece and press Turn left or Turn right. Each press turns it 15 degrees where it stands, at once, for free, without picking it up. A flat picture flips to face the other way. Doors still turn with their doorway (Move).","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6575-004","v":"0.1.6575","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Decorate","t":"Fix","x":"Changing a piece's light, storage or station while it is being turned no longer undoes the other change.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-001","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Project Legacy (by Lattymoy, Ghð§† and Positronico) is now part of the game and is on by default (you can turn it off on its tile in Features). Every new character founds a house, unless you choose No lineage online: a surname, a seat in the first town you stand in, and often a brother or sister or two you can play later.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-002","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"When you create a character you choose how death works for your house. Online the realm keeps your house, and the choice is an Enhanced Plus popup with a third answer:","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-003","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Enduring: death isn't the end, but it costs you. Arkay takes years from your life, and the price depends on your race's lifespan. In old age you get the option to pass the mantle to an heir. When your years run out, your line carries on.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-004","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Bloodline: death is final. A Succession window opens and you pick who takes the mantle: any living member of the family, or, if the fallen was meant to have an heir, a newborn child of theirs.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-005","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"No lineage (online): no house and no heirs. Death works the way it always has online. Offline the choice keeps its two answers; to play there without a house, turn Project Legacy off in Features.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-006","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Heirs are born, not copied. Their stats, skills, career and race draw on their parents', with a share of the family estate (up to 9,900 gold, paid as a letter of credit).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-007","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"A character with a one-word name founds a house named for its seat: the first town you reach makes Janome's family the house \"of Sentinel\", brothers and sisters included, and the game tells you so.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-008","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Heirlooms","t":"New","x":"A fallen character may leave behind an heirloom, their most valuable worn weapon or armour, renamed for the house.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-009","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Heirlooms","t":"New","x":"Their remains lie where they fell, together with the heirloom and part of their purse. Their heir gets the death quest \"The Bones of <name>\": it's in the journal, followed by the Quest Guide, and circled on the map. Reach the spot and the remains open like any container: take what you want, and anything you leave stays with them for your next visit.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-010","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Heirlooms","t":"New","x":"If you sell or drop the bones, they return to where your ancestor fell.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-011","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Heirlooms","t":"New","x":"Lay the remains to rest at a temple or at the family seat. You get the ancestor's blessing (+3 to their best skill, at most +9 on any one skill), and the heirloom grows stronger with each generation that carries it home.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-012","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"Family members you aren't playing now live in the world. If your line owns a house, they live in the family home. Choose which house that is on the Family tab's House page. With no house, they live in your family's seat town, in a house the town lends them.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-013","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"They keep a daily routine like the town's other residents: asleep at home at night, out in the market and the streets by day.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-014","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"A family member you've played appears in their own body: their race and the gear they wore at their last save, drawn the way other players are drawn online (the Other players card in Features decides how). Someone you've never played wears the town's own clothes.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-015","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"Talk to one and they greet you as family (\"Mother! You're home.\"). You can then Play as them, have a normal Talk, or say Goodbye. Your current character is saved first. A member you've never played starts out in the town where you met them.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-016","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"Save a character inside one of your family's houses and they'll be waiting there when you switch to someone else. Save them anywhere else and they're \"on their own journey\" until you play them again.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-017","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"In conversation, a family member shows their own face, the one picked when they were created.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-018","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"New","x":"A family member you kill is dead for good, and the House page records who killed them. One a monster kills in the street is dead for good too, and the town hears of it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-019","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family in the World","t":"Other","x":"On by default. You can turn it off with Family In World in Project Legacy's settings.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-020","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"New","x":"A townsperson who counts you a friend can be courted: ask them about Courtship in conversation, once a day. How it goes depends on your Personality, your Etiquette and your tone.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-021","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"New","x":"When their heart is full, ask for their hand (Marriage). You're wed at the temple of their town: walk in and you're asked whether to marry there and whether they take your house's name.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-022","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"New","x":"Your spouse joins the house, keeping their own face and their own day. They live in your family's house in their town if your line has one there, otherwise in their own home. Every thirty days there's a one-in-four chance of a child, at most six with each spouse. Children can't be played until the mantle passes to them.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-023","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"Other","x":"If someone you're courting dies, the courtship ends.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-024","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"A child born to the house inherits part of their parent's reputation: a quarter of their standing with each region's law and with each guild, and half of how each townsperson felt about them. (\"Your mother saved my son.\") A grudge carries over too.","g":["law","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-025","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Towns talk about your house. A death, a laying to rest, a wedding and a birth are news for a week in the town where it happened and in your family's seat.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-026","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"The revenant that killed your ancestor comes after their heir. The journal and the House page name it.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-027","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Other","x":"Characters made before this update have no house online. Online, a house is founded only when a character is made, so to play Project Legacy online, make a new character. Your existing characters play exactly as before, and their Family tab says why they have no house.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-028","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Online, your family lives in the realm: every device you play on sees the same house, its living and its dead.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-029","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Bloodline is open online. A Bloodline death online is final everywhere: no older save, on any device, can be played past it. The heir you choose is born into the realm as that member of the family.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-030","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Your house's name shows under your name online - over your head, on your Inspect card and on your character list: \"☠ Ysolde II of House Hlaalu\". The skull marks a Bloodline; the numeral, the second of the house to bear that name.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-031","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"New","x":"Two players can wed. Stand in a temple together, inspect the other player and press Propose marriage; they answer yes or no. Each of you keeps your own house, and each family records the other as a spouse. Children come to each house in its own time.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-032","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"New","x":"If your spouse's character dies or is deleted, word reaches you the next time you're online (within ten minutes if you are). You may wed again.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-033","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"A fallen character's Stores, professions and market place fall with them: nothing of theirs can be withdrawn or used after their death.","g":["online","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-034","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"The homes you own in the realm are your family's houses. Your family lives in them, and a character saved in one waits there, just as offline.","g":["online","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-035","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family Tab","t":"New","x":"The pause window has a new Family tab, between Holdings and System, with three pages: the Tree (zoom, pan, play as a sibling, pass the mantle, and where each member lives), the House (model, seat, generations, the living and the fallen, and your homes) and the Hall of Ancestors (every house you have founded). Keypad / opens it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-036","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Family Tab","t":"New","x":"Your character sheet (the pause window's Stats tab) shows your house: its model and your generation, and in an Enduring house your age against your lifespan, the years Arkay has taken, and when you become an elder.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-037","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"A permadeath can't be undone by quick-loading, closing the game under the death screen, or a second tab of the same family. The death is recorded the moment it happens, and if the browser's storage refuses to save it, you're told and it's tried again.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-038","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Loading an older save of a fallen or retired family member shows the house's waiting Succession, or offers you the member who carries the line now, instead of letting you play the past.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-039","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"An heir is saved the moment they're born. If that first save fails, nothing is lost: reload and they're born again, inheritance and all.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-040","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Heirlooms","t":"Fix","x":"An heirloom can't be taken twice by rewinding or switching between family members, and an ancestor's remains can't be stashed in a chest to make a second set of bones.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-041","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"A character copied from online to offline play starts a family of their own instead of sharing the original's (none if it chose No lineage). One copied into online play has no house there, like any character made before this update.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-042","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Holding a key can't confirm a choice by accident. The line's end and \"Play as\" at a family meeting both ask twice. The Family tab can be walked with Tab.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6612-043","v":"0.1.6612","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"The heir no longer inherits the dead character's leftover state. Sibling kits use the sibling's own race and class. Switching characters no longer drops you at the map's corner. Plus the other fixes listed in the design record.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6614-001","v":"0.1.6614","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Leveling","t":"Rework","x":"Online characters no longer get forced onto Oblivion leveling. A new online character levels the Daggerfall way. The Oblivion option is shown locked as \"Offline characters only\".","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6614-002","v":"0.1.6614","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Leveling","t":"Other","x":"Characters already using Oblivion leveling online keep it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6614-003","v":"0.1.6614","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Bring Online","t":"Rework","x":"An offline Oblivion character you bring online switches to Daggerfall leveling, starting from its current level. Any level-up it had already earned is kept.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6616-001","v":"0.1.6616","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Leveling","t":"Rework","x":"Online characters on Oblivion leveling switch to Daggerfall leveling the next time you play them. You keep your level and skills, and any level-up you had already earned. A message tells you once the world loads.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6618-001","v":"0.1.6618","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Character Creation","t":"Fix","x":"On the Project Legacy question (Enduring, Bloodline, No lineage) and the leveling question, moving the mouse no longer jumps the highlight between options. The option under your pointer is the one highlighted, and clicking it selects it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6625-001","v":"0.1.6625","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Accounts","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed the account server falling over again, which left homes and yards without their decorations. When the server slowed down, every game asked it again within seconds, and that kept it down. Games now wait longer after each failed ask, so a busy minute passes instead of turning into an outage.","g":["online","homes"],"n":""},{"id":"0.1.6625-002","v":"0.1.6625","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Login","t":"Fix","x":"Signing into a room after a slow server answer no longer asks for a second sign-in ticket, so you reconnect sooner.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-001","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Signing in, joining a room and loading a town's house layouts now cost the account server far less work, so busy evenings are less likely to slow it down or leave decorations missing.","g":["online","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-002","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Performance","x":"An online family that hasn't changed since the last checkpoint is no longer uploaded again at every checkpoint.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-003","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"Fix","x":"With the living world on, 407 of the game's 410 cities (Ripmarket among them) had nobody walking their streets at any hour. A city's walls and closed gates cut its streets off from the fields around it, and the townspeople were being laid out on the fields' side, where none of their doors are, so every one of them stayed indoors all day. The streets now fill again by day, travellers leave by the gates, and the watch keeps its posts there. Daggerfall, Wayrest and Sentinel were not affected.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-004","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"In 14 cities whose palace stands in its own walled grounds (Sentinel among them), the whole city watch lived at the palace and never came out. The watch now lives where its door opens onto the streets, so it walks its patrols and keeps its posts.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-005","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"People waiting at the same spot keep a little room from one another and from the groups talking there.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-006","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"Two who leave a shop or a tavern at the same moment walk out in single file.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-007","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"A walker steps aside, keeping right, for anyone standing or coming the other way.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-008","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Other","x":"In the towns measured, between a tenth and over half of the people in view at midday or in the evening were standing inside someone else; now almost nobody is.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-009","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"The town square now has several gathering points across it, and each townsperson keeps to their own.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-010","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"Every neighbourhood has a corner where its people meet, and people's favourite places are the ones near their homes.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-011","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"Stall-keepers set up either at the square or at their own market.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-012","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"People head out for the evening, and to the morning market, at their own time instead of all on the hour.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-013","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Other","x":"In the towns measured, the busiest spot in the evening went from 30-64 people (all around one point of the square) to 6-17.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-014","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"A townsperson who stops for you now stays exactly where they stopped.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-015","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"They belong to the guild of their trade or class: scholars, booksellers' and alchemists' people and mages to the Mages Guild; smiths and fighters to the Fighters Guild; courtiers and knights to the town's knightly order. Each spends an evening at their guild hall twice a week.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-016","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"Rework","x":"Sellswords and adventurers now go to their own guild's hall instead of whichever hall is nearest.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-017","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"Rework","x":"Errands go into a shop more often, and to a shop the person has business at: shopkeepers bank their takings, scholars visit the library and the bookseller, households the general store and the clothier.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-018","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"Rework","x":"The people you find inside a guild hall are now its own guild's members. Daggerfall's guild halls now see 18 visitors a day instead of 12, and its banks 7 instead of 2.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-019","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Travellers staying at a tavern, sailors ashore and adventurers who live there each have a room by one of its beds.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-020","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"You'll find them up in their room in the morning and again before bed. They come down to the common room for breakfast and supper, and sleep out of sight.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-021","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Living World","t":"Other","x":"A room you rent is never given to a lodger.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-022","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Guild members walk the streets in their guild's classes: Mages Guild members in a mage's hooded robes, Fighters Guild members in a warrior's arms and armour, the knights of an order as knights. Priests wear the healer's robes. Adventurers, sellswords and couriers wear their own class all day, not only on their way out of town.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-023","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Someone keeping their place on their own appears as one of Daggerfall's own pictures of their kind: an old beggar at their pitch, a merchant, a blacksmith or a porter at their stall, a monk at the temple door in the morning, a lord or a lady at home in the palace. Each kind has several pictures, and the animated ones move as they do in the game.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-024","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Other","x":"They become themselves again the moment they walk on or join a conversation. A look never changes while you are watching.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6640-025","v":"0.1.6640","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Other","x":"In Daggerfall city, 24 of its 317 people now walk in a class, and 17-28 stand as still pictures by day.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-001","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Waypoints","t":"New","x":"Right-click the Overworld or the world map (V) to place a waypoint. Give it a name and a flag colour, and choose who it is for: you alone, your party or your guild.","g":["map","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-002","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Waypoints","t":"New","x":"Party and guild waypoints are shared with the other members. Only the player who placed one can change it for everyone; anyone can rename or remove one on their own screen.","g":["map","social","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-003","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Waypoints","t":"New","x":"Follow a waypoint from the Overworld's filters: it stays marked at the edge of the screen with its distance. A waypoint's own menu can also send you travelling there.","g":["map","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-004","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Waypoints","t":"Other","x":"Leaving a party or a guild removes its waypoints.","g":["map","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-005","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Travel Options","t":"New","x":"Two speed dials while travelling: the journey's speed and the speed while enemies are near. Both go x5, x10, x20, x30, x40 and x60, and x100 on a road only.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-006","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Travel Options","t":"Other","x":"Leaving a road drops a dial at x100 to x60 at once; it does not climb back by itself. Journeys start at x60 - turn the dial up to x100 on a road.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-007","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Travel Options","t":"New","x":"The dials are in every interface: the Overworld's panel, the Enhanced journey bar, and a small speed box with the classic interface and GrimoireUI.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-008","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"The Overworld's filters now sit in their own box at the bottom left, which folds away and can be moved like the rest of the HUD.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-009","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Foe Health Bar","t":"Fix","x":"An enemy's health bar no longer shows an empty box under it; the poise bar appears only when there is something to show, and the bar has one shadow instead of two.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-010","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Fix","x":"With Enhanced Lighting on, shadows no longer blink all at once in some rooms. The shadow cache behind it is now off by default; turn it back on under Enhanced Lighting with \"Shadow cache (faster, may flicker)\".","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-011","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Steady Shadows","t":"Fix","x":"Shadows hold steady through a brief hitch instead of flashing.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-012","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed a cat meowing many times a second while you looked at certain townspeople (reported in Chesterwark).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6646-013","v":"0.1.6646","d":"2026-10-06","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed \"Protect an Honored Mage\" (Mages Guild) online: the three-hour guard could end before the assassins came, leaving the quest impossible to finish. The guard now lasts its full three hours of play, and the attack always comes inside it. A guard that already ended this way stays unfinished.","g":["quests","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6650-001","v":"0.1.6650","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Steel armour has a new look on the Morrowind body: a full suit of plate - breastplate, pauldrons, gauntlets, greaves, boots and helm - made for the port. It shows on your character in third person, on the paperdoll, on other players, and as your gauntlets in first person.","g":["climbing","morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6650-002","v":"0.1.6650","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Features","t":"New","x":"A new switch under Features > Combat, Steel Helm: Closed (a visor and a blue plume, the default) or Open (a nasal helm with a mail aventail that shows the face). It changes at once, and it is how your game draws every steel helm - yours and other players'.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-001","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The grass can now be a meadow made from new hand-drawn sprites: tall and short green tufts, flowering tufts, dry tufts and bushes, mixed across the land.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-002","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"Every tuft and bush grows to its own size. Whole patches run taller or shorter, so the land no longer looks the same everywhere.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-003","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"Flowers gather in lush patches and dry grass in poor ones. Bushes turn up here and there, from shin-high to shoulder-high.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-004","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The meadow doesn't turn to face you. Each tuft and bush stands on crossed cards like the low-poly trees, so you see it from every side as you walk round it, and a low sun lights one face more than the other.","g":["grass","rendering","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-005","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The meadow follows the ground: its greens take the colour of the grass they grow on, so it fits every climate and season (flowers keep their own colours), and on a hillside each tuft stands on the slope instead of hanging over it.","g":["grass","climate","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-006","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The meadow sways in the wind the way the trees do. Bushes are stiffer than grass, as the world's bushes are.","g":["grass","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-007","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"Performance","x":"The meadow does about the same vertex work as the old pixel tufts.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-008","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"Crossing into a new part of the map no longer makes all the grass jump to a new pose in the wind. The trees no longer jump there either.","g":["grass","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-009","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"Pixel-style grass tufts no longer swap to different pictures when you cross into a new part of the map.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-010","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Grass is now off by default. Turn it on under Settings › Grass with Full, Half or Quarter. If you had it on Full before, it is off after this update until you turn it back on; Half and Quarter are kept.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-011","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Grass › Style defaults to Meadow. Pixel (the old tufts) and Smooth are still there.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6656-012","v":"0.1.6656","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Wind","t":"Rework","x":"Wind › Trees sway is now just Sway: it moves the grass as well as the trees, and turning it off holds both still.","g":["grass","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-001","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Every weapon type now has the same base condition, the Warhammer's 1,600. Daggers, tantos and short bows started at 50 and long bows at 100, so they broke 16 to 32 times sooner than a warhammer of the same metal.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-002","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Buff","x":"Enchanted weapons gain the most. A Cast-When-Strikes enchantment costs 10 condition a strike, so an iron Worm's Tooth now lasts 160 strikes instead of 5.","g":["equipment","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-003","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Fix","x":"A Cast-When-Held enchantment pays its spell's casting cost in condition the first time it is equipped, often over a hundred. That broke an iron dagger, tanto or short bow on the spot. Now the weapon keeps the rest and lasts about four game days.","g":["equipment","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-004","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Buff","x":"Bows no longer break after a couple of dozen hits: an iron short bow takes about 800 hits of 20 damage.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-005","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Economy","x":"Light weapons and bows cost less to keep up, because a repair is priced by the share of condition lost.","g":["equipment","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-006","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Rework","x":"Your weapons are updated when you load a save and keep the same percentage of condition. A broken weapon stays broken, and a half-worn dagger is half of its new pool. That covers every weapon your save holds, wherever it is, and a family heirloom paid to an heir. A weapon that comes back from the online market, a guild vault or a trade is updated the first time it takes wear.","g":["equipment","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-007","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Saves","t":"Fix","x":"When you load, older items get their fixes wherever your save keeps them, not only in your pack, wagon and containers. The fixes: a weapon moves to the new condition pool, an item made with no condition gets one, Roleplay & Realism armour gets back the Brigandine, Fur or Mail word its name lost, old Sigil Stones are named Deadlands Embers, and a rolled jewel stuck on an unwearable Wand becomes an Amulet.","g":["saves","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-008","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Saves","t":"Fix","x":"That now includes things set out in your house, quest items, a revenant's takings and a sworn revenant's pack, enemies' and guards' gear, and Project Legacy's bequests and remains. Before, an item in one of those places kept its old record until you carried it back and loaded again.","g":["saves","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-009","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Project Legacy: an heir's bequest gets the same fixes when it is paid, and a fallen relative's remains get them when you open them.","g":["saves","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-010","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Saves","t":"Other","x":"A rolled Wand you set out in your house becomes an Amulet, but it still looks like a wand where it stands until you pick it up.","g":["saves","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6663-011","v":"0.1.6663","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Customs","t":"Fix","x":"Customs now counts gold and letters of credit in a sworn revenant companion's pack, the same as a crew companion's pack. Before, a revenant could carry any amount across uncapped.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6666-001","v":"0.1.6666","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Homes","t":"Fix","x":"A home the Arena moved kept emptying. Homes in Daggerfall city that were moved out of the Arena's way could have their storage emptied at login: every chest, the storage pieces and the things standing in the room. It happened while the account server was failing, as it did through 6 October. The move no longer touches a home its owner already lives in. Items already lost this way are not brought back by this update.","g":["homes","arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6666-002","v":"0.1.6666","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Beautiful Cities","t":"Fix","x":"A moved home's crate could stay hidden. The crate of belongings that comes with a moved house now shows up in the new house when the city uses the Beautiful Cities layout.","g":["homes","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-001","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"Rework","x":"Towns with three or more bulletin boards no longer show two or three Notice Boards. Each town has one: the board nearest the town's middle. The other boards are Daggerfall's rumour boards again, as they are offline. Bounty Boards are unchanged.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-002","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"UI","x":"The Notice Board now says \"Notice Board\" when you point at it.","g":["notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-003","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"UI","x":"Notes stand straight, the text is larger, and anything written on the cork sits on a dark panel.","g":["notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-004","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"QoL","x":"On a phone the tab row scrolls sideways, so Guilds and Seat can be reached.","g":["notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-005","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"UI","x":"Tabs show counts: new notes on Notices, and open writs on Work once you've looked at it.","g":["notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-006","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"UI","x":"Notices shows town and server news first, then players' notes.","g":["notice-board","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-007","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Court Writs","t":"UI","x":"Work shows \"Court writs today\" at the top instead of under the last card.","g":["notice-board","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-008","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"UI","x":"Views are grouped: Buy (Materials, Crafted, Auctions, Goods), Sell (Orders, My listings), then History.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-009","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"UI","x":"Your silver is shown at the top, and listings have column names.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-010","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"UI","x":"The Weavers' and Apothecaries' counters are folded under one \"Suppliers\" line.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-011","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"UI","x":"My listings is split into the List form, your listings, auctions, bids and buy orders. Form fields are labelled (a stall's \"Put up a piece\" form too), and the List button is full size again.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-012","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"UI","x":"The Vendors list has the same column names.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-013","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"Performance","x":"The Notice Board's window now downloads in the background after the game starts, so it is usually ready the first time you open it.","g":["notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-014","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"Performance","x":"The Market starts loading as soon as the board opens.","g":["market","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-015","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Seat Tab","t":"Performance","x":"The Seat tab loads its standings and works at the same time.","g":["seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-016","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Seat Tab","t":"UI","x":"Split into panels: the Charter, This week (Muster, Reckoning, Turning), the battle, Standings, Your guild, the holder's orders, the Works and the Chronicle.","g":["seats","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-017","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Seat Tab","t":"New","x":"Each challenging guild has a bar showing how close it is to claiming the Charter or winning the Right of Siege.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-018","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Seat Tab","t":"New","x":"New \"How the seat war works\" guide: pledging, earning influence, claiming, sieges and holding.","g":["seats","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-019","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"Rework","x":"Messages across the board, Market, Work, Vendors and Seat tabs are shorter and plainer. For example, \"The counting-house is not answering. The market cannot be read now.\" is now \"The market did not load.\"","g":["notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-020","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Word Filter","t":"New","x":"Slurs and crude words are starred out () in chat on every channel, Notice Board notes, guild notes, letters and shared journal pages. The rest of the message stays as written, and ordinary words that only contain a filtered one (\"spiced wine\", \"snigger\", \"don't get cocky\") are left alone.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-021","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Word Filter","t":"New","x":"Notes pinned before this update are starred too when a board is read.","g":["notice-board","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-022","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Word Filter","t":"New","x":"A guild rank name or a ship's name with such a word is refused, and the message names the word.","g":["guild","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-023","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Word Filter","t":"New","x":"A custom class name with such a word isn't shown to other players, and a maker's mark with one is left off the item.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-024","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Word Filter","t":"New","x":"A name given with the Item Maker is starred wherever the item is shown.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-025","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Profile","t":"UI","x":"The inspect card is tidied up: the name always keeps its line, badges sit on their own row under it, and the duel, breach, town and serpent records are compact plaques.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-026","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Profile","t":"UI","x":"Worn gear is grouped into In hand, Armour, Clothing and Jewellery. A pair, such as two rings, shares one row.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6678-027","v":"0.1.6678","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Wallet","t":"UI","x":"The wallet's sheet is now a ledger: Coin (gold, silver) and In the wallet (letters of credit, Deadlands Embers, Welkynd Shards), with each amount lined up on the right.","g":["marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-001","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Performance","x":"The shadow cache is on again by default, so lamp-lit rooms such as taverns, shops and guild halls get their frame rate back.","g":["lighting","interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-002","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed the shadow flicker with Enhanced Lighting on Windows: a rapid, strobing flicker on some NVIDIA cards, and on others every shadow in a room blinking at once. It came from how the cached shadows were copied on Direct3D, not from the cache itself.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-003","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Removal","x":"The \"Shadow cache (faster, may flicker)\" switch is gone from Enhanced Lighting. It is no longer needed.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-004","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Off-Road Placement","t":"New","x":"Trees, bushes and rocks no longer stand on roads and tracks, and their branches no longer hang over them. This includes the 3D trees from Low Poly Trees.","g":["roads","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-005","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Off-Road Placement","t":"New","x":"Herb patches, ore veins on open stone and Motherlodes keep off the roads too.","g":["roads","foraging","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-006","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Off-Road Placement","t":"New","x":"Forests no longer grow across dirt tracks.","g":["roads","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-007","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Off-Road Placement","t":"New","x":"Settings › Clear roadsides (on by default). Off lets them grow up to the edge of the road, as Daggerfall does.","g":["roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-008","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Blended Climates","t":"New","x":"Where two climates meet, the land no longer changes along a straight line. The border wanders and breaks into patches about two hundred metres deep: grass thins out into sand, rock creeps into the woods, snow comes in drifts.","g":["climate","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-009","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Blended Climates","t":"New","x":"The trees follow the same border. Near it, each tree belongs to the climate of the ground it stands on.","g":["climate","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-010","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The grass follows it too.","g":["grass","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-011","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Blended Climates","t":"New","x":"Settings › Blended climates (on by default). Off changes them at a straight edge, as Daggerfall does.","g":["climate","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6690-012","v":"0.1.6690","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Cover","t":"Fix","x":"In winter, the trees of a wood are cover the way they are the rest of the year: enemies hide behind the trunk and under the crown.","g":["seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6693-001","v":"0.1.6693","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Big cities no longer drop to a frame or two a second between 4 and 6 in the morning (game time). Every time the game looked at a city watchman who sets out for their post before the day begins, it worked out the whole town's day again from scratch - hundreds of townspeople, every frame. It was worst in the great cities, Daggerfall among them; offline the slowdown kept itself going, and online it came back with every in-game dawn. The people on the street are exactly where they were before.","g":["water","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6693-002","v":"0.1.6693","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Harbours","t":"Fix","x":"A port whose harbour lies far from any street no longer searches for its dock four times a second.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6700-001","v":"0.1.6700","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repairs","t":"Fix","x":"Repairs Objects now mends the gear you are wearing. Before, each repair went to the first damaged thing anywhere in your pack: a worn piece of loot, a looted book, spare shoes, even a lit torch's fuel. The armour and weapons you wore were rarely touched. Now it mends the most worn piece you are wearing first. Only when everything you wear is whole does it move on to your pack, again most worn first.","g":["loot","torch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6700-002","v":"0.1.6700","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repairs","t":"Fix","x":"Weapons mend at a dagger's pace. Since every weapon type was given the same condition pool, a repair of 1 point barely moved a weapon. Every weapon now mends 32 points every four game minutes (about every 20 seconds of play), the share a dagger always got: 2% for iron and 0.25% for Daedric. A battered weapon is like new in under three game hours at iron, about eight at Dwarven and about a day at Daedric.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6700-003","v":"0.1.6700","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Meditation Candle","t":"Fix","x":"It no longer refills what a smith won't repair. That means torches, lanterns, candles, arrows, a campfire's fuel, a bedroll's nights and the doses of Waking Salts and Meditation Candles.","g":["camping","torch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6700-004","v":"0.1.6700","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Magic Repair","t":"New","x":"Armour, clothing and jewellery still mend Daggerfall's 1 point at a time. So do the uses of classic magic items and artifacts.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6700-005","v":"0.1.6700","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Magic Repair","t":"New","x":"Enchanted items still mend only with Allow Magic Repairs, which is on by default and always on online.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6700-006","v":"0.1.6700","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Magic Repair","t":"New","x":"It still mends one piece every four game minutes, and only for you.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6702-001","v":"0.1.6702","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The grass grows by default again, at Full, in the meadow style.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6702-002","v":"0.1.6702","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"If you picked Half, Quarter or Off yourself, your choice is kept. If you turned the grass off during the day it was off by default, it is on again: turn it off in Features > Grass.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6702-003","v":"0.1.6702","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"The grass is cheaper to draw, and looks exactly the same. The biggest gain is on Windows, the desktop app included, and on Macs.","g":["grass","rendering","desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6702-004","v":"0.1.6702","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Grass","t":"New","x":"If the outdoors still run slow, Features > Grass > Half halves the grass's cost.","g":["grass","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6706-001","v":"0.1.6706","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Yard","t":"New","x":"Lamp posts, torches, braziers and the other lights you place in your home's yard now light the ground and walls around them at night, the way the town's street lamps light theirs: the same light (a warm flame with Enhanced Lighting, white without it) and the same flicker, from 17:00 to 08:00, the hours the town's lanterns are lit.","g":["homes","online","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6706-002","v":"0.1.6706","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Yard","t":"New","x":"Up to eight lamps light in each yard, the most any Daggerfall town block has. Lamps placed after the eighth stay dark until one of the first eight is taken down.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6706-003","v":"0.1.6706","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Yard","t":"New","x":"A lamp you scale up casts a bigger pool of light.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6706-004","v":"0.1.6706","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Yard","t":"New","x":"Lamps you placed before this update light up on their own. You don't need to switch anything on.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6709-001","v":"0.1.6709","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"Mining, Logging, Herbalism (the Basket included), Fishing and Hunting no longer stop for the day. The 60 harvests a day in each profession (120 across your characters), the 40 hauls a day and the 30 hides a day are gone.","g":["professions","online","fishing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6709-002","v":"0.1.6709","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"New","x":"Each node can still be worked once a day by each character, so the next harvest is wherever the next node stands.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6709-003","v":"0.1.6709","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"The chip under the compass shows the day's count without a limit (\"Mining 34 - 12 today\"), and so does the Professions tab.","g":["professions","online","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6709-004","v":"0.1.6709","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Accounts","t":"New","x":"Rare hides (tiers 5 and 6): 3 a day for your account.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6709-005","v":"0.1.6709","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Accounts","t":"New","x":"Veins in dungeons nobody has vouched for: 4 a day for your account.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-001","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Castle Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"The two towers in Castle Daggerfall's courtyard are whole again. Every floor, stair, lantern and piece of furniture is where it belongs, the rooms are lit, and the stairwells no longer open onto the void.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-002","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Project Legacy: the Family tab's House page can now move your family's seat to the town you are standing in. Press Make <town> the family seat, then press again to confirm.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-003","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Your heirs are born in the new seat, your fallen can be laid to rest there, and a family without a home of its own lives there. Your house keeps its name.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-004","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"When you aren't standing in another town, the House page tells you how to move the seat.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-005","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"New","x":"Online, every character now starts Privateer's Hold on their own, with its enemies alive, its doors shut and its loot untouched. Other players are back as soon as you step outside.","g":["online","audit","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-006","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Dungeons","t":"New","x":"If you step out and come back in the same session, the enemies you defeated and the chests you emptied stay that way for up to an hour, as in other dungeons online.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-007","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"New","x":"Local chat in the Hold now tells you that nobody can hear you there.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-008","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"You can no longer climb while you fast travel on the Overworld, whether on a journey or holding the movement keys under the travel view. Walking into a wall at 60x speed no longer farms the Climbing skill, and travellers no longer fall off the rocks along the way.","g":["climbing","online","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-009","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"You can't start a journey while hanging on a wall. Climb down first.","g":["climbing","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6716-010","v":"0.1.6716","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Climbing","t":"New","x":"Climbing works as before at walking pace.","g":["climbing","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6721-001","v":"0.1.6721","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Banishment","t":"New","x":"WAITS: four long online waits shortened - bank hours, Daedra summoning, the King of Worms' messenger, banishment","g":["law","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-001","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Textures","t":"New","x":"The steel plate cuirass now has its skirt, painted with its own texture.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-002","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"The steel plate no longer T-poses in game. It follows the body's arms and legs.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-003","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Attacks now keep up with your attack speed. At high Speed every blow is drawn, and each one connects when its damage does.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-004","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Other players' fast attacks play at their pace too.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-005","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Casting a spell plays the Morrowind casting animation through to the end, and the spell leaves your hands on the cast's release.","g":["animation","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-006","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Weapons","t":"New","x":"Your weapon leaves your hand while a spell is readied.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-007","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Area Spells","t":"New","x":"With Morrowind data installed, spells use Morrowind's own effects: the glow around the caster and on your hands, the bolt a target spell flies as, the hit on whoever it lands on, and the burst of an area spell. Spells from enemies and other players show the casting glow and the bolt too.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-008","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Features","t":"New","x":"New switch under Features > Combat: Morrowind Spell Effects, on by default.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-009","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Travel Options","t":"New","x":"With Travel Options on, a journey down a steep road follows the road instead of flying off it into a fall.","g":["mod","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6751-010","v":"0.1.6751","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Travel Options","t":"New","x":"If the roads arrive after you have loaded in (online, or on a slow connection), whatever lies on the ground stays on it as the ground settles, and so do you. A download of the roads that never answers is tried again instead of leaving you on a roadless world.","g":["mod","overworld","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-001","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Resistance from rolled gear now counts up to 45% per element, and only fills an Aetheric piece's resistance up to that same 45%. Two +25% Fire rings no longer make you immune to fire spells. An Aetheric piece's own resistance, set bonuses, spells, your race and your class still count in full.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-002","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Drops","t":"New","x":"Luck now multiplies drop chances (half at Luck 0, half again at Luck 100) instead of adding a flat amount. Low-luck characters can find Legendaries again, and high luck no longer outweighs where you loot.","g":["online","audit","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-003","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Clothing can drop as Magic and Rare with lines of its own: standing with a social group, warmth and weatherproofing (for Climates & Calories), Personality, and street skills - footwear leans to movement skills. Warmth and weatherproof lines say \"(survival off)\" when survival is off.","g":["loot","audit","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-004","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Superior and Masterwork clothing you make now comes out Magic and Rare, as crafted weapons and armour already did.","g":["loot","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-005","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Six Legendary garments, each with a power: the Alik'r Wayfarer's Robes (the heat is felt 20 less), the Wrothgar Pass Mantle (the cold is felt 20 less), the Vestments of Stendarr (Restoration spells cost 25% less), the Pilgrim's Sandals (you tire 25% slower, falls hurt half as much), the Silks of Queen Barenziah (+5 standing with every group) and the Shade's Cowl (+25 Stealth while hooded). Rare clothing can take their powers at the Reforge's Imprint.","g":["loot","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-006","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"With the loot rarity setting off, clothing stays exactly as in Daggerfall.","g":["loot","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-007","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"One Rare or Legendary in twelve from a body or a pile is cursed: one extra bonus line and one drawback (a bad reputation, bad reactions, damage or wear in holy places, weaker blows against a kind of foe, or a health leech). A drawback never cancels one of the item's own bonuses. You won't know until it is identified - then the card reads \"Cursed Rare\".","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-008","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Temples","t":"New","x":"A temple's Cure Disease priest now offers Lift Curse: the drawback goes, the bonus line stays. It costs a quarter of the item's value, at least 300 gold.","g":["law","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-009","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Hone: raise one line within its own range. It always goes up; each hone on an item doubles the next one's price.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-010","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Welkynd Shards","t":"New","x":"Scry: name a kind of foe and the guild marks the nearest dungeon of theirs in your region that isn't on your map yet (3 Welkynd Shards and 500 gold). An unfound Legendary in the Codex points you there.","g":["portals","guild","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-011","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Sockets: some Rares and Legendaries carry an empty socket. Set one of Daggerfall's eight gems in it for 100 gold for a bonus that depends on the gem and the item; unsetting shatters the gem. A gem you are carrying for a quest is never offered.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-012","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"Salvage every Magic: one button on the Salvage page, asked first.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-013","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"Item cards now compare what the item would change against what it would replace: up or down by how much, \"new\", and the lines you would lose. Resistance lines show how much would count under the cap.","g":["horse","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-014","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"Junk: mark gear as junk from its card, and \"Sell junk\" at a shop puts every junk piece on the counter in one press. A piece you sell loses its junk mark.","g":["horse","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-015","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"Quick loot has a new \"Take gear\" setting (All, Magic+, Rare+) for the take-all key. Gold, supplies, quest items and Daggerfall's own magic items are always taken, and junk is always left.","g":["horse","professions","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6768-016","v":"0.1.6768","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Restore","t":"New","x":"The Welkynd Stone (fills your magicka) and the Varla Stone (restores every enchanted item you wear, magic items' charges included) can turn up in the deepest places.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6773-001","v":"0.1.6773","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Towns have all their Notice Boards again. In towns with three or more boards, every board that isn't a Bounty Board opens the Notice Board, shows its \"new\" count, gets a mark on the town map and, in seat towns, flies a pennant.","g":["notice-board","online","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6773-002","v":"0.1.6773","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Hoods","t":"New","x":"A raised hood now shields a vampire from the sun. With the hood of a cloak or robe up, a vampire in daylight keeps the +20 to their stats instead of taking the daytime -20. Bare-headed, the -20 still applies in the sun.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-001","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Pirates","t":"New","x":"The Carrack (the pirate flagship and the merchant carrack) is a new model, fully textured.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-002","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"Ten gunports, each with its own shutter, and a gun on a platform behind every port. Two bow chasers and a stern barrel.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-003","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"A companion through her middle house leads down to her gun deck.","g":["companions","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-004","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"Her wheel and rudder turn together. Her anchor is weighed and let go, and rope ladders hang down her side.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-005","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Lantern","t":"New","x":"She carries seven lanterns, so a carrack at sea is lit at night.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-006","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"Her rig: a spritsail, fore and main courses, a main topsail and a lateen mizzen. They trim with the wind like every other ship.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-007","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Pirates","t":"New","x":"The Large Boat (the pirate sloop and the coasting trader) is a new clinker-built model.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-008","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"All seven of her sail plans are rebuilt on the new hull.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-009","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"She steers by a tiller: a raked rudder on her sternpost, with the helmsman on a step at her stern.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-010","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"Seven swivel guns sit on her gunwale: three a side and one at her bow.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-011","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Ship Strength","t":"New","x":"A carrack's broadside still hits as hard as before, now from five guns a side instead of seven.","g":["roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6780-012","v":"0.1.6780","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Pirates","t":"New","x":"The pirate sloop now closes to 50 m (it was 55), because the new boat is a taller target.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6783-001","v":"0.1.6783","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A beaten revenant of rank 1 or 2 now usually breaks and runs, and it really gets away. Before, every flight was run down and it knelt every time, so killing you was almost the only way a revenant grew stronger. Now escaping is the usual way.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6783-002","v":"0.1.6783","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A fleeing foe now sprints at twice its walk, which is faster than a player running at average Speed and Running. A fast runner, a bow or a spell can still bring it down.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6783-003","v":"0.1.6783","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Fixed: a foe that broke while circling you used to keep circling instead of running away.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6783-004","v":"0.1.6783","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"From rank 3 nothing changes: you still break its will to make it kneel.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6792-001","v":"0.1.6792","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"Low Poly trees no longer hang over roads, tracks or town streets. Each tree is drawn no wider than the room it has from the nearest road, track or street. This includes the trees inside towns, farms and other locations, and the ones beside the paved ring round a town.","g":["mod","terrain","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6792-002","v":"0.1.6792","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"Trees still stand exactly where they did. Only the drawn size of a tree that would overhang a path changes. A tree planted right on a path shrinks to a sapling.","g":["mod","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6792-003","v":"0.1.6792","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Low Poly Trees","t":"New","x":"This follows the Clear roadsides option, which is on by default.","g":["mod","terrain","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6792-004","v":"0.1.6792","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Hoods","t":"New","x":"A raised hood now protects a character whose class has the Damage from Sunlight disadvantage. With the hood up they take no sun damage outdoors by day, can fast travel by day, and arrive in daylight rather than being held until dusk.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6792-005","v":"0.1.6792","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Hoods","t":"New","x":"Bare-headed, the sun works as before. The travel refusal now also says how to lift it: raise the hood of a cloak or robe.","g":["hunting","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6792-006","v":"0.1.6792","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Hoods","t":"New","x":"A hood carried in your pack, not worn, doesn't count.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6802-001","v":"0.1.6802","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Eye of the Beholder","t":"New","x":"Your third-person sprite no longer flickers between two directions when you start running or strafing at an angle. It turns once and stays turned.","g":["mod","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6802-002","v":"0.1.6802","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Eye of the Beholder","t":"New","x":"An attack now plays one swing instead of a swing and a follow-through. Each attack art holds two strokes (a slash then a chop, a sweep then its return), and your attacks alternate between them, one stroke per click. Other players see the same stroke you do.","g":["mod","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6802-003","v":"0.1.6802","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Eye of the Beholder","t":"New","x":"The \"PingPong Offset\" setting no longer does anything. Under \"Attack Strings\", PingPong now plays like None and Mixed like Mirror.","g":["mod","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6802-004","v":"0.1.6802","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A revenant you beat with a party now always kneels for your judgement (or makes its last stand first). Before, if the fight's ownership passed to a party member (for example, after you died mid-fight), it could die outright with no kill or spare choice and no trophy.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6804-001","v":"0.1.6804","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Invisibility","t":"New","x":"You can now interact with your party members while they are under Chameleon, Shadow or Invisibility, and they can interact with you. The F menu and its plaque, trading, showing a page, spell gifting and the Nearby list all reach a concealed party mate.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6804-002","v":"0.1.6804","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Invisibility","t":"New","x":"Concealed players outside your party stay hidden from all of these, as before.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6804-003","v":"0.1.6804","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Enhanced Combat Visuals","t":"New","x":"How concealed players are drawn has not changed. With Enhanced Combat Visuals off, a concealed party mate is still not drawn, but F reaches them where they stand.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6809-001","v":"0.1.6809","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Players who first played on the evening of September 24 in the Americas now hold the Founder title. The cutoff now counts the 24th in every time zone, not just UTC.","g":["online","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6809-002","v":"0.1.6809","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Played before September 25 on another device or browser? Back up that character to the cloud from your account, or bring it into the realm. Founder is granted automatically if that character was played before the cutoff.","g":["online","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6815-001","v":"0.1.6815","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"New","x":"Shift-click an item in your pack to drop it in front of you as itself. Several drops fan out on the ground instead of piling up, and never land behind a wall or on a table above the floor. Locked, bound and pack-only items still refuse to leave, and so do your horse and wagon. With your wagon or a chest open, Shift still stows there.","g":["morrowind","animation","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6815-002","v":"0.1.6815","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"New","x":"Each item shows its own picture: its Morrowind model when Morrowind data is attached, its classic picture otherwise. Until its picture arrives, a dropped item keeps its loot bag.","g":["morrowind","animation","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6815-003","v":"0.1.6815","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"New","x":"Rarity shows on the ground: Magic-or-better items get an outline in their tier's colour, and Rare-or-better ones stand the same line of light the world boss's spoils do.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6815-004","v":"0.1.6815","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"New","x":"Items come to rest against walls rather than through them, stop moving while the game is paused, and ride along with a body on a moving deck.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6815-005","v":"0.1.6815","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"New","x":"Settings are under Features > Physical Items by demifiend000: turn it off, choose which kinds of loot spill from bodies, how hard it is thrown, and how big items are. Size and outline changes apply straight away.","g":["morrowind","animation","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-001","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Profile","t":"New","x":"The profile that opens from your portrait in the top-right corner has been reorganised. It now opens on your portrait, your name and Renown, the title and glyphs you're wearing, and the character you're playing.","g":["social","equipment","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-002","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Profile","t":"New","x":"Underneath, it is split into sections: Record (duels, breaches closed, towns defended, serpents slain, silver, each in its own tile, with a bar for the share of duels you've won), Characters (each character's Renown, with a bar showing progress to the next level), Wardrobe and Account.","g":["social","equipment","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-003","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Profile","t":"New","x":"On a wide screen the sections sit side by side in two columns. On a phone the profile now fills the screen, so the menu no longer shows through behind it.","g":["social","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-004","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Profile","t":"New","x":"The Close, Sign out and Change password buttons stay pinned to the bottom of the profile, so you never have to scroll to close it.","g":["social","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-005","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Main Menu","t":"New","x":"The main menu buttons are now carved stone slabs in the Enhanced Plus style, all one width. They turn brass when you hover over them or select them with a gamepad, and they follow your chosen Plus colour theme.","g":["desktop-app","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-006","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Main Menu","t":"New","x":"On phones the buttons are a little more compact, so the whole menu now fits above the Screenshots and About buttons.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6821-007","v":"0.1.6821","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Website","t":"New","x":"The website now uses the game's stone and brass. Each section is a carved window with brass corner fittings, and the boxes inside it are stone panels. Play, Install, Discord and the section links are stone buttons that turn brass on hover, and Play is brass all the time.","g":["website","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6837-001","v":"0.1.6837","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Field Bugs","t":"New","x":"FIELD BUGS 2026-10-07: the board crash, potion names, fishing, black screenshots, guild halls, skinning indoors","g":["fishing","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6845-001","v":"0.1.6845","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Puddles","t":"New","x":"WATER-NEXT + AUDIT WATER-NEXT: town puddles dried, the Enhanced water replaced (translucent, swell, shore foam, ripples), audited and its cost measured","g":["water","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-001","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Crafting","t":"New","x":"Refining for a craft costs no extra station fee. You pay only the craft's fee.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-002","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Materials","t":"New","x":"It never refines a material into a lower tier. It won't burn Ghostwood for Charcoal or cure a Dragonling hide into Hardened Leather; do that by hand.","g":["mining","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-003","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Crafting","t":"New","x":"When you are short of something, the box names the raw good you need (e.g. \"short of Iron x2\"), not the ingot.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-004","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Stores","t":"New","x":"When your Stores have no room for what it would refine, the box says so.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-005","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Crafting","t":"New","x":"If a refining step is refused, the message names the step where the chain stopped.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-006","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"Materials you can't make yet are dimmed. Those past your rank say the rank they need (\"Daedric - rank 90\").","g":["crafting","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-007","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"The anvil's Weapons, Armour, Tools and Repair Kits are 39 pieces, not 308 rows behind a metal picker.","g":["crafting","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-008","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"The first-make bonus (+500 XP) is now paid once per piece per tier, not once per material. Your first Adamantium, Ebony, Orcish or Warforged Longsword (all tier 6) pays it, and the rest of that tier don't. A Wand pays it once for Ironwood or Ghostwood, and Arrows once for any fletching. Pieces you made before still count.","g":["crafting","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-009","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"A merged craft keeps the higher of its two XP totals.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-010","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"Each rank's choice is the higher craft's where it chose, else the other's. If you chose under both at the same rank, you keep the higher craft's choice and may change it once for free - no Marks, in effect at once.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-011","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"A merged craft offers four choices at a rank, each named for the craft it acts on.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-012","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Professions","t":"New","x":"You may still take two crafts past Journeyman - now two of five.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-013","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"New","x":"The stations name the craft: \"Building 10\" at the workbench and the mason's bench, \"Smithing 25\" at the jeweller's bench, \"Provisioning\" at the fire and the alchemy station.","g":["alchemy","professions","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-014","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Smithing","t":"New","x":"Temper at an anvil (Smithing) or a loom (Outfitting): a weapon, a piece of metal armour, leather armour or clothing, one quality step better - Crude to Standard, Standard to Fine, Fine to Superior. Found or made, as long as it is Rare or below. A found piece counts as Standard.","g":["smithing","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-015","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Materials","t":"New","x":"A temper costs half the piece's recipe's main material, rounded up (a Steel Longsword: 2 Steel Ingots; a Leather Cuirass: 3 Cured Leather), needs that recipe's rank, and pays craft XP.","g":["mining","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-016","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Market","t":"New","x":"A tempered piece gains condition and loses a little weight. A crafted piece's record is re-signed at its new quality, so the Market shows what it is - and a Fine crafted piece tempered to Superior gains the Superior's Magic roll.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-017","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Sigils","t":"New","x":"Legendary, Aetheric, artifact and Sigil pieces can't be tempered, and a Masterwork keeps its maker's quality.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-018","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Arcane Essence","t":"New","x":"Reforge with Essence: from Enchanting 50, an enchanting station rolls one line of a known Magic piece again for 2 Arcane Essence, a Rare's for 5 - the Mages Guild's Reforge, paid in Essence. Once a piece is reforged, only that line again. No XP.","g":["enchanting","market","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-019","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Smithing","t":"New","x":"Take a worn piece off first. A shop's station charges its usual fee.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-020","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"Repair Kits made at an anvil now come in a quality, like other crafted pieces. A Superior or Masterwork kit mends a weapon or armour up to 90% of its condition; any other kit still stops at 75%. Each use still mends a quarter of the piece's condition.","g":["crafting","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-021","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"The kit's card says its quality and how far it mends. A Masterwork kit carries its maker's name.","g":["crafting","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6864-022","v":"0.1.6864","d":"2026-10-07","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"Kits you already own, and field kits found in loot, work as before.","g":["crafting","smithing","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6866-001","v":"0.1.6866","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Town Layouts","t":"New","x":"Town ponds no longer show flat painted squares. Tiles with a small island, a corner of water or a flipped diagonal shoreline now take the new water like the rest of the pond (Enhanced look).","g":["mod","homes","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6866-002","v":"0.1.6866","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Town Layouts","t":"New","x":"Six lone island tiles in town layouts are now dry ground, and some pond edges the puddle removal had wrongly cleared are back.","g":["mod","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-001","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Towns no longer sit in pits behind sheer walls of earth. The ground round every city, village and dungeon entrance now flows up to it from the surrounding land, so a town on a hillside sits on a hillside.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-002","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Coasts","t":"New","x":"Coastal towns no longer stand behind cliffs at the beach line; the strand rises to them gently.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-003","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Coasts","t":"New","x":"Towns on the coast stand on their own land, not dragged down toward the sea.","g":["water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-004","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"Rolling hills across the whole country, gentle in some regions and rolling hard in others, taller on the high ground.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-005","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"Rivers and streams cut their own valleys: the water lies at the bottom, with the hills rising either side.","g":["water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-006","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"Mountains: long ridgelines that hold their line for kilometres, with spurs and smooth valleys.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-007","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Woods","t":"New","x":"Mountain woods: foothills, half rolling and half ridges.","g":["logging","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-008","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"The Alik'r: dune seas lying across the wind, a long rise to windward and a steep slip face to lee. Dak'fron has mesas and buttes among its dunes.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-009","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"Rainforest: karst towers standing over plains. Subtropics: soft, broad domes.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-010","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"Swamps: near-flat, with shallow hollows and low hummocks.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-011","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Woods","t":"New","x":"Haunted woods: broken ground gashed by ravines and studded with crags.","g":["logging","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-012","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Terrain","t":"New","x":"Where climates meet, their lands blend across about a map pixel.","g":["climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-013","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Roads","t":"New","x":"Roads and tracks no longer climb every hill. The hills ease down beside a road, so it runs through a gentle corridor or over a saddle, and the hills rise again beside it.","g":["roads","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-014","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Town Layouts","t":"New","x":"Every player in a room stands on the same ground, even if a town pack failed to load for one of them.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-015","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"The new steel armour set now moves with the Morrowind body the way Morrowind's own armour does. The gauntlets stay on your hands, the pauldrons on your shoulders and the greaves and boots on your legs, in every pose, in third person and first person. No more T-posing pieces or gauntlets floating over the helm.","g":["climbing","morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6885-016","v":"0.1.6885","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Your companions no longer follow you into the Burning Court. They wait outside and rejoin you when you return, with the health and spells they had.","g":["companions","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-001","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"New","x":"Look around: selecting Info mode underground lights up, for six seconds, what's near you, in sight and nameable (within 8 m). A secrets tier also shows the hidden movers that only a lever chain reaches.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-002","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"New","x":"Lever echoes: a lever that moves something out of sight tells you which way. It marks the spot on the dungeon map until you find it, and the mark glows when you reach it. In Info mode, a lever's plaque says which way its work lies.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-003","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"New","x":"The way out: the compass points you back to the entrance along the trail you walked. It takes you down a drop you jumped from, and never back up one you can't climb.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-004","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"New","x":"Exact quest guidance (optional): a quest's people and things are marked on the dungeon map and the compass - a finished quest's no longer are.","g":["map","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-005","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Spells","t":"New","x":"Detect Treasure now also finds what's hidden in searched objects.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-006","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"Fix","x":"Secret walls are no longer labelled \"Door\".","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-007","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Sizes","t":"New","x":"Online, every dungeon has its own size - small, medium or large - the same for everyone in it. Dungeons that were already small stay small, and about half of all dungeons are medium. The main story's dungeons and Abyss Dungeons are always large.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-008","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Sizes","t":"New","x":"Medium Dungeons (offline): a new option builds dungeons at a medium size: two interior blocks closed by six.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-009","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Sizes","t":"New","x":"Dungeon sizes as online (offline): a new option uses the online sizes offline. A quest keeps the size it was set up at, so quests you started online keep their dungeons at the online sizes.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-010","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeons","t":"UI","x":"Online, a dungeon now says what it is - Regular Dungeon, Elite Dungeon or Abyss Dungeon - with its size beside it, as in \"Elite Dungeon, Small\". It shows on the entrance sign, the overworld name plates and the sighting message, and as a line when you go in; the held map says it for the Bay's own dungeons.","g":["online","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-011","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"One at a time, where the players are: an Abyss Dungeon - a Hollow of the Hour - rises beside a busy city in the region with the most players online.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-012","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Seen and heard of: a column of brass-gold light stands over it from the moment it rises, and the taverns of its city talk of it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-013","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Found: the first player to reach its door finds it, and everyone online hears where - by its city, or its region when no city is near. From then on its ring is on the map, its mark is on the compass, and it has a row in the Timers window and a note on the notice board, until it is gone.","g":["online","map","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-014","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The hardest dungeon in the game: three foes at every spot, each four times as tough and hitting two and a half times as hard, drawn from the strongest monsters there are; six elite foes; half again the loot; and no campfires - the Hour is cold.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-015","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Rift: at an Abyss Dungeon's deepest point stands the Rift - a ring of brass light around a dark membrane, tolling like a bell heard under water. Press it or walk into it. Beside it, a small Return of pale light takes you back to the way in. Once the Remnant has fallen the Rift takes no newcomers, but anyone who already went through can step back in while the Hour collapses.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-016","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Shattered Hour: through the Rift lies the moment the Warp left behind - islands of stone and brass hanging in a void, under a sky of brass aurorae, with the Bay's skylines hanging upside down in it and a clock-face of stars whose hands run backwards. Every player sees the same sky at the same moment. The Hour refuses what the Burning Court refuses: no rest, no saving, no map, no Mark or Recall, no regeneration - and no Levitate. The Rift at its back takes you home to the Hollow.","g":["sky","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-017","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Orrery of Endings: the Shattered Hour's first hall holds six Ending-stones - Daggerfall, Sentinel, Wayrest, Orsinium, the Underking and the Blades - each showing an hour of twelve. Turn a stone by its handles (the right turns it forward, the left back), and its hidden gears turn others with it. Six Ledger plaques round the hall say in riddles the hour each stone keeps; the dial in the floor lights a segment for every stone at its true hour - how many, not which. Every turn frays the Hour: at 48 it snaps back, resetting the stones and lashing a quarter of their health from everyone in the hall whose turns did not bring the stones nearer the Concord - whoever was setting them right, or never touched one, is spared. While others are turning, a player who has turned the stones the wrong way six times since the last snap has to wait, and guests count as one player. Set every stone right - the Concord - and a bridge of light opens toward the Unmoored Steps. Every Hollow's puzzle is its own, and everyone in the Hour turns the same stones.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-018","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Unmoored Steps: past the Orrery, a course of platforms over the void in three spans, each begun at a stone checkpoint. The Drift: eight brass platforms swinging side to side - the leap is in the timing, and a platform carries you as it swings. The Beat: platforms that are there only on the Hour's beat (they blink before they go, and the Hour ticks as they come back), and two brass walls to run up. The Crumble: cracked platforms that shudder and give way moments after you land, while the Warp's breath gusts across them - you hear the wind rise a second before each gust. Fall into the void and the Hour casts you back to the span's checkpoint, at the cost of some of your health (never your life). The platforms move the same for every player; a platform you break is broken only for you.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-019","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Brass Remnant: past the Steps, in the arena of the Last Moment, waits what the Warp kept of the Numidium - a brass colossus four times a man's height, its chest a cage around a heart of shattered soul-gem light. Step into the arena and the fight begins for everyone in the Hour at once; it grows tougher with every fighter who joins, by each fighter's own level, and once you've joined, the arena holds you until the fight ends, you die or you take the way home. The Walking Hour: it stamps a shock ring that rolls out across the arena (jump it), sweeps the Hour-Hand - a beam from its chest - across half the arena (outrun it, or put a pillar between you; its top is no shelter), and hurls gears that leave burning brass where they land. The Dragon Break: at 70% it steps outside time and two Echoes of it, gold and silver, take its place - fell them within 15 seconds of each other, or the one left alone rises again. The Last Moment: at 35% it returns, faster, and about once a minute it winds up the Reset - break every Heart that rises around the arena before it lands, or it takes most of everyone's health and heals. Through it all its heart pulses, a little harder each time - never more than three quarters of your health - and fifteen minutes after it wakes the Hour Ends. Its blows show on the arena's floor as they wind up; a blow about to land on you says Move!, with an arrow to the way out of it, or Jump! for the ring. When it falls, a chart ranks everyone's part in the fight and everyone online hears of it.","g":["online","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-020","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Each Hollow's marks: every Abyss Dungeon keeps one of six Endings - the element the Remnant fights in, its signature and the light it burns with - and two of nine omens that change the fight (a quarter more health, quicker wind-ups, a shorter Hour, a Pulse that climbs twice as fast...). They're said when it's found, shown on a card at its door and as you step into the Hour, and its blows and burning brass take its element - resist it to blunt them.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-021","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Hours broken, Hourbreaker and The Turning Hour: when the Remnant falls, everyone who truly fought it is credited an Hour broken, counted on their account card and on their Inspect card. Each Hour broken has a one-in-four chance to grant the title Hourbreaker and a one-in-eight chance to grant the aura The Turning Hour. Once held, they are yours for good. Online accounts with a username only - a guest's Hour is kept for a week and counted once they add one.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-022","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Brass of Numidium","t":"New","x":"The Brass of Numidium: a new Aetheric set of Dwarven brass - nine pieces, every one at the very top of the Legendary range. Dwemer Brass (2 pieces): +4 to +10 magic and shock resistance. Gearward (4 pieces): the next blow a foe lands on you is 15% to 30% lighter, then the gear winds again. The Hour Turns (6 pieces): a blow that would kill you does not - you are left standing and 15% to 25% of your health returns. Only the Brass Remnant's spoils carry it, one time in three.","g":["equipment","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-023","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Remnant's spoils: when it falls, everyone who truly fought it sees their own share burst from the cage of its chest and scatter across the arena floor - gold, a Rare piece that is Legendary one time in four, two more pieces Rare or better, one time in three a piece of the Brass of Numidium, and one time in fifty the Hourlock. Your share is yours alone. Whatever is left goes into your pack when you leave the Hour.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-024","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The collapse: three minutes after the Remnant falls, the Hour collapses. Everyone still inside the Abyss Dungeon or the Hour is told how long is left. Once the Remnant's body has sunk, a way home of pale light rises where it fell: step into it or press it to leave the Hour for the Abyss Dungeon's door outside.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-025","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"One life: die in the Shattered Hour and it casts you out for good - you wake before the Abyss Dungeon's door, and its Rift will not take you back. It's your account's one life, on every device and tab. When an Abyss Dungeon ends, anyone still inside it or the Hour is put out at its door.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-026","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Its own score: nine songs - the Hollow, the Orrery's hall, the Steps, one for each of the fight's three phases, its last minute, its fall and the collapse - each place's music giving way to the next.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-027","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Its voice and its air: the Remnant's steps, wind-ups and blows are heard where they happen; the Hour has its own wind, the ticking of its works, the Orrery's hum, and motes of brass drifting in its light.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-028","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Seen: every blow bursts in sparks, shakes the arena and lights the floor; the colossus walks, turns and swings with its whole body; its gears fly and the Hour-Hand's beam sweeps the floor it strikes; title cards mark each turn of the fight.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-029","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Its presence: near a standing Abyss Dungeon the land's light and haze lean to brass; at its door a banner names it and how long it has, its marks on a card beside it; its last hour is said to everyone online.","g":["online","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-030","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"A tab hidden through a landing no longer dodges it, and a frozen page no longer holds a place in the fight; the Hardened Hearts omen and the Hearts' toughness are fair to small parties; the Pulse never lands on top of the Reset.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-031","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Performance","x":"The fight runs smoother: its frames make next to no garbage, and its effects are built before the first blow lands.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-032","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The music no longer cuts out or plays the street's song between the Hollow's and the Hour's; the End sounds once, then tolls; nothing plays war over the dead.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-033","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"UI","x":"The banner at an Abyss Dungeon's door fits a phone's screen; the title card stays clear of the Remnant's bar; times read the same everywhere (\"1d 22h\"); its ring's card on the held map can be reached beside its city.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-034","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"A Resurrect in an ended Abyss Dungeon no longer strands you there; /unstuck in the Hour leaves by the Hour's own way home.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-035","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Gilded is the new top of the rarity ladder - above Aetheric, and above even Artifacts - the rarest thing in the game, its name in gold leaf and its frame breathing light in every slot.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-036","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Hourlock","t":"New","x":"A Gilded Thunderlock: what the Warp kept of a Dwemer smith's last commission, gilded in the Hour that never ended. Its lines never vary: +40% damage, +15 Agility, +30 Archery and +10 shock damage a shot - each at the very top of the Legendary range.","g":["thunderlock","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-037","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Hourlock","t":"New","x":"The Hour Tolls: every third shot that lands strikes for double, and a foe it fells gives back the pellet that felled it.","g":["thunderlock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-038","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Hourlock","t":"New","x":"Where to find it: the Brass Remnant's spoils, one time in fifty (online).","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-039","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Hourlock","t":"New","x":"About twice what any Legendary Thunderlock lands a shot, still the slowest weapon to fire. It can't be broken down, reforged, honed, cursed, socketed or made an heirloom, and in a duel its power sleeps. Its first find joins your codex, at the head of the list.","g":["thunderlock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-040","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dwarven Thunderlock","t":"New","x":"Shot in the shops: Dwemer Pellets are now sold wherever weapons are - Weapon Smiths, Armorers, General Stores and Pawn Shops - and restocked each day.","g":["thunderlock","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-041","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dwarven Thunderlock","t":"UI","x":"Its pictures in every slot: the gun and its pellets show their own art in your pack, on the hotbar and in the quick slots, instead of their initials; a list shows the whole gun.","g":["thunderlock","quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6980-042","v":"0.1.6980","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dwarven Thunderlock","t":"Fix","x":"The Morrowind gun, closed and kicking: the 3D gun has no holes left (you no longer see into its receiver), it kicks back at the shot, and the reload tips the gun down and back up - the breech heard after the bang, never before it.","g":["thunderlock","morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6984-001","v":"0.1.6984","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Rift is always reachable: the Rift no longer stands in a sealed room with no way in. It now stands at the deepest monster spawn point in the dungeon's inner rooms.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6984-002","v":"0.1.6984","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"No more flying out of the Hour: leaving the Shattered Hour after its Abyss Dungeon has ended no longer leaves you hanging in the sky above it - you land where you stood outside when you went in.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6984-003","v":"0.1.6984","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Rework","x":"Companions wait outside: your crew and sworn companions no longer follow you through the Rift. They wait outside the Hour and return to your side when you come back. Stepping through with them says *\"Your companions cannot follow you through the Rift.\"*","g":["companions","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6984-004","v":"0.1.6984","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"On the Overworld view, the dungeons near you - Daggerfall's own, the random dungeons online and a standing Abyss Dungeon - now show their own entrance model, enlarged so you can see them from above.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6988-001","v":"0.1.6988","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Stepping through the Rift no longer throws you straight back out of the Shattered Hour. The game was speaking to the Hour's server before the server had finished letting it in, and the server took that as a broken connection and closed the door on you, on almost every try.","g":["portals","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6988-002","v":"0.1.6988","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"A connection that blinks during the boss fight no longer throws you out of the Hour the same way.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6988-003","v":"0.1.6988","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Leaving the Shattered Hour, for any reason, now puts you on the ground in front of the Abyss Dungeon's door. It used to put you hundreds of metres in the air above it.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6988-004","v":"0.1.6988","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Other","x":"Reload the page. A tab left open from before the last update puts the Rift in its old place.","g":["portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-001","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"In winter, outside the deserts, real snow now lies on the ground, deeper in the wild than in towns. It builds up while snow falls and melts back in clear weather.","g":["weather","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-002","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"You, monsters, guards and townsfolk leave tracks in it. Tracks slowly fill back in, faster while it snows, and they are kept in your save.","g":["weather","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-003","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"A fallen enemy leaves a hollow in the snow where it lay.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-004","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"With Basic Roads, its paths and tracks keep only a thin layer of snow, and its main roads get a bank of snow along their edges.","g":["roads","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-005","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"The winter ground under it has new textures.","g":["terrain","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-006","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wind","t":"New","x":"Wind now changes from day to day. Trees and plants sway and shiver, some days turn windy or stormy, and gusts come and go with their own sound.","g":["weather","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-007","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wind","t":"New","x":"Leaves blow off the trees, and in winter snow blows off the boughs.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-008","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wind","t":"Fix","x":"The wind waits while the game is paused.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-009","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Heat Haze","t":"New","x":"In the deserts by day, the distant land and sky shimmer in the heat: fully under a clear sky, half as much under cloud, fading in after sunrise and out before sunset.","g":["distant-land","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-010","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Textures","t":"New","x":"The desert ground has new sand textures with ripples, from Sands of the Alik'r.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.6998-011","v":"0.1.6998","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Features","t":"Other","x":"All of it is on by default in the enhanced outdoors. Snowfall, Windfall and Heat Haze each have their own switch in Features; the desert sand and the winter ground are packs of their own on the Replacement packs card.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7002-001","v":"0.1.7002","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Launcher","t":"New","x":"The launcher can now be used with a controller: D-pad or left stick to move, A or Start to press, B to go back.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7002-002","v":"0.1.7002","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Launcher","t":"New","x":"Add --play to the game's launch options (Playnite, Steam shortcuts, Big Picture) to skip the launcher and go straight into the game.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7002-003","v":"0.1.7002","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Launcher","t":"Other","x":"Updates still arrive: you're told in-game, and they install when you quit.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7002-004","v":"0.1.7002","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Launcher","t":"Other","x":"The launcher still opens when it needs to ask you something: on the first run, or if your Daggerfall folder can't be found.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7016-001","v":"0.1.7016","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Auctions","t":"Fix","x":"An auction won in a town whose seat takes a Tithe now closes on time and pays its seller. Before, when the seller's Marks were near the cap, the sale could stick and never close, and twenty such sales held up every auction behind them.","g":["market","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7016-002","v":"0.1.7016","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Auctions","t":"Fix","x":"Auctions, guild writs and contracts now settle on time on the service's own clock, even when nobody opens the market or the Work tab.","g":["market","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7016-003","v":"0.1.7016","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Your letterbox, the count over a town's Notice Boards and your play time now share one request to the account service instead of three, and the service does about a third less database work for each player. Nothing you see changes.","g":["online","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-001","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Crouch","t":"Rework","x":"C now crouches *and* sneaks. While crouched you move at sneaking pace and the stealth checks apply, so enemies are slower to notice you.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-002","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Crouch","t":"Rework","x":"Left Alt no longer sneaks. The old standing sneak is still in Controls as an optional key, with no key set by default.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-003","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Crouch","t":"Other","x":"If you had your own key bindings saved, you'll see a one-time on-screen note that Sneak lost its key.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-004","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Mode Wheel","t":"New","x":"Hold Left Alt to open the wheel: Talk (up), Grab (right), Steal (down), Info (left).","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-005","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Mode Wheel","t":"New","x":"Flick the mouse toward a mode, then let go or click to choose. Move the mouse back to the middle to cancel.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-006","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Mode Wheel","t":"Rework","x":"F1 through F4 no longer change modes by default, and no longer open the browser's help or find bar. You can bind the four modes back to any keys in Controls.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-007","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Mode Wheel","t":"Other","x":"On a controller, the d-pad's \"next mode\" still cycles through the modes.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-008","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Cursor","t":"Rework","x":"On a controller, the menu cursor now eases in, speeds up on a long full push, slows over buttons and settles onto the nearest one when you let go.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-009","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Cursor","t":"Rework","x":"It works in every menu, on both the Classic and Enhanced skins.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-010","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Cursor","t":"Rework","x":"At the main menu the left stick moves the same cursor and A presses what it's on; the d-pad still jumps from button to button.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-011","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Cursor","t":"Other","x":"Don't like it? Settings → Controls → Controller cursor assist → Off gives back Daggerfall's plain fixed-speed cursor.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7025-012","v":"0.1.7025","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Cursor","t":"Fix","x":"Clicking with the controller cursor no longer acts like a held-down drag in some windows.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-001","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Spells","t":"Rework","x":"Classic spellcasting now runs at the same pace as the Morrowind animation. The spell leaves your hands at half a second, so players using the Morrowind hands are no longer slower than everyone else.","g":["animation","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-002","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Spells","t":"Rework","x":"A new cast can't start until your hands finish the motion. Clicking or recasting during that motion does nothing and costs nothing.","g":["animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-003","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Spells","t":"New","x":"Casting speed now scales with your Speed attribute: up to 25% faster at high Speed, 25% slower at low.","g":["animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-004","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"New rarity affix, +N% casting speed, on jewellery and weapons. Everything you wear adds up, capped at 30%. Because it rolls on jewellery, classes that can't wear plate can still get it.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-005","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"The heart of the Wrothgarian Mountains is now an open PvP zone, marked on the world map with a red border and drifting fog. Wrothgaria itself stays outside it.","g":["map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-006","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Other players in the zone can attack you, except your party, your guild and your duel opponent. That includes its dungeons. Attacking a player inside a city calls the guards, and the zone's guards are ten times as strong.","g":["online","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-007","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Foes in the zone are four times as strong, elites and champions included, and travel in packs four times the size.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-008","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"The zone has four tiers, from the Foothills at its edge to the Heart. Loot rises with each one: +25%, +50%, +75% and +100% (twice the gold, twice the drops, twice the odds of a rare piece).","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-009","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Click the zone on the world map, or press V while inside it, to open its own map. It shows the tiers, the towns, the dungeons and where you stand.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-010","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"When you die you keep your potions, torches, campfire kit, food, ammunition and anything that never changes hands. Your bags and your cart's load drop where you fell and stay there for 10 minutes. They are marked so you can find them again, and anyone can take them.","g":["death-penalty","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-011","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Killed by another player, the killer may also take one piece of your worn gear.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-012","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"You wait two minutes before you can respawn. You rise in the nearest town outside the zone, and your cart comes with you.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-013","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"You cannot fast travel into or out of the zone. Inside it a fast journey costs 2,500 to 15,000 gold depending on the tier you arrive in, and you can take one every 10 minutes. Walking on the Overworld map works as always.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-014","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"In the zone, travel speed is capped at x20 in the wilds and x40 on roads.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-015","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"The Overworld no longer refuses a walk over mountains.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-016","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Other players who are not in your party or guild show as red \"Strangers\" with no name. You can see them from 1.5 km away, and the closer they get the more they slow your travel.","g":["overworld","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-017","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"/unstuck now sends you to the next town when you are outdoors. It has a cooldown. In the zone it works only indoors, takes five minutes and can be cancelled.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-018","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Each tier of the zone has two Greater Giants, shown on the zone map where they wander, and everyone in the zone sees the same ones. At half health a Greater Giant calls ten giants to help. Giants never leave the zone.","g":["online","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-019","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"The zone has its own dungeons, its halls, which change each day. Once you leave a hall you can't go back in for an hour, unless your own remains are still inside; a small lock marks it on the map. Crows circle a hall where a player died.","g":["map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-020","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Banks, house purchases, world events and revenants are restricted inside the zone: only one revenant may walk with you there.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-021","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Temples","t":"New","x":"Temples now offer Heal Curse beside Heal Disease.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-022","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Resting","t":"New","x":"Resting while poisoned or diseased now warns you first.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-023","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Shop Screen","t":"New","x":"Hovering an item in any shop shows the same card as in your inventory.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-024","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Stats Card","t":"New","x":"The stats screen shows your resistances.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7051-025","v":"0.1.7051","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Dungeon Respawn","t":"Rework","x":"Ordinary dungeons outside the zone respawn after 20 minutes, elite dungeons after 40.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7076-001","v":"0.1.7076","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"Sit at a tavern's card table and play Hold'em. The tavern's regulars take the other chairs, and your character is seated in the chair for everyone to see.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7076-002","v":"0.1.7076","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"Online, the relay deals: shuffle, hole cards and the seat clock are the relay's, so nobody's client can see another's hand.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7076-003","v":"0.1.7076","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"Gold tables: buy in with real gold, held in escrow by the account service and paid out on the hand's receipt. Top up between hands.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7076-004","v":"0.1.7076","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"The cards are physical on the cloth: dealt, fanned, peeked at, chips dragged to bet, the deck riffled.","g":["animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7076-005","v":"0.1.7076","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"A two-player collectible game played on the same table: three holdings between you, six turns, hold two of three to win. Units, spells and Daedric Prince cards, each painted in code with the Iliac Bay's own creatures, artifacts and places.","g":["holdings","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7076-006","v":"0.1.7076","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"The Card Binder is an item every character carries from creation; it holds your decks. A new Collections tab under Holdings shows the weapon codex and your cards side by side.","g":["holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7084-001","v":"0.1.7084","d":"2026-10-08","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"New","x":"A monument to Julian LeFay, one of the creators of Daggerfall, now stands in the middle of Gothway Garden. It has three granite steps, a marble pedestal and a gilt-tipped obelisk. A bronze plaque on each side reads \"Julian LeFay, 1965 - 2025, Father of The Elder Scrolls\".","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7084-002","v":"0.1.7084","d":"2026-10-08","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"New","x":"Look at the monument to choose Throw flowers or Read the inscription. In Info mode a press reads the inscription.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7084-003","v":"0.1.7084","d":"2026-10-08","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"New","x":"A thrown flower lands on the monument's steps or at its foot, on your side. Each character keeps its own flowers: up to the 48 newest stay where they landed after you save and load, and the plaque counts how many you have laid.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7084-004","v":"0.1.7084","d":"2026-10-08","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"New","x":"Townspeople walk around the monument.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7084-005","v":"0.1.7084","d":"2026-10-08","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"New","x":"Online, your flowers are yours alone. Other players see the monument, but not the flowers you laid.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7097-001","v":"0.1.7097","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Enhanced Maps","t":"New","x":"Zoom the enhanced map out past the Iliac Bay and the whole of Tamriel is on the sheet, drawn in the same hand: the nine provinces and their borders, the capitals, the mountains, the rivers and the seas, with the Bay inside a faint dotted frame and its coast running on into the continent's. Hover beyond the Bay to read the province, a capital or the sea. Nothing beyond the Bay can be travelled to.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7097-002","v":"0.1.7097","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Land Beyond the Bay","t":"New","x":"Walk off the edge of the Iliac Bay and the land of Tamriel continues under your feet: hills, mountains and coasts under each province's own sky and trees, as far as you care to walk. Empty ground for now - no towns, roads or dungeons stand there yet.","g":["terrain","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7097-003","v":"0.1.7097","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Features","t":"Other","x":"Both are Features rows (Tamriel on the map; Land beyond the Bay), on by default on the enhanced skin.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7099-001","v":"0.1.7099","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Land Beyond the Bay","t":"Fix","x":"The land beyond the Bay had pulled the online relay's code into the terrain worker, and the world froze on its first outdoor build. Fixed.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7101-001","v":"0.1.7101","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Enhanced Maps","t":"Rework","x":"The land beyond the Iliac Bay is now traced from your own game's map of Tamriel (the race screen's picture), so the coast, the provinces and the borders are the ones Daggerfall drew.","g":["map","parity"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7101-002","v":"0.1.7101","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Enhanced Maps","t":"Rework","x":"The Bay is placed on that map by matching its own coastline, so the join is where the game put it.","g":["map","parity"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7101-003","v":"0.1.7101","d":"2026-10-08","e":"Land Beyond the Bay","t":"Rework","x":"The ground past the Bay's edge follows the same traced land.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7110-001","v":"0.1.7110","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"Every tavern and inn now has its own card table: a green-felt poker table with six stools, standing near the entrance.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7110-002","v":"0.1.7110","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"Walk up to it and press activate to sit down and play Hold'em with the regulars, or with other players online.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7110-003","v":"0.1.7110","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Rework","x":"The tavern's ordinary dining tables are no longer card tables.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7112-001","v":"0.1.7112","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Enhanced Maps","t":"Fix","x":"The land past the Iliac Bay is now the shape Daggerfall's own map paints: one continent with the Imperial Province in the middle, not eight islands.","g":["map","parity"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7112-002","v":"0.1.7112","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Enhanced Maps","t":"Fix","x":"The Bay sits on it where its coastline matches.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-001","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"Townsfolk inside a building no longer bunch up by the door. They spread through the whole room and sit at tables set apart, never at a table split by a wall.","g":["interior","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-002","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Nobody sits in the tavern for hours waiting for lunch.","g":["interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-003","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Everyone in a room sees the same people in the same places, whether or not a door was left open.","g":["online","interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-004","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"The watch posted at a city's gates stops strangers coming in and asks their business. Strangers answer civilly, curtly or with open hostility, and sellswords and sailors are rougher.","g":["law","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-005","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Town Watch","t":"New","x":"Patrols stop strangers on their rounds.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-006","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk fall out with each other, more often in the evening between drinkers, and the watch breaks it up.","g":["social","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-007","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Buyers haggle at stalls, and beggars ask passers-by for a coin.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-008","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"When someone shouts, the people nearby fall quiet and turn to look.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-009","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"New","x":"Small voices fill the street: the night watch calls the hour, with words for the weather; stalls cry their wares; beggars call out; drinkers sing on the way home from the tavern.","g":["audio","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-010","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Every player in a town sees the same incidents at the same places.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-011","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"A stranger at the gate names their own home town, and a beggar no longer calls a stranger by name.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-012","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Every stranger stopped at a gate is questioned, and a gate stop no longer keeps a visitor from leaving town.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-013","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"The watch breaks up a quarrel even at a change of shift, and only one of a patrol pair calls the hour.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-014","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"A beggar no longer pulls a stall keeper away from their stall.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-015","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Beggars and stall keepers turn to face whoever they are talking to.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-016","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"People in an incident greet you again once it's over.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7127-017","v":"0.1.7127","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Stall keepers no longer cry their wares before they reach the stall.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7134-001","v":"0.1.7134","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Spellbook","t":"Rework","x":"The spellbook can no longer be dropped, put in a chest, pile or companion's pack, shift-dropped, or sold at a shop. It still goes into your own wagon. The game tells you: \"Your spellbook never leaves you.\"","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7134-002","v":"0.1.7134","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"In an Enduring family, a vampire, werewolf or wereboar who dies loses no years to Arkay's toll and always rises, even with their span spent. Once cured, the toll applies again from the next death.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7134-003","v":"0.1.7134","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"A letter of credit is now dropped at a death in the zone, at its full value, like the purse's gold.","g":["death-penalty","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7134-004","v":"0.1.7134","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Wallet","t":"Fix","x":"The wallet and the Deadlands Embers and Welkynd Shards it holds always stay with you.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-001","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Every quest can now be abandoned and later reclaimed. You'll find this in the pause menu's Quests tab.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-002","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Abandon asks you to click twice to confirm.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-003","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Reclaim takes one click and works from the new Abandoned section.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-004","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"An abandoned quest is set aside, not lost:","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-005","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"its timer stops;","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-006","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"its items, topics and journal are kept;","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-007","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"its dungeon or building stays reserved for it.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-008","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"When you reclaim a quest, it picks up where you left it, and the days it spent abandoned don't count against its deadline.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-009","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Abandoning a quest frees its quest-giver, so the guild offers you work again.","g":["quests","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-010","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"The game's built-in quests (the main quest's core, the curse and the tutorial) and sea raids can't be abandoned.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-011","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"A reclaimed quest doesn't rejoin your party's shared progress. Share it again.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-012","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Fix","x":"Medium dungeons no longer repeat the same layout block twice. Quests already inside a changed dungeon move their targets to match.","g":["online","audit","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-013","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Fix","x":"Lord K'avar in Privateer's Hold: random quests no longer send you into main-story dungeons. Quests that were already stuck there are moved to a proper dungeon.","g":["online","audit","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-014","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Fix","x":"Enduring and Bloodlines characters can marry again. Propose marriage was greyed out for every character who should have been allowed to wed.","g":["online","audit","blood"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-015","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Fix","x":"Mercantile and Personality matter again when selling online. Better skills now get a better price, still within the online limit of half the shop's price.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-016","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Fix","x":"Fast travel no longer drops you inside a mountain. A landing inside rock now puts you on the nearest open ground.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-017","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Fix","x":"Enhanced Water can be switched off online. The toggle was locked while playing online.","g":["online","audit","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7143-018","v":"0.1.7143","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"The bank's ship loan has been removed. Ships are bought outright again. A ship you already bought on credit is unaffected.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-001","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Pause Menu","t":"New","x":"The pause menu now has a mailbox: an envelope beside the hourglass (online).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-002","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Pause Menu","t":"New","x":"When the developers send you a message, the envelope shows a count, and a line in the world chat tells you post has arrived.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-003","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Pause Menu","t":"New","x":"Open a message to read it. If it holds an item, press Claim and the item goes into the pack of the online character you're playing.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-004","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Pause Menu","t":"New","x":"Type /mail in chat to open the mailbox from anywhere: outdoors, indoors or underground, on either menu style.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-005","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Pause Menu","t":"New","x":"A message whose item you haven't claimed can't be thrown away by mistake.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-006","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The thirteen players of the first Abyss Dungeon clear have been honoured:","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-007","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"a new title, Hour's First, drawn in rose gold, pearl and the white of dawn;","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-008","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"a new aura, The First Hour: The Turning Hour's wheel cast in the first dawn's light, with its dial turning forward, the Hour's own mark ablaze, and rays of first light;","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-009","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Hourlock, waiting for each of them in the mailbox.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7153-010","v":"0.1.7153","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Wear the title and aura from your profile.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-001","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Snow","t":"New","x":"With Snowless Swamps and Jungles switched on, swamps and jungles no longer get deep snow on the ground or falling snow in winter.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-002","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Reach","t":"New","x":"Deserts no longer get snow drifting in from nearby snowy regions, and the edge of the desert next to a snowy area stays bare. Snow storms that reach the desert now fall as rain.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-003","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Front Door","t":"New","x":"You can now decorate the ground right outside your own front door. Many desert houses are L-shaped or have an outside stair, and the open ground in front of their doors counted as \"inside your house\". Spots under your own roof or eaves still count as the house.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-004","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Opening the Overworld no longer freezes the game: nearby dungeon models now load one per frame once the view has finished rising.","g":["rendering","map","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-005","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Long journeys no longer slowly use up video memory. The dungeon models' textures are released when you leave them behind.","g":["rendering","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-006","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Deep snow no longer does its work while the Overworld is open, since none of it is shown there.","g":["rendering","map","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-007","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Saving is faster in snowy areas: the snow-track data is only recompressed when it has changed. Online, this removes a hitch that happened every two minutes.","g":["rendering","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-008","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"Fixed a crash (\"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'velocity')\") when another player's ship list changed while you stood on one of their ships.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-009","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Houses","t":"New","x":"When a member of your family dies for good, their houses pass to whoever carries the line on - door, bed, chests and furniture as they left them.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-010","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Houses","t":"New","x":"Online, a fallen character's home moves to their heir, cupboards included.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7163-011","v":"0.1.7163","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Houses","t":"New","x":"If your heir already owns a house in that region, the inherited one waits until they sell theirs.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7166-001","v":"0.1.7166","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Characters","t":"Fix","x":"Card tables locked players out. Each tavern had one table, and whoever sat first decided whether it played for gold or for chips. One realm character staking gold shut every guest out, and one guest playing for chips shut out every realm character.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7166-002","v":"0.1.7166","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Characters","t":"New","x":"The red table plays for gold, and only realm characters can stake at it.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7166-003","v":"0.1.7166","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Characters","t":"New","x":"Realm characters can now also play for chips at the green table, alongside everyone else.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-001","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Whenever a Rare, Legendary, Aetheric, Artifact or Gilded item reaches your pack, wagon or Materials Bag, a banner slides in at the right edge of the screen: the item's picture framed in its tier colour, its tier and pips, its name, and what it is.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-002","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"It works however the item arrives: loot, boss and raid spoils, quest rewards, crafting, the Sigil Broker, shops, trades, the market, and Iliac cards (shown with their own card face and a count when you get several).","g":["arena","seats","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-003","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Aetheric, Artifact and Gilded items get a bigger, glowing banner and a fanfare.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-004","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Up to three banners show at once, newest on top; more wait their turn, best tier first. They pause while a window is open, so a purchase announces itself when you leave the counter.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-005","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Moving items between your pack, wagon and bag, or taking your own things back out of storage, never shows a banner.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-006","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"A first find for your codex now shows \"New to your codex\" on its banner instead of a separate line.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-007","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"The small pickup feed under the crosshair no longer repeats an item its banner is announcing.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7170-008","v":"0.1.7170","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Move or hide the banners in the HUD editor (Alt+U): Loot banners.","g":["arena","seats","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7173-001","v":"0.1.7173","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Realm","t":"Fix","x":"At the red (gold) table, if the realm can't take your stake, the panel now says why, beside the buy-in. Before, \"Deal me in\" seemed to do nothing.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7178-001","v":"0.1.7178","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Land Beyond the Bay","t":"Fix","x":"Clicking a spot on the Overworld while you're past the edge of the Iliac Bay no longer crashes the game (\"RangeError: invalid array length\"). The Overworld now plans journeys across the land beyond the Bay.","g":["terrain","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7178-002","v":"0.1.7178","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Logging","t":"Fix","x":"Online, a player beyond the Bay is no longer invisible. Players there see each other and the players near the edge, and the game no longer drops your connection out there. Logging back in there now works too.","g":["logging","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-001","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Town Map","t":"Fix","x":"A Dark Brotherhood or Thieves Guild member's hall stays named on the town map and at its door while you have a contract.","g":["map","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-002","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Looted weapons, armour, clothing and jewellery can be listed on the market, sold at stalls and traded again.","g":["market","online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-003","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Fix","x":"Motherlodes, veins, boulders, herbs and trees no longer appear inside rocks.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-004","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Talk Window","t":"Fix","x":"The carriage driver at one gate of each walled city (Shrarton in Tasoparet) now has a face in the talk window.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-005","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Spellcasting","t":"New","x":"The casting hands are quick again: a spell leaves your hands 0.2 seconds after you cast it, as it did before the casting speed change.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-006","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Spellcasting","t":"New","x":"Spells still can't be spammed. The next cast waits out a short recovery, and your Speed and any \"+% casting speed\" on your gear shorten it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-007","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Spellcasting","t":"New","x":"The thin dotted line that showed up beside the casting hands on some graphics cards is gone.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-008","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Dungeons","t":"New","x":"If two players' dungeons were built differently (usually one of you on an older version), you now see the host's monsters instead of fighting ones nobody else can see. The game tells you once to reload.","g":["online","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-009","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Foes","t":"New","x":"Other players' monsters keep up better while they run, so you're less likely to swing at the air where a monster used to be.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-010","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Foes","t":"New","x":"More of another player's summoned and called monsters are shown, including all ten of a Greater Giant's call.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-011","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Quest monsters are visible to everyone nearby, and anyone can hit them. When a party member kills one of your quest's monsters, it counts for everyone in the party with that quest.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-012","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"After you die, your own pile of remains now shows up.","g":["online","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-013","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"A red \"My remains\" waypoint marks where your remains lie, on both the Overworld and the world map, and goes away when they do.","g":["online","map","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-014","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"The giant angular rock spires from World of Daggerfall's mountains are off by default. The mountain regions get rounded mountains instead. You can turn the spires back on in the mod's settings (\"Mountains\"); online, the room decides.","g":["mod","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7184-015","v":"0.1.7184","d":"2026-10-09","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"New","x":"Boulders in rock fields no longer hang over slopes with their open undersides showing.","g":["mod","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7186-001","v":"0.1.7186","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Launcher","t":"New","x":"The Discord links on the website, the Terms and Privacy pages, and the desktop launcher now point to our new invite: https://discord.gg/jM2JdwSM8w","g":["desktop-app","gamepad","website"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-001","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"The Rift is now a brass astrolabe standing in a cracked crater, turned to face down its hall's longest line. Its gear ticks forward once a second, and its ring of Roman-numeral hours clicks back an hour on every toll.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-002","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Rift","t":"New","x":"Its iris shows its state. It opens wide while the Hour can be entered, narrows to a pinhole when it can't, and shuts when the Hour closes. Studs round its rim count down the hours the Hollow has left, and during the collapse they go out one by one.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-003","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Rift","t":"New","x":"Through the iris you see the Hour's own sky, with real depth as you move. Gold light drifts in from the rim, and the gear's teeth cast turning spokes of light on the floor.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-004","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Silver","t":"New","x":"The Return is a pale stone arch with silver bands and a window home: the sky over the Hollow's city at the world's real hour, with Masser and Secunda at night.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-005","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Silver","t":"New","x":"A silver hand-plate on every Return's sill lights up when you aim at it.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-006","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Stepping Through","t":"New","x":"Entering the Hour has its own transition: twelve brass blades close over the Rift wherever it is on your screen and lock into a clock face. Its hand sweeps backwards and the broken quarters chime, and if you hold there long enough, the Dragon Break splits the hand and cracks the face. The face then shatters open onto the Threshold.","g":["clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-007","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Silver","t":"New","x":"Leaving by the way back or the Return, the clock is silver and still cracked. Taking the way home, the crack mends as it shuts. Being thrown out by force shatters the face into falling pieces.","g":["marks","online","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-008","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Stepping Through","t":"New","x":"If your system is set to reduce motion, the face holds still and fades in and out instead.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-009","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Stepping Through","t":"New","x":"When you arrive in the Hour, the way back breathes out a spray of brass sparks and its ring turns once.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-010","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Compass","t":"New","x":"The light has been redone, so floors read as stone and brass instead of one amber glow. The Threshold is paved with the Bay's cobbles around a compass rose.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-011","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Shattered Hour","t":"New","x":"The islands hang in the void on jagged rock spires, with half-buried gears and chains swaying on the clock's tick. Distant islands drift slowly below. Far beneath the course, the Works turn: four vast gears, black against the furnace glow, a tooth at a time.","g":["clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-012","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Hanging","t":"New","x":"The sky is hand-painted: dithered bands of void, single-pixel stars, aurorae, a great clock face drawn in stars with its numerals and the six Endings as constellations, and the Bay's cities hanging upside down with their windows lit. Its hands run on the Hour's clock.","g":["climbing","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-013","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Shattered Hour","t":"New","x":"The way back looks into the hall you came from: dark coursed stone lit gold from the front. Its rings turn forward, and it casts the Hour's only cool light.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-014","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Shattered Hour","t":"New","x":"The arena tells you the fight through its floor. Eight fissures flood green each time a Mantella Pulse lands. The rim's numerals light one by one through the Reset and the last two burn ember. When the Hour ends, everything turns red. The sky's clock follows along.","g":["arena","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-015","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Shattered Hour","t":"New","x":"The Stomp's ring now rises as a low wall of brass light you can see to jump. While the fight holds you in the arena, a gold curtain rises at its rim.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-016","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Lantern","t":"New","x":"The arena's four pillars are clock-towers now. Their dials' hands follow the Remnant (the Echoes in the Dragon Break, the way home once it falls), and a lantern burns in each cage. A brass mark on the floor shows where the Remnant and each Echo stand, and the arena's lamps dim as the Reset gathers.","g":["arena","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-017","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Helm","t":"New","x":"The Brass Remnant has been rebuilt from riveted brass plate. It has a domed helm crowned with seven broken clock hands, bell pauldrons, an open ribcage around a cut soul-gem heart, knee and elbow gears, organ-pipe vents, and a right forearm that is the Hour-Hand itself. Its heart lights the arena in its Ending's colour and beats faster as the next Pulse nears.","g":["equipment","arena","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-018","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Shattered Hour","t":"New","x":"The Remnant shows what it's about to do. The part about to strike heats up: its raised foot before a Stomp, its blade before the Hour-Hand, its fist before a Volley, its ribs before a Pulse, its heart before the Reset.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-019","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"A great dial on its back keeps the fight's time: it ticks backwards, runs down a stun, and spins back to twelve on the Reset. In the Dragon Break, the surviving Echo's dial counts down its partner's window. Lamps on its ribs count the Hearts still standing.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-020","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Shattered Hour","t":"New","x":"When it falls, its heart tears out and rises before going dark, and the dial breaks free and rolls away.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-021","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Silver","t":"New","x":"Where it falls, the way home assembles inside a column of pale light: the jambs rise out of the floor, the arch swings shut, and the keystone clock drops into place. In the Hour it stands half again as large, with a silver beacon over it, tall for its first ten seconds and then low.","g":["marks","online","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-022","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Climb","t":"New","x":"Every step shows what it will do next. Beat plates are clock faces whose hand runs down to the moment they vanish, and they dissolve in pixels instead of blinking out. Drift steps hang from pendulums. Risers climb on gear racks.","g":["clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-023","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Unmoored Steps","t":"New","x":"Crumble stones crack in stages under your feet, fall in pieces, and fly back together when they return.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-024","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Unmoored Steps","t":"New","x":"A vane on the last island swings toward the next gust a second before it hits.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-025","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"The Unmoored Steps","t":"New","x":"Waystones mark where the void will send you back, and a golden burst plays in reverse when it does. Faint outlines show where vanished steps will return.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-026","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Orrery of Endings","t":"New","x":"The six stones are rebuilt: carved shafts with their sign, a dial in a bezel, and a gear on top that turns with the hand. The bezel glows gold while a stone turns and ember when your turn is refused.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-027","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"Banners hang from each stone, lecterns hold the plaques' ledgers, and the floor's dial is raised in brass, its lit plates glowing like soul gems. Tabs round the rim count the fray and pulse near the end.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-028","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Orrery of Endings","t":"New","x":"Six rings turn slowly overhead, shivering as the Hour frays. At the Concord they swing flat, the gem flares, and the bridge lays itself in twelve plates.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-029","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Changing weapons or casting on an ally right after a connection blip no longer throws you out of the Hour. Neither does entering the Hour, which a party-status message used to trigger every time.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-030","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Hiding the tab no longer dodges the Pulse, the Reset or the End.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-031","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"A fighter whose connection dropped while a fight was lost can rejoin the next fight instead of being stuck.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-032","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"You can no longer set a Mark inside an Abyss Dungeon.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-033","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Stepping into the Rift now works on slow machines and across a hitch.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-034","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Pressing near the Rift no longer grabs it when you're aiming at a body or the floor.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-035","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Return and the landing back from the Hour no longer stand on or next to the Rift in small rooms.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-036","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Rift is sized to fit its hall and no longer pokes through pillars or ceilings.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-037","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Abyss Dungeons no longer appear on beaches or with their end underwater.","g":["online","portals","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-038","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"A refused or failed step through the Rift leaves you in front of the Hollow's door instead of in its middle.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-039","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"An open door no longer moves where the Rift stands from one player to the next.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-040","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Remnant no longer grunts while it's outside time, a Stomp lands as one thud instead of two, and the Hour's distant sounds stop when you leave.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-041","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Coming back to the tab no longer plays every Heart that broke while you were away all at once.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-042","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Brass of Numidium","t":"Fix","x":"The Brass of Numidium's powers play the right sounds.","g":["equipment","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-043","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The fight's title cards only show near the arena. Interrupted lines are repeated. The Hour's messages wait while a window is open, sit above the arrival and damage cards, and no longer wrap to four lines on phones.","g":["online","portals","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-044","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Remnant's health bar uses the Hour's own colours.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-045","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"After the Concord, a stone's plaque says \"The Concord holds.\" instead of offering a turn.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-046","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The large boat no longer shares its textures with the Shattered Hour.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-047","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Rift's and the Return's textures sit where they belong: the Return's stone and dial were drawing in the Rift's brass, and four of the ring's numerals showed the wrong picture.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-048","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Levitate no longer works in the Shattered Hour. The Steps are walked, not flown.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-049","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"You can no longer walk onto the Concord's bridge before it has finished laying.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-050","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Drift's pendulum rods hang beside its platform instead of through anyone standing at its edge.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-051","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The sky and the arena no longer turn red before a fight has started.","g":["online","portals","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-052","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The way back no longer rings a bell every time you arrive, and its light stays on the island instead of spilling into the void.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-053","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The arrival sparks wait until the step-through animation finishes, and play on every arrival, not only the first.","g":["online","portals","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7296-054","v":"0.1.7296","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"The Hollow and the Hour run with less memory churn: the Rift, the sky, the Orrery's hands and the Hour's sounds no longer allocate every frame.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-001","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Features","t":"New","x":"Settings and Features are now one screen, in tabs: Graphics, Gameplay, Combat, World, Interface, Audio, Controls, Accessibility, Mods & files.","g":["morrowind","weather","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-002","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Settings","t":"New","x":"Graphics opens on a quality preset: Low, Medium, High or Ultra.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-003","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Mods","t":"New","x":"One search across every tab. Filter by what you changed, Enhanced, Mods or Daggerfall Unity.","g":["mod","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-004","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Restore","t":"New","x":"Each tab can restore its own defaults. \"Reset everything to defaults\" resets every setting and mod.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-005","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Mods","t":"New","x":"Mods & files lists every mod and takes you to its options.","g":["mod","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-006","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Settings","t":"New","x":"Less text. Press a row's name to read more about it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-007","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Death Screen","t":"Fix","x":"Quick-loading (F11) after dying in town no longer leaves the death screen up.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-008","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Paperdoll","t":"Fix","x":"Face mods (Paperdoll Enhanced) draw faces at their proper size.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-009","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Morrowind Asset Pack","t":"New","x":"Updated steel armour model: wider breastplate shoulders, larger pauldrons, and the waist band is its own piece.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-010","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Helm","t":"New","x":"The steel helm (closed and open) now sits properly on your head. Before, the top of your head poked through the closed helm.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7312-011","v":"0.1.7312","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"New","x":"Morrowind models (your body, arms, armour, weapons and item pictures) now use smooth shading instead of a faceted look.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-001","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"The Oblivion Gate is a new, handcrafted model: two clawed pillars under a heavy lintel, ringed with burning spines.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-002","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Its stone is cracked basalt veined with fire. The frame around the portal smoulders by night, and the spines burn toward their points.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-003","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"The portal's fire now fills the gate's opening right to the stone, and it meets the ground even on a slope.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-004","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"The gate rises fully out of the ground, with no piece of it showing early on a hillside.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-005","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Anyone caught inside the stone as the gate finishes rising is set down safely in front of it, wherever they stood. Players standing in the doorway or beside the gate's feet are no longer moved.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-006","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Burning Court","t":"New","x":"The portal on the bridge is gone. You step out of a gate of fire that closes behind you, and it opens again when another player arrives (including someone coming back in).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-007","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Burning Court","t":"New","x":"The way home opens where the Warden falls, as before, and now closes as the court comes apart.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-008","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Burning Court","t":"New","x":"Until he falls, the only ways out are death and the Wrath. /unstuck no longer works inside the court.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7319-009","v":"0.1.7319","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Burning Court","t":"New","x":"If the fight stops answering (a full or stalled room), you are returned to Tamriel after 20 seconds instead of being stranded.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-001","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Iliac Hand at the tavern table. Sit at a card table and choose Play Iliac Hand to play the collectible card game with a deck from your Card Binder.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-002","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Offline, against the tavern's regulars. Each regular has a temper (careful, reckless or sly) and a deck to match the tavern: a village's regulars play close to the starter deck, and a city's carry a Daedric Prince.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-003","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Play for fun, or for keeps: each side stakes a card and the loser hands it over. Your staked card is set aside when the game is dealt and returned if you win or draw. A regular pays out one card a day.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-004","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Online, against another player at the same table. The relay deals and keeps every hand hidden.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-005","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Ranked, for realm characters on a registered account. Results count on a season board (the arena's seasons and ratings), and the season's top player wears the new Iliac Champion title.","g":["audio","loot","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-006","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Where cards come from:","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-007","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"A slain creature sometimes drops its own card (a rat drops a Rat). Titled foes drop theirs twice as often.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-008","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"A finished guild, temple or knightly-order quest pays one of that guild's cards about one time in three. A higher rank pays a better card.","g":["audio","loot","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-009","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Card Packs are sold at Enhanced taverns' counters and card tables. Each holds five cards, the last rare or better.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-010","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Three new boss cards: the Oblivion Gate's Warden, Sethrakul, and the Abyss Dungeon's Brass Remnant. The set is now 85 cards.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-011","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"At the Hold'em table:","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-012","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Press your cards and pull down to squeeze them.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-013","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Click your cards to check, or push them up the screen to fold on your turn.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-014","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"New","x":"Other players seated at a card table now sit in their chairs instead of standing in them.","g":["audio","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-015","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"Realm customs counts cards. An offline character entering the realm can bring cards worth the starter deck (285) plus 150 per level. Customs keeps the rest back, dearest first, and tells you how many stayed behind. Sealed packs and cards set out as decor count too.","g":["holdings","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7348-016","v":"0.1.7348","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"Iliac Hand's panel can be played with the keyboard.","g":["holdings","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7350-001","v":"0.1.7350","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"Tavern card tables no longer stand across doorways; they keep a walking lane clear.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7350-002","v":"0.1.7350","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"Ghost and other flying companions no longer climb into the ceiling while following, and their health bar shows again.","g":["social","online","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7350-003","v":"0.1.7350","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"Your PvP remains stay marked on the map if the game crashes or closes before you reach them.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7350-004","v":"0.1.7350","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"Firefox for Android: tapping the screen no longer opens the pause menu.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7350-005","v":"0.1.7350","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"The Stores page now lists looted, shop-bought or traded materials as \"unstorable\" and explains why they can't go in.","g":["social","online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-001","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Characters","t":"New","x":"Every save the realm takes from an online character is now read by the server, not only the first. It checks that every item you hold is one the game can actually make, that your level matches what your character card shows, and that your gold, attributes and skills are within the game's limits.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-002","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Characters","t":"New","x":"Nothing you play is ever lost to this. If something looks wrong, the save is still kept, and only trading is frozen: the market (listings, purchases, auctions, crafted pieces and your Stores), trades between players, guild vaults and treasuries, rent and card-table stakes. You'll see a message naming the item when that happens, and another when trading opens again.","g":["online","guild","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-003","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Characters","t":"New","x":"If the same valuable item turns up on two characters, the character that showed it second is the one checked; the original owner keeps theirs and can still sell it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-004","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Characters","t":"New","x":"Enchanted items brought into the realm from a classic Daggerfall save through customs stay yours, but can't be traded or sold in the realm.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-005","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Online Characters","t":"New","x":"The server now records how fast each character's wealth grows against time actually played. For the first week it only measures; after that, wealth that grows faster than play could earn it will freeze trading until play catches up.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-006","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Shops","t":"Fix","x":"Items handed to you by other players (chests, bodies, shops) are now checked the same way. An impossible item is left out on its own, so an honest chest or body is never lost because of one bad piece.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7357-007","v":"0.1.7357","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Repairs","t":"Fix","x":"Items in for repair could be refused when passed between players; that's fixed.","g":["loot","torch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7361-001","v":"0.1.7361","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"New","x":"Every crafting station now uses the materials in your Materials Bag and pack, not just your Stores: the anvil, forge, workbench, loom, mason's bench, cook fire, jeweller's bench, alchemy and enchanting stations, and tempering.","g":["crafting","alchemy","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7361-002","v":"0.1.7361","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Crafting","t":"New","x":"That includes materials you looted, bought at a shop, were traded, or took out of your Stores before the bag existed. Before, these showed (0) at a station and crafting said you didn't have enough.","g":["crafting","online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7361-003","v":"0.1.7361","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Crafting","t":"New","x":"A craft that needs refining first (ore to ingots, logs to charcoal) plans that from your bag too.","g":["crafting","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7361-004","v":"0.1.7361","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Materials","t":"New","x":"When a station takes something from your pack, any of it you didn't gather or take out of your Stores is kept as \"from your pack\". You'll see it on the Stores page.","g":["mining","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7361-005","v":"0.1.7361","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Materials","t":"New","x":"Goods from your pack can only be used at a crafting station, or taken back out into your pack. They can't be delivered to writs, put in the guild Stores or sold for silver.","g":["mining","smithing","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7361-006","v":"0.1.7361","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Materials","t":"New","x":"A piece crafted from them sells on the market for gold only, the same as any piece from your pack.","g":["mining","smithing","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7363-001","v":"0.1.7363","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Mining","t":"New","x":"Mountain and Mountain Woods veins can now be Silver on ground few players have mined. Before, that ground gave only Iron in the Mountains (and Iron, Copper or Lead in the Mountain Woods).","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7363-002","v":"0.1.7363","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Mining","t":"New","x":"Gold, Platinum, Mithril and a region's own ore still appear only once three different players (each account at least a week old) have gathered on that ground. The Mining page now says so.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7363-003","v":"0.1.7363","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Maps","t":"Rework","x":"New setting: Settings → Interface → Maps → Map text and icons - Auto, or 0.75× to 2×.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7363-004","v":"0.1.7363","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Coasts","t":"New","x":"The map of Tamriel beyond the Iliac Bay is traced more faithfully: provinces meet at their borders instead of across thin channels of sea, specks of paint are no longer drawn as tiny lakes, coastlines are smooth, the continent lines up with the Bay's own coast, and the made-up rivers that ran out to sea are gone. The land past the Bay no longer has sea running down its borders either.","g":["water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7363-005","v":"0.1.7363","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Character Sheet","t":"Rework","x":"New setting: Settings → Interface → Character sheet → Every faction's standing (off by default). With it on, the Standing page lists your reputation with every guild, temple, knightly order, kingdom, witches' coven, vampire clan and Daedric Prince - including a guild you've left or been expelled from.","g":["ascension","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7363-006","v":"0.1.7363","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Beautiful Villages","t":"Fix","x":"Beautiful Villages: in Akatosh's temple villages (Gentle Redeemer of Akatosh in Wayrest among them) one house stood buried inside a hill. It now stands on open ground nearby, and a quest that sends you there (such as An Item On Loan) leads to it.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-001","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Textures","t":"New","x":"Ebony armour now has its own full set on the Morrowind-style body: breastplate with tassets, pauldrons, gauntlets, greaves, boots and helm, each with its own painted texture.","g":["rendering","terrain","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-002","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Ebony Armour","t":"New","x":"Mithril and Adamantium still wear the Morrowind ebony look.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-003","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Cloaks","t":"New","x":"Casual and Formal Cloaks are now real cloaks, worn over your armour instead of a full robe that hid it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-004","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Cloaks","t":"New","x":"The cloak moves with your body: it hangs from the shoulders and swings with your legs as you walk.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-005","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Cloaks","t":"New","x":"Each dye has its own colour. Aquamarine wears the blue and Yellow the light brown.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-006","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Cloaks","t":"New","x":"The cloak is smooth over the shoulders.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-007","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"Its inventory icon shows the cloak itself.","g":["horse","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-008","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Weapons","t":"New","x":"Greatswords and bows worn on the back sit over the cloak and stay visible.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-009","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Weapons","t":"New","x":"Swords, daggers and crossbows at the hip hang under it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-010","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Weapons","t":"New","x":"Stowed weapons follow the cloak as you walk, run and lean, so they no longer cut through it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7372-011","v":"0.1.7372","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Weapons","t":"New","x":"Sitting at a card table, the cloak hangs behind you instead of folding under your legs.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-001","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Online, your reputation with all twenty-two guilds, temples and knightly orders is kept by the realm, not your save. It moves only for things the realm saw you do.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-002","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Reputation can rise by up to 15 a day with each guild. Anything past that isn't lost: it's paid out on the days after.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-003","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Ranks 0 to 7 work exactly as in Daggerfall, earned with reputation and skill. Ranks 8 and 9 are now seats (see below).","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-004","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Court Writs","t":"New","x":"Each chapter posts hall writs on its town's Notice Board, under the Work tab. They ask for the kinds of materials that guild works with.","g":["professions","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-005","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Court Writs","t":"New","x":"A hall writ pays like a Court writ, plus +2 reputation with the guild. Hall writs and Court writs share your three writs a day.","g":["professions","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-006","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Court Writs","t":"New","x":"Members also get their own writ each day, one per guild, which earns Merit for the chapter.","g":["professions","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-007","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Court Writs","t":"New","x":"The Thieves Guild's and the Dark Brotherhood's writs are shown to their members alone.","g":["professions","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-008","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Reputation","t":"New","x":"Slaying a gate's guardian or defending a raided town earns +1 reputation with each guild you belong to that keeps a chapter there.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-009","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Receipts","t":"New","x":"A chapter's receipt writ gives +2 more for your first such deed of the day in that region.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-010","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Merit is what members earn for their chapter: 100 for a member's own writ (only units you gathered yourself count, not bought ones), and a share of 50 for each receipt.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-011","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"You can earn up to 600 Merit a week at a chapter. You start earning it after a week in the guild.","g":["notice-board","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-012","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Every week at the Turning, each chapter's Strength (0 to 100, starting at 50) rises with its members' Merit and slips when they neglect it. At each Season's end it settles halfway back toward 50.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-013","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"A chapter's Strength sets its standing:","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-014","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Failing (0–19): training and spells a quarter dearer, a poorer shelf, fewer writs.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-015","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Steady (20–69): Daggerfall's own prices and shelf.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-016","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Thriving (70–89) and Ascendant (90–100): training and spells a tenth cheaper, a richer shelf, more writs.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-017","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"The Notice Board shows each chapter's standing (\"The chapter of the Fighters Guild here is Thriving\").","g":["notice-board","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-018","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Each chapter has one Master (rank 9) and three officers (rank 8). The seats go to the members who earned the most Merit there over the last four weeks, and are settled at each week's Turning.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-019","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"To hold a seat you need 80 reputation, fourteen days in the guild, an account at least a week old, and rank 7 earned the usual way.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-020","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"A sitting holder keeps the seat on a tie. A seat no one has earned stands empty.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-021","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"At its own chapter's halls a seat gives you rank 8 or 9: its title, services and quests.","g":["seats","online","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-022","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"Titles on your name: Master, Officer, and Former Master for the rest of the Season you lost the seat in. These appear once titles are switched on.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-023","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seats","t":"New","x":"A Master names the chapter's Focus each week: the kind of material its hall writs ask for more of.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-024","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Hall of Records","t":"New","x":"The Hall of Records keeps each region's Chronicle: every seat that changed hands, every Season's ending and every patron. Open it from the Notice Board or at a seat's palace.","g":["seats","online","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-025","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"The first book on every guild hall's shelf is now the hall's roll: its chapter's standing, its Master and its officers.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-026","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"A Living Hall","t":"New","x":"A thriving chapter's hall is busier. Its members gather there more evenings each week, and a failing hall stands half empty.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-027","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk talk about their chapters, whether they're failing, thriving, or caught up in a Season's trouble.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-028","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Calm: a quiet Season.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-029","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Schism: two of the hall's people stand for different doctrines: cheaper training, a deeper shelf, or more writs. Members back a side, and the side whose backers earned more Merit wins. Its doctrine holds for the next Season. A guild is only offered doctrines its hall can actually provide.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-030","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Succession: the hall's head steps down. The Master names an heir from three candidates by the Season's third week; with no Master, the top backer's choice stands.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-031","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Crackdown: the watch hunts the chapter. Members' own writs earn half again Merit. A chapter that ends the Season under 30 Strength has its halls shut for the next Season: no services, no writs, an empty hall. You can still talk there, get your rank review, and receive free healing or recharge.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-032","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Rivalry: two rival chapters in one region race for Merit, and the winner takes 10 Strength from the loser. The rivals are the Fighters Guild and the Thieves Guild; the Dark Brotherhood against the temples of Arkay and Stendarr and every knightly order; and the Mages Guild against the Temple of Julianos.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-033","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Decline: the chapter loses 2 Strength a week unless its members earn twice the usual target.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-034","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"Ascendancy: the halls' training and spells are a further tenth off, and the Master is a High Master for the Season.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-035","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"A Master who holds the seat for an entire Season earns Season Master (\"Master of the Mages Guild, Daggerfall, Season 3\") for good.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-036","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"The Notice Board and the hall's roll tell each chapter's Season. Members can back their side right from the board.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-037","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"A player guild's guildmaster can bid silver from the guild's treasury to become a chapter's patron for the next Season. Bids start at 1,000, are sealed, and can be raised but never lowered.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-038","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"When the Season opens, the highest bid wins and is spent. Every other bid goes back to its guild's treasury.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-039","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Banners","t":"New","x":"A patron's banners hang beside the chapter's halls, and its members pay the Thriving price there whatever the chapter's standing. The Chronicle remembers who held it.","g":["arena","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-040","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Influence","t":"New","x":"Patronage buys no influence over the seats. The Thieves Guild's and Dark Brotherhood's chapters take no patrons.","g":["seats","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7427-041","v":"0.1.7427","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"The Thieves Guild's and the Dark Brotherhood's chapters, writs, Seasons and seats are shown to their members alone. Nothing public says where they keep their halls.","g":["seats","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7431-001","v":"0.1.7431","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Relay","t":"New","x":"The relay passes on each player's movement faster when many players are together: with 200 players in one spot a movement update costs 47 µs instead of 82, and 50 instead of 96 at 256. Everyone receives exactly the same updates as before. Deploying it disconnects every player once.","g":["online","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7438-001","v":"0.1.7438","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Online, the frame no longer stalls while the living world works out its travellers' roads. They used to be planned two a frame, and every trip near you was planned again each frame until they were all done. Now a frame plans as many as fit in 2 ms. In the measured town, the frame with nobody else around went from 36.5 ms to 19.4 ms.","g":["rendering","map","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7438-002","v":"0.1.7438","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The sun's shadows check each object once instead of once per shadow layer: about 0.6 ms a frame saved in a town by day, and the same shadows as before.","g":["rendering","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7438-003","v":"0.1.7438","d":"2026-10-09","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The movable HUD checks its layout four times a second instead of about eight.","g":["rendering","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-001","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"Cast-When-Held gear no longer breaks from re-equipping. Putting a piece back on within six hours of its spell's last casting costs no condition, and the equip cost can never take a piece below 1 condition. Wear while worn still uses it up over time.","g":["online","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-002","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"A Bloodline is never locked out after a failed heir's birth online. The Online page now lists each of your houses whose Succession is waiting, with a \"Carry on as\" button for every living member.","g":["online","map","blood"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-003","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"Your own remains in the Wrothgarian zone now show up. Walking back to your pile from the next cell over no longer loses it, and taking from it works from either side of the cell border.","g":["online","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-004","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Duels","t":"New","x":"Duels are now judged by the server. Every hit and spell is checked against the weapon you hold and the gear your character really has, and the server decides when a duel ends.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-005","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Duels","t":"New","x":"Your health bar in a duel is the duel's own vitality. Your real health is never touched, so nobody drops to 1 HP and nobody needs healing afterwards.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-006","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Duels","t":"New","x":"Both duellists' bars now show as soon as the bout starts, not only after the first hit.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-007","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Duels","t":"New","x":"Wins and losses are recorded from the server's result. Clients can no longer report results themselves.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-008","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Battle","t":"New","x":"Fights in the zone are judged by the server the same way duels are. Your vitality in a fight shows on the battle readout.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-009","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Your vitality goes back to full only after 30 seconds with nobody hitting you, spent in the zone. Stepping out of the zone and back in no longer heals you, and neither does walking into the next area.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-010","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"A fallen player stays down for the full two minutes. Nobody can rise where they fell straight away.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-011","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Characters","t":"New","x":"When you fall to another player, the server takes what you drop from your saved character and puts it in your remains. You no longer hand it over from your own game.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-012","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Pack","t":"New","x":"If your pack holds more than your remains can carry, the gold and your most valuable pieces go into the remains first, and the rest stays with you.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-013","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Pack","t":"New","x":"The piece your killer picks off your body now arrives in their pack by itself once your remains appear.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-014","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"If the fallen player never settles their death within 30 seconds, the killer's game does it for them, and lays the remains where the body fell.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-015","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"A crafted piece you pick back up from your own remains can still be worn, but it can't be traded or sold any more.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-016","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"New","x":"Party members, and anyone who left your party in the last ten minutes, still can't hurt you there. The server now enforces this too.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-017","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"Every damaging spell cast at another player is capped by the server: at most three in five seconds, each to its limit.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7460-018","v":"0.1.7460","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Royal Tourney","t":"New","x":"A Royal Tourney bout is blows only. Spells cast in a bout no longer land.","g":["seats","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7467-001","v":"0.1.7467","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The world events channel now announces Abyss Dungeons: when one rises (never where - it still has to be found), when someone finds it and in which region, when the Hour is broken and by whom, and when a found one fades unbroken.","g":["online","portals","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7467-002","v":"0.1.7467","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The rise and the find ping the world events role, so you hear when there is one to hunt and when its Rift is open.","g":["online","portals","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7467-003","v":"0.1.7467","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Cover","t":"New","x":"Steel and Ebony pauldrons now fully cover the upper arm - no more skin showing through.","g":["enhanced-ai","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7467-004","v":"0.1.7467","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Cover","t":"New","x":"The closed Steel helm and the Ebony helm sit lower, where they were designed to, and the Ebony helm's mail coif covers the neck again.","g":["enhanced-ai","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-001","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"The Small Cart is now drawn as the new Wagon Cart.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-002","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Two new wagons are for sale at General Stores:","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-003","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"The Open Wagon (900 gold) carries 1500 kg and has four seats in the back.","g":["horse","online","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-004","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"The Caravan (2500 gold) carries 2000 kg and you can step inside it.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-005","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"If you own more than one wagon, you drive the best one, and your wagon store holds what that wagon holds.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-006","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Wagon wheels now turn as the wagon moves and turn back when you reverse. Four-wheelers steer on their front axle.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-007","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"You can't sell, trade, list, or put in a guild vault a wagon you're driving while its store holds goods.","g":["horse","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-008","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Online, you can choose Ask to ride on another player's Open Wagon. The owner gets an Accept/Decline strip.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-009","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Fast Travel","t":"New","x":"Once seated, you go where the wagon goes, fast travel included, with no fare.","g":["clock","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-010","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Jump gets you down.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-011","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Your companions take the seats no player is using.","g":["companions","revenants","seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-012","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Companions","t":"New","x":"Riders and companions are drawn in the wagon in the Overworld too.","g":["companions","revenants","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-013","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Houses","t":"New","x":"Inside, the caravan is a room of its own, shaped like the caravan. Use it like a house:","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-014","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Decor","t":"New","x":"Place decor.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-015","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"The Caravan","t":"New","x":"Craft at stations.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-016","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Stores","t":"New","x":"Store things.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-017","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"The Caravan","t":"New","x":"Rest.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-018","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Paint your wagons for free, any time. You can paint the outside of every wagon, and the caravan's walls, floor and ceiling.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-019","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Guilds","t":"New","x":"Online, set Who may enter, like an online home: Only me, My party, My guild or Anyone. Visitors see what you've placed.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-020","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"The Caravan","t":"New","x":"A save or Recall made inside a caravan that can't be re-entered now puts you outside its rear door.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-021","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Houses","t":"New","x":"From the street, house windows show a room behind the glass. At night some rooms are lit and some are dark.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7501-022","v":"0.1.7501","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Houses","t":"New","x":"From inside a house or your caravan, windows show the real street outside, at the current time of day, in the current weather, with the sea where there is one.","g":["homes","online","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7506-001","v":"0.1.7506","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bow","t":"Fix","x":"Hold to keep shooting. With *Draw And Release Bows* off, holding attack now fires again each time the bow is ready, at the same rate as before. You no longer need to spam-click.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7506-002","v":"0.1.7506","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bow","t":"Fix","x":"No more double shots. Under the Morrowind bow, a click while the bow was still being drawn could fire two arrows from one draw, then a draw with no arrow. Each click is now one draw and one arrow.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7506-003","v":"0.1.7506","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bow","t":"Fix","x":"The arrow leaves on the release. Arrows no longer fly off at the start of the draw or halfway through it.","g":["animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7506-004","v":"0.1.7506","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bow","t":"Fix","x":"The Morrowind bow draws properly. The nocked arrow now travels to the string and is drawn back, and the bow's limbs and string bend with the draw. Before, the bow stayed rigid and the arrow sat in its resting spot.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-001","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"New","x":"Weapons now carry sockets you can see: round wells under the item's picture on its card, and small pips along the top of its tile in your pack.","g":["equipment","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-002","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"New","x":"A weapon's size sets how many sockets it can have: one on a short blade (dagger, tanto, shortsword, wakizashi), two on a one-handed weapon, three on a two-handed weapon, a bow or the Thunderlock. Armour and jewellery keep their single socket.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-003","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"New","x":"Socketed weapons drop far more often. Magic weapons can now have one socket. Rare and Legendary weapons can roll extra sockets, up to their size.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-004","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"New","x":"Set gems yourself, right in your pack. Click an empty socket to pick a gem from your pack, or open a gem's card and choose Set in.... Setting a gem is free (the gem is spent), and you can do it on a weapon you're wearing.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-005","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"New","x":"Click a filled socket twice to shatter its gem. To get a gem back whole, go to the Mages Guild's Reforge, which extracts it for gold based on the gem's grade.","g":["equipment","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-006","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"New","x":"A piece that holds a gem is never salvaged (extract or unset the gem first), and a set gem adds its own worth to the piece's price.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-007","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gems","t":"New","x":"Each of the eight classic gems now comes in five grades: Chipped, Flawed, regular, Flawless and Perfect. The better the grade, the stronger the bonus. Socketed in a weapon, a gem adds fire or frost damage, life leech, extra damage or an attribute; in armour or jewellery it adds a resistance or an attribute.","g":["jewelcrafting","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-008","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gems","t":"New","x":"Gems now drop from bodies, dungeon treasure and tavern or guild caches. Deeper, deadlier places drop better grades.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-009","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gems","t":"New","x":"World bosses drop gems. The Oblivion Gate's Warden drops one, Sethrakul drops one to every player who dealt their share of the damage, and the Brass Remnant drops two. All are Flawless or Perfect, and the bosses' weapons and armour can now come socketed.","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-010","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Gems","t":"New","x":"Fair stacking: a weapon's gems of the same kind together give at most one Rare line's worth (for example +6 Fire damage at most). Mixing gem kinds pays more than doubling up, and the item card shows when a weapon hits that limit.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-011","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Dungeon Scaling","t":"Rework","x":"Monsters are now tougher depending on where you meet them, using the same grading that decides how good a place's loot is. Mines, natural caves, cemeteries and towns add nothing. In a Crypt the strongest foes have up to a third more health, in a Vampire Haunt up to 70% more, and in a Dragon's Den or the Volcanic Caves up to double health, hitting up to 25% harder and with more skill.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-012","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Foes","t":"Rework","x":"The wilderness is a little tougher by day and more so at night.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-013","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Dungeon Scaling","t":"Rework","x":"The weaker the creature, the less it gains: rats, bats and imps gain nothing. Offline, turning off Loot rarity turns this off too.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-014","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Physical Combat and Armor Overhaul","t":"Rework","x":"With the Physical Combat and Armor Overhaul on (the default), an enemy's weapon skill now helps it hit exactly as much as yours helps you. Its critical strikes land as often and hit as hard as yours.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-015","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Physical Combat and Armor Overhaul","t":"Rework","x":"A weapon in top condition no longer strikes up to 30% harder, and fresh armour no longer lets 15% less damage through, unless you turn on the overhaul's Equipment Damage Enhanced module (Settings > Combat > Rules & armour > Physical Combat And Armor Overhaul). That module wears gear down fast enough to make the bonus something you earn by maintaining your gear. Worn gear still hits weaker and blocks less, as before.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-016","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Elites","t":"New","x":"Elite enemies now appear offline while Loot rarity is on: about one foe in twenty in the wilds, and sometimes one in a dungeon. An elite is never a creature below level 3, and offline a level-1 or level-2 character meets no elite among a dungeon's bandits and knights.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-017","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Enhanced AI","t":"Rework","x":"Enhanced AI is now on by default offline, as it already was online. You can switch back to the classic enemy AI in Settings > Combat > Enemies (Enhanced AI). If you had pressed All off in the features list, it stays off.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-018","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Death Penalty","t":"Rework","x":"Dying offline now costs gold. When Project Legacy raises you after a death, you lose a tenth of the gold you carry, as online. Gold in the bank is safe. The death screen shows the amount and now says Rise instead of \"End the journey\".","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7524-019","v":"0.1.7524","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Death Screen","t":"UI","x":"Dying offline now costs gold. When Project Legacy raises you after a death, you lose a tenth of the gold you carry, as online. Gold in the bank is safe. The death screen shows the amount and now says Rise instead of \"End the journey\".","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-001","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Every city and town now has a Stable and a Wagon Yard. They are open-air yards on the town's open ground, clear of homes, guild halls and roads.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-002","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"The Stable sells horses and buys them back.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-003","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"The Wagon Yard sells the Small Cart, the Open Wagon and the Caravan, and buys any of them back.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-004","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Each yard has its own keeper, named for the town, and a signboard. Horses and wagons stand on show, and pressing one opens the yard's stock.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-005","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"Rework","x":"General Stores no longer sell or buy horses, carts or wagons.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-006","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"Economy","x":"The Open Wagon now costs 9000 gold and the Caravan 25000. Wagons bought before the change stay valid everywhere.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-007","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"Economy","x":"Every yard charges the same price in every region, and its keepers can't be stolen from.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-008","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Yards keep clear of the boulders, stalls, walls and crop fields the town mods add, and of the spots where travellers arrive.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-009","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"You can see a town's yards through the windows of nearby houses.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-010","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"On the Open Wagon and the Caravan you now sit on the driver's bench with the reins in hand.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-011","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Rework","x":"Both now need a team of two horses. Buy the second one at a Stable. The Small Cart still takes one horse.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-012","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"The horses are harnessed with traces and reins that sag and swing as the wagon moves.","g":["horse","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-013","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"You can zoom out to third person while driving from the bench, on the Open Wagon as well as the Caravan, and you stay in third person after fast travel or a teleport.","g":["third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-014","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Rework","x":"Your parked wagon now blocks you instead of letting you walk through it.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-015","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"If you're left with one horse for a two-horse wagon, you can ride that horse again.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-016","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"Wagons are no longer oversized in the Overworld.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-017","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"Summoning a wagon no longer traps you under it.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-018","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Other players driving a bench wagon are drawn sitting on their bench.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-019","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bounty Boards","t":"Fix","x":"Clicking Take bounty again and again now takes the board's notices in order, top to bottom. Before, the notice you had just taken stayed open with Give up under your cursor, so quick clicks took the top bounty and gave it straight back.","g":["bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-020","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bounty Boards","t":"Fix","x":"After your last take, the notice shows a short line instead of buttons; pick it on the left to share it or give it up. In a party, a stray click there no longer shares the bounty with everyone.","g":["bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-021","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bounty Boards","t":"UI","x":"Give up now asks for a second click (\"Click again to give up\") and sits on the left of the notice.","g":["bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-022","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Bounty Boards","t":"UI","x":"The board keeps one size, so the Take button stays where it is while the list grows.","g":["bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-023","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"World Map","t":"UI","x":"The Enhanced world map now opens on you, as if you had pressed Find me: it glides to where you stand and the red cross blinks over you. Opening it from the journal still shows the quest's place, and a journey under way, a teleport and a carriage or ship driver's map open as before. The classic map opens as it always has.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-024","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"Towns in Hammerfell's regions are now walked by Redguards. Before, Sentinel, the Dragontail Mountains and other towns outside the desert had Breton and Nord townsfolk with Redguard names. Residents there keep their names but get Redguard looks, and so do the townsfolk inside houses (with Roleplay & Realism's Variant Residents on, as it is by default).","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-025","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Damned Weapons","t":"New","x":"Damned weapons: one cursed Legendary weapon in four is now *Damned*. Its curse line rolls at the very top of its range, but it costs you 8 health on every hit, and no temple can lift the curse. Unequip it and the bleeding stops: take it out for a boss, then put it away.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7542-026","v":"0.1.7542","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"In arena bouts, an enchantment's own bite (a Damned blade's, or any Health Leech weapon's) no longer kills you; it leaves you at 1 health like every other blow there.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7553-001","v":"0.1.7553","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Boss Fight Integrity","t":"New","x":"The server now checks the boss's attacks itself. Your game still shows each hit, but the server also works out, from where you were standing, which of the boss's blows reached you.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7553-002","v":"0.1.7553","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Boss Fight Integrity","t":"New","x":"The server keeps its own count of each fighter's health in these fights, and of each ship's hull against the serpent. Your game tells it your health as it changes, and potions, healing spells and repairs count as long as they stay within a set amount over time. Healing from your allies' spells doesn't use up that amount.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7553-003","v":"0.1.7553","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Boss Fight Integrity","t":"New","x":"If you sail off to repair your ship and come back to the serpent, the server counts your hull fresh.","g":["online","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7553-004","v":"0.1.7553","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Boss Fight Integrity","t":"Other","x":"For now the server only records this. Nobody is knocked down or wrecked by it, and fights play exactly as before. Once a week of fights shows how much healing honest players really use, staff will switch it on.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7553-005","v":"0.1.7553","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Boss Fight Integrity","t":"Other","x":"When it is switched on, a fighter the server counts as fallen will fall in their own game too. In the Abyss Dungeon that uses up your one life, and at sea it wrecks your ship.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7553-006","v":"0.1.7553","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Boss Fight Integrity","t":"New","x":"The server always gives you the benefit of the doubt. It only counts a blow if you were well inside the attack's area both just before and just after it landed, and it never counts elemental damage (fire, frost, shock, poison or magic), since your own resistances can block it.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7556-001","v":"0.1.7556","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"Third person now works properly when you drive the Open Wagon or the Caravan from its bench. Before, the camera jammed into your character's head. Now it swings up over the wagon's roof, where you can zoom out and look down at your driver, the team and the road.","g":["third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7556-002","v":"0.1.7556","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Both town maps now show each town's Stable and Wagon Yard: their ground in the shop colour, with their names written on.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7556-003","v":"0.1.7556","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"The Overworld marks each Stable with a horseshoe and each Wagon Yard with a wheel, with their names. They hide with the Towns filter.","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7556-004","v":"0.1.7556","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Ask anyone \"Where is...\" and you'll find new Stables and Wagon yards lists. Townsfolk give directions or mark them on your map, as they do for any shop.","g":["map","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7567-001","v":"0.1.7567","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Towns full of furnished yards are cheaper to draw. Yard pieces behind you are no longer drawn, and many copies of the same placed piece no longer force extra shadow work every frame.","g":["rendering","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7567-002","v":"0.1.7567","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The stables and wagon yards in every town you can see are no longer drawn when they are behind you or far out of view.","g":["culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7567-003","v":"0.1.7567","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Collision no longer gets more expensive as you raise the view distance. Movement for you and every nearby foe costs about the same at Ultra as at Low, including while new land is loading in.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7567-004","v":"0.1.7567","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"A lamp's shadow no longer redraws all six of its sides when someone walks past it. It redraws only the sides they are in front of.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7567-005","v":"0.1.7567","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Other players' name tags are cheaper for the browser to move when you turn the camera in a crowd.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7567-006","v":"0.1.7567","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The game's main per-frame loop now runs as optimized code in the browser.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7572-001","v":"0.1.7572","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Reconnecting after a server update asks less of the account service. When the world chat was too busy to let you straight in, your game used to ask for a fresh sign-in token on every retry. Now it reuses the one it already has.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7572-002","v":"0.1.7572","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"The account service can now answer sign-in token requests from Cloudflare's database read replicas.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7572-003","v":"0.1.7572","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Live Chat","t":"Performance","x":"The world chat server does less work for each player who joins or leaves, and that work grows far less with the number of players online.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7572-004","v":"0.1.7572","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Live Chat","t":"Fix","x":"The World tab's \"Online\" count now stays accurate once more than 512 players are in the world chat. It used to creep upward.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7572-005","v":"0.1.7572","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Live Chat","t":"Fix","x":"A World tab closed because you went online on another device no longer shows the old count over an empty list.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-001","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"With the Morrowind body on, the people and creatures around you stand in Morrowind bodies too. This covers dungeon and wilderness foes, the city watch, townsfolk walking the streets, people in buildings and dungeons, quest givers, the keepers of the Stables and Wagon Yards, ship crews, siege fighters, road parties, and the Oblivion Gate's boss and his host.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-002","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Foes wear the armour and carry the weapons they rolled. Each has a race and face of their own.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-003","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Online, everyone sees a foe as its owner does: the same race, face, armour and weapon. In a dungeon, each player's copy of a foe carries that player's own loot, and wears it.","g":["morrowind","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-004","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk are dressed by their station: priests in robes, nobles in formal wear, merchants, scholars, and the town's guards in steel. In a living town, people wear what their sprite shows: the watch his uniform on duty, a guild's members and priests their class's gear.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-005","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Foes swing, flinch when struck and fall when they die. Their tells show on the body too: the wind-up glint, the elite glow, the hit flash and the dissolve.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-006","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"A body is drawn at its sprite's size: elites stand larger, and the wild zone's giants tower over you. The dead lie where their corpse lies, on a moving deck too.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-007","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Creatures use Morrowind's creatures where Daggerfall's have a match (rats, skeletons, daedra and more). Those with no match keep their classic sprite, as do flyers and swimmers with no Morrowind match that flies or swims.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-008","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"The Daedra Seducer keeps her disguise until she transforms.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-009","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Ghosts and wraiths are Morrowind's ancestor ghost, seen through. Vampires wear their race's vampire face, werewolves stand as Bloodmoon's wolf, and orcs are Orcs.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-010","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Performance","x":"Bodies are drawn for the nearest people only, within one budget for the whole frame. Everyone farther away keeps the classic sprite, and so does everyone seen from the travel view.","g":["morrowind","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-011","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Performance","x":"Third-person Morrowind bodies, yours included, are now skinned on the graphics card instead of the CPU.","g":["morrowind","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7613-012","v":"0.1.7613","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"A new Morrowind People setting (Settings > Combat > With Morrowind data): Off, Near (the default, up to 24 bodies) or All (up to 48).","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-001","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Travellers","t":"New","x":"New travellers set out from the towns: farmers leading a pack horse to market day, hunters heading into the wild, patrols of knights walking a round between a city and its region's towns, nobles travelling between courts with their retainers, and minstrels going to play another town's tavern for the evening.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-002","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Travellers","t":"New","x":"Bigger towns now send out more pedlars, pilgrims and couriers.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-003","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Travellers","t":"New","x":"Parties at night now stop at a roadside inn when one is close ahead. Otherwise they make camp, and every camp has a fire. Parties that meet on the road greet each other once in passing, warn each other of trouble behind them, and share a camp when they stop near each other.","g":["overworld","camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-004","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Travellers","t":"New","x":"Roads a patrol has walked recently see half the trouble. A patrol knight who sees a wanted criminal draws on them, even one the knight is on good terms with.","g":["overworld","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-005","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Caravans","t":"New","x":"A merchant's caravan now travels with a horse and wagon (two wagons from a great house's city), with its guards walking in front and behind. A noble's procession brings a baggage wagon, and pedlars and farmers lead a pack horse.","g":["overworld","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-006","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Caravans","t":"New","x":"The wagons' wheels turn as they roll. At camp the wagons are parked around the fire with their horses unhitched. Seen from the travel map, a caravan's mark is a wagon.","g":["overworld","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-007","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Caravans","t":"New","x":"Trade with them: talk to a caravan's merchant, a farmer or a pedlar on the road to buy and sell. Each one keeps a shop's stock and has a limited purse for the trip, and gives friends 10% off.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-008","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Caravans","t":"New","x":"Hire on as a guard: a merchant's caravan offers you a contract from the day before it sets out until it arrives. Stay within 300 m of it until it reaches its town to be paid by the day, plus more for each foe you beat. Fall behind for more than an hour, let the merchant die, or rob or kill any of them yourself, and you're not paid. If outlaws rob the caravan on the way, you're still paid for getting its people through. Offline, outdoors and with no enemies near, you can travel on with them, skipping ahead to their next stop.","g":["overworld","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-009","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Caravans","t":"New","x":"Rob them: beat every guard of a caravan yourself and it surrenders. Its goods and purse are yours to take. But any survivor who reaches a town reports you: theft, pickpocketing and murder on the road are now charged as crimes in the region where they happened. Leave no witnesses and nobody hears about it.","g":["law","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-010","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Outlaws","t":"New","x":"Each region now has bands of outlaws (up to four), named, with a hideout off a road between two of its towns. A band holds up the parties too weak to fight it off and keeps what it took.","g":["overworld","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-011","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Outlaws","t":"New","x":"Find a hideout and you'll see the camp: tents, a fire, the band, and a chest of what they've stolen. Kill every one of them to rout the band. Step away and come back, and the ones you've already killed stay down; an outlaw chasing you doesn't vanish because you ran. The people it robbed will be grateful, and the region's towns will talk about it. A new band moves in later.","g":["overworld","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-012","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Outlaws","t":"New","x":"Travellers warn you about camps near the road they're on. A band you've heard of is marked on the travel map as a rumoured hideout, near it but never exactly on it.","g":["map","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-013","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Adventuring Companies","t":"New","x":"Adventurers now travel together in named companies, such as \"The Lantern Company\", and dive dungeons more often as a group. Pilgrims going the same way on the same day travel as a band, and each region keeps its own holy day when pilgrims set out for its temple towns.","g":["overworld","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-014","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Adventuring Companies","t":"New","x":"A company introduces itself by name. Your chronicle's People page lists the companies of the people you know.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-015","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Adventuring Companies","t":"New","x":"A company works its way through a dungeon stop by stop, block by block. If you meet them, they're wherever their route has brought them. You may hear fighting ahead before you see them.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-016","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Adventuring Companies","t":"New","x":"Talk to them to have them join you, lead on to their next stop, or part ways. Badly hurt members fall back, and a beaten company heads for the exit.","g":["social","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-017","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Adventuring Companies","t":"New","x":"Offline, for a day after a company passes through, the monsters at the places they reached lie dead with their packs emptied and the treasure there is picked over. Quest monsters and items, fixed monsters and fixed treasure are never touched. Online, the room's dungeon is unchanged.","g":["loot","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-018","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Adventuring Companies","t":"New","x":"A rival company that isn't friendly won't like you taking treasure it was heading for.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-019","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Town Buyers","t":"New","x":"A trader you've hired in a home that's open to the public now sells to the town's people, not only to players. Every hour, the town's people may buy a piece you've listed, at your price. The lower your price against what the piece is worth, the more likely it is to sell. A piece priced above 60% of its worth never sells to them, and a piece is never worth more to them than its own price.","g":["market","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-020","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Town Buyers","t":"New","x":"Pieces you bought at a shop counter online never sell to townspeople: they buy what you found, looted or made.","g":["market","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-021","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Town Buyers","t":"New","x":"A town's traders sell at most four pieces an hour between them. Each seller sells at most two an hour and 20,000 gold a day. Market tax and fees apply as for a sale to a player. Quest items and keepsakes never sell this way, and a crafted piece sells for no more than a found one.","g":["market","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-022","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Town Buyers","t":"New","x":"You'll see the buyer walk in to your house a little later. Some townspeople just come in to look. Your Vendor page shows who bought what: \"Sold to Ada Lark of Wayrest\".","g":["market","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-023","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Town News","t":"New","x":"News now travels between towns: travellers bring what their home town knew when they set out, and couriers bring news from one town further.","g":["social","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-024","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Reputation","t":"New","x":"Your reputation travels too. Strangers who have heard of your deeds (good or bad) may greet you by them. Hearsay alone never makes anyone your friend or your enemy.","g":["social","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7672-025","v":"0.1.7672","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Prices","t":"Fix","x":"Books and potion recipes no longer jump to a much higher price after passing between players online (through a shared container or a shop's shelf in a room), which let them sell back for more than they cost.","g":["market","books"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-001","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Magic, Rare and Legendary weapons can now drop with a technique: a special attack with its own key. By default that is the mouse's back side button, and you can rebind it under Controls → Combat. Unarmed fighters find their techniques on Gauntlets. Phones get a \"Tech\" button you can add to a touch corner, and controllers can put it on the d-pad.","g":["equipment","loot","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-002","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Bows: *Volley*: aim a circle and six arrows rain down on it. *Piercing Shot*: one fast arrow that passes through up to five foes. The Dwarven Thunderlock can carry Piercing Shot.","g":["equipment","thunderlock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-003","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Long blades: *Leap Strike*: leap onto a foe up to 9 m away and hit everything around where you land. *Whirlwind*: hit everything around you.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-004","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Short blades: *Shadowstep*: dash behind a foe and strike. *Lunge*: dash forward and hit everything you pass.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-005","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Axes: *Cleave*: a wide sweep. *Headsman's Chop*: hits harder the more wounded the foe is.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-006","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Blunt weapons: *Ground Slam*: hit everything around you. *Skull Crack*: one heavy, accurate blow.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-007","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Bare hands: *Flying Kick*: leap and strike. *Haymaker*: one heavy, accurate punch.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-008","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Hold the key to aim. A blue marker on the ground shows where a Volley will land or where a leap will end, and it turns red when the spot is out of reach. Let go to fire. A quick tap fires at once where you are looking. Techniques that don't need aiming go off as soon as you press.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-009","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Under a low ceiling a leap flies a lower arc. If no arc fits, you get \"No room to leap.\"","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-010","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Other","x":"The key does nothing while a window is open (a conversation, the pack, a menu).","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-011","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Other","x":"An unidentified piece's technique works, but it is called \"Your technique\" until you identify it.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-012","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Every technique costs fatigue and has a cooldown. The Enhanced HUD shows a chip with the seconds left, and the message line tells you when it is ready again.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-013","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Other","x":"Damage still comes from Daggerfall's own formula. A technique multiplies a normal hit, so a miss is still a miss. The +N% on the item raises that multiplier.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-014","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Other","x":"Techniques are disabled in duels and player-vs-player bouts, and they never hit another player. A technique that hits all around you only hits an ally or a peaceful creature where a normal swing would have.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-015","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Other","x":"Techniques need the loot ladder. With the ladder off, none drop and the key tells you why.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-016","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"The Reforge shows what a technique does under its line, so you can see it before you reforge or hone it.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-017","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Item Card","t":"New","x":"A technique now has its own section on the Enhanced item card, the way set pieces and sigils do. Its header shows its own glyph (three blue strike marks), the technique's name and your roll (+23% [15-30]). Under that is what it does, then a footer with your key, whether you hold to aim or just press, the fatigue cost and the cooldown. The shop's hover card shows the same section.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-018","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Item Card","t":"New","x":"The key shown is the one that actually works: your primary or secondary binding, or the controller button's name (A, Square, RB…) while you're playing on a controller.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-019","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Item Card","t":"QoL","x":"The section is compact, so item cards still fit without scrolling. On a crowded card it drops the \"hold to aim\" hint first, then the footer. The Info box always shows everything.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-020","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Item Card","t":"New","x":"The Info box shows the same section in full, with the word *Technique* over the name, and adds two lines: how your roll raises the technique's own blow (+23% rolled (15-30) on its 140% blow: 172% of a plain blow.), and how to use the key. If no key is bound, it tells you to bind *Weapon technique* in Controls.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-021","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Item Card","t":"Other","x":"In a duel the section greys out and says why.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-022","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"UI","x":"The HUD chip uses the same glyph, so the chip and the card are clearly the same thing. It says \"unbound\" if no key is bound, and it hides during a duel, like set-power chips.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-023","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Item Card","t":"Other","x":"The classic tooltip, the Reforge and the player-to-player trade window still show a technique as two lines.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-024","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Leap Strike / Flying Kick: the view widens as you leave the ground. You land with a hard dip and a thud, and a shock ring with thrown stone spreads to the technique's reach.","g":["combat-visuals","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-025","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Ground Slam: the weapon rises, then the view slams down for the heaviest shake of all. Two shock rings race out across the floor with the most stone and sparks.","g":["combat-visuals","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-026","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Whirlwind: the view leans into the spin, and sparks are flung round a ring at its 3 m, carried the way the blade goes.","g":["combat-visuals","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-027","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Cleave: the view winds up leaning one way and lands leaning the other, and a fan of sparks follows the arc.","g":["combat-visuals","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-028","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Skull Crack / Headsman's Chop / Haymaker: a star of light and a spray of sparks where the blow lands. The Chop adds a ring under it, the Haymaker a ring standing in the air.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-029","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Shadowstep: a quick high whisk and a ring of rising light where you vanish, and a star where you strike.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-030","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Lunge: a trail of sparks down the lane you ran.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-031","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Piercing Shot: the bow kicks the view up, flares, and lays a tracer of sparks down your aim, stopping at the first thing in its way.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-032","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Volley: each of the six arrows lands with a puff of stone exactly where and when it hits the ground (on slopes too), and a ring closes over the circle with the last one.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-033","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"New","x":"Technique camera motion (Settings → Accessibility → Motion): Full, 75%, Half, Low or Off. It scales the view's movement, the shake and the hands' dip. At Off the screen doesn't move; the sparks and sounds stay. Better Ambience's own shake switch and limit still apply. The sounds follow Sound Enhancements.","g":["combat-visuals","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7693-034","v":"0.1.7693","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Keybindings","t":"Performance","x":"The game also does less work every frame than before: polling a bound key no longer builds a list for every binding each time it's asked.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7698-001","v":"0.1.7698","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Performance","x":"Other players' horses and wagons more than 400 m away are no longer updated or drawn. A town full of parked wagons no longer slows the game down wherever you are in its area. They reappear where they stand as you come near.","g":["culling","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7698-002","v":"0.1.7698","d":"2026-10-10","e":"Wagon","t":"Performance","x":"Wagons, carts, harnesses and tents that are off screen are no longer drawn. This covers your own and other players' wagons, the caravans and pack teams on the roads, your cart, camp tents and outlaw hideouts. If one is just off screen, its shadow still falls into view.","g":["culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7703-001","v":"0.1.7703","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Loading","t":"Fix","x":"The game no longer fails to start with \"boot failed: cannot access ... before initialization\". It happened when starting near a port town, or with the travel map's dungeon lists in play.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7705-001","v":"0.1.7705","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Login","t":"New","x":"When many players sign in at once, such as right after an update, you now wait in a short line instead of getting a \"server\" error. The game tells you that you're in line; try again in a few seconds and you keep your place.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-001","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Towns, woods and streets cost less to draw. Every patch of trees, plants and lamps used to carry its own small buffer, so drawing it needed a costly state switch first, nearly a thousand times a frame. Still flats now share large buffers, which cuts those switches almost in half, and the picture is the same, triangle for triangle. Measured in the real game at night, the town's frame takes about 14% less main-thread time.","g":["rendering","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-002","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Night-time towns make less garbage. Each lantern's shadow matrices are worked out in place instead of being rebuilt every frame, and the shadow pass stopped creating temporary numbers for every lantern and tree pair. That means fewer garbage-collector pauses, which show up as stutter.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-003","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Towns by a harbour are much cheaper. Moored ships no longer rebuild every part every frame, which cost up to 7 ms a frame near a port.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-004","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Busy servers stutter less. Other players' name tags, footsteps and sprites make far less garbage, and their sprite art loads in idle time instead of all at once when you turn toward a crowd.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-005","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The first spell, the first fight and the first trip to the coast or the sea no longer stall while their shaders compile. Those shaders are now built in the background.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-006","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The sky skips drawing stars during the day, when they can't be seen.","g":["sky"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-007","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"On laptops with two graphics cards, the game now asks for the faster one.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7720-008","v":"0.1.7720","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Eye of the Beholder","t":"Fix","x":"With Eye of the Beholder in first person, looking up no longer shows your own body. It now follows the mod's visibility setting, which by default casts your shadow but is never seen.","g":["first-person","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-001","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Main menu > Overhauls > UI has a fourth look, DFO Grimoire: everything Enhanced Plus does (the hotbar, camps and tents, the rest, the maps, trading and every online panel) dressed in GrimoireUI's parchment, wood, red-and-gold presses, glass vials and lettering.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-002","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"The vitals are GrimoireUI's three vials, upright in the corner in Daggerfall's order or lying in a row under the hotbar.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-003","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"The card has its own choices, each applied at once: Pages (cream page or tan scroll), Backdrop (the desk or the map), Vitals (upright or in a row) and Spellbook (the DFO book or GrimoireUI's own).","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-004","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"The front door stands on a detailed desk, as large as the screen allows, and every wooden board uses a soft desk wood.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-005","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Rarity, set and sigil names are inked deeper on the page so they stay readable.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-006","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"HUD","t":"New","x":"The compass can be turned over in the HUD editor (Alt+U): a new turn-over press sits beside the X.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-007","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Main Menu","t":"New","x":"Main menu clicks now play the in-game click sound once your game data is loaded.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-008","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Player Trade","t":"New","x":"Letters of credit say what they're worth in the player-trade info box and hover.","g":["marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-009","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wordmark","t":"Fix","x":"The Daggerfall Online logo is repaired: the torn rows through \"DAGGERFALL\" and \"The Elder Scrolls\" are mended, and the clipped tops of its letters are closed.","g":["rebrand"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-010","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Towns and forests draw with far fewer graphics state switches. The shared buffers that hold trees, plants and lamps now grow to fit a large town, and each kind of flat stays together, so drawing a street jumps between buffers far less often. Measured in the real game at night, a town's frame takes about 14% less main-thread time than before this change, and about a quarter less than before the previous one. Nothing looks different.","g":["rendering","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7736-011","v":"0.1.7736","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Notice Board","t":"Fix","x":"The account service was being slowed down by the Notice Board's trader directory, which every player standing in a town reads. That read now looks only at the traders of its own region, so sign-ins, saves and everything else on the account service should stop failing under load.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7745-001","v":"0.1.7745","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Performance","x":"Other players far away are no longer drawn. Before, everyone up to about 3 km away was animated and drawn every frame, even when they were a pixel or two tall.","g":["online","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7745-002","v":"0.1.7745","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"New","x":"The new Draw distance setting on the Other players card chooses how far out other players are drawn: 150 m, 300 m (the default), 600 m, or Everyone.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7745-003","v":"0.1.7745","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Other","x":"Your party, and the player you're dueling, always show at any distance.","g":["online","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7745-004","v":"0.1.7745","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Other","x":"At the default 300 m you still see anyone close enough to hit you with an arrow or a spell. The 150 m option can hide a distant archer.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7745-005","v":"0.1.7745","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Performance","x":"Near the edge between two map areas, each nearby player's position used to reach you two to four times. Now it mostly arrives once, which cuts network traffic and CPU in busy towns.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7745-006","v":"0.1.7745","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Other","x":"Other players move as smoothly as before.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7754-001","v":"0.1.7754","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"The Small Cart's boards and stakes now run square to its box. They used to sit about 10° off, most visibly with a horse in the shafts.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7754-002","v":"0.1.7754","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"The Caravan's side windows are now centred: one in the middle of each half of the side, and midway between the trim lines. From inside, the windows still line up with the outside.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-001","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"New","x":"Leave a wagon parked on a road in a city, hamlet or village for 10 minutes and a guard comes for it.","g":["law","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-002","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"New","x":"A town holds four parked wagons. When a fifth arrives, the one parked longest is thrown out first. Each player counts once per town: park a second wagon of your own there and that one goes first.","g":["law","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-003","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"New","x":"The guard walks up, lifts the wagon (horses and all) over their head, and throws it out of town. It tumbles through the air and lands about 40 m past the town's edge.","g":["law","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-004","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"Other","x":"Nothing is lost. The wagon keeps its cargo, its paint and its horse. Walk out to fetch it, or summon it. Summon it while the guard is still carrying it and the throw stops there.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-005","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"Other","x":"The wagon usually lands on a side of town that keeps it in the same area. In the biggest cities it lands just over the edge of the map square, and appears once you walk out to it.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-006","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"New","x":"You're told when the watch throws your wagon. If you weren't nearby, you're told the next time you're back near it.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-007","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"New","x":"Everyone nearby sees the throw. A caravan the watch threw can still be visited where it lands.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-008","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"Fix","x":"If you're riding in the back of someone's wagon when the guard lifts it, you're set down first.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-009","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"Other","x":"A horse left on its own is never thrown. Only wagons and carts are. A horse standing beside the wagon goes with it; one you rode off and left elsewhere stays where you left it.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-010","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon Parking","t":"New","x":"Offline, the 10-minute road rule still applies. The clock is kept in your save, so a wagon left on a road and loaded later is thrown as soon as you're outdoors.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-011","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Water Surface","t":"Fix","x":"From high ground the sea no longer fades into a pale band of fog that ends in a hard square edge with a darker plane behind it. It now runs on through the haze to the horizon in one piece, and the far sea reflects the sky the way the near water does.","g":["water","distant-land"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-012","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Water Surface","t":"Fix","x":"The far sea now uses the same colour, light and sun glints as the water near you, so the two meet without a line.","g":["water","distant-land"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7774-013","v":"0.1.7774","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Water Surface","t":"Performance","x":"No extra cost: nothing new is drawn. The far horizon that was already there now shows the sea correctly, and it now skips shading the parts hidden behind nearer ground.","g":["water","distant-land"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-001","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Home Votes","t":"New","x":"Walk up to another player's home and its door now offers Vote up and Vote down. Once you've voted, that row becomes \"Take back your vote up\" (or down). On a touch screen, on the Classic interface, or with World Tooltips off, click the door in Info mode to vote.","g":["homes","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-002","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Home Votes","t":"New","x":"Each account has one vote per home. You can't vote on your own home, your own guild's hall, or a house given by a Knightly Order. You need to have had a username and password for at least a week to vote, and you can cast up to 30 votes an hour. Taking a vote back is always allowed.","g":["homes","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-003","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Home Votes","t":"New","x":"If a home's votes add up to less than zero, other players see it as Daggerfall built it: no placed decorations inside, nothing outside, and the town's own paint. A hired trader with goods on sale stays open for business. The owner, and a hall's guild members, still see everything. Nothing is deleted, and the decorations come back once the total is back to zero or above.","g":["homes","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-004","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Home Votes","t":"New","x":"Once a home has votes, its door shows the total. Its owner is told, at the door or in the Info box, when the decorations are hidden.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-005","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Home Votes","t":"Other","x":"If you voted on a guild hall before joining that guild, you can still take that vote back.","g":["homes","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-006","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Decorator","t":"Rework","x":"People you place with the decorator (the Vendors list), inside or in a yard, can no longer be resized. Smaller and Bigger are gone for them.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7789-007","v":"0.1.7789","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Decorator","t":"Rework","x":"People placed earlier at another size now stand at their normal size. Moving one sets it to normal size. One that was enlarged gives back half the price difference, as shrinking any piece does; one that was shrunk costs nothing to move.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7791-001","v":"0.1.7791","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Thorns","t":"Nerf","x":"Thorns now pay back at most 10 damage per blow, down from 25. 25 was nearly two full sword swings returned every time a foe hit you, so standing still in front of an Ancient Lich could kill it.","g":["equipment","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7791-002","v":"0.1.7791","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Thorns","t":"Nerf","x":"Thorns never deal the killing blow. They can wear a foe down to its last point of health, but you have to finish it yourself.","g":["equipment","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7791-003","v":"0.1.7791","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Thorns","t":"Other","x":"Your existing thorns gear keeps every line it rolled.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7791-004","v":"0.1.7791","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spite of the Spurned","t":"Nerf","x":"Same rule: it still returns its share of each blow, but it never takes a foe's last point of health.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7791-005","v":"0.1.7791","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Troll's Blood","t":"Removal","x":"New Rare armour no longer rolls Cast When Held: Troll's Blood. It gave permanent regeneration on a piece that smiths can repair, so it never wore out.","g":["loot","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7791-006","v":"0.1.7791","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Troll's Blood","t":"Other","x":"Pieces you already own keep it and stay valid online. The Mages Guild item maker still sells it at Daggerfall's own price.","g":["loot","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-001","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Gems","t":"Nerf","x":"The graded gems you set into sockets (Chipped, Flawed, Flawless and Perfect stones, plus plain ones found the same way) now drop about a third as often from bodies, dungeon piles and tavern or guild markers. A mid-level foe drops one about once every 33 kills instead of once every 12. In the deepest dungeons and from boss-level foes, a gem drops once every 20 sources instead of once every 7.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-002","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Gems","t":"Other","x":"A gem's grade still depends on where you find it, so a deep source still gives the Flawless and Perfect stones.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-003","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Gems","t":"Other","x":"No change to the gems world bosses drop, the gems shops sell, Daggerfall's own gem drops, or the gems you mine.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-004","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Lamp shadows in towns at night take less work. When nothing near a lamp has moved, it reuses last frame's answer about which nearby plants and trees can cast into it. The shadows are exactly the same.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-005","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Distant small flats are skipped before the game checks whether they are on screen, not after.","g":["culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-006","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"The glow pass skips flats that have no glow before checking whether they are on screen.","g":["culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7804-007","v":"0.1.7804","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Towns use less graphics memory. The large shared buffers for trees, plants and lamps now share one index buffer, where each had its own copy. That saves about 6 MB per buffer, and opening a new one no longer causes a short hitch.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-001","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Rework","x":"With Enhanced Lighting on, taverns, shops, homes and guild halls are no longer lit evenly from wall to wall. A building's own lamps burn at half their old strength, so their light falls in warm pools with darker corners between them.","g":["lighting","interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-002","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Rework","x":"Candles and other plain white lamps indoors now burn with the same warm flame colour as the street lanterns.","g":["lighting","interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-003","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Enhanced Lighting","t":"Rework","x":"Your eyes no longer brighten a dim room as much. Interiors stay moody instead of drifting toward grey.","g":["lighting","interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-004","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"Gold tables refused every buy-in with \"You have too many stakes waiting to be settled\", on every character. You can buy in now. No gold was ever taken by the refusal.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-005","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"UI","x":"A refused stake shows as a warning, a stake being asked shows as a wait, and your turn is highlighted.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-006","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"Quick buttons set your stake: Min and Max for the buy-in, and ½ pot and Pot for a raise. They only move the slider; you still press Deal me in or Raise.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-007","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"UI","x":"The slider shows its amount with its unit (gold or chips).","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-008","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"New","x":"A − button in the panel's title hides the seats and the log so you can see the table. The message and the buttons stay.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-009","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"UI","x":"The log shows one line per event, and the newest line is always visible.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-010","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Keybindings","t":"New","x":"A key you have set but not confirmed says \"Not saved yet - press Confirm.\" on its row.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-011","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Keybindings","t":"New","x":"The top of the page counts your unsaved changes and highlights Confirm.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-012","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Keybindings","t":"Fix","x":"The Confirm bar no longer hides behind the Settings search bar.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-013","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Keybindings","t":"Fix","x":"On a phone, the Confirm bar no longer covers the row you are binding.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-014","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Ship Helm","t":"Fix","x":"Recall, unstuck and other teleports from a ship's helm no longer leave you stuck in the void. You leave the helm the way fast travel does, and a boat you can pack goes back into your pack.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7815-015","v":"0.1.7815","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Soul Trap","t":"Fix","x":"A soul-trapped Dragonling now gives -5000 enchantment points as Soul Bound. Before, only the rare quest Dragonling did; the ones you meet in the world gave 0.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-001","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Mode","t":"Other","x":"This update restarts the multiplayer server once: everyone online is disconnected for a moment and reconnects on their own.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-002","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"After a server update, everyone online no longer reconnects in the same instant. Each game now waits a moment, longer the more players are online, so the account service is not overwhelmed. Rejoining the world chat takes no longer than before, but your own area may take a few extra seconds to reappear.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-003","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Mode","t":"Performance","x":"Games in a crowded town send less: a player with no enemies, camps, horses or boats around no longer repeats \"nothing here\" to everyone every two seconds.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-004","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Asking for a sign-in token costs the account service fewer database reads.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-005","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"The account, realm, heartbeat and profession reads a game keeps asking can be answered by read copies of the database, so they need not queue behind everyone's saves.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-006","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Mode","t":"Performance","x":"After the next server update, crowded towns cost the server far less: other players' movements reach you in small bundles twenty times a second instead of one message per player per step, and the world chat's list of who joined and left arrives once a second.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-007","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Mode","t":"New","x":"After the next server update, an area next to a duel, a Wrothgarian zone fight or a sea serpent fight says so, and your game sends it every step while it does.","g":["online","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-008","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Live Chat","t":"Performance","x":"After the next server update, the world chat is no longer one server for everyone: players are spread over sixteen by account, so it holds many more at once. The World tab still shows how many are online and, while that is no more than 512, lists them all.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-009","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Live Chat","t":"New","x":"After the next server update, type /find <name> (or /who <name>) to find anyone online by name. The Guild tab lists your guildmates online wherever they are.","g":["chat","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-010","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Live Chat","t":"Performance","x":"After the next server update, each region's chat is split four ways the same way, so a crowded start region lets everyone in faster. The Region tab still lists everyone in the region.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-011","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Room Copies","t":"New","x":"After the next server update, a full town, building or dungeon no longer turns you away: you join another copy of the same place (up to eight), and a party out in the open world joins its leader's copy. A sea serpent, a raid, a circle-rite and the card tables stay with the main copy of a place.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-012","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Bosses","t":"New","x":"After the next server update, a world boss's court no longer turns players away when it is full: a newcomer joins a copy of the court and can fight the same boss for the same rewards, beside the players in that copy.","g":["online","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-013","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Renown","t":"Performance","x":"The Renown you earn now reaches the server every few minutes instead of every minute, which saves the server a great deal of work. Your bar still shows what you earned at once (the faint part fills in when it is counted), and a level-up and the hour's limit are still reported within the minute.","g":["renown","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7846-014","v":"0.1.7846","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Renown","t":"Performance","x":"Once you have earned all the Renown an hour allows, nothing more is collected until the next hour, since the server would not count it anyway. Your weapon's sigil already stopped drinking then.","g":["renown","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-001","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Caravans","t":"Fix","x":"With Morrowind models on, a road caravan's campfire showed as a dead body. It's a fire again.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-002","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"Your inventory's Cart slot showed \"Small Cart\" if you still owned your old cart after buying a Caravan. It now shows the wagon you actually drive.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-003","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"A realm trade of an item you looted in the last couple of minutes could fail with \"The realm could not find the goods offered\". It goes through now.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-004","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Slowfall","t":"Rework","x":"You can jump while Slowfall is active. The jump is normal height and you come down at Slowfall's speed. You still can't jump in mid-air.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-005","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Fix","x":"Legendary items no longer lose condition when you equip them. The Aegis of Dawn used to lose about a third of its condition the first time you put it on. Other magic items still pay their usual cost.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-006","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Yard","t":"Rework","x":"Property lines are shared with your neighbours. The ground between two houses is now split down the middle. You can no longer decorate in front of a neighbour's door, and your own door step is yours. The marked edge on the ground hasn't changed shape yet.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7854-007","v":"0.1.7854","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Dying","t":"Buff","x":"No single enemy blow can kill you from full health. It leaves you at 1 HP instead, and the next hit can still kill. Falls, spells, traps and world-boss attacks are unchanged. Your set's death saves (Unbroken, the Hour Turns) aren't used up on these blows, so they're still there for the next one.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7859-001","v":"0.1.7859","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Come Sail Away","t":"Performance","x":"If you own boats from Come Sail Away, towns no longer lose frames for every boat you've placed, wherever it's moored. A fleet parked in a far-off port used to cost frames even in a town deep inland. Other players' boats near you cost less too.","g":["naval","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7859-002","v":"0.1.7859","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Come Sail Away","t":"Performance","x":"The sea's helm and broadside panels no longer do work every frame while you're ashore.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-001","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"A tavern's card tables no longer stand in corridors, doorways or the mouth of an opening. At The Gold Dungeon in Menakat the table stood in the one corridor joining the inn's two halves and shut the back half off; at The Dancing Castle in Pilliweyn the red gold table stood across the hall's way east. Both are fixed, and so is every other tavern laid out like them.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-002","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Rework","x":"A tavern with no floor for a table that is out of the way now has no card table (about one tavern in ten), and some keep only the green chips table where they had both. Almost every table that stays stands exactly where it stood.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-003","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Snowfall","t":"Fix","x":"Foes' ground telegraphs, like a revenant's blast circle, now always draw on top of deep snow. Before, the snow buried them outdoors in winter. Your own technique marks are fixed the same way.","g":["weather","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-004","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"If you would rather not have deep snow at all, turn it off at Settings › Graphics › Sky, water & weather › Snowfall by demifiend000. Searching the settings for \"deep snow\" also finds it.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-005","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Player Trade","t":"UI","x":"In a trade with another player, each letter of credit now shows its worth on its own row (\"Worth 12,500 gold\"). That covers your pack, your offer and theirs, and works on touch without hovering or clicking. The item card shows it too, as Worth.","g":["marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-006","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Mining","t":"New","x":"Copper, Silver, Platinum, Moonstone, Dwarven Scrap, Mithril, Adamantium, Ebony and Orichalcum veins each have their own colour now. Lead and Lodestone keep their classic look.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-007","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"Online, point at open ground on the world map to see a card listing:","g":["map","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-008","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"the ores its veins can be;","g":["map","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-009","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"what its dungeons' deep veins hold;","g":["map","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-010","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"its kingdom's own ore (Daggerfall's Moonstone, Sentinel's Ebony, Wayrest's Mithril, and so on);","g":["map","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-011","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"whether that ground is witnessed yet.","g":["map","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7872-012","v":"0.1.7872","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Mining","t":"Rework","x":"Gold, Platinum, Mithril, Ebony and a kingdom's own ore only appear on ground that three different players have gathered on (each account at least a week old). That's because the servers can't check which land a player claims to be standing on. The card shows which ores are waiting on that for each place. The Mining page now points to it.","g":["mining","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-001","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"Sethrakul's waters now stay open until it dives. The 08:00 storm no longer locks ships out, so latecomers and friends sailing out to help can still join.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-002","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Buff","x":"The serpent has a sixth less health, so fights end sooner. Two ships at average gunnery now win every time, in about 8½ minutes.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-003","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Other","x":"One ship alone still can't bring it down.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-004","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Buff","x":"Inside its waters a gale fills your sails from every direction. No more beating upwind at half speed.","g":["naval","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-005","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Buff","x":"Your ship also turns 1½ times faster while you're in it.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-006","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Buff","x":"Its blows throw your ship half as far and tear half as much canvas. You won't be pushed out of the fight and left unable to sail back.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-007","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"Sethrakul is much thicker now (1.6 times its old girth), so slow cannonballs fired with lag still land.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-008","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Buff","x":"Players standing on someone else's ship can hurt the serpent with their own bows and attack spells.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-009","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Fix","x":"In the serpent's waters ships have a wide invisible buffer around them and bounce off each other, instead of colliding and passing through.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-010","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"Rewards no longer depend on being near the serpent when it dies.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-011","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"Dealing a real part of the damage (several volleys that land) now earns a hoard. Spending a quarter of the fight within range does too, where half was needed before.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7879-012","v":"0.1.7879","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"Rework","x":"When the serpent falls, party members of any ship that dealt heavy damage also get a hoard, as long as they came to the fight.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-001","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Readied Spellcasting Hands","t":"New","x":"With a spell readied, your casting hands are now raised and ready on screen until you cast. This is jefetienne's Readied Spellcasting Hands 1.3, ported 1:1. Self-only spells raise nothing because they cast at once. It's on by default and you can turn it off under Features -> Combat.","g":["animation","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-002","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Chat Window","t":"New","x":"The chat has a search bar above the player list (over the conversation on narrow screens). Type part of a name, or # and a tag, to see every tab's lines from or about that player. The player list filters to match.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-003","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Chat Window","t":"New","x":"Type /search <name> in the chat field to search, and /search on its own to clear it. /find and /who still look up who is online anywhere in the world.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-004","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Text on the parchment is readable again: the Social panel, letters, the guild page and fields you type in are now in the page's ink.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-005","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"The stray ruled lines are gone from the talk window, Professions and Master Skills.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-006","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Enemy and boss health bars scale with your screen resolution. They no longer drain or sit on a board, and they stretch cleanly when made longer in the HUD editor (Alt+U).","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-007","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"HUD","t":"Fix","x":"In the HUD editor (Alt+U), the length handle now follows your pointer, and resizing a piece no longer pushes it off the screen.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-008","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"In the in-game book, a setting's description opens as a scroll beside the book instead of covering the list. The Controls header no longer hides the rows while you scroll.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-009","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"In the decorations menu you can now see which tabs and filters are selected.","g":["mod","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-010","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"World Map","t":"Fix","x":"The world and town maps have their Find me button back. It is still hidden on the dungeon's hand-drawn map.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-011","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Hotbar","t":"Fix","x":"Spamming the hotbar no longer makes the game stutter.","g":["quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7883-012","v":"0.1.7883","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Quest Journal","t":"Fix","x":"You can type in the quest journal's note field on the classic and Grimoire UIs again. It now opens as the game's standard text-entry box.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7887-001","v":"0.1.7887","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Disenchanting","t":"New","x":"Pressing your home's enchanting station now asks what you want: Daggerfall's item maker (Make Magic Items) or Disenchant. Disenchant opens your Stores page, scrolled to the Enchanting Station section, where a crafted piece comes apart into Arcane Essence.","g":["enchanting","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7887-002","v":"0.1.7887","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Alchemy Station","t":"New","x":"The alchemy station works the same way: Make Potions, or Brew on your Stores page.","g":["alchemy","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7887-003","v":"0.1.7887","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Disenchanting","t":"Other","x":"Offline, both stations open Daggerfall's maker as before.","g":["enchanting","alchemy"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7891-001","v":"0.1.7891","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Tab","t":"New","x":"The Members page of the Guild tab now shows whether each member is online, the same way the Friends list does: a green dot while they're playing, and \"Online\" or \"Last online 3 h ago\" under their rank.","g":["guild","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7891-002","v":"0.1.7891","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Tab","t":"New","x":"A member counts as online while they're in the world (within ten minutes of their last check-in), and the time keeps updating while the page is open.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-001","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"Rework","x":"The old tutorial is gone. New characters get a short welcome tour: moving and climbing, using things, the HUD, and the menu and saving.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-002","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"Any key a tutorial mentions is the key you have bound right now, named the way it appears on your keyboard.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-003","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"The first time you reach something new, a short note explains it. About 56 systems have one, including:","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-004","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"Each note shows once. Click or press a key to close it.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-005","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"Other","x":"Notes won't close from a key you're already holding.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-006","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"Other","x":"Notes wait until the pause menu and loading screens are gone.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-007","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"A Tutorials tab in the pause menu and a Tutorials button on the main menu hold all 68 notes, in 13 sections.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-008","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"You can search the notes, and unread ones are marked.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-009","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"You can turn popups off, show them all again, or mark everything read.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-010","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Other players no longer look like they're floating above the ground or sunk into it. Their height was being rounded to the nearest metre on its way to you, so depending on where they stood they could be up to half a metre off the ground.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-011","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"In dungeons, towns and buildings, other players no longer move in one-metre jumps.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-012","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Online Mode","t":"Other","x":"This update restarts the online server once, so everyone online is disconnected briefly and reconnects.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-013","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Tab","t":"New","x":"Members has a new folded list, \"What each rank may do\". It shows every rank's powers in your guild's own rank names, each rank on top of the one below, and what a rank may not do: Officers and the Guildmaster don't fill their own guild's writs or get paid by its contracts. A Member and a Recruit hold the same powers, and the list now says so.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-014","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Treasury","t":"New","x":"Treasury now says which of the gold can buy a hall, or a new name or tag: only gold your realm characters put in.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-015","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Treasury","t":"Rework","x":"The silver ledger now says which way each line went. A Tribute, an upkeep or a claim fee reads \"paid ...\", where it used to read \"put in\". A line the guild made itself, such as a Sellsword hired or a Charter's upkeep, now reads as the guild's (\"The guild hired a Sellsword for 1,500 silver\").","g":["guild","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-016","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Tab","t":"New","x":"Settings lists everything that still stands in the way of disbanding, before you press: gold, the hall, the vault, guild Stores, open writs or contracts, a Charter, a battle, and silver your own account has no room to take. Disband waits on it and says why, and so does Leave for a guildmaster alone in the guild. You no longer clear one thing, press, and only then hear about the next. Opening Settings checks the list again.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-017","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Tab","t":"New","x":"Overview says where the rest of your guild is run: seats and sieges from a seat town's Notice Board, writs and contracts from the Work tab.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-018","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Guild Tab","t":"New","x":"No guild yet? The tab now says, in two lines, what a guild is for.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-019","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Silver","t":"Fix","x":"Silver is called silver everywhere: a siege's Honour, a struck Charter's refund and the daily reset said \"Marks\".","g":["guild","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-020","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Fealty","t":"Rework","x":"A vassal's 5% to its liege is its \"fealty share\", so \"Tribute\" means only what a guild pays at the seat it pledged.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7915-021","v":"0.1.7915","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Heraldry","t":"Rework","x":"Your guild's heraldry is its \"arms\" everywhere, as on the Arms page.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-001","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Arrows","t":"New","x":"A shot that misses now stays in the wall, floor, tree or ground it hit. You can take it back like any other pile: the plaque reads \"Arrow\", and quick loot takes it in one press.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-002","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Arrows","t":"New","x":"Up to 40 stay in one place, and the oldest goes first. They're gone once you leave the area.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-003","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Arrows","t":"Other","x":"Conjured arrows still vanish. Arrows shot in an arena bout are still refunded by the healers instead of sticking.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-004","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Arrows","t":"Buff","x":"An arrow that hits an enemy now survives half the time and can be looted from the body.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-005","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Arrows","t":"Fix","x":"Arrows no longer count toward a normal enemy's three-item drop limit. That limit was throwing them away first, which is why bodies almost never gave arrows back.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-006","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Arrows","t":"New","x":"Use Twigs, a Pine Branch or a Wood Bundle from your inventory (Use mode) to fletch arrows: 2, 4 and 10 arrows each. This works online and offline.","g":["crafting","logging"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7918-007","v":"0.1.7918","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shops","t":"Rework","x":"Weapon Smiths now always keep 50-100 arrows on the counter. Armorers and General Stores keep 14-29, and Pawn Shops 7-14. Better shops keep more.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-001","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Daggerfall Online","t":"Rework","x":"Daggerfall Online is now DFO Online, with a new logo on the intro, the main menu, the menu's masthead, the website and the desktop launcher.","g":["rebrand"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-002","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Desktop App","t":"Rework","x":"The website, the desktop app, its installer and the home-screen app all carry the new name. The home-screen label reads DFO.","g":["rebrand","desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-003","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Daggerfall Online","t":"Rework","x":"Settings and menus now say \"the original game\" or \"classic\" where they used to name it. For example, \"Off uses the classic weather\". The leveling choice and the classic start are titled Classic, and the third view-distance step reads Classic (3).","g":["rebrand","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-004","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Daggerfall Online","t":"Rework","x":"Screenshots and saved loading shots are now named dfo-..., and the saves you export are DFO-Online-Saves.zip.","g":["rebrand","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-005","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Desktop App","t":"Rework","x":"The downloads are named DFO-Online-... from this update on. Your copy finds its update as usual, whatever it was called when you installed it.","g":["rebrand","desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-006","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Desktop App","t":"Other","x":"On a Mac: the new version installs as DFO Online beside your old Daggerfall Online app instead of replacing it. Once DFO Online opens, drag the old app to the Bin. Your saves, settings and game folder stay where they are.","g":["rebrand","mac"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-007","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Desktop App","t":"Other","x":"On Windows: if you pinned the app to your taskbar or Start menu, you may need to pin it again under its new name.","g":["rebrand","desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7926-008","v":"0.1.7926","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Terms","t":"Rework","x":"The Terms of Service and the Privacy Policy now name DFO Online. Nothing else in them changed, and no one is asked to agree again.","g":["rebrand","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-001","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"Fix","x":"Going all in and losing at an online Hold'em table no longer crashes the game. The hand that broke you now plays out on the table before you're stood up.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-002","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"Fix","x":"With All pressed, the 3D dungeon map now draws every ramp in full. Daggerfall's standard ramps used to be cut off at the floor below.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-003","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Raiding Parties","t":"Fix","x":"Kills you make after a raid's fight drifts past the edge of town now count, as long as you're still on the town's map square.","g":["siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-004","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Raiding Parties","t":"Fix","x":"Dying, fast travelling, Recall or /unstuck in the middle of a raid no longer stops raiders from coming when you return.","g":["siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-005","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Raiding Parties","t":"Fix","x":"The raid card on the map shows the town's real count against its real target (anywhere from 15 to 25), not only your own kills.","g":["siege","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-006","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Loot Window","t":"Fix","x":"The loot list on a body or pile now scrolls. The mouse wheel (or the pad) reaches every item, not only the first six, and the list shows how many items are above and below.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-007","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"People placed by a quest now show their name when you look at them, like everyone else in the room.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7932-008","v":"0.1.7932","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Player Trade","t":"Rework","x":"When the realm refuses a trade because a character is under review, it now says whose character it is: yours, with the reason, or the other player's.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7947-001","v":"0.1.7947","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"EG0 + AUDIT EG0 + EG0b + AUDIT EG II: Elite Gates - the Elite Breach and the Battlespire's torn halls, designed, audited and polished","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-001","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"Re-casting an effect that is already on you or a target now resets it to that cast's full duration. It no longer adds the new duration on top, and a shorter re-cast never cuts a longer one short.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-002","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"This applies to buffs and debuffs alike. That covers Shield, Fortify, Regenerate, Levitate, Light, Detect, the resistances and the rest; Paralyze, Silence, Continuous Damage and Soul Trap; a party member's spells on you; and a torch's fire on a foe.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-003","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"Re-casting Regenerate or a Continuous Damage effect on its last round still gives the full number of ticks a fresh cast would.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-004","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spells","t":"Other","x":"Buffs banked before this update keep their time and run out normally. You can also end them yourself from the buff icons.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-005","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Saves","t":"Fix","x":"When a window is open, F11 (Quick Load) now works only from the death screen. Loading from under your pack, a loot window or a sell counter could duplicate what that window was holding.","g":["audit","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-006","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Saves","t":"Fix","x":"Any load closes every open window before the save is read, including windows left waiting behind the death screen.","g":["audit","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-007","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shops","t":"Economy","x":"Shops pay for a crafted Superior or Masterwork piece what they pay for the plain piece its recipe makes. The quality's magic or rare lines are power, not resale value: the piece keeps them, and keeps its worth to other players.","g":["market","crafting","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-008","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shops","t":"Economy","x":"Patrons follow the same rule for crafted pieces. Found magic and rare items are priced as before.","g":["market","crafting","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-009","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shops","t":"Fix","x":"The keyed shelf now prices a sale exactly as the trade window does, and no longer buys conjured (Create Item) pieces.","g":["market","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7961-010","v":"0.1.7961","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"A character whose trade is on hold can no longer move its crafted pieces through another character, by listing, auctioning, filling a commission or disenchanting. Its Stores also cannot go into a guild's Stores or fill a guild writ.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7963-001","v":"0.1.7963","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Yard","t":"Performance","x":"Other players' yard decorations no longer draw across the whole map. Their small pictures (flowers, signs, crates) had no distance limit at all; now they stop where the models stop.","g":["homes","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7963-002","v":"0.1.7963","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Yard","t":"Performance","x":"Tiny yard pieces stop drawing once they would be only a few pixels tall, so a busy street of furnished yards costs much less.","g":["homes","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7963-003","v":"0.1.7963","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Yard","t":"New","x":"New option: Settings → Other players → Yard decorations: Off, 75 m, 150 m or 300 m (the default, as before). Your own yard always shows. If towns run slowly for you, try 150 m or Off.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7963-004","v":"0.1.7963","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Yard","t":"Removal","x":"Yard pieces still standing above the 4 m height limit (built before the limit existed) have been removed. No gold is refunded for them.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7963-005","v":"0.1.7963","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Accounts","t":"Rework","x":"A username can no longer be an email address. If you already signed up with one, you still sign in with it, but other players now see your generated name instead of your address.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7966-001","v":"0.1.7966","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Seat Tab","t":"Fix","x":"The board's Seat tab no longer gets stuck on \"The standings did not load.\" once many guilds have pledged.","g":["seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7966-002","v":"0.1.7966","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Seats","t":"Fix","x":"The weekly Turning hands out Charters again. A guild that earned a seat last week is given it the first time anyone reads a seat after this update.","g":["seats"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-001","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Travellers","t":"Rework","x":"Caravans and travellers now keep to the right of the road, so parties that meet pass side by side instead of walking through each other's wagons. Two caravans heading the same way walk abreast.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-002","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Caravans","t":"Rework","x":"A wagon now follows its horse round a bend instead of swinging round all at once.","g":["horse","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-003","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Caravans","t":"Rework","x":"At a shared camp, every caravan's wagons park round one fire without standing in each other, and each horse is tied alongside its cart.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-004","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Caravans","t":"Fix","x":"In a roadside hold-up, fighters and bandits no longer stand inside the wagons and horses.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-005","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Caravans","t":"Fix","x":"A roadside fight you walk up to no longer ends by itself, killing the caravan's guards and counting as a win you never fought.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-006","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Caravans","t":"Fix","x":"A merchant whose caravan will meet trouble now offers to hire you, and the missing offer no longer gives that away.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-007","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Remains found in a dungeon are no longer laid again after you save and load inside it.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-008","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Townsfolk walking into a shop are inside as soon as they reach the door.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7969-009","v":"0.1.7969","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"In town, people no longer stand inside one another in a three-person conversation.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7974-001","v":"0.1.7974","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Seats","t":"Fix","x":"The weekly seat Turning can no longer swamp the servers. Only one request at a time settles the week; everyone else's seat board answers immediately.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7974-002","v":"0.1.7974","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Seats","t":"Fix","x":"If you act at a seat (pledge, Tribute, a lever) in the moment the week is turning, you're told \"The week is turning at the seats. Try again in a moment.\" The act is never applied to a half-turned week.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-001","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"New","x":"Port towns now have a shipyard on their seaward edge, its back to the water. The shipmaster sells every ship Come Sail Away builds, from the Rowboat to the Carrack and the Large Galley, and buys your ships back. One window holds everything you do with a ship at a port:","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-002","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"New","x":"Ships for sale: each hull's size, crew, guns and price. Buying asks you to confirm. The Rowboat goes into your pack as parts (if you can carry them). Every other ship's deed goes into your Fleet, and she is laid up at that port: the window turns to Your fleet, where Bring her here brings her round to the quay.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-003","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"New","x":"Your fleet: where each ship lies, what she's worth and what the shipmaster will pay. You can bring her here, lay her up, rename her or sell her. Selling asks you to confirm, and a big sale is paid as a letter of credit if the coin would be too heavy.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-004","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"New","x":"Shipwright and Refits: repairs, provisions and the four refit lines for any ship of yours at that port or laid up. These need Naval Combat on.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-005","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"Other","x":"The shipmaster won't buy a ship with cargo in her hold, anything in her cabin (in its chests or on its floor), or her crew ashore with you, and he won't buy a ship that came into the realm through customs: she stays yours. When a ship is sold, her cabin's furniture is sold too, and half its value goes to the bank, as with a house.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-006","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Halls","t":"New","x":"Inside every shipyard, the crewmaster has six named sailors looking for a berth each day. Each one has a class, a grade from Green to Veteran, a trade (First Mate, Bosun, Gunner, Carpenter, Lookout, Cook, Deckhand, or a Bard) and a signing fee. You choose which ship they join and at what post.","g":["naval","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-007","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Halls","t":"New","x":"A ship comes with her whole crew, so on a full deck a recruit signs on in place of a hand you pick. A hire that adds men to her crew costs what the shipwright would charge for them, if that's more than the fee. You can pay hands off from the same page: if her crew still fills her deck, the window names who steps up, and you can't pay off her last hand. Hiring and paying off need Naval Combat on and can't happen during a fight.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-008","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Lighthouses","t":"New","x":"Port towns have a lighthouse: a whitewashed stone tower with red bands, a gallery and a lantern room, and the keeper's cottage beside it. While the town's lanterns are lit (5 pm to 8 am) its lamp lights the harbour, and two beams sweep a full circle, over the sea and the town. Online, everyone sees the beams in the same place.","g":["naval","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-009","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Lighthouses","t":"New","x":"Talk to the lightkeeper (or press the door) to climb up to the gallery: you go up on foot, not at a ship's helm and not with enemies about. You can't fall or climb off the gallery. The hatch takes you back down.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-010","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Quays","t":"Rework","x":"Every quay has been overhauled: cross-braced piles, timbers under the decks, fender piles and iron ladders down into the water, cleats and coils of rope by the bollards, a cargo crane on each harbour's main quay, and lamp posts along the long jetties.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-011","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk can now tell you where to find the shipyard, the crew hall, the lighthouse and the docks. The shipyard and the lighthouse are marked on the town map; for the crew hall and the docks, townsfolk give you directions. On the Overworld the shipyard, the lighthouse and the docks show as an anchor, a tower and a bollard.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-012","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shops","t":"Rework","x":"General Stores and Pawn Shops no longer sell or buy ship deeds and parts. Ships are bought and sold at the shipyards.","g":["market","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-013","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Tutorials","t":"Rework","x":"The tutorial's Sailing page now sends you to the shipyards, Shipwrights is now Shipyards (the shipmaster, the crew hall and the shipwright), and there's a new Lighthouses page. The empty Fleet page and Come Sail Away's setting now point you to the shipyards too.","g":["intro","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-014","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"Fix","x":"A ship sold while you were placing her could be placed and sold again.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-015","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"Fix","x":"A double click could buy two ships.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-016","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Halls","t":"Fix","x":"Paying off a hand could put a stranger on deck, and hiring could raise a wreck back afloat.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-017","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Halls","t":"Fix","x":"Hiring and paying off could push a ship's morale past its limit.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-018","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Halls","t":"Fix","x":"The crew page didn't show which hands were ashore with you.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-019","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Lighthouses","t":"Fix","x":"Climbing or jumping on the lighthouse gallery could take you over the railing.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-020","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Lighthouses","t":"Fix","x":"Coming down the lighthouse stair could leave you stuck in the door's step.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-021","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Lighthouses","t":"Fix","x":"The lighthouse lamp was blocked by its own glass, so it barely lit anything with Enhanced Lighting.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-022","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Lighthouses","t":"Fix","x":"The lighthouse sometimes stood right beside the shipyard instead of along the shore.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-023","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Harbours","t":"Fix","x":"A lake behind a port town could be taken for the sea.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-024","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"Fix","x":"Selling a ship lost whatever lay on her cabin floor.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-025","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shipyards","t":"Fix","x":"Flickering roofs, beams and posts on the shipyard and the lighthouse, and props poking through each other.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.7990-026","v":"0.1.7990","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Harbours","t":"Performance","x":"Ports, lighthouses and quays run lighter: the lighthouse lights cost nothing per frame, the port's textures load over a few frames, and the quays' hidden timbers are left out of collision.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-001","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"Every hand now earns rank from the fights and boardings they have been through: Green, Seasoned, Veteran, Old Salt.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-002","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"The six posts aboard each do something, and do more the longer their holder has served. The Gunner speeds the reload, the Carpenter the mending, the Lookout lets you see further, the Cook keeps spirits up, the Bosun adds way under sail, and the First Mate brings extra hands over the rail (never more than your crew has men for).","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-003","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"A companion who sails with you works his post while you're at the helm.","g":["naval","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-004","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Crew Roles","t":"New","x":"A new hand takes whichever post is emptiest, so a fallen Cook is replaced before you get a third Bosun. You can still reassign posts on the Fleet page.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-005","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Captain Tab","t":"New","x":"The new Captain tab in Holdings keeps your log: leagues sailed, ships sunk, taken and beaten off, contracts done, your best prize and the plunder you hauled.","g":["naval","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-006","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Captain Standing","t":"New","x":"You also build standing with each crown, from Unsworn to Admiral. Each rank brings perks in that crown's harbours: a discount at the shipwright, better-paid and more contracts, a letter of marque for sale (Privateer), the Admiralty's carrack for sale and seasoned hires (Commodore), and the navy always coming to your aid against pirates (Admiral). A captain whose notoriety runs too high in a crown's waters gets none of them there.","g":["naval","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-007","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Boarding","t":"New","x":"Beating off a pirate boarding now pays. The pirate is beaten then: taking or sinking her afterwards is logged but not paid again.","g":["naval","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-008","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Captain Standing","t":"New","x":"A letter of marque makes a rival crown's merchantmen and navy lawful prize in your crown's eyes. The rival still calls it piracy.","g":["naval","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-009","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Deep Waters","t":"New","x":"Far from every port, pirates are more common, bolder and bigger, and every hold and floating cask is richer. The helm plate tells you when you're in the deep.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-010","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spyglass","t":"Rework","x":"Ship names no longer float over every sail. A ship you haven't identified is just her hull, such as \"a sloop\" or \"a two-master\", and her card says nothing else about her: no colours, no damage.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-011","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"You learn her colours by sailing close, from your Lookout's call, when her guns turn on you, or through the spyglass.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-012","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"Press K aboard to raise the glass and use the mouse wheel to zoom (x2, x4, x8). Hold it on a ship to read her name and colours. Hold it on her up close to see her guns, crew, damage and cargo. The glass can't see ships behind land, or dark ships far off at night.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-013","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"Some wary pirates sail under false colours, passing for a merchantman of their own size with a trader's name. The glass can see through them, and they run up the black flag when they come for you.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-014","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"On a controller, the d-pad press you give the Spyglass works at the helm too, and the right stick's click zooms while the glass is up. On a touch screen, the Glass button sits at the helm and as a corner-button choice, and the glass has its own Magnify and Lower buttons.","g":["naval","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-015","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Harbourmaster","t":"New","x":"Every port's shipwright window now has a Harbourmaster tab with the day's contracts, while your ship lies at that port's quay. Bounties on a named pirate, hunts in the crown's waters, cargo to carry to another port, a wreck's casks to raise, and Admiralty surveys of ships through the spyglass.","g":["naval","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-016","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Harbourmaster","t":"New","x":"Contracts pay by your level and rank and run to a deadline. Finishing one raises your standing with the crown; failing or giving one up lowers it. You can hold three at a time, and the Captain tab lists them. Each kill or survey counts toward one contract.","g":["naval","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-017","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Harbourmaster","t":"New","x":"The bounty's pirate is waiting in the waters named on the contract. If someone else sinks her first, the bounty is void, with no loss of standing. A wreck's casks float up when you reach its mark.","g":["naval","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-018","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Exchange","t":"New","x":"An Exchange tab buys and sells eight goods of the Bay: wine, grain, wool, iron, spices, silk, silver and ivory. Each crown's ports make some goods cheaply and pay well for others, every port has a twist of its own, and prices drift from day to day. Each port only deals in so much of a good each day.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-019","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Exchange","t":"New","x":"Goods load into and out of the hold of the ship at the quay. A full hold slows her. The exchange tells you how much more she can carry and won't sell her so much she can't move.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-020","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Shops","t":"Other","x":"Shops don't buy the exchange's goods. Sell them at an exchange.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-021","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Treasure Charts","t":"New","x":"Pirates you sink or take sometimes carry a treasure chart, more often in the deep waters and most flagships. Read it from your inventory to mark its cache, then sail to the spot and the cache floats up beside you: gold and a strongbox's worth of loot. A cache you've already raised stays raised.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-022","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Sail far out on the open Abecean, west of the Bay's mouth and well away from any land, and you're asked whether to sail on into the open sea. Three days later your ship comes out off Veilhaven, the first port past the Veil, with her crew and her hold aboard. Sail back into the Veil, at the sea's eastern edge, to be asked the way home. If an enemy is close or another player is aboard, you're told so, and asked again once the deck is clear.","g":["naval","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-023","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Past the Veil lies an endless sea of isles, the same for every player. Port isles have a town and a freeport quay, ruins have a dungeon to delve, wild isles bear exotic goods, and bare rocks are just rocks.","g":["naval","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-024","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"The farther west you sail, through the Shallows, the Reaches, the Deep Aether and the Abyss, the deadlier the corsairs and the richer every hold. Ruins in the Deep Aether and the Abyss are Elite dungeons.","g":["naval","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-025","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"No crown's law reaches past the Veil. There's no navy to call on, and nothing you sink there counts as a crime. Corsairs and the isles' traders sail under the sea's own names, and a corsair's papers sometimes chart her waters for you.","g":["naval","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-026","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Exotic goods: ether-amber, starglass and voidsilk are made on the isles and wanted in every port of the Bay, and the isles pay well for the Bay's goods. Sail close to a wild isle and casks of its good float out alongside your ship; its strand fills again seven days after you first gather it.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-027","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Six legendary ships haunt the depths, each with her own terror and a purse on her head: Sorrow's Wake, The Drowned Queen, Ninefold Hunger, The Lantern-Eater, The Pale Regent and The Starless. A freeport's harbourmaster will tell you where each was last seen. Sink one for her purse and a name with every crown, though a month later the sea raises her again.","g":["naval","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-028","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"The Chart of the Etheric Sea: past the Veil, the travel map key opens your chart of the isles you've sighted, the depths, the Veil and the legends' haunts you've heard of. Drag to pan; zoom with the wheel, a pinch or the chart's own buttons; point at or tap an isle to name it. Isles are charted as you sight them, and a freeport sells a chart of its waters.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-029","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"The Veil holds the Bay's magic back: Recall, guild teleports, portal stones and a party's travel to its leader don't cross it, and your Fleet can't summon or send a ship across. Sail her yourself. Fall past the Veil and you wake at the nearest port isle.","g":["naval","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-030","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"The light past the Veil is cold and violet.","g":["naval","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8014-031","v":"0.1.8014","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Other","x":"The crossing out is part of the enhanced game and online play. The classic game keeps Daggerfall's own sea, though a captain already past the Veil can always sail home.","g":["naval","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8020-001","v":"0.1.8020","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Gathering","t":"Performance","x":"A herb patch, vein, boulder or tree now goes the moment you finish working it, instead of waiting for the server to answer. If the server refuses the harvest, the node comes back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8020-002","v":"0.1.8020","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Gathering","t":"Performance","x":"Your goods, XP and rank-ups arrive faster after each harvest.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8020-003","v":"0.1.8020","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Market","t":"Performance","x":"The market loads noticeably faster, especially when switching views and after buying.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8020-004","v":"0.1.8020","d":"2026-10-11","e":"Market","t":"Performance","x":"A view you opened in the last minute shows straight away, without a \"Reading the market...\" flash.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-001","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Desktop App","t":"Fix","x":"The desktop app finds and installs updates again. No new desktop release had been published since 0.1.8020, so the launcher had nothing to offer. The next release after this merge brings in everything merged since then.","g":["desktop-app","rebrand"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-002","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"A new What this is panel sits at the top. It says what a seat is in two sentences, plus your next step: join a guild, pledge here, ask an Officer, or earn influence.","g":["notice-board","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-003","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"If your guild can pledge here, the Pledge button is right beside that line. Deadlines show how long is left.","g":["notice-board","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-004","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"How the seat war works is now at the top. It starts open if your guild isn't in this region's war yet.","g":["notice-board","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-005","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Words on this board explains every term the tab uses: Charter, influence, Muster, Reckoning, Turning, Right of Siege, Defence, Standing, Tithe, Edict, Tribute, Sellsword, the Works, Fealty and Pacts, Seasons and Tides.","g":["notice-board","online","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-006","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"You see the explanation even when the standings are still loading or closed to you.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-007","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Seasons","t":"New","x":"How chapters work sits above the chapter cards on the Work tab. It covers what a chapter is and how you belong to one, Merit, Strength, the bands, the Master's and council chairs, Seasons and patrons. Every number comes from the game's own rules.","g":["seats","online","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-008","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"The Chapters Explain Themselves","t":"New","x":"It starts open until you have earned your first Merit.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-009","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"The Family tab has a fourth page, How it works. It covers:","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-010","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"death under your house's rules and the toll you chose;","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-011","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"who carries the line on, and what they inherit;","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-012","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"heirlooms and remains;","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-013","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"marriage and children;","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-014","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"playing another family member;","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-015","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"what the marks on the tree mean.","g":["online","saves","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-016","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"The family tree links to it: \"New to the family? How it works\".","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-017","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"Long names on the tree now wrap onto two lines instead of being cut off. Hover a name to see it in full.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-018","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Living World","t":"New","x":"Talking to a Living World resident now shows how they regard you, under their name. It shows Friend, Known, Enemy or Hostile, a bar from −100 to +100, and the number.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-019","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Talk Window","t":"New","x":"Press it to see what the number means and what raises or lowers it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-020","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Talk Window","t":"New","x":"This works for residents in the street, at home, on the road and in the deep.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-021","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Talk Window","t":"New","x":"Someone who won't talk to you now says where you stand, e.g. \"Mara turns away from you. (Enemy, −52)\".","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-022","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Talk Window","t":"New","x":"On the classic skin, the talk window is the original game's and does not show the badge.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-023","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"The Notice Board's text is a step larger, and the Family tab's tree, card and labels are larger too.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-024","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"On a phone, the fold headers are bigger to tap.","g":["notice-board","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-025","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Windows inside buildings are now see-through. From a house, tavern, shop, guild hall or temple you see the real street, sky and weather through the panes, and the window's lead lattice and frame stay in place. This needs Settings > Graphics > Real windows set to Full, which is the default on High and Ultra.","g":["guild","homes","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-026","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Character Sheet","t":"New","x":"The Standing page now lists your reputation with every guild, temple, knightly order, kingdom, coven, vampire clan and Daedric Prince by default, not only the ones you belong to. If you turned \"Every faction's standing\" off (Settings > Interface > Character sheet), it stays off.","g":["ascension","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-027","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Stables now sell Sacks of Oats and Wagon Yards now sell Wagon Repair Kits online too. Until now they were only sold offline.","g":["market","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-028","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"A worn-out wagon never becomes unusable. At its worst it is Failing: its team pulls it more slowly, but you can still drive it, hitch it, have it follow you and take it on journeys. A Wagon Yard or a repair kit brings its speed back.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-029","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"A wagon that was already broken down in your save is now Failing, so you can drive it again.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-030","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"Horses never die. A horse left unfed goes hungry and then starves. It gets weaker and won't gallop, but it stays yours, and one meal puts it right.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-031","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Developers","t":"New","x":"The Chapters from \"The Chapters\" update are now open to everyone. They had been switched on for developers only.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-032","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Notice Board","t":"New","x":"Guild chapters, hall writs and your own chapter writ now appear on the Notice Board's Work tab.","g":["notice-board","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-033","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Boards fill in town by town: a town's chapters appear once three players have visited its guild halls.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-034","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Harbours","t":"New","x":"Docks no longer cross each other. In harbours round a cape or a bay's horn, two piers could meet over the water in an X; Penwall Derry was one. A pier now ends where it meets its neighbour's, and no berth is placed with its quay over another's.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-035","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Homes","t":"New","x":"Fixed a phantom room tab in two-storey homes, often \"Room 3\". It sat in the gap between the floors, and picking it sent the decorating camera into the walls.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-036","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Trading","t":"New","x":"If your trading is held over an item, a refused trade now names that item instead of \"something\".","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-037","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Trading","t":"New","x":"The hold notice now warns that each hold counts: the third time, trading stays frozen until staff have looked, even after the item is gone.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-038","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Trading","t":"New","x":"If a hold stays after the item is gone, the game now tells you it is waiting on staff review instead of saying nothing.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-039","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"The sea west of the Bay is water again. You can swim there, Buoyancy works, and you can get back to your ship. Before, you stood on a seabed under the surface.","g":["naval","overworld","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-040","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Lighting","t":"New","x":"A torch, lantern or Candle spell underwater no longer whites out the screen. It gives a soft glow and still lights what's near you.","g":["lighting","audit","torch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-041","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Lighting","t":"New","x":"Lights in heavy fog and sandstorms glow a little less, for the same reason.","g":["lighting","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-042","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Snow","t":"New","x":"Rain and snow no longer get choppy after the game has been left open for many hours.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-043","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Elites","t":"New","x":"The Greater Giant in the open zone drops its proper loot again: two elite-table drops (magic and common pieces, a chance at rare or legendary, and gold by level). Before this fix it only dropped an ordinary giant's purse.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-044","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Greater Giant","t":"New","x":"The Greater Giant now hits every player at four times damage. Before, it did that only to the player whose game spawned it. Everyone else took hits like an ordinary zone giant.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-045","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"A quest monster, item or person could be placed outside its dungeon if the dungeon was built at a different size from the one the quest was set up on. One example was the mummy for Dust of Restful Death in Ruins of Old Barbara's Place. Now, each time a dungeon loads, anything on a spot that doesn't exist is moved to a valid spot inside. To fix a quest that's already stuck, leave the dungeon and walk back in, or reload.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-046","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"Fix","x":"Riding with the Morrowind models in third person no longer paints Daggerfall's 2D horse head and neck over the screen. You see only your character on the 3D horse.","g":["morrowind","animation","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-047","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"New Text font setting under Overhauls > UI (for Enhanced Plus and DFO Grimoire), with five choices: Game, Sans, Monospace, Dyslexic (OpenDyslexic) or My font.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-048","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Text Font","t":"New","x":"My font takes the name of a font installed on your computer. List my fonts shows them in browsers that support it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-049","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Text Font","t":"New","x":"The change applies at once. OpenDyslexic downloads only if you choose it.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-050","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Every channel has its own colour:","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-051","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"World is white, Region green, Guild purple, Local grey, Party teal, Language rose.","g":["mod","loot","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-052","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Each tab shows a colour square.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-053","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Turn this off in Settings > Gameplay > Other players > Chat colours by channel.","g":["mod","loot","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-054","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Player names have their own colour, separate from their words: strangers brass (red on Grimoire), you pale gold, party members green, friends blue.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-055","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"Language channels, in 15 languages:","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-056","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"/lang de joins one, /lang off leaves it, /lang lists them all, and /lc <text> speaks there.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-057","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"You can also choose one in Settings > Gameplay > Other players > Language channel.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-058","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"A Lang tab appears while you're in one.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-059","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"@mentions: a line with @YourName is highlighted in gold, shows over the world from any tab, and plays a chime. Turn the chime off with Chime when someone @mentions you.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-060","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"New","x":"On DFO Grimoire, a chat tab's unread count is a seal beside its name: red, or gold when it holds a mention.","g":["mod","loot","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-061","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Inventory: the worn sets lines (e.g. Dagon's Brand 7/9) sit under the paperdoll only, so the item box keeps its full height.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-062","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Pause menu: the right-hand page is centred instead of pushed far to the right.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-063","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Scry (Reforge):","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-064","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"The price no longer runs over the Scry button, so you can read it and buy again.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-065","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"On Grimoire each family's name is in the book's red, and the reason you can't afford it is in soft ink.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-066","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Rows: hovered and chosen rows are washed a shade darker instead of getting a red bar. The dashed boxes round empty lists are gone.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-067","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"Faint text is darkened just enough to read.","g":["mod","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-068","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Lighthouses","t":"New","x":"Port town lighthouses were built like lighthouses from a much later age: whitewash and red stripes, a glass lantern room, a copper dome. They are now beacon towers of the Iliac Bay: bare grey stone with a battlemented parapet round the gallery, an open stone lantern of eight arches under a steep slate roof, and a fire burning in an iron brazier inside.","g":["naval","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-069","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Lighthouses","t":"New","x":"The beacon is lit from dusk to dawn. The flames rise in the brazier at nightfall and its sweeping beams still reach far out to sea. By day its coals smoulder.","g":["naval","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-070","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Lighthouses","t":"New","x":"Windows on the lighthouse and the shipyard office now have small leaded panes.","g":["naval","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-071","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"Looking toward a far-off ship used to show her card, with her type and how far off she was, before you had identified her at all. You could spot and range ships without ever raising the spyglass. Now a ship you have not made out shows no card, whether you are simply looking at her or have your broadside laid on her.","g":["naval","audio","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-072","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Ships","t":"New","x":"To make her out, come within plain sight of her, let your Lookout call her colours, or hold your spyglass on her. Then her card shows as before.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-073","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"Raising the spyglass at the helm used to fill most of the view with your own masts, sails and crew. The glass now looks past your own ship: while it is raised, her rigging and hands drop out of the view.","g":["naval","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-074","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"Every ship beyond yours stays in view and can be studied with the glass, even one lying close alongside.","g":["naval","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-075","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Spyglass","t":"New","x":"Looking straight along the deck toward the bow of a very long ship, such as the Large Galley, part of her bow can still show.","g":["naval","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-076","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Ships","t":"Performance","x":"Ships sailing around other players far across the map are no longer built and animated on your screen. They come into view, fading in as any ship does, well before the haze would let you see them. On a busy server this gave back about a third of each frame: one player went from 38-45 FPS to 103-150 FPS.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-077","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Shadows","t":"New","x":"With Morrowind data attached, townsfolk, guards, shopkeepers, foes, travellers and the figures you place now cast the shadow of their own Morrowind body (its shape, its pose, its clothes) instead of the old Daggerfall sprite's outline on the wall behind them.","g":["lighting","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-078","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Shadows","t":"New","x":"Someone just out of view still throws their shadow into it, as the old sprites did.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-079","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Stepping Through","t":"New","x":"A foe burning away, or a companion stepping through a portal, loses their shadow once more of them is gone than whole, as the old sprites did.","g":["clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-080","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"In a room with many lamps, such as a guild hall, people standing still cast a shadow from every lamp, not only from the nearest twelve.","g":["guild","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-081","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Shadows","t":"New","x":"Your own body, other players' bodies and your household's do not cast a shadow yet.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-082","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Guilds","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk, shopkeepers, guild members, nobles and priests are dressed from a wardrobe of their own: tops, breeches, skirts, robes and cloaks, each drawn as one of Morrowind's own garments of its kind, in their kind's colours. Their station sets how fine the clothes are, on Morrowind's ladder from common up to exquisite.","g":["guild","online","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-083","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"No Two Alike","t":"New","x":"A noble never wears common clothes, a farmhand never wears silk, and a dyed garment keeps its colour.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-084","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Character Creation","t":"New","x":"Heads and hairs are now paired freely, from every pairing of the heads and hairs your Morrowind data offers a race at character creation (before, there were ten). Together with their clothes, this makes two people who look alike rare.","g":["online","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-085","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"No Two Alike","t":"New","x":"Who wears what is sharper:","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-086","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"No Two Alike","t":"New","x":"A knightly order's people wear full plate of one metal by rank: iron and steel at the bottom, up to dwarven, orcish and ebony.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-087","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Guilds","t":"New","x":"A fighters' guild's people wear whatever armour came to hand.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-088","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"No Two Alike","t":"New","x":"The Dark Brotherhood dress in dark clothes.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-089","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Sprites","t":"New","x":"The street's walkers keep the cut their sprite shows: robes, a skirt or breeches.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-090","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Argonian","t":"New","x":"Khajiit and Argonians go barefoot and bareheaded, as Morrowind dresses them.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-091","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"A person you place as a decoration in your home or your yard now stands in a Morrowind body too, dressed for who the figure is and of the region's race.","g":["morrowind","climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-092","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"You can now ride in third person with the Morrowind body. Zoom out with the wheel or the view toggle as you would on foot.","g":["morrowind","climbing","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-093","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"In first person, you look down over the 3D horse's neck instead of the old riding sprite.","g":["morrowind","climbing","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-094","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse Cart and Cargo","t":"New","x":"Other riders on the Morrowind body, Horse Cart and Cargo's horses (standing, following, parked and pulling) and the road's wagon teams are all 3D horses too.","g":["horse","online","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-095","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"The 3D horse wears the same coat, pattern, legs and markings as your sprite horse, and each flank has markings of its own.","g":["morrowind","climbing","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-096","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"Gallop on its breath. Hold Run on horseback to gallop. Your horse spends its breath instead of your fatigue. When it runs out the horse is winded and won't gallop until it has caught its breath. A horse bar appears on the HUD while you ride.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-097","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"Feed it to grow your bond. Feed your horse oats (sold at the Stable) or give it an apple as a treat. Every meal grows your bond, from Wary up to Kindred, and a stronger bond makes every stat better, up to +20.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-098","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"Keep it fed. A hungry horse is weaker. A starving one won't gallop, and your bond slowly fades. A horse never dies of hunger. A horse sent to the stable is fed there, and one left waiting in the wild grazes. On long journeys and rests, your horse eats oats you carry in your pack or wagon.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-099","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"More than one horse. The Stable page (Holdings tab) shows every horse you own, with its stats, bond, hunger and breath. Feed any of them, or pick which one you ride.","g":["horse","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-100","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"New","x":"Mend it at a Wagon Yard. The wagonwright now has a Mend option. If your wagon isn't with you, they'll go out to it for a little more.","g":["market","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-101","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Repair Kits","t":"New","x":"Patch it in the field with a Wagon Repair Kit (sold at the Wagon Yard). Each kit takes an hour and mends a quarter, up to 60%, enough to limp a broken wagon into town.","g":["crafting","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-102","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Wagon","t":"New","x":"Smiths and the Repairs Objects enchantment don't repair wagons or horses.","g":["horse","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-103","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Enhanced Plus","t":"New","x":"See how your horse is doing: its breath, its hunger (with how many hours of food it has left) and its bond, plus your gait and speed. On a wagon it also shows the wagon's condition and its load.","g":["audit","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-104","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Enhanced Plus","t":"New","x":"Do it from the panel: Feed oats, give an Apple, use a Repair kit, open the wagon's Cargo, open the Stable page, switch the View, or Dismount, all without a menu or a key.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-105","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Enhanced Plus","t":"New","x":"Teams count: on a wagon, the hunger shown is your team's hungriest horse, and Feed goes to that horse.","g":["audit","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-106","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Enhanced Plus","t":"New","x":"Greyed out means not now: a button you can't use yet is greyed out, and hovering it says why (no oats, full, out of reach).","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-107","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Enhanced Plus","t":"New","x":"Free the mouse (Y) to click the buttons, or tap them on a phone.","g":["audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-108","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"Each horse's bond is a bar now, with the points left to its next level.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-109","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"A fed horse says how many hours of food it has left, and a winded horse says so.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-110","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"Hover a stat to see where it comes from: what the horse was born with, its bond bonus and any hunger penalty.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-111","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Stable","t":"New","x":"The wagon's condition bar is coloured by its state, and the card shows what a Wagon Yard charges to mend it.","g":["holdings","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8127-112","v":"0.1.8127","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Seat boards, market sales and courier deliveries no longer slow the whole account service down in regions where a guild holds a Charter.","g":["market","online","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-001","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Nerf","x":"The curse's +40 Strength, Agility, Endurance and Speed and +30 to its seven skills now apply only in beast form. In human form you are your own character again. The beast itself is unchanged.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-002","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Nerf","x":"Changing form fully heals you once a day. Changing back, or changing again with Hircine's Ring, no longer heals.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-003","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Buff","x":"The beast's claws count as silver against creatures that need a better metal. A Lich or an Ancient Lich now takes reduced damage from claws, the same as from a silver weapon.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-004","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Hoods","t":"Nerf","x":"A raised hood still protects you from the sun's penalty, but no longer gives the night's +20 in daylight. Indoors, underground and at night you keep the full +20.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-005","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Nerf","x":"Rare weapons can no longer roll Vampiric Effect (heal all the damage you deal). Weapons that already have it keep it.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-006","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Nerf","x":"Life leech from a weapon's lines and gems together is capped at 10% of each hit.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-007","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Nerf","x":"Hist-Sap (the Mark of the Hist) now regenerates 1% a round (2% under half health), down from 2% (4%).","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-008","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Nerf","x":"Open Hand (the Gauntlets of the Rose): the second bare-handed hit now deals half damage.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-009","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Duels","t":"Rework","x":"Melee and ranged attacks now share the same damage ceiling as spells: at most 180 damage in any 5 seconds, counting blows and casts together.","g":["arena","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8130-010","v":"0.1.8130","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed: in arena bouts, hits from one side of your opponent always counted as backstabs (triple damage), whichever way they faced. Backstabs no longer happen against players.","g":["arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8133-001","v":"0.1.8133","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"With Morrowind models on, other characters and horses no longer shrink when the camera is high above them, or grow back as it comes down. They stay the right size wherever the camera is.","g":["morrowind","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-001","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Home Votes","t":"Rework","x":"A house's decorations are now hidden from other players only when its votes reach -5 or lower. Before, a single vote down (-1) hid them. A house at -1 to -4 stays fully visible, so people can see it and vote it up.","g":["homes","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-002","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Caravans","t":"Fix","x":"If you take the overhead lantern (or any other built-in piece) out of your caravan, visitors no longer see it or its light. Visitors see the change the next time you stand in your caravan while online.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-003","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Decorator","t":"Fix","x":"Decorations set against a wall now sit in front of it instead of sinking into it, at any size and with the grid on. The grid now snaps along the wall.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-004","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"A shop, temple or tavern next to your house no longer claims half your yard. The ground between two houses is still split down the middle.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-005","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"Grass no longer draws over a portal's vortex. Veiled foes and ghosts are fixed the same way.","g":["grass","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-006","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Travellers","t":"Fix","x":"Caravans and other road parties now set off from outside the city walls instead of walking through them.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-007","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Mining","t":"Fix","x":"Ore veins are clearly different colours: Moonstone a pale blue, Lodestone rust red, Copper orange, and so on. A boulder no longer looks like Lodestone.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8145-008","v":"0.1.8145","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"Morrowind-style NPCs whose helmet fails to load now show their head instead of a stump of neck.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-001","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"At high travel speeds (×100) your character, the ring under them and the route line now move smoothly instead of stuttering.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-002","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"Your speed no longer drops to ×60 for the rest of a trip after a small gap in the road. Leaving the road still slows you to ×60, but your chosen speed comes back as soon as you're on a road again.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-003","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"The ring under you is smaller and centred on your feet, with a dark rim so it shows up on snow and sand.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-004","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"The route is now a trail of gold dots fixed to the ground, evenly spaced all the way to the horizon.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-005","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"The spot you clicked is marked with a gold X instead of a circle. A journey to a town ends in a slightly larger X.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-006","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"Map dots and diamonds are now symbols, in the same colours as before:","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-007","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"roaming monster bands: a skull","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-008","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"dungeons: a stone arch (red if undiscovered, brass if found)","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-009","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"party members and other players: a person (two people for a crowd)","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-010","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"pilgrims and pedlars: a backpack","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-011","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"UI","x":"gathering nodes: a pickaxe (Mining), a pine (Logging), a leaf (Herbalism), a paw print (Hunting) and a fish (Fishing)","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-012","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Quest monsters now appear only for the quest's owner and the owner's party, in dungeons, buildings and outdoors. This covers side quests and the main quest.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-013","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Other players can't see them, can't hit them, and won't be attacked by them. Party members holding the same quest still get kill credit.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-014","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Quests","t":"Other","x":"A player standing next to you may see you fighting something they can't see.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-015","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Quick Loot","t":"New","x":"Quick loot shows each item's rarity: a coloured gem before the name and a soft band of that colour under the row (blue Magic, gold Rare, orange Legendary, pale blue Aetheric, purple Artifact, gold-leaf Gilded). Enhanced Plus and DFO Grimoire.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-016","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Chat Window","t":"New","x":"Chat tabs scroll sideways with the mouse wheel. The edge with more tabs fades, and a clicked tab scrolls fully into view.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8148-017","v":"0.1.8148","d":"2026-10-12","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Rework","x":"DFO Grimoire's Tab dial now uses Daggerfall's own icons: your character's face for Skills, the HUD star for Magic, the sack for Inventory and the scroll for Map. To bring back the old paintings, go to Settings → Overhauls → DFO Grimoire → \"Tab dial\".","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8151-001","v":"0.1.8151","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Fix","x":"Online, a magic school past 100 no longer makes spells nearly free. Before, a mastered school with gear on top pushed a spell's cost below zero, so everything cast for 5 magicka, Area buffs included.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8151-002","v":"0.1.8151","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Other","x":"Past 100 each point still makes spells cheaper. A school at 200 casts at half what it costs at 100.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8151-003","v":"0.1.8151","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Magic Costs","t":"Fix","x":"The spell maker no longer shows negative costs.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-001","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"Companions no longer get in the way. When one stands between you and a body, a loot pile, your ship's helm, a door or a container within reach, clicking uses that object instead of opening their inventory. With nothing usable behind them, clicking still opens their pack, and the on-screen label shows which one a click will use.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-002","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Companions","t":"Fix","x":"With Morrowind data attached, crew companions and sworn revenants keep their own race, face and clothes through every door, dungeon and reload, and other players see them the same way. A revenant is the same person every time it returns.","g":["morrowind","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-003","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Passing the mantle online can no longer overwrite a sibling with the new heir's name and class.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-004","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Heirs resumed from the Online page now start at the family seat instead of Privateer's Hold.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-005","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Project Legacy","t":"New","x":"A home you own on a farm or manor can now be made your family seat, and family members met there begin their story there.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-006","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Salvage","t":"Fix","x":"Classic Daggerfall magic items (guild-shop and Item Maker pieces, like a \"Blazing Holy Dagger of Fireballs\") now appear on the Salvage page marked \"Classic magic\" and explain why they give no shards, instead of silently missing.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8168-007","v":"0.1.8168","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Fix","x":"After crossing the Veil, a ship too heavily loaded to move now says so (\"You're going to need a bigger boat\"), where the crossing banner used to hide it. Everything you carry, gold and wagon included, counts against a ship's hold.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8172-001","v":"0.1.8172","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"The horses that stand in towns, at World of Daggerfall's bandit camps and forts, and in the Stables now stand as the 3D horse when Morrowind data is attached (the nearest eight within 60 m).","g":["morrowind","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8172-002","v":"0.1.8172","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"People who used to stay as sprites now stand in Morrowind bodies: a town's figures that belong to no faction, World of Daggerfall's dock people, the captives, merchants and prisoners its markers place, and the crews on Come Sail Away's boats.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8172-003","v":"0.1.8172","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Other","x":"Past the body range, Daggerfall's own sprites still stand, as they do for the walkers. Other animals, children, vampires' people and Daedra Princes keep their sprites.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-001","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Rework","x":"Privateer's Hold is no longer a private copy for each character. It is a shared dungeon like every other: its enemies, doors, levers and loot are the same for everyone inside, and you can see, chat and party with other players there.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-002","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Rework","x":"Once you leave Privateer's Hold online, you can't go back in. Its door, a Recall to a spot marked inside it, and a quest that would send you there all say \"You cannot go back into Privateer's Hold.\" A Recall or quest arrival lands you outside instead.","g":["online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-003","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Other","x":"You still start a new game inside the Hold, and a character saved inside it still loads back in.","g":["online","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-004","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Other","x":"Offline, nothing changes.","g":["classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-005","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Furniture Stores","t":"Fix","x":"Furniture Stores now show in the shop colour on both town maps. They used to be drawn as houses. Like every other shop, a store is named on the map once you have been inside or someone has marked it for you.","g":["map","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-006","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Furniture Stores","t":"New","x":"You can now ask townspeople where they are. The Where-is list has a new \"Furniture stores\" group.","g":["map","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-007","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Joinery","t":"New","x":"Every city and town now has a Joinery beside its Stables and Wagon Yard, as long as the town has room for one. It is a carpenter's open-air yard: a shingled workshop, a timber rack, a log pile, sawhorses and a chopping block, with a table, chairs and a bench on show by the gate.","g":["carpentry"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-008","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Joinery","t":"New","x":"Its workbench is a Carpentry station. Talk to the carpenter, or use the sign or the bench, to open your Stores page at The Workbench. A craft or a saw costs 50 gold, the same as at a Furniture Store's bench. Carpentry is done online, as before.","g":["carpentry","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-009","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Furniture Stores","t":"Other","x":"Linen for beds is still sold only at Furniture Stores.","g":["carpentry","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8184-010","v":"0.1.8184","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Joinery","t":"New","x":"To find a Joinery, ask townspeople under \"Carpenters\", look on either town map, or look for the saw mark on the Overworld map.","g":["map","carpentry"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-001","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Entering the world freezes for less. The game no longer stalls while it works out where every town's pilgrims go for their holy days, or while it picks the day's elite halls in the Wrothgarian zone. The pilgrimages and halls are the same, but the frozen screen is seconds shorter.","g":["overworld","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-002","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"World Map","t":"Performance","x":"The map opens without the long freeze. Opening the map for the first time in a session took 6.7 s on a desktop and now takes 0.7 s.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-003","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Ships","t":"Performance","x":"Far-off ships no longer weigh on your frame rate. Ships far out at sea, including the ones other players leave behind when they log off, no longer keep a full animated hull hundreds of kilometres away, and they make decisions less often while nobody can see them. Their voyages, fights and damage carry on as before. With such a fleet in the world, one player's frame rate went from 37 back to 90 FPS.","g":["naval","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-004","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Overworld","t":"Performance","x":"Smoother walking in the overworld. Ships, their map lookups and wagon harness ropes do the same work for less effort and less memory garbage: 79 -> 93 FPS walking the coast.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-005","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Horse","t":"Performance","x":"Horse coats no longer stutter. Meeting a horse with a new coat on the road no longer freezes the game for a moment. Its coat is painted a few pictures at a time instead of all forty at once.","g":["horse","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-006","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Wagon","t":"Performance","x":"Parked carts cost less. A parked team's harness stops recomputing its ropes while nothing moves.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8213-007","v":"0.1.8213","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Desktop App","t":"Performance","x":"Desktop app: smoother frames. The app no longer reads your account and settings files from disk every frame. It keeps them in memory, as the browser does: about 86 -> 110 FPS in a town.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8217-001","v":"0.1.8217","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Yard","t":"Performance","x":"Player yards now take far fewer draw calls. Each yard's 3D pieces are drawn together, and its repeated sprites (the same plant, the same statue) are drawn as one. Where decorated yards are in view, a town makes about 17-18% fewer draw calls a frame. This helps most where each draw call is expensive: the browser version and weaker CPUs and drivers.","g":["homes","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-001","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Spells","t":"Buff","x":"Mastering Destruction now makes your damage spells hit harder. Online, a mastered Destruction past 100 adds to your Damage Health and Continuous Damage spells as it climbs - 1% for each point of its effective value past 100, +40% when mastered to 200. Until now those points only made spells cheaper, while the same mastery made dungeon foes tougher. Gear that raises Destruction still makes spells cheaper, as before; the extra damage comes from the mastery itself.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-002","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Skill Training","t":"Rework","x":"Spells now count the foe you are fighting when they train a mastered school. Past 100, a skill learns from tough foes, but only a weapon blow ever told it who you were fighting. A spell landing on a foe (or a foe's spell landing on you) now does too, so blasting a tough foe trains your school as fast as fighting it with a weapon. A cast never trains slower than it did before.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-003","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Potency, a new line on jewellery and weapons: +3% to +15% spell damage. Everything you wear adds up to at most +30%.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-004","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Wellspring, a new line on jewellery: 2% to 10% of your magicka back when you kill a foe, at most 10% a kill from everything you wear.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-005","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"The Eye of Magnus (amulet) - *Magnus's Gaze*: your Destruction spells meet a saving throw 15 lower. A foe immune to the element stays immune.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-006","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"The Ring of Artaeum (ring) - *Wellspring of Artaeum*: 1% of your magicka returns every magic round, 2% while you are under half.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-007","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"New","x":"Shalidor's Brand (broadsword, saber or longsword) - *Arcane Surge*: while you wield it, your Destruction spells strike 25% harder while your magicka is above three quarters.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8220-008","v":"0.1.8220","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Other","x":"Spell damage from loot is capped at +50% all together. None of the new spell damage reaches a fight against another player.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-001","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Nerf","x":"The beast's claws no longer count as silver. Creatures that need a better metal to hurt, such as a Lich or an Ancient Lich, take full damage from claws again, as they did before the last balance update.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-002","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Buff","x":"Your gauntlets now strengthen your claws. In beast form, plate gauntlets add their metal's damage bonus to every claw hit, in every fight, duels and sieges included. It's the same bonus a weapon of that metal gets: Elven +1, Dwarven +2, Mithril and Adamantium +3, Ebony +4, Orcish +5, Daedric +6. Your hit chance doesn't change.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-003","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Other","x":"Leather and chain gauntlets add nothing. So do brigandine gloves, which count as leather, and broken gauntlets. No gauntlets ever make your claws weaker. Put them on before you change, because the beast can't open its pack.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-004","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Werewolf","t":"Fix","x":"Loading a save while in beast form no longer leaves the loaded character treated as a beast until the game is restarted. Before, townspeople wouldn't stop for them, as they don't stop for a beast.","g":["saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-005","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Elites","t":"Rework","x":"Elite enemies no longer appear in the wilds or rise from searched graves until your character reaches Renown 5.","g":["elites","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-006","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"Revenants wait for Renown 10. Below it, no foe becomes a revenant or breaks and runs to become one, and none comes back for you. Any revenants you already have are held: the Revenants page marks each one Held and says when it will come.","g":["revenants","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8234-007","v":"0.1.8234","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Revenants","t":"Buff","x":"Revenants come back a little less often: a revenant that is due now takes 2 in 5 encounter chances instead of 1 in 2.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8241-001","v":"0.1.8241","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Most menus that talk to the server should load much faster: the Guild tab, the market, the notice board's Seat tab, letters, your account card and signing in. The account server had been running on the other side of the world from its database, so each request crossed the Pacific once for every database question it asked. It now runs next to the database.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8241-002","v":"0.1.8241","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Joining the world, the chat's player list and the friends list should come up sooner after you sign in, because each connection waits on the account server for its pass.","g":["online","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8245-001","v":"0.1.8245","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Name in Game","t":"New","x":"Your profile card has a new Name in game choice in its Account section: Account name or Character name. With Character name, other players see the name of the character you are playing: over your head, in chat and in the online list.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8245-002","v":"0.1.8245","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Name in Game","t":"New","x":"The change shows within moments in every room you are in. You don't need to change area or sign in again.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8245-003","v":"0.1.8245","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Name in Game","t":"Other","x":"If your character's name can't be shown online, other players see your account name instead, and the chat tells you why, once. This happens when the name is longer than 24 characters, uses accented letters or symbols, is caught by the name filter, looks like an email address, or is another player's username.","g":["online","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8245-004","v":"0.1.8245","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Name in Game","t":"Fix","x":"A letter sent from your friends list now reaches that friend even when they go by their character's name.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8245-005","v":"0.1.8245","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Name in Game","t":"Fix","x":"Answering a notice-board duel finds its author even when they go by their character's name.","g":["online","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8245-006","v":"0.1.8245","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Chat Window","t":"Rework","x":"Titles no longer appear in chat. Guild tags and glyphs still show after names, and your title still shows over your head and on your Inspect card.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-001","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Rework","x":"Online, a letter of credit can't be put into a chest, a cupboard or a body any more. A shared container is everyone's, so the letter stays in your pack. To give one to another player, hand it over in a trade.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-002","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Other","x":"Your own storage (your house's cupboards, your ship's chest), a pile you dropped yourself and your wagon still take letters. Offline nothing changes.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-003","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Rework","x":"Outside a trade, a letter of credit never reaches you through another player's game. That covers a shared chest, a body they let you loot, and a foe's pack handed to you.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-004","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Removal","x":"A letter of credit that was already lying in a shared chest or on a body when this update arrived is gone from it. Anyone could take it from there before, and the game can't tell it from a forged one.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-005","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Prices","t":"Fix","x":"An item that reaches you through another player's game (a chest, a body, a shelf) can't carry a higher price than an honest item of its kind could.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-006","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Online Death","t":"Fix","x":"The gear a fallen player leaves in the wilds holds only things that can be worn.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8253-007","v":"0.1.8253","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Player Trade","t":"Rework","x":"A purse, a letter of credit or a pile of gold holding more than 2,147,483,647 gold (more than Daggerfall itself can count) is now flagged as tampered. That character can't trade, sell or send gold to other players until the problem is gone or staff clear it.","g":["marks","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8258-001","v":"0.1.8258","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"When a monster attacks you in town, the town guard still comes to help. They used to disappear on the spot about ten seconds after the fight ended, even while you were looking at them. Now they walk off instead. A guard only leaves the world once he is far away or behind you, the same rule that hides townspeople coming and going.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8258-002","v":"0.1.8258","d":"2026-10-12","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"If another monster turns up while the guards are walking off, the same guards turn back to the fight instead of a fresh squad appearing. A guard attacked on his way out defends himself before carrying on. Commit a crime and they come for you, as before.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8270-001","v":"0.1.8270","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"Rework","x":"Your horse now walks by default. Hold Run (Shift unless you rebound it) to gallop, the same way you walk and run on foot.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8270-002","v":"0.1.8270","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"Rework","x":"The gallop is as fast as before and still spends your horse's breath. A winded or starving horse walks even with Run held, until it can gallop again.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8270-003","v":"0.1.8270","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"Rework","x":"In towns your horse walks, because Roleplay & Realism doesn't allow galloping there. To gallop in towns too, turn on its Galloping In Towns option (under Enhanced Riding).","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8270-004","v":"0.1.8270","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"A walking horse looks and sounds like one: a slower clop, a slower nod of its head in first person, and a trot rather than a gallop on the 3D horse. The saddle panel says Walking.","g":["horse","animation","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8270-005","v":"0.1.8270","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"Other","x":"With Horse care turned off in Settings > Features, or on the classic interface, horses ride as they always did.","g":["horse","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-001","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Elite Dungeons","t":"Rework","x":"Walking past a spawned or Elite dungeon no longer starts its despawn timer. The timer (7 in-game days, about 14 real hours online) now starts only when someone enters the dungeon. A dungeon nobody goes into stays where it is.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-002","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Elite Dungeons","t":"New","x":"A dungeon that has despawned now comes back 24 real hours later: the same dungeon in the same spot, with fresh timers. Regions that were emptied out repopulate.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-003","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Elite Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Your character's save no longer keeps despawned dungeons gone forever. Players who walked an area weeks ago now see the same dungeons as everyone else.","g":["saves","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-004","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"Wild Zone halls no longer vanish partway through their day after someone has been inside one.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-005","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quest enemies, like the Fighters Guild's rats, now appear in shops, not only in houses.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-006","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"\"Open a Chest\" and other quests whose shop is in another town now show that town in the quest list, on the travel map and on the compass.","g":["quests","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-007","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Homes","t":"Fix","x":"A home's chests no longer lose their contents when furniture fails to load; anything without a chest or box to go in is set down at your feet.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-008","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Fix","x":"The Gauntlets of the Rose's second hit now lands on the Oblivion Gate's boss.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-009","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Rework","x":"Motherlodes appear on the compass from their warning onward, in their own colour, drawn over nearby veins.","g":["mining","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-010","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Houses","t":"Fix","x":"Windows no longer show the street where your building's own wall stands.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-011","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed Morrowind models (you, NPCs, enemies, horses) turning invisible until restart.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8288-012","v":"0.1.8288","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Keybindings","t":"Fix","x":"Swing Weapon bound to Left Click (with mouse activate unbound) now survives a restart.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8291-001","v":"0.1.8291","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Water Surface","t":"Fix","x":"Inland water banks (ponds, moats, rivers, streams, town canals) no longer show flat blue blotches on the grass beside the water. The shore's painted water now sits under the riverbed, and the strip just past the water's edge reads as dark wet mud.","g":["water","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8291-002","v":"0.1.8291","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Water Surface","t":"Fix","x":"Standing on a bank, you can no longer see under the water's surface. The water's edge now meets the ground instead of floating over a dip.","g":["water","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-001","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Climates & Calories has a fourth setting, Boons, between Off and Casual, and Boons is now the default. If you never picked a setting you play Boons; Off, Hard or Boons, if you chose one, is kept.","g":["survival","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-002","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Boons takes nothing away. Keeping your character fed, watered and rested earns bonuses instead:","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-003","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Well fed: +5 Strength, +5 Endurance","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-004","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Quenched: +5 Agility, +5 Speed","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-005","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Well rested: +5 Intelligence, +5 Willpower. Sleeping in a bed or by a fire banks rest, up to 12 hours, and you spend it while awake.","g":["survival","camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-006","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Thriving (all three at once): +5 Luck","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-007","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"New","x":"Hearth: standing by a lit fire gives stamina back.","g":["survival","camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-008","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"UI","x":"Boons show as green tiles on the status strip. Nothing turns red in Boons except a drink's effect.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-009","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Boons","t":"UI","x":"On the Status page, the hours of rest you have banked are a line of their own (\"Rested for another 12 hours.\"), so the classic status box no longer grows wider for them.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-010","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Resting","t":"UI","x":"Online, the tile that counts down until you can sleep through a night again is called \"Next night\" (it was \"Rested\", easily mistaken for Well rested).","g":["survival","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-011","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Temperature Display","t":"New","x":"A temperature plate sits at the right end of the compass (Enhanced HUD): your felt temperature, its word, and a scale from deadly cold to scorching. It stays on the screen at every HUD scale and on phones, clear of the FPS counter, the enemy health bar, the arena session button and the travel pace box. It can be moved and hidden on its own, and it still shows when the compass is hidden. \"Temperature on the HUD\" in the Climates & Calories settings turns it off.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-012","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Temperature Display","t":"New","x":"The Enhanced inventory shows your felt temperature beside your armour rating. An item's card says what wearing it, or taking it off, would do to your temperature. An unidentified item's comparison no longer counts powers you can't see yet.","g":["climate","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-013","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Temperature Display","t":"New","x":"The Stats side lists everything that makes up your temperature, and the Status page shows the number.","g":["climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-014","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Temperature Display","t":"UI","x":"Red now means the setting you play on charges you for it, and amber means you feel it but it costs nothing. In Hard every need that costs is red; being wet is amber in every setting. Each level is also said in words, not by colour alone.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-015","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Resist Fire no longer makes a blizzard colder, and Resist Frost no longer makes the desert hotter. Underground, resistances now act on the dungeon's own air.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-016","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Swimming on the surface soaks you a little at a time; only going under soaks you at once. A short river swim no longer leaves you drenched for hours.","g":["survival","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-017","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"Rain and snow soak you at the original mod's rates. A cloak keeps snow off, and a hood keeps rain off.","g":["weather","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-018","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"Robes and cloaks keep the sun off your armour. Surcoats and straps no longer do, because they are worn under it.","g":["climate","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-019","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Underground, clothes, metal armour and food follow the dungeon's air, not the weather above it.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-020","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Warm weather now takes effect on your clothing and a hood's shade gradually. A slightly warmer day no longer reads much colder.","g":["weather","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-021","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Indoors, a warmer street no longer reads colder inside.","g":["climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-022","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Having a drink to hand cools you down to 9 degrees at most, instead of dropping you to 0.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-023","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"Cold metal armour chills you a degree less, as in the original mod.","g":["climate","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-024","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"The temperature number and its word always agree. The breakdown's \"Bare skin\" row is now called \"Heat loss\".","g":["climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-025","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"The open sea is no longer as warm as a beach. A winter crossing is cold now.","g":["climate","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-026","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Offline, a long rest or a fast-travel journey feels each hour as it passes, including the minute you arrive. Nights are cold, noons warm, and the sun shines only by day.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-027","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"A long journey no longer keeps the weather you set out in all the way: the road is felt under a fair sky.","g":["weather","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-028","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"UI","x":"In a castle, the Stats breakdown names the row \"Castle walls\" instead of \"Underground\".","g":["climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-029","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Hard: a long fast-travel journey can no longer collapse you from exhaustion over and over on the way, or kill you in the minute you land.","g":["survival","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-030","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"Collapsing from exhaustion now counts as an hour's sleep on the ground.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-031","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"You can no longer save partway through a fast-travel journey (\"You cannot save now.\"); the online checkpoint waits until you arrive.","g":["saves","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-032","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Leaving prison, you start fed, watered and rested, not starving, soaked and exhausted.","g":["survival","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-033","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"A vampire who is cured is no longer instantly starving and exhausted. In beast form, a werewolf neither hungers nor thirsts.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-034","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Stamina no longer stays above its maximum after a boon or a Fortify ends.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-035","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Survival messages no longer repeat when you step in and out of a fire's reach, and loading a game no longer repeats them all.","g":["survival","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-036","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Bare feet are hurt by the weather's own heat or cold, before your clothes count, measured against your current Endurance, so Fortify Endurance helps. They are no longer hurt underground.","g":["climate","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-037","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Campfire","t":"New","x":"Resting at your own burnt-out Campfire relights it if it has fuel. A worn-out tent no longer claims to stoke its fire.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-038","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Tents","t":"Fix","x":"Sleeping in your tent keeps the rain and snow off, and armour no longer rusts while you rest or under a roof.","g":["camping","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-039","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Campfire","t":"Fix","x":"A cold camp no longer offers Cook.","g":["camping","cooking"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-040","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Campfire","t":"Rework","x":"Resting at a brazier or fire bowl needs you within the fire's reach. From further away you are told to move closer, instead of getting a rough night's rest.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-041","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Campfire","t":"Fix","x":"A campfire on a ship's deck no longer counts as a fire while the ship is out of sight.","g":["camping","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-042","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Food that spoils in your pack shows its spoiled name and picture. Putrid food says it cannot be eaten.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-043","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"New characters start with the original mod's Formal cloak, hood up, and Shoes, both well worn.","g":["equipment","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-044","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"An empty waterskin from a shop is called \"Empty Waterskin\".","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-045","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"Tavern menus follow the original mod's regional menus, prices and holiday free drinks.","g":["survival","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-046","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"A meal you order when you are nearly full is served whole and leaves you fed.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-047","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Rework","x":"A soft drink refreshes you (+5 stamina); an alcoholic drink restores stamina and magicka.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-048","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Online, passing out drunk wakes you at the next dawn under the sky everyone shares.","g":["survival","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8328-049","v":"0.1.8328","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Duels","t":"Fix","x":"Your Boons and other buffs count properly in duels, sieges and the Royal Tourney. Before, your own attributes and Luck were counted against you.","g":["arena","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8331-001","v":"0.1.8331","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"When you climb or hang from a ledge in first person (classic view), your hands now stay on the wall. Turn your view and they slide across with the stone; look up and they go down the wall with it. They no longer turn with the screen.","g":["climbing","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8331-002","v":"0.1.8331","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climbing","t":"Rework","x":"The two fists grip further apart, about shoulder width.","g":["climbing","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8331-003","v":"0.1.8331","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Climbing","t":"Fix","x":"When you look away from the wall to find your next jump, the arm that reaches out is now the one on the side you look: your right arm from the right when you look right, your left arm from the left when you look left. Only that arm stays fixed to the screen. Its hand lets go of the wall, and the other hand keeps its hold.","g":["climbing","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8331-004","v":"0.1.8331","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"With the Morrowind model in first person, your arms now grip the wall while you climb even with your weapon sheathed. Before this, the screen showed nothing unless a weapon was drawn.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8331-005","v":"0.1.8331","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Weapon Widget","t":"Fix","x":"Weapon Widget's bob and sway no longer push the Morrowind hands off the stone while they climb.","g":["climbing","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8334-001","v":"0.1.8334","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"Rework","x":"Your horse no longer has to walk in towns. It still walks by default, and holding Run gallops it anywhere, in town or out, as long as it has the breath. This applies online too.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8334-002","v":"0.1.8334","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Horse","t":"New","x":"Watch where you gallop in town: riding into someone at a gallop tramples them. That's a crime, and the guards will come.","g":["horse","law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8396-001","v":"0.1.8396","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Front Door","t":"Fix","x":"On a handheld held sideways, like the ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X, the front door's logo no longer fills the screen. The menu now keeps its two columns: the sections down the side and the open page using the full height. Settings, Load, Online and the rest can be read and used again. A narrowed browser window on a desktop gets the same layout.","g":["touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8396-002","v":"0.1.8396","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Language","t":"New","x":"Settings > Interface > Language now offers 13 languages besides English: Bulgarian, Czech, Danish, French, German, Indonesian, Italian, Korean, Norwegian, Portuguese (Brazil), Romanian, Russian and Spanish. The choice applies at once and is remembered. If your browser reads one of them first, the game offers it to you once, in that language.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8396-003","v":"0.1.8396","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Language","t":"New","x":"These translations cover the game's own menus and screens: the front door and Settings, the pause window, the death screens, the account and online messages, the Professions and Stores pages and every crafting station, the Features screen and every mod's settings. They are machine translated, and the game says so. A fix from a speaker is welcome. More languages are on the way.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8396-004","v":"0.1.8396","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Translation Packs","t":"New","x":"Under the Language row, Translation pack installs a Daggerfall Unity translation (a folder or its .zip) from your own files. Nothing is uploaded. A pack translates Daggerfall's own text too: dialogue, quests, books, and the names of places, enemies, items and spells. It also works for a language not in the list yet. The French pack's grammar works.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8396-005","v":"0.1.8396","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Language","t":"Fix","x":"The classic windows now draw any script: Cyrillic, Greek, Vietnamese, Chinese, Japanese and Korean. Before, anything past plain English letters came out as question marks.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8396-006","v":"0.1.8396","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Language","t":"New","x":"The About pane credits each language's translation.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8404-001","v":"0.1.8404","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"Fix","x":"Players, NPCs and horses no longer turn invisible online with Morrowind models. If one Morrowind body in view got a bad position (for example from another player's glitched position update), every Morrowind body drawn after it vanished and your own could show the wrong picture, until that player left or you restarted. Now only that one body is affected: it stays at its last good position, and everyone else keeps drawing.","g":["morrowind","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8404-002","v":"0.1.8404","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Crime","t":"Fix","x":"Pleading guilty no longer loops. The first time you went to court, the Crime tutorial page opened on top of the plea. Clicking Guilty or Not Guilty while the page was showing answered the plea underneath it, and the plea box then kept coming back: every click pleaded again, took the fine again and halved the sentence again. Now the plea waits until you've read the page. Click anywhere or press any key to close the page, then plead once.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-001","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"You can now rise into the Overworld while sailing the Eltheric Ocean, as you can in the Iliac Bay. Open your chart (the map key) and press Overworld (O), or press O while the chart is open.","g":["overworld","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-002","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"From the Overworld, click the sea to sail there at the helm, or click a port or ruin you have charted to travel to it. Charted ports further off are shown at the edge of the screen with their distance. Ruins appear as they do in the Bay: a \"?\" until you have charted or found them.","g":["overworld","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-003","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"An island you chart (by sight, a harbourmaster's chart or a corsair's papers) shows on the Overworld at once, without moving first.","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-004","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Fix","x":"A fast journey past the Veil now slows while the land ahead is still loading, so you no longer outrun the world.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-005","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Enemy bands now roam the Eltheric isles, and with Naval Combat on, pirate raiders sail its open sea. The Overworld shows both as it does in the Bay. They chase you the same way, and your journey slows as they close in.","g":["overworld","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-006","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"A raider past the Veil comes as one of the Eltheric's own corsairs, a ship you fight at sea: the sea's names, the black flag, and a hold as rich as the waters she sails. For a newer captain, the deeper the water, the bigger the ship she may be.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-007","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Online, other players now see a band or raider chasing you past the Veil.","g":["online","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-008","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Rework","x":"The sea past the Veil is now called the Eltheric Ocean, its proper name. It used to be called the \"Etheric Sea\". The chart, the harbourmasters, the crossing, your captain's log and the legends now all use the new name.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-009","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Rework","x":"The water past the Veil used to be only a stride deep, with the seabed just under the surface. It now has a real seabed: shallow by each island's shore, then dropping to the open ocean floor about two hundred metres down, as deep as the Iliac Bay's open sea.","g":["water","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-010","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"You can swim, dive and surface there as you do in the Bay. The seafloor's plants, fish, creatures and sunken loot now appear past the Veil too.","g":["water","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-011","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Other","x":"The ocean holes (the pits down into drowned dungeons) still appear only in the Iliac Bay.","g":["water","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-012","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Fix","x":"Herbs, trees, ore veins and boulders on the islands past the Veil can now be gathered. They used to stand there but answered \"There is nothing here to gather\". Fishing in the Eltheric Ocean now works too.","g":["foraging","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-013","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Other","x":"Gathering there works as it does in the Bay: each spot gives its full finds only once three players (with accounts at least a week old) have gathered there.","g":["foraging","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-014","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Other","x":"Motherlodes still rise only in the Iliac Bay, where the Watch can see you strike them.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-015","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"The chart's names are now in the game's own enhanced font. They used to be drawn in a fallback serif.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-016","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"Names are drawn after every island marker, with a dark outline, so a marker can no longer cover a name.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-017","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"Each name sits on whichever side of its island is clear. Names and haunt labels no longer stand over each other, and your ship's label takes the clearest spot.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-018","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"New","x":"A depth ruler runs along the top of the chart. It names each stretch of water in view that has room for its name: the Shallows, the Reaches, the Deep Aether, the Abyss, the Veil and the world's edge.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-019","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"The scale bar now sits in the key below the chart, so it no longer hides islands.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-020","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"Other","x":"The chart's words follow the language you chose, in each fully translated language. The sea's own names (the Eltheric Ocean, its depths, its island types and compass directions) are still in English for now.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-021","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"Each island type has its own shape as well as its own colour:","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-022","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"a port is round with a harbour dot","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-023","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"a ruin is a diamond","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-024","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"a wild isle is a peak","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-025","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"a bare rock is a cross","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-026","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"Zoom in and larger islands show their real size around the icon. Veilhaven is ringed in gold.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-027","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"New","x":"A key under the chart explains every icon.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-028","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"Each depth band is its own shade of water, lightest by the Veil and darkest in the Abyss. A league grid replaces the old background stars, which didn't move when you dragged the map. The edge of the world is marked.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-029","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"A legend's haunt is a red-washed square while she sails, and hatched grey while she lies sunk. When enough of the square is in view, her name and status (\"Her haunt\", \"Sunk - she will rise again\") sit in a corner of it, chosen to hide as few islands as possible. When you're zoomed far out, her name alone stands above the square.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-030","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"UI","x":"Your ship is a white arrow in a brass ring, marked on the ruler too. When she's off-screen, an arrow at the chart's edge points to her and says how far away she is.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-031","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"New","x":"Point at or tap an island to ring it, draw a bearing line to it from your ship, and show a card with its name, type and distance.","g":["map","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-032","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"Fix","x":"The chart now fits the screen at any size. On a phone held sideways, the key, the zoom buttons and Ship are no longer pushed off the bottom. On a phone held upright, the chart's title wraps instead of being cut off.","g":["map","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-033","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"Fix","x":"Naming an island no longer makes the chart jump.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-034","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"Fix","x":"The chart no longer gets stuck in a fallback font if it opens before the game's fonts finish loading.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-035","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Sea Chart","t":"Fix","x":"On phones the Close and zoom buttons keep their size, and the zoom buttons grey out at the closest and farthest zoom.","g":["map","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8424-036","v":"0.1.8424","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"Fix","x":"Your Ship can no longer be boarded from past the Veil. Boarding it there carried you to the Iliac Bay without the crossing. Leaving it still takes you back to where you boarded.","g":["naval","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-001","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Decorator","t":"UI","x":"The furniture catalogue, the pieces in your room, the built-in pieces and your own things are now laid out as picture tiles. Each tile shows the piece's own 3D model, its name and price, plus badges for what it does (holds things, gives light, crafting station). A Pictures / List switch brings the old lines back.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-002","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Decorator","t":"UI","x":"Every tab, type, size and filter has its own icon. Filters sit under named rows (Sort, Type, Size, Show only), and on phones they fold behind one Filters button that shows how many are set.","g":["homes","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-003","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Decorator","t":"UI","x":"A placed piece's buttons are grouped by what they do (Arrange, Light and storage, Crafting station). Remove stands alone, marked as the costly one.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-004","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Decorator","t":"UI","x":"The placing bar is now icon buttons, with a Keys button that shows the controls only when you ask. On a portrait phone the bar spans the full screen width.","g":["homes","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-005","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Shops","t":"UI","x":"Every shelf item shows its price before you click it. A List / Pictures switch shows both sides as item tiles.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-006","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Shops","t":"UI","x":"Your side is labelled \"Your pack\". The footer shows \"To pay\" (or \"You get\") and \"Your gold\" as separate figures. A magic-only counter is titled \"Sell magic items\", and Steal sits apart from the other buttons.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-007","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Stores","t":"UI","x":"The Stores page opens with a row of station tiles marked Here or Away. A station you are away from stays folded until you tap its tile. Smelting, other workings and patterns appear as cards instead of long lines.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-008","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Stores","t":"UI","x":"Materials and items on the Stores page, the Notice Board's Market and Vendors, and the Vendor page show the game's own item pictures.","g":["market","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-009","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Shops","t":"QoL","x":"A button you can't use yet now explains why when you press it, instead of sitting greyed out with no reason.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-010","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Shipyards","t":"UI","x":"Shipmaster cards show each ship's own 3D picture. The Reforge, shipyard and naval-yard pages and a merchant's options each have their own icon.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-011","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Decorator","t":"Fix","x":"Panel previews (bank, decorator) no longer show the world behind their background.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-012","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Decorator","t":"Fix","x":"On landscape phones, the decorator's catalogue is no longer squeezed to a sliver.","g":["homes","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8438-013","v":"0.1.8438","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Shops","t":"Fix","x":"The shop header no longer squashes the shop's name on a phone.","g":["market","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8445-001","v":"0.1.8445","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Weather","t":"Rework","x":"It rains about half as often. A woodland spring used to be wet a third of the time; now it's about one hour in six. The hours it no longer rains are that region's usual dry weather: sun, cloud, the grey deck and fog.","g":["weather","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8445-002","v":"0.1.8445","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Weather","t":"Rework","x":"Rain now comes in every strength. Each rain front has its own: about a third are a light sprinkle from edge to middle, most are a steady shower, and only about a quarter build to a downpour at their heart. Walking into a front still starts light at its edge.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8445-003","v":"0.1.8445","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Weather","t":"Rework","x":"Thunderstorms are still downpours, but they come half as often.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8449-001","v":"0.1.8449","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Quest Journal","t":"New","x":"The journal (the L key) now has an Abandon button on every quest except the main story's. Click it twice to set the quest aside. The quest keeps everything it had and stops running until you take it back up. Reclaim it from the pause menu's Quests tab, where it waits under Abandoned.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8449-002","v":"0.1.8449","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Quest Journal","t":"Other","x":"The main story's quests show no Abandon in the journal. Bounties and revenant hunts keep their own Abandon, as before.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-001","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Buff","x":"Surface veins now show on your compass from 500 m (was 200). Dungeon veins stay at 200 m.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-002","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Rework","x":"On the Overworld, each nearby vein is marked on its own and named by its ore (\"Silver Vein\"), instead of one \"Mining ×N\" group.","g":["mining","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-003","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Other","x":"Gems still come a tenth more often.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-004","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Buff","x":"Dungeon veins yield double (was +50%).","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-005","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Buff","x":"Every vein in the dungeon shows on your compass, wherever you stand in it.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-006","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Buff","x":"The day's Motherlodes are marked on your map and the Overworld from the start of the day. Each mark shows its ore and, until it rises, when it rises (\"Tue 13:00\", on your own clock).","g":["mining","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-007","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Motherlodes","t":"Other","x":"Warnings still come 30 minutes ahead.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-008","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Rework","x":"Your own word vouches for unwitnessed ground, so your surface veins there can be any of that land's ores. A region's own ore (Mithril, Orichalcum and the rest) still needs witnesses.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-009","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Other","x":"Quarrying still yields Cut Stone directly. If you chose Stonebreaker, you are now a Surveyor.","g":["mining","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8455-010","v":"0.1.8455","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Fix","x":"Dungeon veins no longer sink halfway into the wall. They sit on the floor at the wall's foot.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8457-001","v":"0.1.8457","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Harbourmaster","t":"Fix","x":"The harbourmaster's cargo contracts now send you only to port towns on the sea. They used to name tombs, farms, inns, temples, manors and ruins (most cargoes went to one), and region capitals far inland where no ship can reach.","g":["naval","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8457-002","v":"0.1.8457","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Harbourmaster","t":"Fix","x":"A harbourmaster's board now stands only in a port town, never at a tomb's or a farm's shore.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8457-003","v":"0.1.8457","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Harbourmaster","t":"Fix","x":"A cargo you already hold for such a place is cancelled with a notice (\"Contract void - ... No ship can make port there.\"), and your standing with the crown is unchanged.","g":["naval","bounty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-001","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Felling a tree: the axe's swing and its bite into the trunk (a Clean Cut rings fuller), the tree groaning when it starts to give, its crash as it lands, and the logs gathered up.","g":["logging","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-002","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Mining: the pick striking rock, the ring of a strike on the glint, and rubble as a vein or boulder gives out.","g":["mining","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-003","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Herbs and the Basket: leaves rustling as you kneel, the herb pulling free (or bruising), and the Basket's find.","g":["herbalism","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-004","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Skinning: the knife's strokes climbing along the line, a tear when it slips, and the pelt peeling free.","g":["hunting","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-005","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Net fishing: the throw, the splash where the net lands, the water by the floats while you wait, the tug, the catch fighting as you haul, and the net coming in.","g":["fishing","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-006","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Your goods going into the bag, a clean finish's chime, and a chime for a new rank.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-007","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Fix","x":"An axe or pick blow now sounds the moment the tool hits, not when you press the button. Its sound, its weight and its chunks all land together, at any frame rate.","g":["audio","logging"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-008","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Rework","x":"Each sound comes from where it happens: the tree, the vein, or where your net landed.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-009","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Rework","x":"The tool stays in your hand through your last swing, and the tree starts to fall (or the vein crumbles) as that last blow lands, instead of the moment you press. Starting on the next tree or vein straight away doesn't cut that last blow short.","g":["logging","mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-010","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"On the Enhanced skin, each axe or pick blow dips your view and your hands slightly as it lands, a little deeper for a Clean Cut or a strike on the glint, and always lighter than a weapon technique's hit.","g":["combat-visuals","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-011","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Other","x":"It follows Technique camera motion (Settings > Accessibility > Motion), so you can turn it down or off there. It never plays when your system asks for reduced motion.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-012","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"New","x":"A vein or a Motherlode cracks as you work it, and so does a boulder's loose stone: the cracks spread out from its middle with each blow until it breaks.","g":["mining","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-013","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"New","x":"Every blow knocks chunks of ore loose toward you. They land on the ground where they fall, slopes included, lie there a moment and sink away. The blow that breaks the vein sheds the most.","g":["mining","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-014","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mining","t":"Other","x":"If you stop before it breaks, the cracks close up again. Like the vein itself, the cracks are yours alone.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-015","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"Other players now see you at work. Every body type shows your tool swinging. Class sprites also show you kneeling and throwing your net, Eye Of The Beholder sprites show the throw, and Morrowind bodies crouch where you kneel.","g":["online","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-016","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"New","x":"They hear it too, from where you are working: each chop and strike as it lands, the herb pulled, the knife, the net thrown and landing, the water while it waits, the tug and the haul. A blow you take back with Escape isn't heard.","g":["online","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-017","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Other","x":"The still paperdoll (shown while a sprite loads, or with other players' class sprites turned off) doesn't show it, but you still hear it.","g":["online","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-018","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Rework","x":"The Attack sounds switch for other players now covers their gathering sounds too.","g":["online","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-019","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Other","x":"The new sounds are part of Enhanced sounds on the Features screen. With it off, or on the Classic skin, gathering plays Daggerfall's own sounds as before, now timed to the blows.","g":["audio","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8469-020","v":"0.1.8469","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Gathering","t":"Fix","x":"The veins, boulders, herbs and trees around you no longer blink out for a frame when you finish gathering one of them or when the day turns.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-001","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Tavern Cards","t":"UI","x":"The Hold'em and Iliac Hand panels at tavern tables now use the Enhanced Plus stone-and-brass look and the game's pixel font, matching every other window. The classic skin gets the same look for these panels.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-002","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"UI","x":"Under the DFO Grimoire dress, every mark on the card tables shows in the dress's own colours: your seat, whose turn it is, the winner, who holds each holding, the power that is ahead, and the holding you are aiming at.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-003","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"Iliac Hand's panel gets the fold button Hold'em's already had, which tucks the table's words away so you can watch the cards on the cloth. Both folds now say what they do: \"Collapse the panel\" and \"Expand the panel\".","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-004","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"Fix","x":"Both panels fit on any phone screen, upright or sideways, and scroll inside it when the table is full.","g":["social","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-005","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"UI","x":"The turn is a track of six marks, and your magicka is a row of gems; the magicka your staged plays will spend shows dimmed.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-006","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"UI","x":"Your opponent's hand shows as card backs beside their deck count, with a mark once they have committed their turn.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-007","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"UI","x":"Each holding sits under its own painted location card: their cards above, yours below, empty places for the room left on each side, and each side's power next to its name, with the side that is ahead lit. Cards never cover one another, even on a phone.","g":["social","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-008","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"UI","x":"Your hand sits in a tray, painted as the cards themselves, with the card you have picked raised in brass. A card you play face down shows veiled.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-009","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"Fix","x":"Online, the board appears once the game is dealt.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-010","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"UI","x":"A game ends with a banner (\"Victory\", \"Defeat\", \"A draw\" or \"No contest\"); if you are watching, the log line says how it ended. The log keeps one line for each thing that happens, the newest always in view.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-011","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"Fix","x":"When you play by keyboard, the focus stays on the panel, so Space never makes your character jump up from the table in the middle of a game.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-012","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"UI","x":"The Cards page's switch, filters, deck list and deck name use the same look.","g":["holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-013","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"A chosen, hovered or keyboard-selected tile is marked again on every page that uses tiles. Buttons that cost you something (Concede, Scuttle, Steal and the like) now change when you hover them or reach them with the keyboard.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8478-014","v":"0.1.8478","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Language","t":"New","x":"The new table's words, and Hold'em's fold, are translated into all 13 complete languages. The magicka label uses Daggerfall Unity's own text, like the vitals bar, so it follows an installed Daggerfall Unity language pack.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8487-001","v":"0.1.8487","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"The remains of your house's fallen now appear where they fell: a body you can see, with a line of light over it, in dungeons and out in the open. Press it like any body to take back their bones, their heirloom and their share of the purse. Before this, nothing was drawn at all, and underground the remains only opened if you happened to stand within a few paces of the exact spot.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8487-002","v":"0.1.8487","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"The remains appear only in the dungeon your relative actually fell in. Spawned ruins, wilderness halls and the Arena's undercroft no longer show another dungeon's remains. A dungeon laid out at a different size (Smaller Dungeons) shows them only at the size it had when they fell.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8487-003","v":"0.1.8487","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Remains no longer stay shut because of an enemy back in the street. Whether you are \"in a fight\" is now judged where you actually are (the dungeon or building you're in), not by monsters you left outside. A duel, your own arena bout, or a hostile ship within reach now counts as a fight too. All of this also applies to Play as, Pass the mantle and weddings.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8487-004","v":"0.1.8487","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Fix","x":"Putting the bones back into the remains no longer leaves the death quest stuck. They lie there again, still yours to carry.","g":["death-penalty","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8487-005","v":"0.1.8487","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Performance","x":"Fixed a brief stutter when walking into a new area with Project Legacy on.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8490-001","v":"0.1.8490","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Homes","t":"Performance","x":"When the servers are under heavy load, your game now waits longer between tries to load a town's homes, instead of asking again every 10 seconds. That helps the servers recover sooner.","g":["online","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8490-002","v":"0.1.8490","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Homes","t":"Performance","x":"Loading a town's homes now costs the servers half as many database requests.","g":["online","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8494-001","v":"0.1.8494","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"When the servers are overloaded, your game now holds off on loading homes, yards, seats, traders, guild invitations, Marks and your save list, and asks again a little later, waiting longer the longer the overload lasts. Your actions (buying, crafting, saving, claiming) still go through as before.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8494-002","v":"0.1.8494","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"The servers also turn those requests away for a moment when they're overloaded, so they recover faster even before you update.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-001","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Door Griefing","t":"Fix","x":"A door another player locked with a Lock spell is no longer locked for you. Shop and inn doors in Daggerfall that trapped players inside (Lock Level 40+) open again, including copies your save had already kept.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-002","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Houses","t":"Fix","x":"A door's label now names the building that door opens. The Issaqumbaa tavern is no longer labelled \"Residence\" or offered for sale.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-003","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Houses","t":"Fix","x":"Houses built on grassy hills (for example at some Temples of Kynareth) no longer float over the slope. The hill now reaches under the whole house.","g":["terrain","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-004","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"When a party member's progress on a shared quest reveals a place on their map, it now appears on yours too. If your copy already says \"Not on your map yet\", use Settings > Repair active quests.","g":["quests","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-005","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"The Lost Child: answering \"No\" by mistake no longer locks the quest. Click the child again and you are asked again, including on a save already stuck after a \"No\".","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-006","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Fatigue","t":"Fix","x":"Running out of fatigue with enemies nearby no longer kills you outright at full health. Each time you hit empty you lose a tenth of your health and see \"You are too exhausted to fight - get clear and rest!\".","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-007","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Mace of Molag Bal","t":"Fix","x":"The Mace of Molag Bal works. Draining a foe's strength now raises yours past 100, as described. Spell points it drains count once even on two quick hits, and the bonus ends when you take the Mace off.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-008","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Crafting","t":"Rework","x":"Crafted Superior and Masterwork pieces can now roll the special lines loot can: focus, cast speed, potency and wellspring on jewelry, and the weapon and armour equivalents. Pieces crafted before stay as they were.","g":["crafting","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-009","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Court Writs","t":"Fix","x":"A writ's card now tells you how many of the material you hold that it can't take, and why: only gathered or silver-bought materials fill writs. Before, it said \"0 held\" with no reason.","g":["professions","notice-board"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8512-010","v":"0.1.8512","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Performance","x":"The Oblivion Gate boss's own mark and his host's paths no longer shade large areas of empty ground. The ground markings in a boss AoE frame cost about a quarter less to draw.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-001","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"New","x":"Master two schools of magic and you can choose a specialisation: fifteen of them, one for every pair of schools. The choice is permanent, like a mastery.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-002","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"New","x":"Each specialisation has its own passive and a signature spell. The Mages Guild sells that spell only to its own specialists, and it does something extra when they cast it.","g":["professions","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-003","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"New","x":"You are asked once, the first time two of your schools are mastered. If more than one specialisation is open to you, you are told which, and you choose on your skill screen. After that, choose any time from your skill screen: the Specialisation card on the Master Skills page (enhanced), or the S row on the skill pages (classic).","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-004","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"New","x":"Battlemage (Alteration + Destruction): Spellsteel, Aegis Bolt. Trickster (Alteration + Illusion): Slip Away, Fleeting Hold. Riftwalker (Alteration + Mysticism): Between Moments, Rift Lance. Warden (Alteration + Restoration): Steadfast, Living Aegis. Wardwright (Alteration + Thaumaturgy): Attuned Wards, Prismatic Ward. Shadowcaster (Destruction + Illusion): Unseen Strike, Shadow Bolt. Spellbreaker (Destruction + Mysticism): Sunder, Unravel. Bloodmage (Destruction + Restoration): Sanguine Tide, Blood Boil. Elementalist (Destruction + Thaumaturgy): Conflux, Chain Lightning. Seer (Illusion + Mysticism): Foresight, Psychic Lance. Lightbringer (Illusion + Restoration): Dawn's Ward, Dawnbolt. Enchanter (Illusion + Thaumaturgy): Glamour, Beguile. Necromancer (Mysticism + Restoration): Death's Due, Siphon Life. Soulbinder (Mysticism + Thaumaturgy): Soul Well, Soul Lance. Hierophant (Restoration + Thaumaturgy): Absolution, Sanctify.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-005","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"New","x":"A signature spell is priced and trained by your specialisation's two schools, so a Necromancer's Siphon Life costs what their Restoration says, not their Destruction. That stays true while you mentor a lower party.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-006","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"Other","x":"Chain Lightning and Rift Lance never arc onto your allies, onto foes you have calmed, or through walls.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-007","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"New","x":"Signature spells show their names in your language.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-008","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Arcane Specialisations","t":"Other","x":"Specialisations work wherever Master Skills is on. They do nothing in duels and other refereed fights, and nothing against other players.","g":["professions","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-009","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Online, every mastered school past 100 now strengthens its own spells, not just their price. The bonus is 1% per effective point, up to +40% at 200, the same rule as Destruction's damage.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-010","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Restoration: your heals heal more.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-011","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Alteration: your Shield holds more.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-012","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Illusion: your invisibility, chameleon and shadow last longer.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-013","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Thaumaturgy: your Spell Reflection and Spell Resistance hold more often.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8519-014","v":"0.1.8519","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Mysticism: your Silence, Dispel and Soul Trap take hold more often.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8521-001","v":"0.1.8521","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"The account server has been overloaded since this afternoon, so town seats, homes, the market and other online menus have been slow to load or failing. The heaviest read, the town seats list, no longer runs on the main database, which should bring them back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8523-001","v":"0.1.8523","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Town homes, home rooms and decorations, gathering nodes, traders, Marks, guild invites, lineages, unions, cloud saves and the Arena board now load from read copies of the account database, not the one main database everyone was queued on. Menus should stop timing out and load much faster.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8525-001","v":"0.1.8525","d":"2026-10-13","e":"Seats","t":"Performance","x":"Town seats are now worked out once a minute for the whole server, not by every server process on every request. The seats list, Watch claims, Levies, Tithes and sieges load faster and put far less strain on the database.","g":["seats","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-001","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Restart a quest. A stuck quest can now be restarted from its first step: press Restart twice in the pause window's Quests tab or in the chronicle (main-story steps included). The quest picks fresh places, and its old items, links and topics are cleared.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-002","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A party member's kill no longer steals yours. Killing your own copy of a main-story foe (like the Dust of Restful Death's mummy) is no longer counted because a party member killed theirs.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-003","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quest markers in small and medium buildings sit inside the building, and quest foes no longer stand on top of a hall's ceiling.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-004","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"When a quest's foe falls you are told (HUD, chat and the classic line), and a quest box ignores presses for a moment so it isn't clicked away by accident.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-005","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"An abandoned quest's item can be dropped from your pack, and it is handed back if you reclaim the quest.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-006","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Chat Window","t":"Fix","x":"The chat roster search now finds every known player, not just the first page.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-007","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Clicking in the world no longer stutters.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-008","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"A found dungeon shows as a dungeon on the Overworld grid.","g":["overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-009","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Compass","t":"Fix","x":"Compass marks draw over the Grimoire frame.","g":["map","mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8529-010","v":"0.1.8529","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Text Font","t":"UI","x":"The installed-font picker is a scrolling, filterable list.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8532-001","v":"0.1.8532","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Account Recovery","t":"New","x":"Eight recovery codes instead of one. New accounts get a set of 8 recovery codes. Each code works once, if you forget your password.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8532-002","v":"0.1.8532","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Account Recovery","t":"New","x":"See your codes in your profile. The Account section shows how many recovery codes you have left. Make new codes gives you a fresh set: type your password and one of your current codes. Your old codes stop working.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8532-003","v":"0.1.8532","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Account Recovery","t":"New","x":"Copy or save them. When codes are shown you can Copy them or Save as a file (dfo-recovery-codes-<username>.txt).","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8532-004","v":"0.1.8532","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Account Recovery","t":"Rework","x":"Never left with none. Using a code spends only that code. Using your last one gives you a fresh 8.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8532-005","v":"0.1.8532","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Account Recovery","t":"Rework","x":"Safer: someone who learns your password alone can't replace your codes, so your codes can always take your account back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8532-006","v":"0.1.8532","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Account Recovery","t":"Rework","x":"The codes screen can't be closed by accident (no Close, Escape or tap outside) until you confirm you've written them down.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8538-001","v":"0.1.8538","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Joinery","t":"Fix","x":"Carpentry crash. Using a Joinery's workbench, or opening Esc → Stores afterwards, no longer crashes the game.","g":["carpentry"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8538-002","v":"0.1.8538","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Resting","t":"Fix","x":"Inn beds. Beds in dormitory-style inn rooms (and ship bunks) offer Rest and Loiter again.","g":["camping"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8538-003","v":"0.1.8538","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Crew Spirits","t":"Fix","x":"Crew morale at the shipwright. Once the crew has had the day's grog, the shipwright now shows their real spirits (e.g. \"low\") and says \"Tomorrow\". It no longer claims spirits are \"as high as they go\".","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8538-004","v":"0.1.8538","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Magic Repair","t":"Fix","x":"Repairs Objects. The enchantment repairs your gear again when you wear a Cast When Held or Item Deteriorates piece. That piece used to take every repair and undo it in the same moment; it is now repaired last.","g":["enchanting","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8538-005","v":"0.1.8538","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Town Watch","t":"Rework","x":"Paying the watch's fine now mends your name. Paying on the spot raises your standing in that region by 5, up to the point where the watch stops recognising you. Before, a paid fine only bought a day without stops, so the watch kept charging the same fine.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8538-006","v":"0.1.8538","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"UI","x":"Life leech says whose blows it heals on. The line now reads \"N% life leech on this weapon's own blows\". An off-hand weapon's leech applies only when you fight with that hand (switch with H).","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8540-001","v":"0.1.8540","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Online Death","t":"Fix","x":"REVIVE: a death taken back holds, and the operator's Realm revive run","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8548-001","v":"0.1.8548","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"Stutter in cities. Arriving in a large city, or walking out of a building in one, no longer freezes the game for several seconds. It was worst in Firefox. Thanks to ghandhikus for finding and fixing it.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8552-001","v":"0.1.8552","d":"2026-10-14","e":"Horse","t":"Performance","x":"The first seconds after entering the world stutter less. The horses' coats on the road's wagons are painted in under half the time, so the frame rate settles sooner. Every coat looks exactly as before. Thanks to joaomdb3.","g":["horse","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-001","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"With Morrowind attached, Breton men now wear three new heads and three new hairs - nine faces between them - on townspeople, NPCs and a Breton player alike.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-002","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Each of the ten Breton portraits at character creation shows the face most like it; portrait 6 wears the eyepatch.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-003","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"If the new heads fail to load, Breton men show Morrowind's own Breton faces instead of appearing without a head.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-004","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Eleven of Daggerfall's townspeople now wear their own 3D outfits on the Morrowind body, in their picture's colours: all four Redguard men, all four Nord men, two Breton men and the hooded Redguard woman. Up close, a walker wears what their picture shows from afar.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-005","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Hoods sit over the hair, and sleeves, hems and boots move with the body.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-006","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"Legs stay inside skirts, robes, kilts and the hooded dress as townspeople walk, and tunics no longer pinch in at the sides when they stand.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-007","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"If an outfit fails to load, the person is drawn without it and with no missing body parts; a woman wears her modest shirt while Show Nudity is off.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-008","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Other","x":"Townspeople without an outfit yet (two of the Breton men's pictures, and every woman's but the hooded Redguard's) keep their varied wardrobe.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-009","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"The cape on the Morrowind body now hangs from the chest alone and moves only with it, as one stiff sheet. Walking, swinging your arms and sitting no longer bend it.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-010","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"Leaning back swings the whole cape with the chest.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-011","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Terrain","t":"Rework","x":"The Dragontail and Wrothgarian Mountains are taller and sharper: pointed peaks up to 400 m over the ridges, where they were 200 m and rounded, on ridges 40% taller.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-012","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Terrain","t":"Other","x":"The mountain woods around them keep their rounded hills.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-013","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Billboard Look","t":"New","x":"New setting: Billboard Look (Settings > Combat > With Morrowind data, off by default). On, Morrowind bodies and horses stand upright like the classic sprites, so they look shorter when the camera is above them, as they did before they started leaning toward the camera. Off, they keep their true height from every angle.","g":["morrowind","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8569-014","v":"0.1.8569","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Online Mode","t":"Performance","x":"Loading an online character into the world takes about 3 seconds less. The game now asks the server for your family, your character list, the towns' homes and the homes of the towns you arrive in all at once, while it reads the world, instead of waiting on each in turn. Thanks to joaomdb3.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8573-001","v":"0.1.8573","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Textures","t":"Rework","x":"Ships, wagons and town buildings now use Daggerfall's own textures. This covers the galleon, the carrack and the large boat; the Wagon Cart, the Open Wagon, the Caravan and the caravan's room; the Stable, the Wagon Yard and the Joinery; the shipyard and the lighthouse; the stone of the Julian LeFay monument; and the tapestries, banners and rugs in towns. Each texture is read from your own Daggerfall files. The ships wear the same textures as Come Sail Away's ships.","g":["rendering","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8573-002","v":"0.1.8573","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Wagon","t":"Rework","x":"Wagon paints are now Daggerfall's colours, fabrics, woods, rugs, tiles and night sky. Every paint still applies.","g":["horse","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8573-003","v":"0.1.8573","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Textures","t":"Rework","x":"Windows are see-through. The caravan's windows and the stern windows of the galleon and the carrack are Daggerfall's leaded window, and you can see through the glass between the leads. The ships' stern windows no longer glow at night.","g":["rendering","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8573-004","v":"0.1.8573","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Textures","t":"Rework","x":"Signboards. STABLES, WAGONS, JOINERY, SHIPS and CREW are lettered on Daggerfall planks. The Joinery's sign also carries Daggerfall's axe-and-sword shop sign.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8573-005","v":"0.1.8573","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Lighthouses","t":"Rework","x":"The lighthouse beacon now burns with Daggerfall's own brazier fire.","g":["lighting","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8575-001","v":"0.1.8575","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"The ships' stern windows glow at night again. By day you can still see through the galleon's stern windows into her great cabin, and through the carrack's transom windows. When the lanterns are lit, the glass closes and glows warm, as it did before. The caravan's windows stay see-through day and night.","g":["naval","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8583-001","v":"0.1.8583","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Channels","t":"New","x":"Trade — buy, sell and swap with players anywhere. /trade (or /tr) says a line there.","g":["chat","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8583-002","v":"0.1.8583","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Channels","t":"New","x":"LFG — find a group, or one more for yours. /lfg says a line there.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8583-003","v":"0.1.8583","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Channels","t":"New","x":"Both are opt-in, so your tab bar stays as it was until you want them. Press the new + beside the chat tabs to pick channels: one click joins or leaves, and joined channels show a checkmark.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8583-004","v":"0.1.8583","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Channels","t":"New","x":"You can also use /join trade, /join lfg, /leave trade and /leave lfg, or the switches in Settings > Other players > Chat. Saying /trade … or /lfg … before joining joins the channel for you.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8583-005","v":"0.1.8583","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Window","t":"New","x":"/rp <text> says a line of roleplay on the tab you're on, in green italics: /rp draws her blade shows as *\\*draws her blade\\.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8583-006","v":"0.1.8583","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Window","t":"UI","x":"/help now lists /trade, /lfg, /join, /leave and /rp.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8591-001","v":"0.1.8591","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Sitting","t":"New","x":"Sit on chairs. Use a chair, bench or throne inside a building to sit on it. Your character sits in the same pose as at the card tables, other players see you seated, and third person shows you on the chair. Move, jump, attack, press Escape or use it again to stand up.","g":["seats","third-person","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8591-002","v":"0.1.8591","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Lamp Keeper","t":"New","x":"The lamp keeper. Every so often a shopkeeper is... a lamp. Talk to it for its own lines, trade with it as usual, and earn the title I Love Lamp (online, signed in to a registered account).","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8591-003","v":"0.1.8591","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Title and aura popups. A title or aura you earn now gets a loot popup (Enhanced Plus), including the Abyss Dungeon's Hourbreaker and The Turning Hour. It shows only the first time you earn each one.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8591-004","v":"0.1.8591","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Dungeon Respawn","t":"Buff","x":"Faster dungeon respawns. Chests and foes in Abyss Dungeons and Wrothgarian Zone dungeon halls now come back after 30 minutes instead of an hour. Normal dungeons are still 20 minutes and elite dungeons 40.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8591-005","v":"0.1.8591","d":"2026-10-15","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"Rework","x":"The Monument to Julian LeFay now stands outside Privateer's Hold, beside the path every new character walks out on, instead of in Gothway Garden.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8594-001","v":"0.1.8594","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Wagon","t":"Rework","x":"The wagon wheels are back. Carts, open wagons and caravans roll on the painted wheels they had before the Daggerfall-texture pass: seven wooden spokes, a dark hub and an iron tyre with its rivets. Everything else on the wagons keeps its Daggerfall textures.","g":["horse","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8599-001","v":"0.1.8599","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Face Portraits","t":"New","x":"With Morrowind data attached, every face portrait now shows the 3D head your character wears: save tiles, profile and account cards, character creation, the large HUD, the tab dial, and the party panel.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8599-002","v":"0.1.8599","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Face Portraits","t":"New","x":"NPC faces in the talk window, the family and succession pages, and the escort faces show the head their body wears too.","g":["morrowind","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8599-003","v":"0.1.8599","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Face Portraits","t":"New","x":"Portraits show the helmet or hood you are wearing, the vampire head when you are a vampire, and the werewolf head when transformed.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8599-004","v":"0.1.8599","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Face Portraits","t":"Fix","x":"Catching vampirism now changes your body's face right away, and a cure changes it back - no reload needed.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8599-005","v":"0.1.8599","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"The new Breton heads no longer sit backwards on the body.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8599-006","v":"0.1.8599","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Rework","x":"The new Breton heads are for player characters only. NPCs wear Morrowind's own heads again.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8643-001","v":"0.1.8643","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Face Portraits","t":"Fix","x":"Character portraits now show the face instead of the back of the head.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8643-002","v":"0.1.8643","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"The Breton eyepatch face now sits on the right head, and wears its own hair instead of the red headband.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-001","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"New","x":"A new passive tree for everything you do online. Open it from the Firmament button on the Stats page (pause menu or character sheet).","g":["online","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-002","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"New","x":"Choose one of seven birthsigns, then spend Stars on combat stars and Craft points on the life ring - gathering, crafting, trading, hunting and sailing.","g":["online","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-003","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"New","x":"You earn 2 Stars for every Renown level, and 1 Craft point for every 8 profession ranks.","g":["online","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-004","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"New","x":"Changes are free to plan until you confirm them. Taking stars back is free below Renown 10, then costs 10 silver per star. A full reset costs 10,000 gold.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-005","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Other","x":"Your stars never affect hits or spells against other players, and they switch off in duels and while you mentor.","g":["online","arena"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-006","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Other","x":"Works in Enhanced Plus and DFO Grimoire, and on phones: tap a star to read it, tap again to take it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-007","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Other","x":"The Firmament's own text is English for now.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-008","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Main Menu","t":"Rework","x":"The main menu first asks one question: Online or Offline. Offline opens Continue, New Game, Load Game and the Test Room, with a way back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-009","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Main Menu","t":"UI","x":"Settings and Overhauls are now in the menu's bottom bar beside Screenshots and About.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-010","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Main Menu","t":"Fix","x":"The bottom bar no longer covers the menu's buttons on phones, small or short screens, and long languages.","g":["touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-011","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"UI","x":"In DFO Grimoire, the menu's two pages appear only where the screen is tall enough; otherwise one page is shown.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-012","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Main Menu","t":"Fix","x":"Double-clicking Offline no longer opens Load Game by accident.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-013","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Main Menu","t":"QoL","x":"Escape puts the keyboard back on the button you came from.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-014","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Main Menu","t":"Fix","x":"Tutorials and Screenshots are now translated.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-015","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"UI","x":"Classes are grouped as Magic, Stealth and Combat, and each shows the two attributes it relies on.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-016","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"UI","x":"The class card shows the class's attributes, skills and health per level before you read its description. Health now reads as the real range, for example \"3-6 a level, more with Endurance\".","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-017","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"Fix","x":"On phones, \"Begin your life\" and \"Play as...\" stay on screen.","g":["touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-018","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"Fix","x":"A greyed-out button that is waiting (for example \"18 left to spend\") is now readable.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-019","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"Fix","x":"The province names on the map no longer overlap or run off it.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-020","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"Fix","x":"Clicking through classes no longer plays the drums every time - only when you choose one.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-021","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"QoL","x":"Start over now sits beside Back.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-022","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"Fix","x":"Buttons say \"Play as an Acrobat\", not \"Play as a Acrobat\".","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-023","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Calm HUD","t":"New","x":"Calm HUD (Features, on by default): the health, fatigue and magicka bars fade out while all three are full and no enemy is targeted, and come back the moment you lose or spend a point.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-024","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Horse","t":"Rework","x":"The saddle panel is a small block in the bottom-right corner. F2 shows or hides it (rebindable in Controls). The Horse care setting chooses When needed, Always or Off.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-025","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Horse","t":"Fix","x":"On touch screens the saddle panel no longer covers the compass.","g":["horse","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-026","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Temperature Display","t":"Rework","x":"The temperature reading sits in the bottom-left corner.","g":["climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-027","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"DFO Grimoire no longer draws dotted lines.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-028","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Stable","t":"UI","x":"The Stable's horse look is now swatches and arrows instead of large buttons.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-029","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Character Creation","t":"UI","x":"Small text across Settings and character creation is now at least 12px and easier to read.","g":["intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-030","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"The pause window's tabs wrap instead of running off the window in long languages.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8662-031","v":"0.1.8662","d":"2026-10-15","e":"DFO Grimoire","t":"Fix","x":"In DFO Grimoire on phones, the side menu (including \"Main menu\") is readable again.","g":["mod","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-001","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Sit at any tavern's card table and press Play The King's Gambit on the Hold'em or Iliac Hand panel to start a battle of armies and kings against the tavern's regulars.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-002","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Choose whom to challenge. Each regular plays at a tier, from Amateur to Grandmaster, and their row tells you their army's size, their potions, how often they blunder and the least they will play for.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-003","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Put down a stake of 1, 2 or 5 times that least stake. Win and you take back twice your stake. A regular can only pay out so much in a night, and after that they play for fun.","g":["social","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-004","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Pick one of the Iliac Bay's four kings and build an army of up to 12 units from 300 points. Every unit wears its Iliac Hand card's picture.","g":["social","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-005","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Fight on a board laid across the table. Each turn you have two actions: move a piece, strike, or give it a potion. Fire, spikes and poison spread across the board as the rounds pass. Fell the other king to win, and guard your own.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-006","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Play with the mouse, a finger, the keyboard or a gamepad. On a touchscreen, a press snaps to your pieces and asks you to confirm a move or a strike.","g":["social","gamepad","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-007","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Other","x":"Forfeiting or standing up while gold is down asks you twice, and you cannot save with gold on the table.","g":["social","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-008","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"A built-in guide and glossary explain every rule. The game's words read in all thirteen fully translated languages.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-009","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"QoL","x":"You can turn the game off in Settings, on the World tab.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-010","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"The board now stands on the table. Walls are stone blocks, pillars are columns, and water lies low with ripples drifting across it.","g":["social","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-011","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Every piece is its card standing in a stand. Your stands are pale, the regular's are dark with notched rims, and the kings stand on brass. A bar over each card shows its health.","g":["social","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-012","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Pieces walk the path they take, lunge at their foes, and shake and flash red when they are hit. A potion makes a card glow green. The damage or the healing rises over the piece as a number, and shots fly across the board.","g":["social","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-013","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"A fallen piece topples and slides into its owner's pile beside the board, so you can count the losses at a glance.","g":["social","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-014","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Fire flickers, spikes stand up and poison bubbles. A warning pulses where a new hazard will appear.","g":["social","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-015","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"When the battle starts, the cards are dealt onto the board one at a time, and your view leans over the table so the whole board fits beside the panel. Fold the panel to give the board more room.","g":["social","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-016","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Other","x":"With reduced motion turned on, a hit piece does not shake.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-017","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"The King's Gambit now sounds as the mod does: dice as the game opens, coins as a stake goes down, a click as a unit joins or a piece is chosen.","g":["social","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-018","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Monsters cry as they move and strike, swords swing and bowstrings loose, spells crackle, potions bubble, and a fallen piece hits the cloth. Fire, spikes and poison each bite with their own sound.","g":["social","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-019","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"A win ends in a fanfare (and the clink of coins when gold was down); a loss in a groan. Forfeiting is silent, as in the mod.","g":["social","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-020","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Online, sit at a tavern's card table and The King's Gambit offers the board's two seats: press Sit at the board, build your army, then press Ready. When both players are ready, the table lays the board and deals both armies.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-021","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"The table runs the game: it lays the board, rolls every die and keeps a turn clock of 60 seconds. A turn that runs out ends as End turn does; three in a row stand that player up and give the game to the other.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-022","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Other","x":"Your king's row is always at your own edge of the board, and the board lies in the same place on the cloth for both players.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-023","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"The other player's moves play out one at a time, half a second apart, so you can follow each.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-024","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Anyone else in the tavern can watch a game: the board stands on its cloth for everyone near the table.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-025","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Play a regular instead takes you back to the tavern's regulars at any time.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-026","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"At a tavern's red table, a realm character can play another player for gold: stake 10, 50, 200, 1,000 or 5,000 gold, the same as your opponent. The realm holds both stakes, and the winner takes the whole pot.","g":["social","online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-027","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"Every online game between two registered accounts counts on The King's Gambit's season board. Press Season board to see the top ten and your own rank.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-028","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"The season's first player, after ten counted games against five different opponents, wears the Grandmaster title.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-029","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Fix","x":"No single press loses a staked game: a gamepad's Start button and a stray finger on a touchscreen now ask before you stand up, as Escape does.","g":["social","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-030","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Fix","x":"Leaving the board just as a game is dealt cancels that game, and both stakes go home.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-031","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Fix","x":"If your connection drops mid-game, the panel tells you how the game ended when you are back.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-032","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Fix","x":"A move followed at once by End turn now goes through, and the realm's own reason is shown when it cannot hold your stake.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-033","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"New","x":"On a gamepad with the Enhanced Plus hotbar, the d-pad moves the board's cursor during a battle.","g":["social","gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-034","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"UI","x":"On a phone, the turn clock shows first, and anyone watching a game has Stand up, Play a regular instead and More.","g":["social","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-035","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"UI","x":"A piece's information now names the foes it can strike and any hazard under it.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-036","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"King's Gambit","t":"Fix","x":"The online board's buttons read correctly in every translated language.","g":["social","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-037","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"The Grizzly Bear, the Sabretooth Tiger, the Spider, the Slaughterfish, the Mummy, the Frost Daedra, the Fire Daedra, the Archer and the Ranger join the Iliac Hand set, each with its own painted picture.","g":["social","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-038","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"Their creatures drop them, as every other creature drops its own card - and every creature in the game now has one.","g":["social","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8698-039","v":"0.1.8698","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Iliac Hand","t":"New","x":"Every Iliac Hand card's rules and flavor text now read in your chosen language, in all thirteen fully translated languages.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8737-001","v":"0.1.8737","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Points of Interest","t":"New","x":"Points of interest built by the developers now stand in the world: ruins, shrines, camps and more, streamed in as you travel, solid to walk on and lit at night.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8737-002","v":"0.1.8737","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Points of Interest","t":"New","x":"Places that ask to be marked show on the world map and the travel map.","g":["map","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-001","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guilds","t":"Buff","x":"Online, you are promoted the moment you qualify for your guild's next rank. Talk to a guild-service NPC at the hall to get it. There is no 28-day wait for a promotion any more. Demotion, probation and expulsion still wait 28 days, so one bad day doesn't cost you a rank. Offline play is unchanged.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-002","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Online, if you don't yet qualify, the guild popup lists what the next rank needs that you lack:","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-003","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"the rank's name (\"Next rank: Swordsman\")","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-004","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"your reputation against what's needed (\"Reputation 14 of 20\")","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-005","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"the guild-skill level you're short of, with your best guild skill named (\"A guild skill at 31 - your best, Axe, is 25\")","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-006","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"a second guild skill at the lower bar","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8741-007","v":"0.1.8741","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"the guild's own skills by name","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-001","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Desktop App","t":"Rework","x":"Updates download only what changed. The desktop app now updates the game one file at a time instead of downloading about 130 MB and replacing the whole game folder. The full installer runs only when the app itself changes, or when a file-by-file update fails. This applies on Windows, macOS, Linux and the portable build.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-002","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Spellbook","t":"Fix","x":"Spellbook details. A spell you made now shows its real settings in the Spellbook, and only the parts its effects use.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-003","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Boarding","t":"Fix","x":"Your ship's crew. Your crew no longer rushes the rail shouting at nobody while you stand at the helm. They muster only when a boarding can actually happen.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-004","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Shipyards","t":"Fix","x":"Shipyards by ponds. Towns away from the open sea, such as Ilessan Hills, no longer have a shipyard and a lighthouse beside a pond.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-005","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Enemies stuck in doorways. Tall enemies (mages, healers, spellswords, liches, Daedra lords) duck under dungeon doorways again instead of jamming in them.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-006","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Daedra summoning. A summoning whose quest cannot be offered where you are no longer takes your gold or marks the Daedra as summoned. Staff can repair characters already affected.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-007","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"PvP looting. A worn item you loot from a player in the open PvP zone now reaches you even if you share a guild or party with them. The item stays held until you collect it, and goes back to its owner if nobody does.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-008","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quests sending you to a player's home. Quests no longer pick another player's home as a quest residence, in any town.","g":["quests","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-009","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Party loot. Party members in a dungeon now see the same loot on the same body or container, and each player gets their own bonus on top. Taking an item no longer replaces the other players' list.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-010","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"Overworld travel stuck at 1x. Overworld travel no longer drops to 1x speed and stays there. Land that fails to load is loaded again instead of leaving a hole.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-011","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Shadows","t":"Performance","x":"Moving lights. Moving lights, such as a boss's glow, no longer redraw all their shadows every frame.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-012","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Rework","x":"Guildmates are friends in the PvP zone. Members of the same guild can no longer attack each other there, as with a party.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-013","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"HUD","t":"New","x":"Movable riding and helm panels. The riding panel and the ship's helm panel are now pieces in the HUD editor (Alt+U). You can move, resize or hide them.","g":["first-person","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8786-014","v":"0.1.8786","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Horse","t":"Rework","x":"Horse care and wagon upkeep tiers. Horse care and wagon upkeep each have Off, Boons (the default) and Hard, like Climates & Calories. On Boons nothing is taken: a hungry horse is no weaker, a worn wagon is no slower, and a wagon kept Sound rolls 10% faster. Hard is the system as it was. Off is the classic horse or wagon.","g":["horse","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8791-001","v":"0.1.8791","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Rework","x":"Many of a sign's stars added up past what the Firmament allows for that stat, so the last stars you bought did nothing. The values have come down so that every star in a sign now adds something.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8791-002","v":"0.1.8791","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Rework","x":"Small stars and roads now give their attribute and skill bonus one for one as a percent (+2 Strength is +2% of your Strength; it was +4%).","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8791-003","v":"0.1.8791","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Rework","x":"Notables, keystones and life stars were scaled down to fit. Some examples: Night Mother's Embrace is +19% damage to unaware foes (was +30%), Merchant Prince is +11 Mercantile / +6 Etiquette (was +20 / +10), and Hermit's Covenant is +10% herb yield (was +20%).","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8791-004","v":"0.1.8791","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Firmament","t":"Rework","x":"A Firmament attribute bonus now counts on a stat already at 100. With the sky's full +15, a 100 Strength reads 115. A Fortify fills up to that raised cap but never passes it, and offline the cap is 100 again.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8794-001","v":"0.1.8794","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"Looting a fallen enemy in a dungeon no longer turns its Morrowind body back into the old sprite while the loot window is open.","g":["morrowind","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8794-002","v":"0.1.8794","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"Morrowind bodies no longer clip through floors and walls: a body lying on the ground no longer sinks halfway into it, and a figure standing beside a wall is no longer sliced off by it.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8802-001","v":"0.1.8802","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Chat Window","t":"Fix","x":"Searching for a player in the chat now finds anyone online, not just the people listed on your screen. With hundreds of players online, the World list only shows part of the server, and the search used to look in that part alone. It now asks the server too, so players on other parts of the server show up a moment after you type.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-001","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Gilded Weapons","t":"New","x":"The Dragonfire Oath is a Daedric Dai-Katana that can drop from the Warden of the Burning Gate, about one fight in a hundred. It gives +40% damage, +15 Strength, +30 Long Blade and +15 Endurance.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-002","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Gilded Weapons","t":"New","x":"Dragonfire: a blow that lands on a Daedra burns it again for another third of the hit, and burns every other Daedra within 3 m for the same.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-003","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Gilded Weapons","t":"New","x":"The Sunken Sovereign is an Ebony Saber that can drop from the Old Coil, about one kill in a hundred, for a ship that did damage. It gives +40% damage, +15 Agility, +30 Long Blade and 10% life leech.","g":["loot","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-004","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Gilded Weapons","t":"New","x":"Undertow: each blow on the same foe adds +10% damage, up to +50%, and the stacks fade after 6 seconds without a hit. A foe it kills heals you for 10%.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-005","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Gilded Weapons","t":"New","x":"Both are shown in the Collections codex, each with its own hint.","g":["loot","holdings"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-006","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"Killing the sea serpent now has a rare chance to grant the title Coilbreaker (1 in 20 kills) and the aura The Maelstrom (1 in 50). You keep them for good.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-007","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"The Maelstrom is a three-armed whirlpool of tide and foam around your feet, with a curling lip and spray.","g":["naval","water"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8809-008","v":"0.1.8809","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Sea Serpent","t":"New","x":"An honour you have not held before is announced and shown in a popup.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-001","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"Fix","x":"Sending your wagon or horse away from the Stable now keeps them there. They no longer reappear outside the next building or dungeon you enter, and mounting your horse no longer drops a stabled wagon behind you. Summon them to bring them back. A wagon or horse you never sent away is shown as With you on the Stable page and is left outside doors as before. If you sent yours away before this update, send it away once more.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-002","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Magic Repair","t":"Fix","x":"The Repairs Objects enchantment mends your worn gear first, then a worn Cast When Held or Item Deteriorates piece, and only then what you carry. Damaged loot in your pack no longer takes the repairs while the ring on your finger wears down. While such a piece is damaged it holds the repairs, so your pack waits.","g":["enchanting","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-003","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Rework","x":"Flying Kick can now be used while jumping, falling or stepping off a ledge. Every other leap and dash still needs solid ground. A kick near the ground no longer cancels the damage from a long fall.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-004","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"If you die in the Wrothgarian Mountains while your wagon is parked outside the zone, or sent to the stable, nothing in it is lost. Its items and gold stay put. A wagon you drive, lead or park inside the zone still loses its cargo as before.","g":["death-penalty","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-005","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Slaughterfish from crates. Searching a crate or chest in a dungeon no longer wakes Slaughterfish, Dreugh or Lamia on dry land.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-006","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"A duplicate player after a server restart. A player who reconnects now stands once. An old connection from before the restart, or a second tab, no longer leaves a frozen copy of them in town or in a dungeon.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-007","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"Market stalls full of people. In towns with market stalls (such as Penbrugh), the food, goods and animals at the stalls show as themselves again with the Morrowind people on, instead of crowds of bowed, turning figures.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-008","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"Bare feet in chain boots. Chain boots, gauntlets and pauldrons, including Legendary ones like The Wayrest Courier's Treads, now show on your Morrowind body (in iron) instead of bare skin.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-009","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Stuck quest foes. A foe that appears inside a pillar is moved out beside it.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-010","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Arrows","t":"Fix","x":"Arrows from twigs. Using a twig makes 2 arrows again, as intended, so the workbench's 20 arrows from 4 twigs are worth their plank and ingot.","g":["crafting","logging"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-011","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Missing quest residences. If a quest's residence is in another player's home, its door now shows the quest's name, for example \"The Hawkley Residence (Aldric's home)\".","g":["quests","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-012","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Morrowind Models","t":"Fix","x":"Battle axes and war axes. With the Morrowind look, a Battle Axe (one-handed) now looks and swings like a one-handed axe, and a War Axe (two-handed) like a two-handed one.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-013","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Boulders","t":"Fix","x":"Boulder glint. A boulder's glint now sits on its stones, not in the air above them.","g":["mining"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-014","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Stores","t":"Rework","x":"Looted ingredients can be stored. Ingredients you looted, bought or were given now go into your Stores as \"loose\". You can craft with them at any station, but they can't be used for writs, your guild's Stores or market sales; only what you gathered can.","g":["crafting","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8826-015","v":"0.1.8826","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Online Players","t":"Rework","x":"One player per account in a place. If you log in to the same account a second time in the same area, the older connection is closed.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8829-001","v":"0.1.8829","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Townspeople","t":"Rework","x":"How a person takes your tone now changes what they think of you. Townsfolk like plain speaking: a Blunt question raises their regard, and a Polite one lowers it. Before, being polite raised everyone's regard, even with the commoners who refuse polite questions.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8829-002","v":"0.1.8829","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Courtship and Marriage","t":"Rework","x":"Courtship works the same way. A tone they like helps the day's courtship, and one they dislike costs a little affection (never below nothing). They will tell you so.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8829-003","v":"0.1.8829","d":"2026-10-15","e":"Talk Panel","t":"UI","x":"The regard explanation on the talk panel now says which tone townsfolk prefer.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8832-001","v":"0.1.8832","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Fix","x":"Gauntlets of the Rose (Open Hand): the second blow from a bare-handed hit now shows its own damage number, tagged \"Open Hand\", next to the first. The bonus was always being applied (each fist that lands hits again for half), but it never showed on screen, so it looked like nothing was happening.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8832-002","v":"0.1.8832","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Loot Rarity","t":"Fix","x":"Many Endings: its echo now shows its own number too, tagged \"Many Endings\".","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8840-001","v":"0.1.8840","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"The galleon, carrack and large boat wear their own painted liveries again: the oxblood strakes, the gilt and the stern gallery.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8840-002","v":"0.1.8840","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"The wagons and the caravan have their own paint back, with the caravan's livery, shutters, curtains and sunburst.","g":["horse","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8840-003","v":"0.1.8840","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Wagon Yards","t":"Fix","x":"The Stable, Wagon Yard, Joinery, shipyard and lighthouse signs have their emblems back: the horseshoe, the wheel, the saw, the anchor and the coil.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8840-004","v":"0.1.8840","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Textures","t":"Fix","x":"The town's banners and hangings show their regions' and gods' own charges again.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8840-005","v":"0.1.8840","d":"2026-10-16","e":"LeFay Monument","t":"Fix","x":"The LeFay monument has its painted stone and bronze plaque again.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8840-006","v":"0.1.8840","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Textures","t":"Rework","x":"Every one of these textures is now drawn in Daggerfall's own colour palette, with Daggerfall's grain, so they sit beside the classic walls and ships instead of standing out.","g":["rendering","parity"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8859-001","v":"0.1.8859","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Invisibility","t":"Fix","x":"Invisibility in dungeons. Monsters that cannot see through Invisibility no longer swing at you just because you walked in front of them. The undead, vampires and Daedra still see through it, as in Daggerfall. Wilderness enemies also no longer notice an invisible traveller during fast travel.","g":["enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8859-002","v":"0.1.8859","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Beautiful Villages","t":"Fix","x":"Blocked temple entrances. Temples in Beautiful Villages towns, including the School of Julianos in Makehda and the temples of Kynareth, no longer sit behind a wall of stone. You can walk up their steps to the door again. The Akatosh Chantry's steps in Merdale are no longer buried under grass banks.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8859-003","v":"0.1.8859","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Climates & Calories","t":"Fix","x":"Getting wet when it isn't raining. You only get wet when rain or snow is actually falling on you, and a light shower soaks you slowly.","g":["weather","survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8859-004","v":"0.1.8859","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Beautiful Villages","t":"Fix","x":"Boulders and market stalls. Boulders in Beautiful Villages and Beautiful Cities towns show at their real size (most had sunk out of sight), and market stalls stand where the town's author placed them.","g":["mod","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8859-005","v":"0.1.8859","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guilds","t":"Rework","x":"Guild ranks online. Reputation you earn with a guild before joining still counts, but online a new member rises no faster than the guild records standing: about a rank and a half a day from the day you join. The guild hall now tells you when your next promotion can come at the earliest.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8859-006","v":"0.1.8859","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"New","x":"First-time crafting bonus. Crafting stations now show each pattern's XP and the 500 XP bonus for making it the first time. Pieces made only of cloth bought from the Weavers (Linen and Wool, including the Fishing Net) earn no first-time bonus. The stations and the craft messages now say so.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8863-001","v":"0.1.8863","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Keybindings","t":"QoL","x":"When assigning a key that is already in use, the confirmation now appears beside the binding being changed instead of at the top of the controls list. You no longer need to scroll away from the binding to choose whether to move the key or use it for both actions.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-001","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Instances","t":"New","x":"Instances. At a dungeon or building where one of your quests is running, at Privateer's Hold, or where a party member is already in an instance, the door now asks whether to enter the public world or your own instance. Only you and your party can enter your instance. It keeps its own looted chests and slain monsters (they return after half an hour, like everywhere else), and it closes for good when the quest that opened it ends.","g":["quests","online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-002","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Instances","t":"New","x":"Joining your party. A party member's instance shows at the door as \"*Name*'s instance\". Pick it to join them.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-003","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Privateer's Hold","t":"Rework","x":"Privateer's Hold can be visited again. Its public hall is still for new characters only, but you can return to your own instance of the Hold at any time.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-004","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Quest dungeons are complete again. Quest targets, like the main quest's mummy, could end up in a part of a smaller online dungeon that can't be reached from its entrance. Quest dungeons are now always the full Daggerfall layout, in your instance or in the full public layout.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-005","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Instances","t":"Other","x":"Quest teleports, Recall, loading a save and staff teleports return you to the instance you were in, or to the public room if that instance has closed. They never stop to ask.","g":["quests","saves","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-006","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Instances","t":"Other","x":"The door only asks when there is a real choice. Every other door opens as it always did. Homes and the Wrothgarian open zone never have instances.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8875-007","v":"0.1.8875","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Instances","t":"QoL","x":"Press Esc at the door to leave without entering.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-001","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"New","x":"Weapons with a fire, frost or shock damage bonus now show it. Whether the bonus is the weapon's own or comes from a Ruby or Sapphire set in it, the weapon wears an animated outline of its element:","g":["combat-visuals","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-002","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"New","x":"Fire gives off rising flames and drifting embers.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-003","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"New","x":"Frost forms a breathing rime with glinting ice spikes.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-004","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"New","x":"Shock crackles along the edge and throws off arcs.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-005","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"New","x":"On the Morrowind first-person and third-person models the outline wraps the 3D weapon, and the blade's surface is charged with its element as well. An enchanted Morrowind weapon with no element now glows with an arcane light, like classic enchanted weapons always have.","g":["morrowind","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-006","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"New","x":"Once the servers are updated, other players' weapons glow on their Morrowind bodies as they do in their hands. Your Weapon glow switch decides only what you see.","g":["online","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-007","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"Other","x":"A weapon you haven't identified keeps its element hidden until you identify it, as its card does.","g":["combat-visuals","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8884-008","v":"0.1.8884","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Weapon Glow","t":"QoL","x":"Turn it off under Settings → Combat → Weapons in hand → Weapon glow. Off shows weapons exactly as before.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8893-001","v":"0.1.8893","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Ships","t":"Performance","x":"Towns with ships in port run smoother online. In our measurement the ships cost about a quarter of their old share of each frame, and they leave far less garbage behind, so there are fewer stutters.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8899-001","v":"0.1.8899","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Inventory","t":"Performance","x":"Containers, the wagon, your storage and pack pages holding hundreds of items now open in a fraction of a second. A 700-item container used to freeze the game for many seconds while its item pictures loaded.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8899-002","v":"0.1.8899","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Inventory","t":"Performance","x":"Clicking, taking and picking items in a long list is near-instant again, down from a second or more.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8899-003","v":"0.1.8899","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Inventory","t":"Performance","x":"Item pictures fill in as they load without redrawing the whole window, so hover cards and drags are no longer interrupted.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8899-004","v":"0.1.8899","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Loot Window","t":"Fix","x":"Searching your wagon or storage keeps your place in the list.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8899-005","v":"0.1.8899","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Loot Window","t":"Fix","x":"On phones, the loot window's two columns stay the same width and no longer run off the side of the screen.","g":["loot","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8903-001","v":"0.1.8903","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Horse","t":"Fix","x":"Your horse (and your cart's horse) now darkens with the world around it - at night, in a cave mouth or under a storm - instead of glowing as bright as noon under a dimmed weapon. It follows the same Features -> First-person lighting switch as your weapon and hands.","g":["horse","lighting","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8912-001","v":"0.1.8912","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Live Chat","t":"Fix","x":"World and region chat, friends, parties and guild lines are steadier at busy hours. The relay had been refusing a large share of the messages passed between its chat servers, so lines, invites and counts could go missing for players on some chat shards. That traffic now flows a different way that can't be refused.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8912-002","v":"0.1.8912","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Live Chat","t":"Fix","x":"When a room's server restarts just as you connect, you now get in on the first try instead of waiting out a reconnect.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8912-003","v":"0.1.8912","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"Logging in, saving, and the town, seat and notice-board panels should stay responsive at peak hours. The account database was hitting its limit on how many requests it could take each second; several of the busiest requests now ask it far fewer times, with the same answers.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8912-004","v":"0.1.8912","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"A yard piece you just placed, moved or removed no longer snaps back on your own screen for up to a minute afterwards.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-001","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"At rank 7 a guild hall now tells you the next rank is a chapter chair - a council chair or the Master's - won by Merit at each Sunday's Turning, and what it asks: reputation 80, 14 real days in the guild and an account 7 real days old.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-002","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"A service only a chair opens (the Mages Guild's Teleport, Zenithar's summoning) now says so at any rank, instead of promising a review that never comes online. A knight is told a chair brings no house.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-003","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"When your rank is held at 7, the new Guild Chapters tutorial page opens. You also see it the first time you come online as a member of a guild, temple or order.","g":["guild","intro"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-004","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"Every change to a guild's standing online is said in chat: \"Standing: Mages Guild +25 (now 40, 10 more to come)\".","g":["guild","chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-005","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"What the realm still owes you shows in the guild hall and on the Standing page, with the daily pace: 15 a real day, days turning at midnight UTC.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-006","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"When a quest's reward passes the day's pace you're told how much more is owed; if you're already at 100, you're told the rest is lost.","g":["guild","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-007","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Standing","t":"Fix","x":"Guild names appear in your language.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-008","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"The guild hall and the Standing page now warn you before a review puts you on probation or lowers your rank, with when it happens and why.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-009","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"On probation you're told the stakes: below -10 you're expelled at the review, below 0 it runs 28 more days, and at 0 or more it ends. Online, earning the next rank ends it sooner.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-010","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Quests","t":"Rework","x":"Online, \"Guard the Guild\" now needs Mages Guild standing 10 and \"Protect an Honored Mage\" standing 20 - the standing their own quest headers ask. New apprentices are no longer handed them. Their penalties are unchanged.","g":["quests","guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-011","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"The guild window's rank text scrolls on its own, so Talk, Service and Reforge stay on screen.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-012","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Guild Hall","t":"Fix","x":"Long refusals in the classic guild window no longer run off the screen.","g":["guild","classic-mode"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-013","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Standing","t":"Fix","x":"Joining a guild in the same minute as a standing loss is no longer dropped by the server.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8922-014","v":"0.1.8922","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Language","t":"Fix","x":"Translations updated in all 13 languages.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-001","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Fists","t":"New","x":"Bare-handed, both fists are now on screen. Punches alternate between the hands: the hand that leads opens, the other answers if you strike again quickly, and the idle fist tucks in toward the middle while the other punches.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-002","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Fists","t":"New","x":"Each punch shows the arm that throws it, on its own side. Daggerfall's own fist art has punches for both arms, and each hand now uses its own.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-003","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"New","x":"Equip a one-handed weapon in each hand (swords, daggers, maces, war axes) and both are drawn and swung. You no longer swap hands to use the second weapon.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-004","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Rework","x":"H now chooses which hand leads (\"Leading with the right hand.\" / \"Leading with the left hand.\"). It no longer costs a switch delay with both hands up. With one weapon it still swaps hands, as before.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-005","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"A shield, a two-handed weapon, a bow, or a torch or lantern held in a hand still means one weapon, as before.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-006","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"New","x":"With weapon glow on, each weapon in a pair shows its own element (a frost dagger beside a fire sword).","g":["combat-visuals","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-007","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"A pair is quicker, not twice as strong. The next blow straight after a strike comes from the other hand, a little sooner.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-008","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"The off hand (the one not leading) does 80% damage and has -5 to hit at Agility 50. Higher Agility shrinks the penalty to nothing; lower Agility raises it to -10.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-009","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"A heavy weapon in the off hand swings slower (a longer follow-through after its hit).","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-010","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"The off hand's blows count as 0.8 of a blow for everything a hit sets off: on-strike enchantments, per-hit item and set powers, and skill training. A pair doesn't proc or train faster than its damage.","g":["equipment","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-011","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"New","x":"When one weapon attacks, the other lowers slightly, straight down (it never slides sideways and shows where the sprite is cut off).","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-012","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"Measured, a matched pair of light weapons deals about 9% more damage per second than one of them, and a heavier pair about 4% (the off arm feels the weight). That holds at any frame rate. In return you spend up to a quarter more fatigue per second and give up your shield. A light off-hand weapon (a dagger next to a longsword) is quicker but weaker overall.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-013","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Other","x":"The same rules apply in duels, sieges and the open PvP zone.","g":["arena","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-014","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Running Hands","t":"New","x":"Running with nothing in either hand shows your arms pumping in step with your stride (on the head bob's own rhythm), using Daggerfall's own fist-and-forearm frames. The arm always runs off the bottom of the screen; no floating hands.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-015","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Running Hands","t":"New","x":"The arms keep running through a short hop, stay smooth when you stop and start again, and ease away when you ready a spell.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-016","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Running Hands","t":"Other","x":"Works with every mod switched off. A punch thrown mid-run shows at once.","g":["first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-017","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"First-Person Arms","t":"New","x":"both fists punch in turn, each with its own hand;","g":["morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-018","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"First-Person Arms","t":"New","x":"a pair of weapons shows the left weapon in the left hand, swinging with its own blows - now on the game's own skeletons too (they have no left weapon bone, so one is made by mirroring the right); the arm not attacking dips slightly at the shoulder;","g":["morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8940-019","v":"0.1.8940","d":"2026-10-16","e":"First-Person Arms","t":"New","x":"the arms pump while you run empty-handed.","g":["morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-001","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"Rework","x":"When the realm finds the same item in two places, it now locks that item only. Your character keeps trading, and nobody has to review it.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-002","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"Rework","x":"A locked item stays with you: it can't be traded, sold, dropped or left where others can take it. Your wagon and your own storage still take it.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-003","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"New","x":"You're told which item was locked, once on each device.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-004","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"Fix","x":"If you were handed an item by someone whose game closed before it saved the hand-off, your copy is locked, but it no longer counts against you.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-005","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"Fix","x":"Every character frozen for copied items has been unfrozen. The copied items themselves stay locked.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-006","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Player Trade","t":"Rework","x":"The third time the realm's rules hold a character's trading, it is frozen for a week and then reopens on its own. Each time after that, it's a month. Strikes clear a month after the last one.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-007","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Player Trade","t":"New","x":"The notice names the item and says when trading reopens.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-008","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"Fix","x":"Shop shelves no longer hand back an item you already took, which used to create a copy by accident.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8955-009","v":"0.1.8955","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Copied Items","t":"Fix","x":"Another player can no longer plant a copy of your item on you through a body or a container.","g":["online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8961-001","v":"0.1.8961","d":"2026-10-16","e":"First-Person Arms","t":"Fix","x":"With two weapons in first person, the left arm and its weapon are now on screen. Before, only the right arm showed.","g":["morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8961-002","v":"0.1.8961","d":"2026-10-16","e":"First-Person Arms","t":"Fix","x":"With two weapons in third person, the arms now swing against each other as you walk or run. Before, both swung the same way at once.","g":["morrowind","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8961-003","v":"0.1.8961","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Running Hands","t":"Fix","x":"The running fists stay low and pump with your stride, rising about a third of the way up the screen. Before, they rose to half the screen and looked like uppercuts.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8961-004","v":"0.1.8961","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Running Hands","t":"Fix","x":"A running fist now shows its back and knuckles, like your fists at rest. Before, it showed its underside.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8963-001","v":"0.1.8963","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Homes","t":"Performance","x":"A home's furnishings load faster, especially when the server is busy.","g":["homes","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8965-001","v":"0.1.8965","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Accounts","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed online features (homes, the notice board, mail, gathering, the market and the arena board) taking up to a minute to answer, or failing, since this afternoon.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.8969-001","v":"0.1.8969","d":"2026-10-16","e":"Accounts","t":"Performance","x":"When the account service is overloaded, the game now backs off its background checks (mail, the notice board, the day's motherlodes) instead of asking again at once, so the service recovers instead of staying slow.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-001","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Death","t":"Rework","x":"A party member's Resurrection now saves a Bloodline character. While the death screen is up (up to two minutes), their Resurrection brings you back with no death on your family tree, no Succession and no tombstone.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-002","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Death","t":"Fix","x":"The death is now held by the server, so closing the tab, reloading or logging in from another device no longer escapes it.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-003","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Death","t":"Other","x":"If the death is already settled, the caster is told \"<name> has fallen for good\" and keeps their magicka.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-004","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Crime","t":"New","x":"Anything you steal is now marked stolen, including a robbed caravan's goods and the hold of a lawful ship you board or sink. A merchant still buys it but never puts it back on the shelf.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-005","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Crime","t":"Rework","x":"When you're found guilty (jail, a fine or banishment), the guards take every stolen item you carry and tell you how many. Win your case, or get out through the Thieves Guild, and you keep them.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-006","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Crime","t":"Fix","x":"Your own items put into someone else's cupboard and taken back are no longer marked stolen.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-007","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Crime","t":"Fix","x":"Paying a fine or doing a penance now restores your reputation with the people of the kingdom too, not only with the law.","g":["law","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-008","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Guards called into a building now walk round through the doorway to reach you, even between deep shelves or inside a closet, and they attack when they get there. A locked door or a ladder only keeps them out for two seconds.","g":["law"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-009","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Town Watch","t":"Fix","x":"Guards and dungeon enemies standing next to you now turn to face you and attack, instead of standing still.","g":["law","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-010","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"A headstone your party has searched counts as searched for the whole party, and the game tells you who searched it. A stranger's search no longer locks it for you.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-011","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"In tombs, coffins a stranger opened are yours to search, and you can search one standing right next to it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-012","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Party members no longer vanish for a few seconds when you go through a tomb door.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-013","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Arena Bouts","t":"Fix","x":"The arena now waits for the server instead of briefly showing your offline rank and season. Your title and wins were never lost.","g":["arena","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-014","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Magic Repair","t":"Rework","x":"With a Repairs Objects enchantment worn, every worn piece of armour and clothing now repairs 2% of itself per tick, the same as weapons. A battered steel set is whole in about an hour.","g":["enchanting","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-015","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Stable","t":"Fix","x":"With horse care Off, the Stable page now shows every horse you own and lets you ride any of them.","g":["horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-016","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Another player's Disintegrate no longer deletes your revenant outright. It now counts as a killing blow, and only you decide your revenant's fate.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-017","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Market","t":"Fix","x":"Market stalls now look the way the pack draws them: the keeper behind the counter, goods on the counter.","g":["market","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-018","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Yard","t":"Fix","x":"Stalls and boulders you placed in your own yard are back where you put them, at the size you placed them.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-019","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Shipyards","t":"Fix","x":"The shipyard's fleet page reads properly again.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9087-020","v":"0.1.9087","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Professions","t":"Fix","x":"A pending perk change no longer blocks you from choosing perks when you reach a new rank.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-001","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guild Hall","t":"UI","x":"The guild hall now says what reputation still on its way means: it is already earned and arrives at most 15 a real day. Quests done the same day add to what is waiting, not to your standing.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-002","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guilds","t":"Fix","x":"A member on probation is no longer expelled over reputation the guild still owes them. The probation is renewed instead.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-003","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"Pieces of Ruhn's Regalia (and the raiding parties' sets) that were enchanted before enchanting them was closed no longer freeze your trading. Holds placed because of them are lifted.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-004","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Gathering","t":"Fix","x":"The loot panel and its tooltip no longer cover skinning, or any other gathering minigame, while it plays.","g":["hunting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-005","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Instances","t":"UI","x":"At a quest's dungeon whose shared version is laid smaller, the Public / Your instance prompt now says the quest's business is in your instance only.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-006","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Instances","t":"Fix","x":"Quest Repair in that shared dungeon now tells you where the quest's things are, instead of \"Nothing was missing\".","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9091-007","v":"0.1.9091","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"Fix","x":"A dungeon's automap keeps your exploration of both the shared dungeon and your instance. Switching between them no longer wipes the map, its notes or its portals.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-001","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The tier above Dagon's Breach. Your party of up to 8 goes down through the torn halls of the Battlespire under a 30-minute count.","g":["elites","online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-002","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Open one with a Weir Key. Stand outdoors, online and signed in, and use the key from your inventory. Your party at that moment becomes the breach's company and is called.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-003","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"No key yet? Choose *Rehearse* in the start window, or type /breach rehearse, to open the day's Rehearsal. It runs the first circle of five halls, needs no key, and pays nothing.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-004","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"The breach rises for 5 minutes while your company gathers, then takes members for 5 more.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-005","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The start window. Using a Weir Key asks where to begin before any key is spent:","g":["elites","online","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-006","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Wager. Before you open, choose up to three decrees, one from each family, to take on from the first hall.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-007","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The arch. An arch of the gate's white marble and gold rises out of the ground in front of you, with a gold beacon 400 m tall. Other players nearby see it too. It burns open when the breach opens and sinks once the first hall wakes.","g":["elites","portals","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-008","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The key tells you why when it can't open here: indoors; in a duel or a siege; with enemies nearby; while travelling; in water or aboard a boat; inside a town; within 300 m of a Dagon's Breach or 150 m of another arch; while you already hold a breach; while the road is shut; or without 8 m of clear ground for the arch.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-009","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The call. Wherever your party is in the Bay, they hear a war horn and see a prompt with the time until the breach opens. Once it is open, press Enter (A on a gamepad) or the prompt's button to answer. A portal opens at your feet: step into it. The opener steps through the arch itself. A late step through the arch still admits you.","g":["elites","online","portals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-010","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A key that fails to open comes back. If the Spire fails to open, your Weir Key comes back on its own the next time you are online within a week, even if you reload. A stake the Spire never settles is spent after two weeks, and a letter in your mailbox says why.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-011","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"One breach at a time. A call to another breach while you stand in one no longer takes you out of yours.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-012","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Finding it: the breach is in the Timers row (its opening, then the hall and the count), you get a sight line (*You see an Elite Breach 140 metres to the North!*), and your company's arch is marked in gold on the map and the compass.","g":["elites","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-013","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Weir Keys","t":"New","x":"Closing a Dagon's Breach can drop a Weir Key:","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-014","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Weir Keys","t":"New","x":"Clearing an Abyss Dungeon's Hour drops one 1 in 3.","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-015","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Weir Keys","t":"New","x":"Everyone who has already closed a Dagon's Breach gets one key as a launch gift.","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-016","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Weir Keys","t":"Other","x":"Opening a breach spends a key. You need to have closed a Dagon's Breach before you can open a keyed one.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-017","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Broken Galleries (circles 1-5), the Soul Cairn (6-10), the Shade Perilous (11-15) and the Havoc Wellhead (16 and deeper). Each region has its own enemies, lords, platforms and element.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-018","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A Brink opens the Soul Cairn, the Shade Perilous and the Wellhead: a long crossing through the Spire's broken passages, ending in the new region's own set piece. The Brink into the Cairn always carries its Sinking Stair.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-019","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each circle is five halls: a fight, a crossing, a trial, a second fight, then the lord's Court. Enemies get tougher every circle.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-020","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Entering a new region, you fall past the Spire's broken underside: torn floors, hanging spires, broken galleries and upside-down columns, lit by that region's glow. Other steps are a quick fade; reduced motion gives a plain cut. The hall number shows each time.","g":["elites","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-021","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A hall is a way through the torn academy. Corridors turn, rooms have more than one way out, and the way climbs and falls between the arrival plate and the door, crossing over and under itself.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-022","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Rooms: stair halls with a grand stair up to a gallery, towers with spiral stairs, two-level gallery halls, cloisters round a court, broken halls whose floor fell into the undercroft, and crossings where two ways pass at two heights.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-023","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Climbing: short climbs on the main way, never more than two pitches in a row and never longer than 9 m, sized so a character at Climbing 0 with no grip left can make them. Each has a stair or ramp somewhere in the hall for anyone who would rather walk. Harder optional climbs lead off the way to the academy's caches and vantage points.","g":["elites","climbing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-024","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Floors can stand over other floors. Blows, danger shapes, the legion and the lords all judge the floor you are actually standing on, never the one above or below.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-025","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A fall that would skip you ahead along the way casts you back, as the void does.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-026","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Yards:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-027","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Ramparts:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-028","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Stairs climb to the Rampart's caster pillars, the Wyrm's perches and the Council Rotunda's balconies: every raised floor has its way up.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-029","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Crossings: the Span's platforms and, from circle 3, the Deepway's chambers. Deeper spans carry more passages. The platforms grow in kind as you go down:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-030","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"walled Drops to a landing below, with a doorway onward and a lamp on the far wall;","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-031","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"in the Soul Cairn, Rails that carry you along the course (their tracks marked at both ends) and Gusts that push you sideways, with wind vanes and a rising wind a second before each gust;","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-032","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Islands carry waystones that light up gold where you would be cast back. A teammate standing on a crumbling platform that already fell for you stands on a faint gold outline instead of floating.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-033","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Every crossing is proven crossable before you ever see it. The Spire checks every jump's timing at the slowest build the game makes, and lays the course again if a jump is ever unfair or if the usual crossing takes far longer than the fastest.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-034","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The toll. If you are still on the road when your company is pulled at the end of a crossing hall, you pay 5% of your health for each quarter of the road you didn't cross, at most 20%. Reaching a new island in your last 15 seconds waives it, and it never takes your last point of health. The toll rings when it is taken.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-035","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Late to the hall? After you have arrived late to two halls in a row, the next hall waits only 10 seconds for you instead of 30.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-036","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Trials:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-037","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Twists turn about one hall in four, trials included:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-038","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Sixteen kinds of enemy:","g":["elites","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-039","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The legion hunts:","g":["elites","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-040","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Enemies stand on the ground they're actually on: a Court raised above the hall, a chamber past a Deepway's shaft, Harriers following you down a course. Your blows reach them where they are.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-041","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Every enemy blow is drawn on the floor before it lands: a disc, a lane, a cone, a ring, or the whole floor with safe havens marked in gold. Every blow gives you time to step out of it, and the Spire never stacks blows so that nowhere is safe. A chained follow-up blow is drawn dim until the first one lands.","g":["elites","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-042","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Your company gathers on each hall's arrival plate, and the hall wakes once everyone is there. When the door opens, step through it to be pulled to the next hall.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-043","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Count: you have 30 minutes from the first hall. It runs during fights and pauses briefly between halls. If it runs out during a fight, the breach tears shut.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-044","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Falling into the void is not death. You are cast back to the last solid ground you stood on, for a tenth of your health. It never takes you below a quarter.","g":["elites","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-045","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Two restoring potions a hall. Healing, Heal True and Purification count toward the limit; every other potion and every spell is free. The count refills at each hall's wake and at each Redoubt, and a reload keeps it. The desktop HUD shows it.","g":["elites","alchemy"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-046","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"In the Spire you cannot save, rest, open the map, use Mark or Recall, levitate, or bring companions.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-047","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Ten places, each with its own danger:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-048","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"in the Soul Cairn:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-049","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"in the Shade Perilous:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-050","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"in the Wellhead:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-051","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Cooling slag (the Wellhead's Forge Gut): two spouts take turns pouring magma, and you cross on the crust while it holds. Its edge glows white in the last second before it breaks, and the spill's warning is drawn on the slag itself.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-052","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Shafts: a Deepway goes down through a shaft of its region's kind, such as the Hollow Trunk's moonlit branches or the Slag Chute. Standing on a shaft's ledge facing the drop, the third-person camera tilts down and lifts over the edge so you can see where you'll land.","g":["elites","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-053","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The fork. From circle 2 every Span splits at an island:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-054","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Set pieces, one per region:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-055","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Molten Rim leaves gold causeways across its magma.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-056","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Chambers. Some Yards and Proving Walks stand in modelled chambers, with a second floor up a stair, a chokepoint arch, surging channels, or an engine.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-057","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Engines:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-058","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Honour Horn (the Clan Pit). Answer the Kynval alone and the crowd throws every member a Reliquary. If anyone else steps into the ring, the crowd throws fire instead, for the rest of the hall.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-059","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Alcoves. Look for a faint gold seam in a wall. One blow breaks the false wall, and the alcove behind it holds lumen, a Vestige shard, or a page of the Annals.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-060","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Annals of 3E 398. Thirty pages the Battlemages left behind: seventeen hidden in the alcoves, and thirteen that each lord gives up at its first fall. Read the pages you have found with /breach annals, anywhere: your account keeps them.","g":["elites","books"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-061","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Grath's islands fall. In the first Court, the island Grath leaps from cracks and falls into the magma for 15 seconds. If you fall with it, you are thrown back onto an island that still stands.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-062","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"In third person, walls, shelves, pillars and other rock between the camera and your character fade to a see-through dither instead of hiding you.","g":["elites","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-063","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each Court has its own lord, with phases, errands for the company to run, and a fury that builds. Every phase shows its card:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-064","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Courts of two lords (Garoth beside the Last Armsmaster, the Twin Lords) are won when both fall. Each lord keeps its own element, mirrors and decree, and the HUD shows a bar for each lord standing.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-065","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The lords' own marks:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-066","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Proving Walks have their champions: the Kynreeve (Shield-Wall, facing where he guards), the Kynmarcher (The Citadel) and the Markynaz (The Grand Duke's Decree). The Markynaz's arrival card names the decree he lays, and his decree adds to the circle's decrees instead of replacing them.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-067","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Lords and champions walk around walls instead of through them: through an arch's opening, up a stair, across Grath's bridges. A Charge or Lunge stops at an arch's wall.","g":["elites","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-068","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Lords resize with your company: when a companion falls, the lord loses that companion's share of health, and it comes back when they're recalled.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-069","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A Colossal lord looks as big as it is and can be struck at its true size.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-070","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Standing still, or with the game in a background tab, a lord's blow still lands on you.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-071","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"A death in the breach is a fall, not the end. A FALLEN card says whether a Redoubt can call you back and how many Reliquaries you lost (reduced motion cuts straight through). The end theme plays. Then you become a witness who can ping the floor for the living.","g":["elites","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-072","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The next Redoubt calls you back at full health, once a breach, at the cost of your newest Vestige. A companion can carry your Memento from where you fell to a niche to bring you back sooner.","g":["elites","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-073","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"A second fall is final. A witness can also leave for good with /breach forsake (press twice).","g":["elites","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-074","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Witnesses see more: dormant Lurkers, hidden alcoves, and the next hall's twist. Pings show as blue pillars with a chime. A witness sees whom they watch, taps a row to watch another, and pings from the pad or touch.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-075","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"If the whole company falls, the breach ends.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-076","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"If your page reloads or your connection drops mid-breach, you're offered *Return to the Spire* while the breach still stands, even after the call has closed. You come back to the hall your company holds: at your last safe footing during a trial, or on the arrival plate between trials.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-077","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Returning from a new device or browser drops you straight into the right hall. If the Spire doesn't answer, you're told so and can try again.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-078","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Joining or reloading in the middle of a fight shows everything at once: burning ground, Grath's fallen islands, the lord's phase and where every enemy is.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-079","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Receipts wait for you. A breach that ended while you were offline keeps your receipts, and you collect them when you come back.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-080","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A server restart no longer loses a breach (see below).","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-081","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Defeating a circle's lord takes its Redoubt:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-082","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Choose a Vestige. Each member is offered three. Press 1-3 or type /breach pick N.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-083","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Stoneskin's extra health is a true cushion: the Spire's percentage hits count against your health without it, and the Spire's one-life count includes it.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-084","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A companion who has gone home or been left behind no longer strengthens your blows.","g":["elites","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-085","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Three of one family resonate into a capstone: Rooted makes you immune to pushes, Spellweave makes every fourth damage spell free, Rallying Cry gives back a spent Second Wind when a hall's door opens, Bladestorm's fifth melee blow strikes every foe around you, and Deadeye's long arrows pierce the add behind the target.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-086","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Accords take effect when their pair of holders stand within 10 m, among them Shield-Hymn (Bastion and Rally: the whole company gets Bastion's protection for 4 seconds when Rally heals at a door), Hammer and Anvil, Ambush, Kindled Steel, Living Wall and War-Chorus. The offer card names the Accord a pick would form with a companion.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-087","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Spare shards buy extra picks, and a Surplus buys a fourth card or a reroll.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-088","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Vote on the next circle's decrees. Each is a hardship with a reward: gusts on every span, crumbling halls, raging lords, a new one, The Fraying (the Athenaeum's Orrery frays sooner), and more. Press 1-3 or type /breach vote N. The decrees you choose are the next circle's, and the Redoubt's beacon names them and the next Court.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-089","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Ready up to end the rest early (Y, or /breach vote yes), or vote for a respite to make it longer. A respite can be asked for again after each one.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-090","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The way home opens at the Court's heart: press it twice, or type /breach home. Or stay, and the stair takes you down to the next circle.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-091","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Along the way:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-092","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A Redoubt raises a beacon at the Court's heart, and each recall stands as a blue pillar.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-093","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The damage chart: when a Court's lord falls, the gate's chart shows each member's damage, their share of the lord, blows, best hit, falls and healing.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-094","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"At the end, the recap shows your depth, your time, the circles you crossed and your Vestiges, each member's share of the damage and what they healed, every fall, and your place on the boards (*The Descent, the Few: 14th*). It survives a reload and has a Close button.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-095","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each Redoubt pays once per arena week (Monday to Monday). Taken again in the same week, it pays its gold only.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-096","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Spoils are thrown from the Court's heart when you stand in it, or go straight into your pack. They are decided when your claim is made:","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-097","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A Valkynaz's Redoubt (every fifth) rolls its spoils twice.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-098","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"Reliquaries: a circle's Reliquaries open once per account a week.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-099","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Silver: 20 Marks a Redoubt, inside the daily combat cap shared with gates, raids and serpents.","g":["elites","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-100","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Guild deeds: three members of one guild taking the same Redoubt pay 25 silver to the guild's treasury.","g":["elites","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-101","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Deadlands Embers go into your pack:","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-102","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Weir Keys","t":"New","x":"Weir Keys: a Valkynaz's Redoubt drops one 1 in 4, at most once a week. Elite foes in dungeons can drop one too:","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-103","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Battlemage's Panoply","t":"New","x":"A new Aetheric Sigil Set: nine Mithril pieces (the Warhelm, both Pauldrons, the Cuirass, Gauntlets, Greaves, Boots, the Spire-Shield and the Spire-Saber).","g":["loot","equipment","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-104","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Battlemage's Panoply","t":"New","x":"2 pieces, Battlemage's Bearing: +5 to +15 to every resistance and +10 to +30 magicka.","g":["equipment","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-105","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Battlemage's Panoply","t":"New","x":"4 pieces, Battlemage's Discipline: a spell you cast arms your next weapon blow with its element for +20% to +50%. Weapon blows return 5% to 15% of your last spell's cost. With a weapon in each hand, an off-hand blow returns it only when it counts in full, like any other per-blow power.","g":["equipment","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-106","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Battlemage's Panoply","t":"New","x":"6 pieces, Battlemage's Reprieve: a blow that takes you under 20% (never a killing blow) raises a shield of 15% to 40% of your health for 6 seconds. Party members within 8 m get half of it. It recovers in 240 down to 120 seconds.","g":["equipment","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-107","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Battlemage's Panoply","t":"New","x":"Pieces drop from Redoubts: 1 in 12 at Redoubt 1, improving to 1 in 4 from Redoubt 16, and 1 in 3 at a Valkynaz's.","g":["loot","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-108","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Battlemage's Panoply","t":"Rework","x":"In an Elite Breach, the Reprieve and Shed Skin answer the Spire's blows, and death-saving powers (Unbroken, The Hour Turns, Shed Skin, the Reprieve, Divine Grace and the Ghost-King's Vigil) recover at the next Redoubt, not on a timer.","g":["equipment","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-109","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Feats: each lord has three:","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-110","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"New titles:","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-111","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"New auras: Beaconlight (Redoubt 10), The Burning Stair (Redoubt 20) and Firstlight.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-112","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The boards (/breach board, the *Boards* button on the Timers window's Elite rows, or the start window):","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-113","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The herald posts to the gate's Discord channel when a company takes every tenth Redoubt, sets a new top of the Descent, earns First of the Spire or the Lone Beacon, or a sealed region opens.","g":["elites","online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-114","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The count chip is gold above 10:00, white to 2:00 and red below, pulsing in the last 30 seconds. When the count is held it shows a pause mark and why.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-115","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Arrivals: each hall announces itself with an arrival card naming the hall, its objective and its twist. Reduced motion stills the title cards.","g":["elites","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-116","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"First breach: short lines explain the Spire the first time you meet each part of it, once per account, so a new device doesn't repeat them.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-117","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Touch and gamepad: the panel, the votes and the Surplus work on touch and gamepad, and the pad reaches every panel choice. On touch screens you can flick up to jump and run at full speed on the spans.","g":["elites","gamepad","touch"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-118","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Settings > Accessibility: *Danger colours* (Standard, High contrast, Deutan-Protan, Tritan), *Danger fill* (50-100%) and *Reduced motion*.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-119","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"The Spire speaks English for now. Its own words (cards, lines, the panel) are in English whatever language you play in.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-120","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The relay judges where you really were when a blow landed: your movement history at that moment, on a clock corrected to yours. Lag no longer counts against you.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-121","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A feint is shown as a pulsing outline and fades out dashed when it's cut. A wind-up's sound plays only for a blow that will really land.","g":["elites","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-122","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Performance","x":"The next circle is built while you rest at the Redoubt, off the main thread, so stepping down is a swap rather than a fresh load: no stutter stepping into a new circle, in a breach opened before an update too.","g":["elites","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-123","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A breach survives a server restart. It picks up where it was, and the time the server was down is given back to the Count, the hall and every timer.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-124","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Jumps are more forgiving in the Spire. A jump pressed just before you land fires as you land, and a jump pressed just after you step off an edge still leaps.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-125","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"Leaping and dashing techniques don't work on the crossings (*The Spire's spans are walked, not flown.*). On fight floors they work as usual.","g":["elites","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-126","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Spire rebuilt to look like the Fractured Battlespire: every hall stands in the ruin of the Imperial Battlemages' academy - columns, arches, statues, cornices and lamps around and under every floor, in each region's own stone and forms.","g":["elites","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-127","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each region has its own air and light: ash and embers over the Deadlands' fire-sea in the Galleries, violet mist and drifting soul-motes in the Soul Cairn, near-black dusk and silver moon-dust under a great moon in the Shade Perilous, smoke and sparks over the magma in the Wellhead. Each has its own painted sky.","g":["elites","sky","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-128","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The lords are drawn as oversized sprites, towering over the company; their hit area grows with them.","g":["elites","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-129","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Every platform edge has a thin, steady gold line, so you can read where the ground ends even in fog or the dark. It keeps its width in the Retro picture modes.","g":["elites","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-130","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Danger shapes stay readable:","g":["elites","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-131","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Spire's own score: fourteen songs for the halls, the Courts, the Valkynaz, a lord's wake, the Redoubt's hymn, the last two minutes of the Count and the end. Each region and lord has its own motif.","g":["elites","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-132","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The door: when the way down opens, a gold beam and a draining ring mark it, and it appears on the compass.","g":["elites","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-133","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Danger shapes lie on every floor they cover, at that floor's height, instead of floating or hiding under ledges. A \"move!\" arrow points the way out over safe ground. Tethers, burning pools, marks over companions' heads and the Eclipse each have their own clear look.","g":["elites","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-134","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Allies' spells are dimmed during trials so warnings stay readable, and a Vestige aura is a thin blue ring.","g":["elites","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-135","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each hall has its own echo: a cave, a stone room or open air, fading smoothly as you walk into a passage.","g":["elites","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-136","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The Caverns' fire falls burn in Daggerfall's own fire, the camera no longer snaps back out of walls, a faded Spirebridge plank is no longer solid, and the Weir Key has its own icon.","g":["elites","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9374-137","v":"0.1.9374","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Performance","x":"Moving platforms are drawn in far fewer draw calls, and those out of view are skipped.","g":["elites","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9377-001","v":"0.1.9377","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Arcane Essence","t":"Fix","x":"At an enchanting station, Reforge with Essence no longer stacks its buttons on top of each other. Each line of a piece now has its own Reforge button in a list under the piece's name and price, and the name is readable again instead of wrapping one word per line.","g":["enchanting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9377-002","v":"0.1.9377","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"Fix","x":"The profession stations' short notes (\"Needs 2 Arcane Essence; your Stores hold 1.\", \"Needs 2 Steel Ingot.\", the Stores-full note) now span the row under the piece, instead of being squeezed into a narrow column.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9381-001","v":"0.1.9381","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A stair rising above one of the Spire's chambers is now always there. Before, a handful of halls lost it, leaving the way on unreachable.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9381-002","v":"0.1.9381","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A Gust only pushes players on its own crossing, never someone on a bridge or floor high above it.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9398-001","v":"0.1.9398","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Loot Window","t":"New","x":"Chests, corpses and the wagon can be filtered by name, by item type, by rarity and by material. The rarity menu starts at Any Rarity and the material menu at Any Material. Each lists only what that pile holds, with a count beside each one. A piece whose card does not show its metal, such as an unidentified magic item or an artifact, is not listed under one.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9398-002","v":"0.1.9398","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Loot Window","t":"New","x":"Take all moves items from the list on screen into your pack, from the top, until the next item does not fit. Emptying someone else's cupboard this way is still stealing. Stash all does the same from the current pack page into your wagon, your own storage or the Materials Bag, and the button sits centred along the bottom edge of your item list. The pack page in use still starts on Weapons.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9398-003","v":"0.1.9398","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Loot Window","t":"New","x":"Looking at your own cupboard or chest, or at a stranger's cupboard that has already been stocked today, lists what it holds, the way a corpse or a pile does. Nothing is taken until you open it.","g":["loot","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9398-004","v":"0.1.9398","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Item Card","t":"New","x":"Armour and weapons of Rare quality and above say their metal (Iron, Ebony, and the rest) on the line under the name, even before they are identified. A Legendary keeps its own name, and so does one handed down as an heirloom.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9400-001","v":"0.1.9400","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"The $50 Hierophant tier now grants its title and glyph in game: the rose \"Hierophant\" and the crown beside your name. If you have already linked your Patreon, it appears on your next sign-in. You don't need to relink.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9404-001","v":"0.1.9404","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"WikiMaid - a new title, drawn amethyst into lilac into a bunny's blush.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9404-002","v":"0.1.9404","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Its glyph - a lilac bunny in a maid's lace headdress, beside her name (and on the account card, the chat roster and the travel view).","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9404-003","v":"0.1.9404","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Auras","t":"New","x":"Lilac Warren - a new aura: six lilac bunnies with cotton tails and little maid's headdresses hop round your feet on a ring of lilac light, leaving paw-print tracks that fade behind them. Every so often one does a happy binky. Sparkles of lilac, pink and white rise around you.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9409-001","v":"0.1.9409","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"Carrying a Weir Key no longer flags your character for review or freezes your trading. Any freeze and strike a Weir Key caused is lifted automatically.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9416-001","v":"0.1.9416","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"The Possessed Child can turn out to be a scam: sometimes the \"possessed\" child is faking, the Daedroth the priest warned of never appears, and the child runs off with the relic. Before this fix the journal said nothing at that point, so the quest looked broken. Now a journal entry records what happened and sends you back to the tavern where the guardian was staying. Someone there knows where they went. The entry is translated into every fully supported language.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-001","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"A player walking near you no longer stands frozen for minutes and then jumps to where they really are.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-002","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"A player who dies is laid down once: no more second body and second cry, and they no longer stand up for a moment on their own body.","g":["online","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-003","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Coming into a place where someone has just died (in the Wild, for example) shows their body instead of showing them standing there alive.","g":["online","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-004","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"A player who died in the Wild no longer stands up on their body for everyone when their connection blips.","g":["online","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-005","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"Stepping into a building and back out beside a body no longer lays a second body on top of it, and a party member's body no longer appears twice.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-006","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"A player who has already got up is no longer knocked down again by an old message about their death.","g":["online","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-007","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Players","t":"Fix","x":"When you cross into the next area, the area you left now sees you change your armour or clothes.","g":["online","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-008","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Mode","t":"Fix","x":"Setting your computer's clock back no longer makes you vanish from everyone's screen, leaves the game stuck on \"reconnecting\", or gets you refused with \"token expired\" when you enter a new place.","g":["online","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-009","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Mode","t":"Fix","x":"Entering a siege no longer has a rare chance of the server refusing you for good.","g":["online","siege"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-010","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Live Chat","t":"Fix","x":"When another tab or window takes over your session, the World tab no longer keeps showing the old \"Online\" count.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9426-011","v":"0.1.9426","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Mode","t":"Fix","x":"Crossing into the next area while the server is updating no longer disconnects you when the game looks for graves.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-001","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"/block <name> hides everything a player says to you: chat, invites, notes, letters, and trade, duel, wedding, card or journal requests. /unblock <name> undoes it, and /blocked lists who you've blocked.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-002","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"The block is tied to their account, so a new name or a new character doesn't get around it. It follows you to every device you sign in on.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-003","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"Click a player's name on any chat line to Report or Block them. A report sends the moderators that line and the lines before it.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-004","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"/report <name> [reason]: <note> sends everything that player said in your chat, with an optional note for the moderators. Reasons: harassment, hate, sexual, threat, spam, other.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-005","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"The game server signs every line it relays. A report can only carry words that player really said, so it can't be faked.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-006","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"/rules shows the Code of Conduct. Everyone agrees to it once, before their first chat line.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-007","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"Breaking the rules leads to a mute, then longer mutes (30 minutes, a day, a week), then a ban.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-008","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"Moderators now see every past mute and ban a player has had.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-009","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"If three established players report someone within an hour, that player is muted for 30 minutes until a moderator looks.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-010","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"Guest accounts and accounts under 14 days old can post one public channel line every 4 seconds. Party, guild and local chat aren't slowed, and a line sent too soon goes back in your chat box.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9434-011","v":"0.1.9434","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Chat Safety","t":"New","x":"/cases lists open reports, /case <name> shows one (the lines, reasons, notes and the AI reviewer's view), and /dismiss <name> closes it. /modhelp lists them.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9450-001","v":"0.1.9450","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Fix","x":"Under Physical Combat And Armor Overhaul (on by default), a weapon in your left hand no longer rolls a shield block. Dual wielding gives up the shield's block, as intended. An iron off-hand weapon had been blocking like a leather shield, taking 5-8% off the damage a nimble character took. Shields block as before.","g":["equipment","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9450-002","v":"0.1.9450","d":"2026-10-17","e":"First-Person Arms","t":"Fix","x":"Dual wielding in first person: the left-hand weapon is now the exact mirror of the right, in the left fist the way the right weapon sits in the right. Before, it could stand well off, depending on your Morrowind first-person skeleton. Third person is unchanged.","g":["morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9450-003","v":"0.1.9450","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Dwarven Thunderlock","t":"New","x":"The Dwarven Thunderlock is held like a rifle.","g":["thunderlock","morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9462-001","v":"0.1.9462","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Mode","t":"Fix","x":"A modified game client could stand huge hordes of enemies around nearby players, and mark every one of them as elite. Your game now refuses more enemies from any one player than an honest game can send, and believes only as many elites, revenants and Greater Giants as honest play produces.","g":["online","audit","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9462-002","v":"0.1.9462","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"A crafted piece could be listed on the market from a second device's stale tab while your live character still carried it. A crafted piece you list, auction or hand to a commission now leaves your character's own pack (or home) on the realm at the moment it goes up, and one you cancel, or that expires or goes unsold, comes back into your pack as the very piece that left.","g":["online","market","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9462-003","v":"0.1.9462","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Online Mode","t":"Rework","x":"Renown, raid rewards, bounty and orc camps, the Watch, silver finds and profession XP now count only for the realm character you are playing on this device. A character another device has taken up, or one whose trading is frozen, earns none until it is yours again. Honest play is unaffected.","g":["online","renown","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9462-004","v":"0.1.9462","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Project Legacy","t":"Rework","x":"Your family's record (Project Legacy) is checked against the family's own rules when it is saved to the realm.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9462-005","v":"0.1.9462","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"A crafted piece you bought back from another player can be sold again even while the character who made it has its trading frozen.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-001","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"New","x":"Master any two weapon skills (Long Blade, Short Blade, Axe, Blunt Weapon, Archery, Hand-to-Hand) and you can choose one of fifteen martial paths, such as the Blademaster, Ranger, Juggernaut, Assassin or Brawler. The choice is permanent, like a mastery.","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-002","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"New","x":"Each path has a passive of its own (for example the Vanguard's foes hit 10% lighter, and the Woodsman gets fatigue back on every kill) and a signature technique.","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-003","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"New","x":"The signature technique uses your Weapon Technique key whenever you wield one of the path's two weapons and that weapon has no technique of its own. A path with Archery has a bow form and a melee form, and the two share one cooldown. It works with the loot ladder off, and with the ladder off a looted weapon's own technique sleeps, so the signature takes the key.","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-004","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"Rework","x":"Techniques that give you a timed effect (Rallying Cleave, Cyclone, Phantom Strike, Earthsplitter, Savage Whirl) start it as you use them, so every foe the sweep reaches gets it.","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-005","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"New","x":"You can hold an arcane path and a martial path at once if you master two schools and two weapons.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-006","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"New","x":"You choose on the skill screen: W on the classic sheet, or the Martial Specialisation card under Master Skills on the enhanced skin. The game also asks once, the first time a path opens.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-007","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"A mastered weapon skill past 100 now pays in its own way. Until now it only raised your to-hit, which is capped at 97%.","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-008","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Axe: up to 80% harder against wounded foes (under half health).","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-009","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Master Skills","t":"Buff","x":"Short Blade: swings up to 40% faster.","g":["professions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-010","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Fists","t":"Buff","x":"Fists now benefit from your bonuses. Firmament fist stars, sets and loot powers never applied to bare-handed blows; now they do. Werewolf claws are unchanged.","g":["equipment","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-011","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Master Skills","t":"Fix","x":"Every short blade swings like a dagger. Tanto, Shortsword and Wakizashi were swinging at long-blade speed.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-012","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Firmament","t":"Rework","x":"Firmament: every weapon family now has two notables that raise its skill, and Axe and Blunt get a third. Blade Dancer, Iron Knuckles, Headsman and Bonebreaker keep every stat they had and gain the skill on top. The Ritual's *Battlemage's Focus* is now *Templar's Mace*, a mace notable. No star moved, so shared build codes still load.","g":["professions","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-013","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Stats Card","t":"Fix","x":"Opening the Stats page no longer changes your next blows. It used to spend a set's Riposte or Battlemage's Discipline and nudge the rounding of your damage bonuses.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9472-014","v":"0.1.9472","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"UI","x":"Choosing a specialisation (arcane or martial) now says so in one line that fits the classic screen.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-001","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Hold","t":"New","x":"F4 (rebindable, \"Cargo\" under Come Sail Away) opens the hold of the ship you're on: at the helm, on deck or in the cabin. Away from it, F4 opens the last ship you helmed, or the first ship in your fleet with a hold, wherever it's moored or laid up.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-002","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Hold","t":"New","x":"The helm panel has a Hold button, and so does each ship on the Fleet page.","g":["naval","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-003","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Pirates","t":"Fix","x":"If pirates raid you while you're ashore with your cabin ship and you beat them, the raid now ends. The crews that kept spawning, passive, after the fight are gone, and leftover raiders are removed from the street and from the room you're in.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-004","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ramming","t":"New","x":"Ram a ship hard enough and the two ships lock together for 20 seconds. The enemy ship lowers its sails and slows to a crawl, but its guns keep firing.","g":["naval","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-005","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Shot Types","t":"New","x":"Each battery can be loaded with round, grape, chain or heated shot. The broadsides share one load; the bow chasers and the stern guns each have their own.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-006","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Shot Types","t":"New","x":"Change the load with the mouse wheel while aiming, with the helm's Shot button, or with the new Shot key (unbound by default, under Combat). Switching unloads a ready battery and reloads it with the new shot.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-007","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"New","x":"Gun smoke drifts with the wind. A broadside leaves a bank of smoke that hangs over the fight and drifts downwind. Smoke from a burning or damaged ship trails away from it.","g":["naval","combat-visuals","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-008","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"New","x":"Near misses. A ball passing close to your ship whistles, louder the closer it passes. One landing right beside you throws water over the rail and rocks the deck.","g":["naval","audio","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-009","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"New","x":"Sinking ships. A ship that sinks while on fire may blow its powder magazine, and every player sees the same blast. Air bubbles up where a ship goes under.","g":["naval","combat-visuals","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-010","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"New","x":"Enemy crew on the card. The target card now shows the enemy's crew, and your broadside's tally says how many crew went down, so you can see grapeshot working.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-011","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"Fix","x":"Within 700 m of a hostile ship, a journey now runs at normal speed. Before, an avoided encounter could carry you past a pirate at up to 60x speed, with the pirate firing at that speed while you couldn't fire back from the Overworld.","g":["naval","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-012","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"Fix","x":"Online, sea combat near another player always runs in real time. One player's fast travel or helm time acceleration can no longer speed up enemy ships fighting someone else.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-013","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Flags","t":"New","x":"On the Fleet page, Colours opens a flag designer. Pick a shape (flag, swallowtail, pennant or burgee), a field colour with an optional division and second colour, a border, and a device with its own colour.","g":["naval","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-014","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Flags","t":"New","x":"The flag is real waving cloth at the masthead, in place of the old pennant, sized to the hull. Every player sees it.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-015","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"New","x":"Navies use their kingdom's paint and royal ensign: Daggerfall's blue with the dagger, Wayrest's crimson with the rose, Sentinel's gold with the sun.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-016","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Rework","x":"A ship that surrenders, sinks or is captured lowers its flag. Every player sees the same ship in the same colours. Cloth flags show on ships within 450 m, up to 24 at once. Further away, ships fly the old pennant, and a ship fading in or out of view fades its flag too.","g":["naval","rendering","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-017","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Paint","t":"New","x":"On the Fleet page, Paint lets you choose a colour for each part of your ship:","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-018","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Paint","t":"New","x":"Painting is free, works wherever the ship is, and every player sees it. Remove paint puts the ship back to its original look.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-019","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Paint","t":"New","x":"Ships with a cabin (Small Ship, Large Galley and Carrack) can also choose a wood stain for the cabin in the Paint panel. Walls, floor, beams and built-in furniture all take that stain. It applies the next time you enter the cabin, and the windows light up as before.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-020","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Deck Fittings","t":"New","x":"On the Fleet page, Deck opens a top-down plan of the deck. On a wide screen a long hull is shown bow to the right, so it's drawn larger.","g":["naval","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-021","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Deck Fittings","t":"New","x":"Fittings stand on the deck in the world and rock with the ship. You can walk around them and climb on them. Every player sees them.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-022","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Names","t":"New","x":"On the Fleet page, Show name puts your ship's name on both sides of the bow: a dark wooden board with the name in gold, in Daggerfall's own lettering, fitted to the curve of the hull just below the rail. Hide name removes it.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-023","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Captain's Stars","t":"New","x":"You now have a captain level (up to 30). Captain XP comes from sinking and capturing ships, beating off boarders, claiming prizes, finishing contracts, distance sailed, treasure charts, charting isles and selling goods at the exchange.","g":["naval","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-024","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Captain's Stars","t":"New","x":"The Master (left) improves seamanship: speed under sail and oars, turning, cargo, hull, repairs, and better prices at the exchange.","g":["naval","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-025","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Captain's Stars","t":"New","x":"Keystones give a big bonus with a cost (for example, Master of the Wind: +12% speed under sail, -12% under oars). Stars apply to every ship you own. Removing or changing stars is free.","g":["naval","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-026","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Refits","t":"New","x":"After the shipwright's three refit tiers, each upgrade line now has nine metal tiers: Steel, Silver, Elven, Dwarven, Mithril, Adamantium, Ebony, Orcish and Daedric. Each needs a captain level, from 3 for Steel up to 28 for Daedric.","g":["naval","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-027","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Refits","t":"New","x":"Each tier needs ingots of its metal, or weapons and plate armour of that metal for the shipwright to melt down. Only plain items are melted: never gear you're wearing, locked or bound gear, quest items, artifacts, player-made, enchanted, conjured, Magic-or-better, Legendary or socketed items. Ingots are used first.","g":["naval","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-028","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Buff","x":"With no enemies near, no ship chasing you, and no boarding or aiming going on, your ship's sails and oars give 15% more speed.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-029","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Etheric Sea","t":"New","x":"Every port isle in the Eltheric Ocean now sells at least one ordinary trade good alongside its ether goods. Veilhaven sells spice. The sea chart's isle card shows it.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-030","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ships","t":"Rework","x":"Ship text no longer calls a ship \"her\" or \"she\". Messages, buttons, cards and hints across the sea, the Fleet page, the shipyard, the crew hall, the Captain's Stars, the sea chart, the tutorials and the crew's chatter now say \"the ship\", \"this ship\" or \"it\", in plain wording.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-031","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Refits","t":"Fix","x":"Metal refits never melt valuable gear. The shipwright only melts plain items, never ones you're wearing, locked or bound, player-made, enchanted (including your own enchantments), conjured with Create Item, Magic or better, Legendary, or socketed. Ingots still go first, with iron ingots before steel ones for an Iron requirement. A refit you can pay for with steel ingots and steel weapons together is no longer refused.","g":["naval","smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-032","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Captain's Stars","t":"Fix","x":"The Captain's Stars apply to every ship. Accepting stars now updates laid-up and packed ships too, so a ship summoned later no longer uses stars you've since removed. Keystone costs (like Boarders Away's hull penalty or Merchant Prince's gun damage penalty) now apply in combat. Taking a star mid-fight no longer reloads your guns. The Quick Dial key now asks before closing the stars window with unaccepted changes.","g":["naval","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-033","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Exchange","t":"Fix","x":"The exchange no longer lets you buy a cheap good back at the price you sold it for when your trade stars are maxed.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-034","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"Fix","x":"Other players see the same fight. A ship sinking on another player's screen now plays its sinking sound, and its powder magazine explodes on every screen alike. Chain shot and grapeshot now kill crew on ships another player controls. A rammed ship being boarded keeps its flag up on other players' screens. Ramming a ship another player controls locks it for boarding on every screen.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-035","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"Fix","x":"Combat fixes. The shot wheel steps once per scroll on a trackpad. The tally's crew count matches what the enemy actually loses. A hit on one of your moored ships no longer flashes your helm plate or shakes your camera. Sailing up to a ship that's already sinking no longer replays its sinking or explosion. A ram that sinks a ship no longer tells you to board it. Your hull bar is correct when you take the helm of a different ship.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-036","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Names","t":"Fix","x":"Name boards no longer show on hidden players' boats or float in the room when you're indoors, and other players see a board shown or hidden right away.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-037","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Deck Fittings","t":"Fix","x":"Deck crates no longer disappear from the deck after you've visited several houses.","g":["naval","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-038","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Paint","t":"Fix","x":"Another player's cabin shows its original look, not your own ship's stain.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-039","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ship Hold","t":"Fix","x":"The hold. Taking cargo out of a packed ship's hold no longer counts its weight twice. Putting a packed ship's parts in its own hold no longer loses the ship. A rowboat's plunder can now be opened. F4 no longer opens a ship you can't otherwise reach. The ship's hold can now be bound to a controller button.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-040","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"The Fleet page no longer says a hold or deck plan opened when it didn't.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-041","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Naval Combat","t":"Fix","x":"The aiming arcs stay visible in a crowded fight full of grapeshot and chain shot.","g":["naval","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9503-042","v":"0.1.9503","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Ships","t":"Performance","x":"Smoother frames. No stutter the first time a named or painted ship comes into view. Painted sea ships no longer slow rendering. Deck fittings, near-miss checks, the out-of-combat speed check and damaged-ship smoke are all faster.","g":["naval","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-001","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Gear","t":"New","x":"Sworn revenants now have ten gear slots: a weapon, a shield, a helm, two pauldrons, a cuirass, gauntlets, greaves, boots and a charm. Open the Companions page (pause menu, Holdings), press Gear on a companion's card, and give it pieces from your pack. Take back returns a piece to your pack.","g":["revenants","companions","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-002","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Gear","t":"New","x":"A revenant's rank limits what it can bear:","g":["revenants","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-003","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Gear","t":"New","x":"A piece you give replaces the one it would have rolled for itself, and its rarity bonuses apply to it.","g":["revenants","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-004","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Arts","t":"New","x":"One revenant in three is born with an art: Mending, Ward, War Cry, Siphon, Barrage or Nova.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-005","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Arts","t":"New","x":"Against you, from Rank II (with Enhanced AI):","g":["revenants","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-006","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Arts","t":"New","x":"For you, once sworn, at any rank:","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-007","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Missions","t":"New","x":"Press Mission on a sworn revenant to send it to any of Tamriel's nine provinces.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-008","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Missions","t":"New","x":"Each province has its own danger and its own goods: Skyrim's orichalcum and pelts, Morrowind's ebony and Dwemer metal, Black Marsh's venom.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9514-009","v":"0.1.9514","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Missions","t":"Other","x":"Up to two revenants can be abroad at once. Recall brings one back at once, empty-handed, and it must rest from the road. The page asks before recalling.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9517-001","v":"0.1.9517","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The Athenaeum can be solved again. In most breaches the Orrery's stones could not be turned. The crosshair never named a stone, the count stayed at \"Stones true: 0 of 6\", and the hall's door never opened. Each stone now answers your crosshair just above its gold ring: look there to turn it forward or back an hour.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9524-001","v":"0.1.9524","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guilds","t":"Fix","x":"Becoming a vampire no longer shuts you out of the Dark Brotherhood or the Thieves Guild. You can only join those two by invitation, and the invitation is never sent twice, so turning used to lock members out until they were cured. Your membership and rank now carry over when you turn, and stay with you if you're cured.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9524-002","v":"0.1.9524","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guilds","t":"Fix","x":"If you're already a vampire and lost the Brotherhood or the Thieves Guild, you get it back, rank and all, the first time the game reads your guilds after this update.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9543-001","v":"0.1.9543","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"Expelled from a guild, or turned away for your standing? The guild now tells you how to get back in. At its hall, you see your standing, the standing it takes members at, how many quests bring you back there, and how fast it recovers on its own. On the classic look, the guild's refusal when you ask to join says the same.","g":["guild","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9543-002","v":"0.1.9543","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guilds","t":"Rework","x":"You can always ask a guild's quest-giver for work as a stranger, even after an expulsion. Each quest done raises your standing with that guild by 5.","g":["guild","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9543-003","v":"0.1.9543","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Standing","t":"Rework","x":"A standing below 0 also recovers a point every 7 days of your character's own time. Resting and travelling count, and online so does time logged off.","g":["guild","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9543-004","v":"0.1.9543","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Guild Hall","t":"New","x":"If the guild also wants skills you don't have yet, it says which. A hall shut for the Season says the guild's halls in other regions still have work.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9543-005","v":"0.1.9543","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Standing","t":"New","x":"The Standing page shows the quest count under each guild, temple or knightly order that would turn you away.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-001","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Stars","t":"New","x":"Every sworn revenant now has its own star tree, built like the Firmament and the Captain's Stars. Open the Companions page (pause menu, Holdings) and press Stars on a companion's card.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-002","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Stars","t":"New","x":"Levels:","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-003","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Stars","t":"New","x":"The Blade: health and damage. Its keystones are Deathless (+25% health, -10% damage) and Bloodrage (+20% damage, -10% health).","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-004","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Stars","t":"New","x":"The Road: missions and loyalty.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-005","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Stars","t":"New","x":"It uses the same window as the Captain's Stars: click a star to take it and the stars on the way to it, and right-click to remove it. Changes are pending until you press Accept.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-006","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Stars","t":"Other","x":"Health and damage change at once, and taking a star back takes its health back too.","g":["revenants","companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9558-007","v":"0.1.9558","d":"2026-10-17","e":"Revenant Arts","t":"Rework","x":"However many Menders are at your side, together they heal you at most once a minute (every 45 seconds with a fully hasted Grave).","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9600-001","v":"0.1.9600","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"In an Athenaeum, the six riddles that give each Orrery stone its true hour now appear on the HUD, under \"Turn the Orrery true.\"","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9600-002","v":"0.1.9600","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each stone shows its name and the hour its hand stands at (*Wayrest - 4*) above it. The labels update after every turn.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9600-003","v":"0.1.9600","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Turning a stone from too far away now tells you to \"Stand closer to the stone.\" Before, the turn was silently ignored.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9610-001","v":"0.1.9610","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Bug Reports","t":"New","x":"Type /bug in chat to tell the developers about an exploit, a bug or a security problem. On the enhanced skin you can also open the mailbox beside the hourglass in the pause menu and press Report a bug or exploit. Only the developers who read reports can see it. Other players and moderators can't.","g":["chat","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9610-002","v":"0.1.9610","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Bug Reports","t":"New","x":"Choose what it is, give it a short title, and say what happens and how to make it happen. The form shows what's sent with it (your username and the game's build) before you send.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9610-003","v":"0.1.9610","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Bug Reports","t":"New","x":"Your reports are listed under the form, each showing whether a developer has read it and whether it was fixed.","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9610-004","v":"0.1.9610","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Bug Reports","t":"Other","x":"Please keep exploits out of chat, Discord and the Notice Board until they're fixed. (To report another *player*, /report <name> still goes to the moderators.)","g":["chat"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9619-001","v":"0.1.9619","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Dungeon Scaling","t":"Nerf","x":"From character level 10 and Renown 15, the foes in dungeons and the wilds now keep pace with you. Each level past 10 a foe hits 7% harder and stands 4% tougher. Each Renown past 15 adds 1% to its hits and 0.5% to its health. Both compound, up to level 30 and Renown 50:","g":["elites","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9619-002","v":"0.1.9619","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Dungeon Scaling","t":"Nerf","x":"Plain foes, champions, elites, revenants and the open zone's foes all answer you, on top of what they already were. The early game is unchanged: nothing moves at or under level 10 and Renown 15.","g":["elites","renown"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9619-003","v":"0.1.9619","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Dungeon Scaling","t":"Other","x":"Towns and buildings, the city watch and your allies.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9619-004","v":"0.1.9619","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Dungeon Scaling","t":"Other","x":"A foe hits each player at that player's own level. Its health is set by whoever's game built it.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9632-001","v":"0.1.9632","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"Characters whose trading was still frozen for a week (\"The realm's law has held this character three times...\") because of the Weir Key are unfrozen. A forged piece a character still carries still holds its trade until it is gone.","g":["online","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9632-002","v":"0.1.9632","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Online Mode","t":"Rework","x":"Other players no longer float in mid-air for players on an outdated copy of the game. An outdated copy (an old desktop app or a page left open since an update) is now asked to update before it joins the world online: reload the page, or download the latest desktop release.","g":["online","desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-001","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"Not every elite or champion can become a revenant any more. About one in four is marked Unquiet, and its title says so (\"Unquiet Elite Orc\"). Only a marked foe can rise.","g":["revenants","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-002","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Buff","x":"At most three revenants hunt you at once, and no new one rises while three do. None of yours is pushed out to make room.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-003","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"A revenant comes back after two to four days (it was one to three).","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-004","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"A marked foe breaks and runs at a third of its health, one time in two, as fast as a bolting beast. Most revenants are now born by getting away, not by killing you - however fast you run.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-005","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Rework","x":"A revenant ranks up every time it gets away from you, or you from it.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-006","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"When a revenant gets away in the open, it goes to ground in the nearest dungeon and leaves a trail there. The dungeon appears on your map at once.","g":["revenants","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-007","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Leave it alone and its wounds heal: the oldest one every five days. The Revenants page says when the next one will.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-008","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A revenant that seeks mastery trains while it waits. It learns to counter whatever weapon or habit you have hurt it with most, such as your blade, your arrows or your footwork, and a card tells you when it has.","g":["revenants","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-009","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"The day a revenant comes back to hunt you, you are warned in its own way:","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-010","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Nerf","x":"Each rank adds more: +40% health, +15% damage and +3 levels for a class foe. Your sworn revenants keep the old values.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-011","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Smoke (people): it throws down smoke and is lost to sight as it runs. A blow still finds it.","g":["revenants","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-012","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"When it gets away, the blow that broke it leaves a wound, and the card says which (\"It bears the wound you left: Lamed\").","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-013","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"Vengeance (the brutal, the zealous, the unhinged): it comes for you sooner, and more often.","g":["revenants","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-014","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"New","x":"A rank-V revenant that gets away once more becomes the Dread. It goes to ground in its lair for good, and every town knows where. Only one Dread waits for you at a time.","g":["revenants","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-015","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Online, another player's revenant that kills you no longer becomes a fourth revenant of yours and pushes one of yours out.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-016","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A foe that was running to become a revenant no longer vanishes without a body when you already have three: it turns and fights.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9652-017","v":"0.1.9652","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A revenant's blink or sink no longer completes while a window is open over the game.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9659-001","v":"0.1.9659","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Online Foes","t":"Fix","x":"Another player's monsters can no longer hit you twice as hard by claiming a revenant's signature strike. Only real revenants strike that way.","g":["online","revenants","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9659-002","v":"0.1.9659","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Online Foes","t":"Fix","x":"In dungeons, another player's monsters can only cast spells their own kind knows, and a paralysed one casts nothing.","g":["online","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9659-003","v":"0.1.9659","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Online Foes","t":"Fix","x":"One player can no longer make every monster near you a champion: at most 17 of theirs count as champions on your screen, more than honest play ever reaches.","g":["online","elites","audit"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-001","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"New","x":"A new Growth tab in the pause menu, next to Stats. Everything about how your character grows is in one place:","g":["ascension","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-002","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Level-Up Window","t":"New","x":"Level: your attributes, and when you have a level up waiting, where you place your points and press Ascend. On a smaller window it opens full screen. If you leave before pressing Ascend, your points stay unspent and the bonus never re-rolls.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-003","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"New","x":"Specialisations: a guide to all thirty paths, fifteen arcane and fifteen martial, including the ones you can't choose yet. Each path shows:","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-004","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Firmament","t":"Rework","x":"Firmament: the online passive tree, now drawn inside the menu.","g":["online","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-005","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Captain's Stars","t":"Rework","x":"Captain's Stars: your ship captain's tree, now drawn inside the menu too.","g":["naval","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-006","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"New","x":"The Firmament and the Captain's Stars can go full screen with one press. On a phone, each opens over the whole screen.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-007","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"New","x":"The page list marks what's waiting: a level up, a specialisation to choose, captain's stars to set. The Stats page's Growth button shows the total.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-008","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"Rework","x":"The Stats page's Ascend and Firmament buttons, the specialisation cards on the Master Skills page and the Captain page's Open the stars now all lead to the Growth tab.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-009","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"Rework","x":"Classic interface: the S (arcane paths) and W (martial paths) rows on the character sheet now show whenever your class can earn a path, and open the same guide.","g":["classic-mode","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-010","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"UI","x":"Clearer descriptions: every specialisation's passive and signature, the level-up screen and the Firmament are reworded in plain terms - for example \"deal 20% more damage\" instead of \"strike 20% harder\", \"Spend your points\" instead of \"Choose what rises\", \"Not enough points.\" instead of \"You lack the points for that.\" The level-up screen and the Firmament are now translated into every language.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-011","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"Fix","x":"With unsaved star changes, switching page or tab, pressing the character sheet key, the pack key, the QuickDial key, tapping outside the menu or opening a timer's board now asks first, the same way Escape does - and asks again if you change more stars after the first warning. This includes a revenant's stars.","g":["ascension","revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-012","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"Fix","x":"Classic interface: with a level up being spent on the character sheet, the S and W rows no longer open the Growth tab, which could lose the level's bonus points.","g":["classic-mode","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-013","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"Fix","x":"The guide no longer shows a path as reachable when your mastery slots can't hold both of its skills (for example two minor schools of magic).","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-014","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Level-Up Window","t":"Fix","x":"The level-up fanfare plays once per level, not every time you open the Level page.","g":["audio","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-015","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Pause Menu","t":"Fix","x":"Enter on a menu tab no longer presses Ascend; typing in the account window no longer moves the sky behind it.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-016","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Martial Specialisations","t":"Fix","x":"The Brawler's, Bloodmage's and Berserker's descriptions now say exactly what they do.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9687-017","v":"0.1.9687","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Your own Disintegrate no longer deletes your revenant. It still breaks through a revenant's last stand and its will, but now it brings the revenant to its knees like any other killing blow. You choose to Kill it (its trophy weapon drops) or Spare it (it joins you as a companion). A revenant already killed this way stays dead.","g":["revenants","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9699-001","v":"0.1.9699","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Rework","x":"With two weapons drawn in the Morrowind first-person view, your arms now stand a little wider. Long blades no longer cross over each other in the middle of the screen. How far the arms spread depends on the weapons: a pair of longswords spreads further than a pair of daggers. The arms ease out when you draw and ease back when you sheathe. Third person is unchanged.","g":["morrowind","first-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9699-002","v":"0.1.9699","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Dwarven Thunderlock","t":"Rework","x":"In the Morrowind first-person view, the Dwarven Thunderlock no longer rides up over your crosshair when you raise it to shoot. The aimed gun now sits below the middle of the screen, with your left hand still visible on its forend. The lowered idle stance and third person are unchanged.","g":["morrowind","first-person","thunderlock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9718-001","v":"0.1.9718","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Wagon","t":"Fix","x":"When your wagon stops, companions riding in the back now climb down over the side, where a player rider would, instead of dropping through the bed and getting stuck inside the wagon. A parked wagon also no longer closes its body around a companion standing where it was laid.","g":["companions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9718-002","v":"0.1.9718","d":"2026-10-18","e":"FPS Counter","t":"UI","x":"The FPS counter's draw count now includes what a building draws through its windows (view) and the shadow maps (shadow). It also shows whether VSync is off or a Frame Rate Cap is set.","g":["fps-counter"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9718-003","v":"0.1.9718","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Performance","x":"Animated loot piles no longer keep being animated behind the scenes after you leave a room, load a save or a pile is emptied. A pile laid again where it now lies keeps animating instead of standing still.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9718-004","v":"0.1.9718","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"Putting a helm on or taking it off no longer leaves the old head picture in GPU memory, and a slow load can no longer put back the helm you just took off.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9718-005","v":"0.1.9718","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Morrowind People","t":"Fix","x":"A helm put on while the large HUD is first loading now shows on its head.","g":["morrowind","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9718-006","v":"0.1.9718","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"Players can fight each other in the PvP zone's dungeons again, as intended. Before, every attack on another player underground was refused. Their blood now shows in the dungeon.","g":["online","blood"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-001","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Specialisation Reset","t":"New","x":"You can now give up your arcane or your martial specialisation for 200,000 gold each. Open the Growth tab in the pause menu, go to Specialisations, open your chosen path, and press Reset. A confirmation shows the price, what you lose, and which paths you can pick afterwards.","g":["ascension","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-002","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Specialisation Reset","t":"New","x":"Your mastered skills stay mastered. After a reset you can choose any path your masteries unlock, including the same one.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-003","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Specialisation Reset","t":"New","x":"If you bought the path's signature spell, it stays in your spellbook as an ordinary spell.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-004","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Specialisation Reset","t":"Economy","x":"Online, the price is paid from your coins, then letters of credit, then your bank account. Offline it is paid in coins or letters of credit.","g":["online","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-005","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Specialisation Reset","t":"QoL","x":"If no other path of that kind could ever open for you, the Reset button explains why instead of charging you.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-006","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Specialisation Reset","t":"UI","x":"The specialisation choice boxes now say what a later reset costs instead of \"cannot be undone\".","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-007","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Growth Tab","t":"Fix","x":"A newly chosen specialisation's stat bonuses apply at once instead of at the next magic round.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9725-008","v":"0.1.9725","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Pause Menu","t":"Fix","x":"The Yes/No confirmation in the pause menu now keeps keyboard focus inside the box and answers only once.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9742-001","v":"0.1.9742","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Overworld","t":"Performance","x":"When you travel fast in the Overworld, the world no longer spends time building ground you've already passed. Holes in the view and drops to 1x speed on roads with turns are much rarer.","g":["overworld","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-001","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Corpse Loot","t":"Fix","x":"A party member's kill no longer reads \"Empty\" when it is full. Press it and you open the body like any other: you see what is in it and take what you choose, piece by piece, with Take all, or with Quick Loot.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-002","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Corpse Loot","t":"Fix","x":"Taking from a body someone else killed can no longer wipe out their loot. A slow connection used to destroy the pieces in transit; a take now lands exactly once, however late the answer comes, and two players taking the same piece at the same moment get one copy between them - the second hears \"Someone took that first.\"","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-003","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Corpse Loot","t":"Fix","x":"Anything you put into another player's kill comes back to you when you close the window, even if they left or lost connection while it was open.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-004","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"A building's cupboards and chests are one shared list for everyone inside. Closing a window no longer brings back an item someone else took, and no longer erases one someone else put in. Two players opening a cupboard at the same moment now see the same contents, and nothing either of them took or put in is lost when the game settles on one.","g":["loot","online","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-005","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"Taking part of a stack from someone else's cupboard can no longer leave you with a copy when another player took it first.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-006","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"An item you put into a cupboard that the building's host never accepted (an older game version) comes back to you when you leave.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-007","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"Take all and Stash all on a cupboard land every piece, however many there are.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-008","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Rework","x":"A find from a coffin or other search spot is shared by your party the same way a dungeon pile is: one list, one copy of each piece, no matter who closes their window first.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-009","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"Two separate groups searching the same coffin each loot their own find.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-010","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"Searching a spot again after its five hours locks it for your whole party again.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-011","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"Take all on a long dungeon list now always lands every piece. A pile from a newer game version shows its name instead of \"Empty\".","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-012","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Fix","x":"Putting a stack into a dungeon pile and taking part of it back no longer loses the rest.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9790-013","v":"0.1.9790","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Shared Containers","t":"Other","x":"Players on an older version of the game still see the old behaviour in the same room; reloading the page brings them onto the new rules.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-001","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"A boss no longer throws a blow you have no fair way out of. It weighs each attack first and picks another, or moves in, if the attack would leave someone nowhere to stand. This includes the safe havens of a pending CHECK, burning pools from earlier blows, and a duel's ring of fire.","g":["combat-visuals","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-002","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"If a boss can't fairly hit someone, for example a player on a balcony, it now turns on the rest of the party for a few seconds instead of walking at them.","g":["combat-visuals","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-003","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Feints no longer glint. A feint that is cut off is cancelled at the right moment on every screen.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-004","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A burst of damage that crosses two phase lines now plays both phase turns in order, each with its card.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-005","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"The Valkynaz signatures (the Conquest, the Chaining, the Eclipse) now start at their second phase. The Conquest plants its banners one at a time, and each third burns until its banner falls.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-006","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"The Last Spellmaster's Arcane Lattice now sweeps the whole floor in strips, rim to rim. Her Final Examination returns later in the fight. A caged player is never struck while the cage holds them.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-007","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The Wellhead Wyrm takes flight again from its risen perches, and its breath reaches the far rim of its court.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-008","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Garoth's Wellfire is aimed at its target.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-009","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Duels keep their lord inside the ring, and ring-filling blows stay out of them.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-010","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The Armsmaster's guard glint shows only on lords, and the Wingbeat's lane is warned a second ahead.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-011","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Broken Way. The bridges between sections now break apart. You cross them on Drifts, Beats, Crumbles, Pendulums, Vents and Rails, in every direction. Long bridges break several times.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-012","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Forks are real choices. The Low Road has its own platforming, and the High Road keeps time with Beats.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-013","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"In fight halls, the rooms come before the trial, and the door opens right after it. The trial waits for your party to arrive: its waves, the Scriptorium's quiet and the Deserter all hold until you're there.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-014","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Approaches mix two kinds of platforms. Passages have real gaps, Drops really drop, Rails never collide, and Pendulums are checked across your whole jump.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-015","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Alcoves sit at the edge of the court, behind a doorway in its wall. Balconies and other fittings are where you can actually reach them.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-016","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The running leap is off on the Spire's and the Hour's proven courses, so a jump lands where the course was proven to land.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-017","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A collapsing tube in a routed hall starts falling when you reach it, not on a fixed timer.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-018","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Falling through a void zone to a lower way sends you back instead of letting you skip ahead. A Drop is never mistaken for the void.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-019","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Vents burn for their whole eruption. A Pendulum hits exactly where it is drawn. A Drift's chains no longer pass through floors above it.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-020","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Broken bridge ends are drawn closed, and every hall of a large circle shows the outlines of its Beats and Crumbles.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-021","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Each room's floor counts as new ground for the toll.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-022","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Other","x":"Breaches opened before this update keep their old halls until they end.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-023","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Every song in the Elite Breach has been re-orchestrated. String sections, brass, choir and organ now play as full ensembles with stereo width instead of single thin voices, and the war drums are real taiko, kick, toms and snare with weight and attack.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-024","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"The fights drive harder: driving low strings under everything, the legion's chant, brass blasts at the top of each phrase, cymbal swells into each one, and high string shrieks as a Court reaches its last phase.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-025","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"The halls between fights build as you go: each one starts sparse and climbs to a peak, in each band's own colour. The Galleries have timpani and fanfares, the Cairn a soul-bell and chant, the Shade a rippling harp and a heartbeat, and the Wellhead anvils.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-026","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"A trial now breaks down and builds back up. The last two minutes of the count have a ticking clock.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-027","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"The Spire has its own ambience. The dungeon drips and creaking doors are gone. In their place you hear the roar of the void, a drone in each band's own voice, and in the distance the legion's war horns and drums, daedra roaring, and stone breaking and falling into the abyss.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-028","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"Each band has its own far-off sounds: a cracked bell, wailing souls, howls and whispers, a forge's hammers.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9824-029","v":"0.1.9824","d":"2026-10-18","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"While a Court's lord sleeps, you can hear it breathe.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9832-001","v":"0.1.9832","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Fix","x":"A revenant that kills you no longer takes a letter of credit. It never takes gold, and a letter is gold.","g":["revenants","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9832-002","v":"0.1.9832","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Fix","x":"If a revenant is already holding one of your letters, it comes back to your wallet the next time you load.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9832-003","v":"0.1.9832","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Fix","x":"A sworn revenant that deserts gives back any letter it carried.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9832-004","v":"0.1.9832","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Death Screen","t":"Rework","x":"The death screen now names any letters of credit you lost and what they were worth.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9832-005","v":"0.1.9832","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Death Screen","t":"Fix","x":"If your character's trading is frozen, the death screen now says that what you dropped was lost outright. Before, it said nothing.","g":["death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9832-006","v":"0.1.9832","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Fix","x":"Selling a very large batch of gear at once (for example dozens of Daedric pieces) no longer pays you millions of gold *below* zero. A sale that large now pays its real price, as a letter of credit. A purchase that large no longer pays you either.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9836-001","v":"0.1.9836","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Overworld","t":"Performance","x":"While you travel in the Overworld, the land ahead of you loads up to three times faster. Fast travel drops to 1x speed far less often, including on straight roads.","g":["overworld","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9836-002","v":"0.1.9836","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Overworld","t":"Other","x":"While ground is still loading, the Overworld view may run at about 30 fps instead of 60. Once the land is built it goes back to normal.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9841-001","v":"0.1.9841","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Weir Keys","t":"Fix","x":"Tapping or picking the top line of the Weir Key's window (\"Weir Keys: 3 - one will be staked.\", or \"You hold no Weir Key.\") no longer closes the window and leaves the key saying \"The Spire already asks where you begin.\" The line is your key count, not a choice: the window now stays up with its list. The quest warning line under it behaves the same way.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9841-002","v":"0.1.9841","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Weir Keys","t":"Fix","x":"Answering No to \"Go without ...?\" in the Weir Key's window now brings the list of starts back, instead of quietly closing the window.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9841-003","v":"0.1.9841","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Weir Keys","t":"Fix","x":"Using a Weir Key from your pack now closes the pack so the window can open. Before, the window never appeared while the pack was up.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-001","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Economy","t":"New","x":"Every city, town and village now has its own economy online, rated from Destitute to Booming. Hover a town on the Held Map or the Overworld to see its economy, whether its market is rising or falling, how its prices compare with the region's usual ones, and who holds the area.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-002","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Economy","t":"Economy","x":"A Booming town's shops ask up to a quarter less. A Destitute town's ask up to a quarter more, and pay less for what you sell.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-003","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Economy","t":"New","x":"What you do in a town raises it: walking its streets, buying at its players' traders, and driving a raid from its gates. Gold spent never moves a town, and each player's part is capped per town per day.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-004","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Economy","t":"New","x":"Townsfolk talk about how trade is going in their town. A Booming town holds a second market day each week, and a Destitute one holds a market only every other week.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-005","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Map","t":"New","x":"A town's card names the guilds that hold patronage of the area's guild chapters.","g":["guild","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-006","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Economy","t":"New","x":"A port town's sea lanes lift its economy: the busier the harbour, the better its town does.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-007","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Exchange","t":"Economy","x":"A port's exchange now prices by its town's economy. A Booming port sells goods cheaper, and a Destitute one dearer. The Exchange tab shows the port's economy.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-008","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Exchange","t":"Rework","x":"Every deal at a port's exchange raises that town's share of the players' activity, like trading at a player's stall.","g":["naval","market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-009","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Economy","x":"On a seat's Market Day, and for a holder's members, shops now pay less for what you sell as well as asking less. Essentials can no longer be bought and sold back for a profit there. A friend's caravan on the road now gives its friend's price both ways.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-010","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Economy","x":"A shop never pays more for an item than you paid a shop for it, so carrying shop goods from a cheap region to a dear one no longer makes gold. Loot you find sells as before. Improving a bought item (setting a gem, honing, reforging) is now paid for when you sell it.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-011","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Rework","x":"Materials bought at a shop stay in your pack instead of going into the Stores. Crafting stations still use them straight from your pack.","g":["market","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-012","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Gem Sockets","t":"Fix","x":"A gem bought at a shop keeps its shop price when you set it in a socket and when you take it out again.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9853-013","v":"0.1.9853","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Town Map","t":"UI","x":"A town's card now shows two chapter patrons by name and a count of the rest, with the guild holding the most chapters first. It shows them only when the card has room, so it fits on a phone screen.","g":["guild","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9855-001","v":"0.1.9855","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"In the Elite Breach, a bridge that runs above a Gust course no longer blows you off it. A Gust course laid straight after another one, on a different line or height, now gusts as it should.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9858-001","v":"0.1.9858","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"The Shadow Fang title now carries moderator powers: /mute, /unmute, /ban, /unban, /strikes and the reports' queue. Moderators can't ban or mute a Shadow Fang holder.","g":["online","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-001","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Professions","t":"UI","x":"Smithing, Building, Outfitting and Provisioning's cooking now say on the Professions page where their stations are, how to work them from the Stores page (press your Professions key, then Holdings > Stores), and what earns XP.","g":["professions","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-002","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Tutorials","t":"New","x":"A new Crafting page in Tutorials lists which shops hold which station.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-003","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Controls Screen","t":"UI","x":"The Professions key's row in Controls now says it opens your Professions page.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-004","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Homes","t":"Rework","x":"Your other characters can now use the crafting stations in a home your account owns, the same as the character who bought it: forge, workbench, loom, mason's and jeweller's benches, alchemy and enchanting. The home's storage still belongs to the character who bought it.","g":["homes","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-005","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Weapon Techniques","t":"Fix","x":"Leap and dash weapon techniques, Flying Kick included, now work from the ground while you wear Slowfalling gear such as The Raven's Wings, and they land where you aim.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-006","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The Twin Lords: a Sapper that reaches a fallen twin now crumbles instead of healing it. A fallen twin can no longer get up early, untouchable, while still attacking.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-007","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Valkynaz Ilthys's banners can now be broken with arrows and spells from the court floor.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-008","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"UI","x":"While two banners stand, her health bar shows a hatched \"Warded\" cage.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-009","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"UI","x":"The Last Armsmaster's ring of fire is now drawn on the floor, and a solo challenge is told it is fought in the open.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-010","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A solo player who defeats him mid-challenge is no longer told the challenge went unmet.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-011","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Players who are down or watching see the ring too.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-012","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"UI","x":"Winch plates are marked in gold.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-013","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Boss callouts no longer go silent after a dozen lines in a long fight.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-014","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Bodies and their loot no longer come back when you re-enter a dungeon while another player in it has the game in the background. The room now follows whoever is actually playing. A player returning from being away rejoins without overwriting the room.","g":["online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-015","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"If that background player's game then closed without saying goodbye (a crash, a lost connection), the room could stay stuck the same way. It now moves on to whoever is playing.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-016","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Controls Screen","t":"UI","x":"The Controls menu now names the window the L and N keys open. On Enhanced Plus that is the Chronicle, on its Quests or Notes page; on Classic it is the logbook.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-017","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"FPS Counter","t":"New","x":"The FPS counter now remembers stutters. When a frame took 50 ms or longer in the last minute, a \"hitch\" line shows the worst one and how much of that frame was the game's own work.","g":["fps-counter"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9891-018","v":"0.1.9891","d":"2026-10-19","e":"FPS Counter","t":"Fix","x":"The FPS counter no longer shows \"0 fps\" after you switch away from the game and come back.","g":["fps-counter"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9894-001","v":"0.1.9894","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Ship Hold","t":"Fix","x":"A packed ship's parts now weigh only her hull (120 kg at most). Cargo in her hold no longer adds to that, so storing things in a packed ship's hold can't make her too heavy to pick back up.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9894-002","v":"0.1.9894","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"Ship parts that were already too heavy to take out of a chest or other storage are fixed when you load your save. Nothing in their hold is lost.","g":["naval","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9894-003","v":"0.1.9894","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Ships","t":"Fix","x":"When your character is too weak to carry a ship's parts, the pick-up now says \"The ship's parts are too heavy for you to carry.\" It used to tell you to unload cargo, which didn't help.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-001","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Fix","x":"Magic items from guild vendors, shops and loot no longer come on wands or holy items when their power only works while worn. An \"Enhances skill\" or \"Cast when held\" item is now always something you can equip.","g":["loot","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-002","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Enchanting","t":"Fix","x":"An enchanted jewel that used to be a Wand, held in a guild vault or market listing and turned into an Amulet when you loaded it, no longer gets your character flagged by the anti-cheat check.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-003","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Spellbook","t":"Fix","x":"The spellbook keeps your place: picking a spell no longer jumps the list back to the top, and the list now scrolls on its own so the spell you picked stays in view beside it (below it on a phone).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-004","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Chronicle","t":"Fix","x":"The Chronicle keeps its place when you fold a quest or note, remove a note, or share or abandon a quest, and a long Chronicle no longer stalls when you do.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-005","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Spellbook","t":"Fix","x":"Deleting a spell no longer opens the next one scrolled down to where the deleted one was.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-006","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Rare and Legendary Gear","t":"Fix","x":"Sweet Mother's Kiss (The Night Mother's Embrace, and any Rare imprinted with it) now gives its +50% against bosses under a quarter of their health: the Oblivion Gate's Warden and his host, the Abyss Dungeon's Remnant, the sea serpent, and every foe in an Elite Breach. Before this it never triggered against any of them.","g":["loot","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-007","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Rare and Legendary Gear","t":"Fix","x":"The same fix applies to the other \"under its health\" effects against those foes: Serpent's Kiss's double poison, Run Them Down, Gutting Lunge, Headsman's Chop, and the Axe and Blunt Weapon mastery bonuses.","g":["loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-008","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Hotbar","t":"Fix","x":"Number keys 1-9 now pick rows in the Use Magic Item list (and other windows) inside dungeons, not just outdoors.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-009","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Hotbar","t":"Fix","x":"In a dungeon, pressing a number with a window open no longer fires the hotbar slot behind it (for example, drinking the potion on slot 1), even a number pressed the instant the window opens. The HUD now hides under dungeon windows, as it already did elsewhere, and the keyboard and controller agree on when the hotbar is yours.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-010","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"UI","x":"The imps that follow you across a span's platforms can't be hurt from the platforms, by design. Your blows there used to look like they landed. Now they ring off with \"No footing\". Step onto an island or plate to fight them.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-011","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Blows that hit a ward (Vengeful Shades, guarded Ward-Bearers, a lord's shield) or a lord still asleep in its ring now say \"Warded\", and no longer heal you.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-012","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Vampiric and leech weapons, the Mace of Molag Bal, spells (Siphon Life and the other path spells), Cast When Strikes and set bonuses no longer heal you or give anything back off blows that deal nothing, including the Warden's shield and the Brass Remnant while it's closed.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-013","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A Court lord can be hit the moment it wakes; for up to two seconds your blows used to ring off it.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-014","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"A foe on a storey above or below you now says \"Warded\" instead of looking hit, and arrows and spells that land nothing say \"No footing\" or \"Warded\" too.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-015","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Beautiful Cities","t":"Fix","x":"Bushes no longer grow out of house walls in the towns rebuilt by Beautiful Cities and Beautiful Villages, including the one by Penwall Derry's east gate.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-016","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"World of Daggerfall","t":"Fix","x":"World of Daggerfall's rocks, camps, shrines and ruins no longer stand on the low open sea or on the lowest shore of the coastal regions. The mod meant to keep them off, but its check never worked.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-017","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Boulders","t":"Fix","x":"The boulders in rebuilt towns and villages, such as the stream rocks in Ipsmoth, are solid again. They had been drawn inside out, as hollow shells you could see through, and their stone texture is no longer smeared. The ramps and steps on the rebuilt villages' docks are no longer drawn inside out either.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-018","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"UI","x":"Crafting stations now say when the crafter's limit stops a craft's XP. A character raises only two crafts past Journeyman (rank 50); the rest stop at 50. The station now names your two, instead of promising XP it won't pay.","g":["crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-019","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Professions","t":"UI","x":"The Professions tab explains the limit before you reach it, and a station's XP now includes your Firmament stars' bonus.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-020","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Professions","t":"Fix","x":"Two crafts finished at the same moment could push a third craft past Journeyman and then freeze all three at rank 50 for good. The service now decides the limit inside each craft, so that can no longer happen.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9936-021","v":"0.1.9936","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Professions","t":"Fix","x":"A craft below 50 shows its next rank's XP again, and a Master's craft no longer claims a first-time bonus it didn't pay.","g":["professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9954-001","v":"0.1.9954","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Burning Court","t":"Rework","x":"When the gate opens, its court lets a crowd in about five times faster. If it is busy you now wait at its door instead of being thrown out of the court.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9954-002","v":"0.1.9954","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Burning Court","t":"New","x":"When all 256 places in the Burning Court's fight are taken you are no longer sent away: you stay at its edge and watch the whole fight, and you join it if a place frees (one frees when someone who took a place leaves without really fighting - a fighter who fought keeps theirs). While you watch nothing in the court can hurt you, you cannot strike, and you earn no share of the spoils.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9954-003","v":"0.1.9954","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Online Saving","t":"Rework","x":"Your online character now saves itself every five minutes instead of every two. Trades, crafting, profession work and everything the server settles still save at once, and the game still saves when you switch away from it - only a crash could cost you up to five minutes of play: walking, looting, quest steps, a level-up.","g":["saves","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9954-004","v":"0.1.9954","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Server","t":"Performance","x":"The account service makes fewer trips to its database, so busy evenings should load faster.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9968-001","v":"0.1.9968","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A revenant marked at its lair is now found there: it stands where you can walk to from the entrance, never in a sealed pocket or a cap no path reaches.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9968-002","v":"0.1.9968","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"A revenant the road had stood goes home to its lair when you visit, instead of standing nowhere - and the road body it left never comes back as the revenant after you deal with it at its lair.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9968-003","v":"0.1.9968","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Fix","x":"Winning a raid at sea now ends it: the raid's crew and any late wave are removed, so travel, resting and the Overworld no longer say enemies are near.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9968-004","v":"0.1.9968","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Fix","x":"If the enemy ship leaves the sea mid-fight, its raid's crew goes home with it.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9968-005","v":"0.1.9968","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Fix","x":"The pirate attack's victory gong rings again.","g":["naval","audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9968-006","v":"0.1.9968","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Wallet","t":"UI","x":"The wallet's row and card show what its contents weigh; each holding in the wallet shows its own weight. Nothing's weight changed.","g":["marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9982-001","v":"0.1.9982","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shared Foes","t":"New","x":"A monster handed to you by another player's game is now checked against what the game itself can build. One with health or a level no real spawn could have is removed from your world instead of fighting you, and is never rescaled.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9982-002","v":"0.1.9982","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shared Foes","t":"Rework","x":"You are never blamed for a monster someone else's game handed you.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9982-003","v":"0.1.9982","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Moderation","t":"New","x":"The relay now counts the impossible monsters it drops itself, and an account that asks for far more spawns than play allows opens a moderation case on its own. One batch of findings is one line on the case, and the Discord card says the spawn grants opened it.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-001","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Morrowind-bodied characters in third person now walk and run on their own legs. Each foot is set down on the ground where it lands and stays there until it lifts, so feet no longer slide. The hips, chest, arms and head move with each step.","g":["morrowind","animation","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-002","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"The legs follow where the body actually goes. Walk into a wall and the legs stop. Strafe or walk backwards and the legs step that way, for other players' characters too.","g":["morrowind","animation","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-003","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Walking, running and sneaking each have their own posture, and sneaking while standing still crouches. Strafing turns the hips toward the direction of travel, walking backwards is a backpedal, and turning on the spot steps the feet around.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-004","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"The stride fits the pace and the body. Men and women each have their own gait, and Argonians and Khajiit share the beast gait. Every race's height and build sets the stride.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-005","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"Slopes are walked on the slope. Sudden changes of direction are much smoother: the body dips far less, and the feet no longer jump in the air.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-006","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"One-handed weapons hang down and away from the side at rest, and a running character carries the blade low with its point trailing behind.","g":["morrowind","equipment","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-007","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Two-handed weapons are held in a low guard with both hands at rest, and carried at the hip at a run.","g":["morrowind","equipment","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-008","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Paired weapons are held out from both sides at rest, and swept back behind the body at a run.","g":["morrowind","equipment","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-009","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Staves and spears are held in both hands on the haft, and bare fists have their own guard.","g":["morrowind","equipment","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-010","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"Wrists stay in a natural range, and blades stay clear of the ground and the body, including between walking and running.","g":["morrowind","equipment","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-011","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"Third-person slashes, chops, thrusts and backhands now use the whole body. The hips and chest turn into the blow, the weight shifts forward, the lead foot steps in, and the weapon leads with its edge.","g":["morrowind","animation","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-012","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"The weapon moves smoothly through each attack without flipping, and meets its target at close to full speed.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-013","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"Two-handed blows keep both hands on the weapon. A left-hand blow is the mirror of a right-hand one, and a one-handed weapon held alone strikes with its own hand.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-014","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"The legs keep walking during an attack, so the body no longer stops mid-stride and slides. An attack that is interrupted, or cut short by the next one, flows into what comes next.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.9992-015","v":"0.1.9992","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"New","x":"This is on by default. To turn it off and go back to the original animation clips, use the Morrowind Body Motion switch in Settings, under Combat > With Morrowind data. The switch's text is now translated into every language the game ships.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-001","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Nerf","x":"Orcish and Daedric gear no longer drops for brand-new characters as often. Below level 20, an orc's or a daedra's metal drop is often a mid-tier metal instead (Elven at low levels, rising through Dwarven, Mithril and Adamantium to Ebony). From level 20 the drops are as before.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-002","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Economy","x":"Online, Orcish and Daedric pieces dropped by orcs and daedra, and bounty rewards, now sell for the condition they were found in, even after a repair, like all other loot.","g":["online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-003","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Loot Drops","t":"Rework","x":"In an online room, an orc's or a daedra's armour drop is now the same for everyone in the room.","g":["loot","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-004","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Leveling","t":"Buff","x":"Your maximum health is never below what an average roll at every level would have given you with your current Endurance. Raising Endurance later, including from the Firmament's stars, now counts for every level you have already gained. Nobody loses health.","g":["online","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-005","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Leveling","t":"Rework","x":"Every level now gives exactly 5 attribute points instead of 4 to 6.","g":["online","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-006","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Leveling","t":"Fix","x":"Levelling up online no longer changes your current health.","g":["online","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-007","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Skill Training","t":"UI","x":"The Stats page shows how many uses each skill has toward its next point, says when it is ready (and, inside the 6 hours between skill checks, how long until a rest or journey raises it), and says why when it is held (at 100 unmastered, or the 95 lock).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-008","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Skill Training","t":"QoL","x":"A \"Skills can be improved\" notice stays on screen while a rest or a journey would raise a skill.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-009","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Class Skill Swap","t":"New","x":"On the Growth tab you can now change one class skill you have not mastered for a skill outside your class, in the same group, for 100,000 gold. Your level and skill values stay the same. A class with only one weapon skill (or school of magic) can now reach a specialisation. The page warns you if the new skill could never be mastered, and an heir keeps the changed class.","g":["ascension","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-010","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Master Skills","t":"Rework","x":"On the Growth tab you can now change one class skill you have not mastered for a skill outside your class, in the same group, for 100,000 gold. Your level and skill values stay the same. A class with only one weapon skill (or school of magic) can now reach a specialisation. The page warns you if the new skill could never be mastered, and an heir keeps the changed class.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-011","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Guild Vault","t":"UI","x":"Guild vault: hover a piece (or tap its name) to see its full item card, base and modifiers included. Filter the vault by name, pack page and rarity. Unidentified pieces keep their names hidden.","g":["guild","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-012","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Guild Vault","t":"New","x":"Guild vault: hover a piece (or tap its name) to see its full item card, base and modifiers included. Filter the vault by name, pack page and rarity. Unidentified pieces keep their names hidden.","g":["guild","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-013","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Guild Stores","t":"UI","x":"Guild Stores: the put in / take out form is now above the list, leaving Units empty moves all of it, and a new Put in all button empties your Stores into the guild's.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10000-014","v":"0.1.10000","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Guild Stores","t":"QoL","x":"Guild Stores: the put in / take out form is now above the list, leaving Units empty moves all of it, and a new Put in all button empties your Stores into the guild's.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10025-001","v":"0.1.10025","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Jungle of Bantha","t":"New","x":"Hammerfell's south-eastern shore, from Lainlyn and Satakalaam east to Mournoth, is now dense jungle: giant trees close overhead with taller ones breaking through, young trees and palms fill the light gaps, and the floor is carpeted in ferns, broad leaves and grass.","g":["terrain","grass","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10025-002","v":"0.1.10025","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Jungle of Bantha","t":"New","x":"A humid haze hangs under the canopy, thickest at dawn and in rain, and it thins as you climb out of it.","g":["climate","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10025-003","v":"0.1.10025","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Features","t":"New","x":"On by default: switch it in the Features menu under \"The world\" (\"Jungle of Bantha\"). It is always on when playing online.","g":["climate","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10025-004","v":"0.1.10025","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Weather","t":"Rework","x":"What falls now depends on the air where you stand: its climate, the season, the hour and your height. Cold peaks get snow, warm lowlands get rain, and sleet falls in between, so one storm can rain in a valley and snow on the ridge above it.","g":["weather","climate","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10025-005","v":"0.1.10025","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Snowfall","t":"New","x":"Snow settles where it falls and melts as the air warms. In a thaw, white mountains stand over green valleys.","g":["weather","climate"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10025-006","v":"0.1.10025","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Sky","t":"Fix","x":"A hard, smooth arc that could cut across the sky at dusk is gone.","g":["sky"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10029-001","v":"0.1.10029","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"UI","x":"Every crafting station now spells out its quality odds. The old line, *\"Your rank 28, margin 18: Standard 50 | Fine 40 | Superior 10. A clean heat is a step better.\"*, now reads: *\"Quality chances: Standard 50% | Fine 40% | Superior 10%. They get better the further your rank (28) is above the recipe's (10). Land every strike while the glow is in the band to raise the result one quality.\"*","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10029-002","v":"0.1.10029","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"UI","x":"Each station says what its minigame asks for the bonus: the anvil's strikes, the plane along the grain, every stitch on the beat, the chisel on the marked line, the facet that catches the light.","g":["crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10029-003","v":"0.1.10029","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Crafting Stations","t":"UI","x":"A Tailor's clothing, a Leatherworker's leather and the town Apothecary's bonus are each said in a sentence of their own.","g":["crafting","professions"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-001","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"New","x":"Friendly merchant and navy ships moored at a port's quays can now carry you. Walk up to one, look at her hull and press Activate.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-002","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"New","x":"Her captain lists every port you know, nearest first, with the direction it lies and the fare (Daggerfall's ship fare for the whole voyage).","g":["naval","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-003","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"New","x":"Pick a port and confirm. You board at her helm and the voyage is sailed across the Overworld - never a jump. Nothing is paid until she sets sail.","g":["naval","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-004","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"New","x":"If the voyage stops (an enemy nearby, a fight, loading a save), her captain sails on by himself while you stay aboard. He keeps to the port you paid for.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-005","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"New","x":"At the far port she lands you, and you walk the rest of the way in. Step off her anywhere and the passage ends; anything you put in her hold comes back to your pack.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-006","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"New","x":"Online, any player at the port can book a ship there, and once she has sailed she is gone from that berth for everyone for the rest of the day. Other players can board and ride along.","g":["naval","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-007","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"The enhanced inventory has a new Batch salvage button. Tap pieces to tick them, or use All Magic, All Rare or All junk to select in one go.","g":["crafting","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-008","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Salvage","t":"New","x":"A sweep never picks a Legendary piece - you choose those by hand.","g":["loot","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-009","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Salvage","t":"UI","x":"Pieces that can't be salvaged (worn, locked, set with gems) are dimmed and say why.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10041-010","v":"0.1.10041","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Salvage","t":"QoL","x":"One question confirms the whole batch: it lists the pieces and the shards you'll get. Keep cancels and leaves your selection in place.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-001","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"On by default: on foot you are now drawn in the helmet, chest armor and leg armor you actually wear: leather, chain, or plate in iron, steel, mithril, adamantium, ebony, orcish or daedric. Each character uses its own body.","g":["equipment","rendering","third-person"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-002","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"The profile's Skin card now opens on a Look toggle: Skins or Layered Gearing (WIP).","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-003","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"Layered Gearing lets you choose the Female or Male body. If you switch to Skins and back, it keeps the body you chose for the rest of the session.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-004","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"A worn Casual or Formal Cloak adds its hood and cape in its dye, over any armor.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-005","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"On a horse you are drawn in your Mounted skin. As a werewolf or wereboar you are drawn as the beast.","g":["equipment","horse"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-006","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"Other","x":"Other players see your Layered Gearing look once the servers are updated. Until then they see your skin.","g":["online","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-007","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Quick Slots","t":"New","x":"Settings > Features > Quick slots: Off, Diamond (slots 1-4), Hotbar (the default, ten squares) and the new Diamonds (ten diamond-shaped slots).","g":["quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-008","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Quick Slots","t":"QoL","x":"With the pack or spellbook open, point at an item or spell and press a slot key to put it on that slot. This works with every bar style.","g":["quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-009","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Language","t":"Rework","x":"The game's own text now uses American spelling (armor, color, harbor, specialization, jeweler, catalog).","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-010","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Language","t":"Rework","x":"Instructions and messages are written as plain, complete sentences, with \"experience\" in place of \"XP\".","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-011","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Glyphs","t":"UI","x":"On the enhanced skin the 2 and the Z are redrawn so they can no longer be mistaken for each other.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-012","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"A journey no longer drops to x1 while the land ahead is still loading. It holds back only as much as needed, and full speed returns as soon as the land is built.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10046-013","v":"0.1.10046","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"An enemy camp that has not noticed you no longer keeps the Overworld view down and the journey at x1.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10051-001","v":"0.1.10051","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Economy","x":"Online, mending a looted weapon or piece of armour yourself raises its sell price again. A merchant pays for the condition it was found at, plus a third of what your own repair kits, Repairs Objects and the Varla Stone mended past that.","g":["online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10051-002","v":"0.1.10051","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Fix","x":"An enchanted found piece now sells at the Mages Guild for its found condition, not as if it were undamaged.","g":["online","loot","enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10051-003","v":"0.1.10051","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Hired Traders","t":"Fix","x":"Hired-trader patrons now pay less for worn pieces, the same way shops do.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10051-004","v":"0.1.10051","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Shops","t":"Fix","x":"Tempering a found piece no longer lowers its sell price.","g":["online","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10051-005","v":"0.1.10051","d":"2026-10-19","e":"Gear Wear","t":"Fix","x":"A worn book you find no longer becomes undamaged when it stacks with, or splits from, another copy.","g":["books"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10053-001","v":"0.1.10053","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"With Layered Gearing on, you now see every other player on foot in the armor they wear, not only yourself and players who chose it too.","g":["equipment","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10053-002","v":"0.1.10053","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Layered Gearing","t":"New","x":"Each player is drawn in the body they chose, or their character's own if they never chose one.","g":["equipment","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10058-001","v":"0.1.10058","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"Two-handed weapons such as greatswords, warhammers and battle axes are now carried low at the hip in both hands when running, held out in front of the hip rather than against it. The blade trails behind, and the chest turns toward the weapon.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10058-002","v":"0.1.10058","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"Running with a one-handed weapon and a shield no longer swings the shield up behind your head. The shield arm keeps Morrowind's own shield pose.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10058-003","v":"0.1.10058","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"The running stride is stiffer. The knees bend less and the heel no longer kicks up behind, so the body rides higher and more upright.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10058-004","v":"0.1.10058","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Running Hands","t":"Rework","x":"When running with empty hands or fists, each hand now stays on its own side instead of crossing in front of the chest.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10058-005","v":"0.1.10058","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Running Hands","t":"Rework","x":"In first person, the running fists come up in front of each shoulder instead of near the middle of the screen.","g":["first-person","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10063-001","v":"0.1.10063","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"In the Gauntlet, killing a Caster now silences its pillar. Before, only standing on the pillar's plate counted, and a group that killed every Caster was stuck with \"Casters left\" never dropping and a door that never opened. Runs already stuck in a Gauntlet get unstuck as soon as this goes live.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10070-001","v":"0.1.10070","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Nerf","x":"A lord no longer gets weaker when members of your company fall. A fallen member's part of the lord's health used to leave with them, so the lord melted under the survivors' blows the moment the team went down. Now the living have to finish what the fallen left: losing members in a Court makes the fight harder, never easier.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10070-002","v":"0.1.10070","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"A lord is now sized for the members who actually reached its hall. A teammate still on the stairs, or disconnected, when the hall wakes no longer makes the lord tougher for everyone else. They add their part when they arrive, at the health the lord has left, so a late arrival never heals him.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10070-003","v":"0.1.10070","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"A lord still asleep in its ring when a member falls on the way to it wakes sized for the company still standing.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-001","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Language","t":"Rework","x":"Descriptions, tooltips, guides and messages across the game have been rewritten in short, plain sentences. Codes and file names no longer show up on screen.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-002","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Mods","t":"Rework","x":"Mod settings now say in a sentence or two what each setting does. Settings that do nothing in this game say \"Has no effect\".","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-003","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Mods","t":"Rework","x":"The credits in the About pane say what each mod and library does for you. Every author, version and license is still named. Two credits were wrong and are fixed: Roleplay & Realism's later parts and Eye of the Beholder's animations, footsteps and cart are already in the game.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-004","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"King's Gambit","t":"UI","x":"In The King's Gambit, \"Least stake\" is now \"Minimum stake\".","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-005","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Translation Packs","t":"Fix","x":"Every language's translation has been updated to the new wording.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-006","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"UI","x":"The Elite Breach's windows now use the Enhanced Plus style: the card offer, the run recap, the boards and the call tracker.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-007","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"New","x":"On Enhanced Plus, a new start window opens the breach. It shows your Weir Keys, where you can start, which of your company can start there, and up to three decrees to wager. Then choose Open the breach, Rehearse Halls 1-5, Boards or Cancel. If the breach can't open, the reason is shown above the buttons.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-008","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"QoL","x":"Choosing cards: press 1-6 to choose, Y for Ready and R for a respite. Spending a Surplus now reads \"draw new cards\". Press Enter to close the recap.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10080-009","v":"0.1.10080","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Language","t":"Other","x":"Some of these messages come from the game servers. You will see their new wording after the servers are updated.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-001","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Every quest in the game now shows its objectives, one at a time. Your journal and the quest tracker name the step you're on, and a herald line tells you when you finish one.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-002","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Many quests, the guilds' and the great houses' best-known jobs among them, now ask you to choose how they end: spare the wounded spriggan or finish the job, sell a lich's books to the Mages Guild or burn them as the temple asks. Each ending pays and is remembered in its own way.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-003","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"Thirteen questlines now run alongside the quests you take at guild halls and taverns. Each opens with a letter or a courier when you're ready for it.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-004","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"The Dagon Cycle: *The Burning Doors*, *The Covens' Hoard* and *The Weir Road*. Someone is opening Dagon's Breaches on purpose. Follow the trail through the Breaches, the Elite Dungeons and the Elite Breaches to the Valkynaz who guard them.","g":["quests","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-005","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"The Hour That Was Not: the priests of Akatosh feel a wound in time under the Bay. It leads you into the Abyss Dungeons.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-006","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"The Old Coil: Sentinel's sailors say what the World-Skin shed still swims.","g":["quests","naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-007","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"Eight introductions: *The Court Crafter*, *The Smith's Secrets*, *The Harbormaster's Word*, *The Merchant's Road*, *A Seat at the Table*, *The Herald's Call*, *The Bay's Troubles* and *Written in the Stars*. Each shows you one of the game's newer pursuits: crafting, gear, sailing, trade, the tavern tables, the Arena, the Bay's troubles and the Firmament.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-008","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"A failed step comes back the next day, so a questline never closes on you. If a step needs something switched on (Loot rarity, Naval Combat, The King's Gambit) or a registered account, the questline's page says so.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-009","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Quests that pay gear now let you choose one of three pieces made for your class: a weapon in one of your best skills, a piece of armor and a jewel, better the harder the quest. Each card shows the piece's damage or armor, its hands and its weight, and Take asks you to press it twice.","g":["quests","equipment","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-010","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"A questline's ending pays a named piece of its own, 22 in all.","g":["quests","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-011","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"New","x":"Endings with guilds, temples and houses move your standing with them; online, a quest that ends unfinished still costs you no standing.","g":["quests","renown","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-012","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"Online, the Dagon Cycle, the Hour and the Old Coil also pay titles, held by your account: Doorwarden, Covenbane, Weirwalker, Witness of the Hour and Satakal's Witness. The Covens' Hoard can pay a Weir Key, once an account. These are only paid for what the service saw you do: a breach closed, a Redoubt taken, an Hour broken, the Serpent slain.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-013","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quest Journal","t":"New","x":"The Quests window has a new Questlines section. It shows every questline (running, waiting, locked or done), the step you're on and what opens the next one. Each guild you've joined appears there too, as a ladder of its quests by rank. A reward waiting can be reached from the pause menu on either skin.","g":["quests","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10101-014","v":"0.1.10101","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Features","t":"New","x":"The questlines are always on in the online world. Offline, they're a Features switch, on by default. The classic logbook is unchanged.","g":["quests","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-001","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Some nights Dagon's Breach holds more than the Warden. A portent is a third kind of mark beside his aspect and his trials, and it is always announced: in the chat with his marks, on the map's card, on the marks card, and in the Discord omen post. About two breaches in five carry one, and never two breaches in a row. A Legion-Lord night never does.","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-002","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Vanguard - *His vanguard holds the approach.* You arrive on a platform out in the fire, with the Warden in sight across it.","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-003","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Sundering - *He tears in two at the second phase.*","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-004","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Captive - *A knight of the Covenant lies chained in the Pen.*","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-005","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Dire Breach - *Dagon's Breach runs deep.* The Vanguard and the Sundering on the same night.","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-006","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"6 seconds after the first fighter lands, the first wave rises from the fire. Each next wave comes when a quarter or fewer of the last still stand, or after 30 seconds. Clear the Bridgehead's 3 waves and a walkway rises to the Muster. Its third wave brings the Markynaz, the Warden's lieutenant. He calls Imps out of the fire every 15 seconds. When he falls his Imps crumble with him; bring down whatever else stands and the way to the Warden opens.","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-007","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"New foes: the Brute (a Daedroth that smashes the ground around it), the Caster (it keeps its distance and throws bolts of the Warden's element at your feet) and the Markynaz (a Daedra Lord whose Rend hits hard and wide).","g":["elites","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-008","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"Rework","x":"The waves are sized to how many of you stand on the platform, so a full court breaks them in about the same time as a few. The Warden himself has less health on a Vanguard night, so the night takes no longer than a plain one.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-009","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Stall too long (4 minutes) and the Warden tires of waiting: his meteors start falling on the platforms (twice each, if he is Echoing).","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-010","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"UI","x":"The Warden's bar shows where you are: *The Vanguard - Bridgehead, wave 2 of 3*.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-011","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"On a Sundering night Valkynaz Ruhn doesn't bound to the Burning Court at his second phase. He leaps to his court's heart and calls the Sundering (step out of its 8 m disc), then tears himself in two: Ruhn's Blade, his body, and Ruhn's Flame, his aspect's fire made flesh (Ruhn's Rime, Storm or Venom under his other aspects: an Atronach of fire, ice, iron or flesh).","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-012","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"With 4 or more of you in the fight, the Blade bounds to the Burning Court and the Flame to the third court over the Rift Way, a new walkway. Split up and take both. With fewer, both fight you side by side in the Burning Court.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-013","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Blade keeps his steel (Cleave, Ground Slam, Charge, Leap, Chains). The Flame keeps his fire (Hellfire, Meteor, Flame Nova, Dagon's Brand).","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-014","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Each half has its own health, shown on its own track under his bar. Bring one down and it kneels for 20 seconds. Bring the other down before it rises, or the first gets back up. It rises with as much health as the other half has left, so the two are even for the next try.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-015","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"A half left with nobody in its court for 10 seconds starts to mend (its track says *Alone*).","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-016","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Both down together and the halves rejoin in the first court (keep off its heart: the Rejoining is a 9 m disc). Run back: his last stand as Dagon's Champion is fought there.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-017","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Chains of the Warden - a burning chain to one fighter near him. Be more than 16 m from him when it lands or you're dragged to his feet, and a Ground Slam follows.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-018","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Dagon's Brand - rings under up to 3 fighters. When it lands, each ring bursts on everyone *else* near it. Branded fighters: get away from the group.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-019","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Shared Torment - a gold ring under one fighter. Its blow is split between everyone standing in it, so gather on them. It only comes when 3 or more of you stand before him.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-020","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Scything Wheel - 2 blades turn around him for 6 seconds. Stay ahead of them, or out of reach.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-021","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Burning Gaze - nothing on the ground. If you're looking at him when it lands, it hits and blinds you. Look away.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-022","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The Unmaking - half his court's wedges burn, then the other half. Step into a dark wedge, then back into one that has already burned.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-023","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"UI","x":"When one of these is on you, the order shows under your crosshair (Chained! Run from him!, Look away!), with an arrow pointing the way out.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-024","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"2 to 4 gaolers rise as the first of you steps into the Pen, by how many of you are fighting then. They don't move, but they pulse at anyone who comes near.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-025","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"Cut them all down and the knight goes free, standing in gold: *The Covenant's ward stands over the court.*","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-026","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"The next Dagon's Reckoning to land breaks on the ward and hits nobody. Its crystals still shatter for the stun if you break them. If you break a Reckoning before it lands, the ward waits for the next one.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-027","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"UI","x":"The Warden's bar shows *Gaolers: 3*, then *The Covenant's ward* until it's used.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-028","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"Buff","x":"Beat the Warden on a portent night and your spoils carry one more piece of Magic or better for each portent: one for the Vanguard, one for the Sundering, and one for the Captive if the knight goes free. A Dire Breach pays 2. Each such piece can be socketed, carry a technique or turn Exalted like any other. Your Weir Key chance on a night whose portent pays (a Captive night only if the knight goes free) rises from one in six to one in four.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-029","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"Buff","x":"Beat the Warden on a portent night and your spoils carry one more piece of Magic or better for each portent: one for the Vanguard, one for the Sundering, and one for the Captive if the knight goes free. A Dire Breach pays 2. Each such piece can be socketed, carry a technique or turn Exalted like any other. Your Weir Key chance on a night whose portent pays (a Captive night only if the knight goes free) rises from one in six to one in four.","g":["elites","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10133-030","v":"0.1.10133","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dagon's Breach","t":"New","x":"About one breach in five, with no warning, a Tithe-Imp bolts from the fire while the Warden is in his first or second phase: a large Imp burning gold, carrying a tithe to its master. It strikes nobody and runs from whoever is nearest, a little slower than you can run, so expect a chase. Catch it within 22 seconds, before he leaves its court, or it dives back into the fire. Everyone who landed a blow on it gets their own tithe: gold by their level and a gem, straight into the pack.","g":["elites","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-001","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quest Marks","t":"New","x":"Your quests' destinations now appear on the Overworld as gold diamonds. The quest you're following is filled in and stays pinned to the screen edge, showing its distance and time left.","g":["quests","overworld","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-002","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"Click a quest mark to start a journey there.","g":["quests","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-003","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"Dungeons on the Overworld are slightly smaller and now stay the same size as you zoom in and out.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-004","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"While travelling, the Overworld tells you what weather you'll run into ahead, and when you'll get there (\"Rain ahead - 2.4 km, in 20 min\").","g":["overworld","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-005","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"When you're standing still, it shows the next few hours' weather where you are. Hover over a place to see its forecast too.","g":["overworld","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-006","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Travel Pathing","t":"Fix","x":"Planned routes now stay on the road from start to finish, including around corners, through towns on diagonal roads, and up to a spot you clicked near a road.","g":["overworld","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-007","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"Travel inside a town slows to x5 and follows the streets instead of running into buildings.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-008","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"New","x":"If the city gates are shut for the night, your journey stops and tells you why.","g":["overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10140-009","v":"0.1.10140","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Roaming Bands","t":"Rework","x":"You can now see other players being chased by bands from as far away as the bands themselves are drawn.","g":["online","overworld"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10145-001","v":"0.1.10145","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"Weapons held while running no longer wag side to side with your shoulders. Dual-wielded daggers, one-handers, two-handers, staves and spears all stay steady as you run.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10145-002","v":"0.1.10145","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dual Wielding","t":"Rework","x":"Running with two weapons drawn is no longer stiff. Your arms stay swept behind you, but they now pump with your stride and your elbows bend, instead of being locked straight back with your wrists twisted round.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10145-003","v":"0.1.10145","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Fix","x":"With a two-handed weapon (or a staff or spear held in both hands), your shoulders no longer twist with each step, so the weapon stays still in both hands.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10145-004","v":"0.1.10145","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Morrowind Body","t":"Rework","x":"Running is less stiff-legged. Your knees bend and spring more, roughly halfway between the original run and the stiffer one from the last update.","g":["morrowind","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10145-005","v":"0.1.10145","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Lantern","t":"Fix","x":"A lantern hung at your waist on the Morrowind body is now a sensible belt-lantern size (about 30 cm). It was hanging at full street-lantern size. It is the same size the Eye of the Beholder sprite's lantern already was.","g":["morrowind","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10161-001","v":"0.1.10161","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Logging","t":"Buff","x":"Every map square of the jungle now stands 48 trees a day for Logging, four times the richest woods anywhere else. Every one of them can be felled: on ground that hasn't been vouched for yet, trees that would be Teak or Mahogany stand as Pine instead of standing nothing.","g":["logging","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10161-002","v":"0.1.10161","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Jungle of Bantha","t":"Rework","x":"The jungle's big trees now stand about 16 m apart instead of crowding in every 12 m, and its young trees and palms stand at most one to a patch of ground. That is less than half as many trees, so you can see and walk between them, while their crowns still meet overhead.","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10161-003","v":"0.1.10161","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Jungle of Bantha","t":"New","x":"Winding dirt trails now cut through the jungle, meeting, crossing and looping, about one through every map square. The ferns and grass keep off them, and the big trees stand back from them as they do from roads.","g":["terrain","roads"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10161-004","v":"0.1.10161","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Collision","t":"Fix","x":"You no longer walk through trees, rocks, stumps, fallen logs, barrels, crates, statues and other solid props, on foot or on horseback. Walk into one and you slide around it. Grass, flowers, ferns and bushes can still be walked through. If you ever end up inside one (after a teleport, say), you can walk straight out.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10161-005","v":"0.1.10161","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"UI","x":"Herb patches, veins, boulders, fishing schools, dungeon veins and trees now have a crisp outline in their profession's colour. It follows the outline of the node itself, including the full 3D tree, instead of the faint sparkle in front of it. The outline fades in as you approach, fades with distance and fog, and is hidden by anything standing in front of the node. A skinnable body drawn as a 3D character keeps the old glow.","g":["foraging","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10161-006","v":"0.1.10161","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Jungle of Bantha","t":"Rework","x":"The jungle floor now carries as much grass as meadows elsewhere, growing between the same ferns and flowers. The ferns and flowers stay at the amount they were thinned to.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10165-001","v":"0.1.10165","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Name Filter","t":"Rework","x":"The name filter now refuses names containing \"prostitute\" or \"strangler\", even when they are run together with another word. In chat, letters and notes these words are starred out.","g":["chat","social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10167-001","v":"0.1.10167","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"Ysolde Marnhel, Prior Anselm Vey, Hamid al-Rasheen and Corvane Tull now carry their own names when you meet them. Before, the person you had to find and talk to wore a different, random name from the one the quest's letters, journal and guide gave you, on their nameplate, in the talk window and under the Info cursor. Every quest's people now answer to the name their quest uses.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-001","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Weir Keys","t":"Fix","x":"Weir Keys now stay in your pack. They can no longer be stowed in the wagon or in storage, and keys stowed earlier are cleared when you load. Your account's real key count is unchanged; the extra keys that turned to rust on use were never real.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-002","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Enchanting","t":"Fix","x":"The item maker takes each side effect's setting once. A drawback such as User Takes Damage in holy places can no longer be stacked for extra points, and an effect with every setting taken leaves the list. Items you enchanted before keep their enchantments.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-003","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"In the Wrothgarian Mountains a companion's pack is at stake with yours: a death there drops what your crew hand or sworn revenant carries. Companions can't be sent away from inside the zone, and one knocked out there leaves its pack with you.","g":["companions","death-penalty"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-004","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"Disintegrate now works on online bosses (the Oblivion Gate Warden, his crystals and host, the Abyss Dungeon's Remnant, Elite Breach foes and arena opponents). It lands the biggest blow the fight allows instead of nothing, and spell damage numbers on these bosses show what can actually land.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-005","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Spells","t":"Fix","x":"Damage-over-time spells keep burning on those online bosses (not arena opponents) and the sea serpent instead of stopping after their first hit. Recasting refreshes the effect rather than stacking it.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-006","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Spells","t":"UI","x":"Chain Lightning, Earthshaker and Dragonfire now show their own damage numbers, tagged with the power's name.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-007","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"UI","x":"The Elite Breach Gauntlet's caster plates now glow gold on their pillars and dim once that caster is silenced, and the objective names both ways to silence a caster: hold its plate, or slay it.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-008","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Duels","t":"UI","x":"In a duel, your health bar now shows your duel vitality and drops when your opponent hits you. It goes back to your real health when the duel ends; duels still never touch your real health.","g":["combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-009","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Collision","t":"Fix","x":"Furniture in a player's home or yard, and a mountain, camp or town that loads in around you, no longer trap you. They appear, you walk out, and they turn solid once you're clear.","g":["homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-010","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Dungeon lifts and moving floors no longer trap you or push you out of the map. A lift that meets your head waits until you step clear, and a lowering floor stops above you. If you ever fall out of a dungeon, you're returned to its entrance.","g":["interior"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-011","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Town Map","t":"Fix","x":"Find me on the town map now takes you to where you're standing, zooms to your street and marks you with the red cross, instead of jumping to the edge of town. On the dungeon map it also brings you back to your own floor.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-012","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Dungeon Map","t":"Fix","x":"Find me on the town map now takes you to where you're standing, zooms to your street and marks you with the red cross, instead of jumping to the edge of town. On the dungeon map it also brings you back to your own floor.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-013","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Guild Refusal","t":"Fix","x":"At a guild's Buy Spells counter, a purchase the shop refuses now tells you why (no spellbook, or not enough gold) instead of doing nothing. The message goes away with a click, and Leave works on the next press.","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-014","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Guild Refusal","t":"Fix","x":"A guild or coven whose quest you haven't finished now says so and names that quest, instead of \"That service is not available yet.\"","g":["guild","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-015","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Invisibility","t":"Fix","x":"Worn items that make you invisible, blending or a shade no longer stay switched off after you land a blow. The effect comes back on its own within six game hours while the item is still worn.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-016","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Status Box","t":"New","x":"Catching a disease now shows an \"Unwell\" tile on the Enhanced HUD and \"You feel unwell.\" in the Status box while it incubates. The disease's name appears once its symptoms begin.","g":["survival"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-017","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Enchanting","t":"UI","x":"The Enchanting Station now lists crafted pieces too small to give Arcane Essence, greaves and pauldrons among them, grayed out with the reason: a piece needs 100 enchantment points for one Essence.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-018","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Revenants","t":"Fix","x":"Revenants no longer take your horse, cart, deeds or spellbook. Anything one took before comes back to your pack the next time you load, and you'll be told.","g":["revenants"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-019","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Heirlooms","t":"Fix","x":"An heir can now reach the remains of an ancestor who died inside another player's instance. Where the shared dungeon is laid smaller, its door offers you an instance of your own, and the remains lie where they fell.","g":["death-penalty","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10230-020","v":"0.1.10230","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Letters of Credit","t":"Fix","x":"Characters left with negative gold by the old large-sale bug (fixed in 0.0.249) can now be repaired by staff: the gold is reset, what you were owed comes back as a letter of credit, and the trading freeze the bad sale caused is lifted. Contact staff if this happened to you.","g":["online","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10243-001","v":"0.1.10243","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Server","t":"Performance","x":"Gathering, the Notice Board's writs and traders, town yards, the guild chapters and the arena board ask far less of the account database, so they answer quickly in the evening rush.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10243-002","v":"0.1.10243","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Server","t":"Performance","x":"When the account service is slow, your game now waits a moment before asking for display data again instead of asking harder. Gathering, crafting, trading and saving are never held back.","g":["online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10249-001","v":"0.1.10249","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"Abyss Dungeons stopped appearing when most players online were at sea. A new one now always rises by a town. If players are crowded at sea, it goes to the busiest region on land, or to one of the Bay's great cities.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10249-002","v":"0.1.10249","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"Fix","x":"An Abyss Dungeon that already rose \"at sea\" before this update now shows up by one of the Bay's great cities, so you don't have to wait for it to fade.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-001","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"HUD","t":"New","x":"Two new tiles beside the Renown bar: Skills ready (left) counts the skills a rest or a journey would raise; Firmament stars (right) counts the stars and craft points you haven't placed yet. Click the stars to open the Firmament page. Both can be moved with Alt+U.","g":["renown","ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-002","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"HUD","t":"QoL","x":"Hover any buff, debuff, need or disease tile to see what it does, in the same card the inventory uses.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-003","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Level-Up Notification","t":"UI","x":"Under DFO Grimoire, the level-up notes are now written in full, readable ink.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-004","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Inventory","t":"New","x":"A new Lantern slot, after the Crystals. A lantern placed there hangs at your belt, is lit while it hangs, and goes out when you take it off.","g":["equipment","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-005","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Monster Volume","t":"New","x":"New Monster Volume setting (0-100%) under Audio. It controls monster calls, attack sounds and pain cries.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-006","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Monster Volume","t":"Rework","x":"Monsters call 60% less often. The city watch and companions are unchanged.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-007","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"QoL","x":"Clicking an NPC that a quest is waiting on now shows the quest's message and reward right away. The talk window, guild or shop opens after them, instead of the quest words appearing only after you pressed Exit.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-008","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Growth Tab","t":"UI","x":"The window no longer changes size when you switch pages. The page list always sits on the left, with a short description under each entry.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-009","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Growth Tab","t":"UI","x":"The Level page opens on a card showing your level.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-010","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Growth Tab","t":"UI","x":"Mastery bars are now thin red bars, the same height as the yellow ones.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-011","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"The World Map has a Players filter (Shown / Hidden). It shares its setting with the Overworld's Travellers switch.","g":["map","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-012","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hoods","t":"Fix","x":"The female hooded armour no longer floats over the shoulders, and the mace head is no longer pale and black.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10256-013","v":"0.1.10256","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Weapons","t":"Fix","x":"The female hooded armour no longer floats over the shoulders, and the mace head is no longer pale and black.","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-001","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"Kamer & Kab's Daggerfall Enemy Expansion 1.3.4 is in the Mods pane and is on by default. Online, the room's setting applies to everyone in it.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-002","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"The mod's fifty new enemies are registered, with their art. While the mod is on, its changes to sixteen classic monsters and two classic classes apply, and quests can name the new enemies.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-003","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"The new enemies animate and stand at the size the mod gives them. Their glowing parts glow, and their spirits are drawn see-through, in dungeons, in towns and in the Overworld's bands. Female riders and Dark Slayers fall as their own female corpses, and the Hell Hound's corpse burns on outside dungeons too.","g":["mod","animation"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-004","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"The new enemies now turn up in the world: every dungeon type, the water, and each climate's towns by night, wilderness by day and wilderness by night use the mod's encounter tables. Laboratories pick one of two tables each, the same one every visit and for every player. Arriving in a town by fast travel or a load picks that climate's town-night table, as in Daggerfall Unity.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-005","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"The new enemies cast their own spells. The mod's four new spells join the spell list and are hidden from shops, as in Daggerfall Unity. Each spellcaster casts its own book: King Lysandus his Bolt of Vengeance, the spellcasting classes by their level.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-006","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"The new enemies' attacks carry their effects: The Blood Spider's bite leeches blood. The Gloom Wraith's touch silences. The Fire Daemon's touch burns. The Will-o'-wisp's touch wracks. The lizard men paralyse like a spider. The bat and the ghouls carry disease. The nymph tires you.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-007","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"Blunt weapons do half damage to the Skeletal Soldier and silver does double, as against the Skeletal Warrior. While the mod is on, Barbarians no longer take that rule, as in the mod. Each new enemy has its own kind (beast, humanoid, undead, daedra) for racial bonuses, Detect, Dispel and Pacify, and its own language.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-008","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"The Troll gets back up. Ten seconds after it falls, a new Troll stands where the body lay, unless a spell's missile burns the body to ash first. Fire is the Troll's weakness; blades and arrows do nothing to the body. The body can't be searched. A Troll still down when you save keeps its time on load, and a burnt one stays burnt, after a reload and for a player who arrives later. The mod's \"Disable Troll Respawn\" setting keeps them down. Online, every player sees the same body rise or burn.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-009","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"New","x":"With Morrowind attached, the new enemies stand in Morrowind's bodies where Morrowind has the same creature: the Goblin, the wolves, the Troll, the Boar, the Mudcrab, the Ogre, the Dremora Churl, the golems, the ghouls, the Scamp, the Dwemer centurions, the Skeletal Soldier and the ghosts (seen through). The lizard men stand as Argonians, and the new classes as people. The riders, the flyers and the creatures Morrowind lacks keep their Daggerfall sprites.","g":["mod","morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-010","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"New","x":"With Roleplay & Realism: Items' realistic enemy equipment on, the mod kits every class enemy, the classic classes included:","g":["mod","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-011","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"New","x":"The new classes are armed as the class they are drawn from: a Knight Rider fights as a Knight, a Druid as a Mage, a Bounty Hunter as an Assassin (with the Assassin's chance of a poisoned blade).","g":["mod","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-012","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"New","x":"Class enemies wear their second weapon.","g":["mod","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-013","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"Rework","x":"Armour follows what each class may wear. With Roleplay & Realism: Items' new armour on, a class that may not wear plate sometimes wears the chain or leather set instead. A Monk wears about half the armour it did, and Rangers and Burglars wear their classic pieces rather than chain or leather.","g":["mod","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-014","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"Rework","x":"In There's a Hole in the Bottom of the Ocean's abyss, the new classes are treated as monsters, as that mod's own code does.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-015","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"Fix","x":"Fix: the vampires, the ancient vampires, the frost and fire daedra and the fire atronach no longer cast shadows, sprite or Morrowind body, as in Daggerfall Unity.","g":["mod","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-016","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Roleplay & Realism","t":"Fix","x":"Fix: with realistic enemy equipment, an enemy no longer holds a two-handed weapon and a shield at once, and an orc's poisoned blade is rolled before its gear turns orcish, as in Daggerfall Unity.","g":["mod","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-017","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"Performance","x":"The mod's pictures leave memory once drawn.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-018","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Daggerfall Enemy Expansion","t":"Fix","x":"The new enemies' names are translated into every language the game offers. Before this, they showed in English everywhere, as in Daggerfall Unity.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-019","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Meaner Monsters","t":"Rework","x":"With both mods on (the default, and always online), Meaner Monsters plays as MUDEX, the version its author Ralzar made for Daggerfall Enemy Expansion. Meaner Monsters itself asks players to make this switch.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-020","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Meaner Monsters","t":"Rework","x":"MUDEX sets the health, damage, level and armour of 35 monsters, classic and new. The Grizzly Bear now hits for 1-20 with 50-100 health, and the Goblin for 4-15.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10308-021","v":"0.1.10308","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Meaner Monsters","t":"New","x":"Every dungeon type gets themed encounter tables that don't scale with your level, beside its usual one. A crypt might be a lich's, a vampire's, a mummy's, a necromancer's or a haunted one.","g":["mod"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-001","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Enhanced Sounds","t":"Fix","x":"The game no longer distorts when many loud sounds play at once. A limiter now sits on the final output, so the Legion-Lord's heavy blows, his roars and the gate music can't push the mix past full volume. Everyday sound is unchanged.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-002","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Hellfire, Meteor, Brand and Torment play at most two copies of their sound, instead of one per targeted player. In a group, a third-phase Hellfire played ten copies at once.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-003","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Rework","x":"Inside the gate, other players' sounds play 4 dB quieter, as they already do in the Elite Gates Spire, so the boss's warnings stand out.","g":["audio"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-004","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Performance","x":"The gate fight's spark, meteor, crystal and portal effects are prepared as you arrive in the court, instead of the first time each appears mid-fight.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-005","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Oblivion Gates","t":"Performance","x":"The monsters a gate can field are loaded as you arrive, instead of when the first wave rises or the boss splits in two.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-006","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Blood","t":"Performance","x":"Blood splashes no longer redo their image work on every hit.","g":["blood"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10312-007","v":"0.1.10312","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Shadows","t":"Performance","x":"With Enhanced Lighting shadows on, the brief flashes of the boss's landings, his fall and the Wrath no longer cast shadows, so they no longer force shadow redraws.","g":["lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10314-001","v":"0.1.10314","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Titles","t":"New","x":"Severide is the first ever to take Redoubt 10 of the Battlespire, alone, in 1:17:40. He now holds the First of the Spire title and its aura, Firstlight. Equip them from your profile. A letter from the Developers waits in the mailbox.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10314-002","v":"0.1.10314","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Auras","t":"Rework","x":"Firstlight is now a one-of-a-kind aura, worn only by the first company ever to take Redoubt 10. A dial of the ten Redoubts lights round the wearer's feet one after another, and ten spires of dawn-light rise as each is taken. When the tenth falls, the dawn breaks: a sunburst runs out across the ground and a shaft of first light rises past the head.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10316-001","v":"0.1.10316","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Titles","t":"Fix","x":"The First of the Spire title and its aura, Firstlight, now go to Serveride (seen in the world as Severide), the first ever to take Redoubt 10 of the Battlespire. The last update had named the wrong account, so nobody received them.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-001","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Rework","x":"Herbs, veins, boulders, trees and fishing schools no longer wear a coloured outline. They catch the light instead: small star-shaped glints flash on the node itself and fade, and from a distance a soft sheen of light passes over it now and then.","g":["foraging","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-002","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Rework","x":"The node you're working goes quiet: no glints and no sheen while you pick, mine, chop or skin it, so the Basket's and the Pick-Axe's own glints are the only ones to watch.","g":["foraging","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-003","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Fix","x":"Glints stay on the spot of the plant, vein or tree they belong to as you walk; they no longer hop about.","g":["foraging","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-004","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Rework","x":"Walls and rocks in front of a node hide its glint, and fog and the sea's murk fade it as they fade the node.","g":["foraging","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-005","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"QoL","x":"With reduced motion turned on in your system, the glints hold still and no sheen crosses.","g":["foraging","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-006","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Rework","x":"The glints follow the light where the node stands. They are bright in daylight and dim at night, underground and in a storm, but never so dim you can't find the node. A node beside a lamp in a mine catches its light.","g":["foraging","lighting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10322-007","v":"0.1.10322","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Performance","x":"Gathering nodes behind you no longer cost a full-screen pass each frame.","g":["foraging"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-001","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"The first live event, from 20 October to 7 November.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-002","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Killing foes, gathering, crafting, fishing, winning tavern games, finishing quests and bounties, sailing, the endgame and holding a fallen star can all earn you Soul Cakes. They go straight into your pack.","g":["events","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-003","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Every find is doubled on All Hallows' Eve, 31 October, and on the in-game 13th of Frostfall and 3rd of Hearthfire, when the dead walk (about an hour of real time each).","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-004","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"The Wyrd's Raiment: a nine-piece Aetheric set: eight leather pieces, so casters can wear it, and the Witchmoon Athame. Its set bonuses are Wyrd-Sight, Tallow-Ward and Soul Harvest.","g":["events","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-005","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Witchwarden: a title.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-006","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Witchfire: an aura of green fire and tallow candles.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-007","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Profile icons: a new kind of cosmetic, worn in your portrait instead of your face and seen by other players. Three to buy, one to earn.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-008","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Six festival cards for the Iliac Hand, including the legendary King Lysandus' Spectre.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-009","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"New","x":"Every town is decorated in its own region's style: turnip lanterns and straw effigies in High Rock; candles and bowls of fire in Hammerfell; bonfires and horned skulls in the mountains; ward-staves in the fens; bones in the Haunted Woodlands","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-010","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"New","x":"Set a Hearth Offering out at the door of your home and fill it with Soul Cakes.","g":["events","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-011","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"New","x":"Other players can take one cake from each offering per day.","g":["events","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-012","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"New","x":"You can take your offering back in at any time, even after the festival. You get back the bowl and every cake still in it.","g":["events","homes"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-013","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"New","x":"When other players have taken 25 cakes from your offerings, you earn the Hearthkeeper title.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-014","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"New","x":"Take 10 cakes from other players' offerings to earn the Soul Cake icon.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-015","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"Every real hour is a night. Each night one of the Bay's twelve covens pulls three stars down into the wilds of its region, each near a different town.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-016","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"A new star burns in the sky for a minute and a half before it falls. Chat names the town it is falling toward, and the map, the compass and the Timers window point to it.","g":["events","map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-017","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"When it lands, hold it. The coven comes in four waves, then their master. What they summon goes for the star itself, and if its light runs out, the coven takes it.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-018","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"The master calls a circle twice. While any of the circle stands, the master takes only a quarter of every blow. Break the circle first.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-019","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"An unheld star is lost 15 minutes after it falls.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-020","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"On the 13th of Frostfall, the night's last star is the Heart-Star. Its master's circle is twice the size, and so are its rewards.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-021","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"A held star gives Renown, 30 silver, gold, 1 to 3 pieces of Starfall Glass, a magic item or better, and Soul Cakes. Your account card counts your Stars held.","g":["events","renown","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-022","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"Starfall Glass is pale glass that still holds some of the star's light. It stacks, and any merchant pays well for it.","g":["events","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-023","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"One star in four also gives a piece of the Starspun Weave, Mephala's nine-piece set. The Heart-Star always gives one.","g":["events","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-024","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Starfall","t":"New","x":"2 pieces, Spinner's Thread: poison resistance and Agility. 4 pieces, Bound in Silk: every 4th full-weight weapon hit on the same enemy deals 60 to 140% more damage. 6 pieces, Mephala's Veil: a hit that drops you below 30% health gives you Chameleon for 10 seconds. It recovers in 4 minutes.","g":["events","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-025","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"A new festival questline from Morwen, a Wyrd Sister of Glenmoril. It opens at level 6, online with a registered account, while the festival runs. A Wyrd Sister hands you Morwen's letter, or her raven brings it if you hold a star first.","g":["quests","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-026","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"Hold a fallen star, face the Coven on the Bluff, then hold three more stars to earn the title Starwarden and 30 Soul Cakes. The Wyrd Sisters' window shows the title once you hold it.","g":["quests","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-027","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"Holding the Heart-Star during Three Stars is an optional objective: it pays more and adds Morwen's Heart-Star Ring to your choice of reward.","g":["quests","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-028","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"New","x":"At the end, decide what becomes of the Spinner's spindle: burn it in Hircine's fire, sell it to the Mages Guild, or take it to a priest of Arkay at Arkay's own temple. Each choice has its own reward.","g":["quests","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10373-029","v":"0.1.10373","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Compass","t":"Fix","x":"The compass on the Enhanced HUD now shows the Sea Serpent and a found Abyss Dungeon. Both marks were being dropped before they reached it.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-001","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"Fix","x":"Interacting in a town where a player has set out a Hearth Offering no longer crashes the game. The crash happened whatever you interacted with there: a body, a door or a person.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-002","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Hearth Offerings","t":"Fix","x":"In those towns the names under your crosshair show again, and Hearth Offerings work: take a Soul Cake from someone else's, or fill or take in your own.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-003","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Questlines","t":"Rework","x":"Questline letters no longer arrive in a heap. Each new questline's opening letter now waits until the last one has reached you, and an hour of your character's time after it.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-004","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A quest giver placed in a Mages Guild hall no longer stands inside the guild's own quest-giver.","g":["quests","guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-005","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"World Map","t":"New","x":"When a townsperson marks a building on your map, you can now see it from the world map too. In a town, the world map has a tab for the town's streets.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-006","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Town Map","t":"UI","x":"On a crowded town map, a name with no room is drawn as a star. Pointing at the star shows the building's name, so a marked building always shows.","g":["map"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-007","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Town Layouts","t":"Fix","x":"Trees in towns no longer grow around fountains, wells and crates. A tree that stands close to one is drawn smaller.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-008","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Cooking","t":"Fix","x":"Raw Fish in your Materials Bag can be cooked over a fire. The cooked fish goes into your pack.","g":["cooking","fishing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-009","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Joinery","t":"Fix","x":"The joinery's carpenter, signboard and workbench all open the workbench with its craft buttons. Before, the carpenter and the signboard opened it with the Workbench marked as away.","g":["carpentry"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-010","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Stores","t":"Performance","x":"Putting your goods in the Stores no longer locks the buttons for a long time. Everything you put in at once is saved once, not once a material.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-011","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Stores","t":"Fix","x":"Temper at the Anvil and Temper at the Loom are back on the Stores page.","g":["smithing"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-012","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Ship Handling","t":"Fix","x":"After a journey across the sea, your ship stops instead of rowing on by itself. This happened when you left the helm on oars, without full sails.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-013","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Harbours","t":"Fix","x":"Port towns along the coast that had no harbour now have one, including Daggerfall, Sentinel and Wayrest. A harbour can stand a little way from its town where the shore lies far out.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-014","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Tutorials","t":"Fix","x":"Sailing from one port to another now counts at every port, so the Under Sail tutorial completes.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10393-015","v":"0.1.10393","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Fix","x":"You can't go below to your ship's cabin while enemies are nearby. Before, going below made pirates vanish.","g":["naval"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-001","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"The Overworld now shows the land out to the horizon. The haze over sunny and cloudy skies used to close a few kilometres out, leaving one pale wash. It now thins out to where the land meets the sky, and you can tilt the camera up to look along it (down to 15 degrees, from 30).","g":["overworld","distant-land"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-002","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"Fix","x":"Clouds' shadows now carry on out to the far hills, with no straight edge where they used to stop.","g":["overworld","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-003","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"You can click on land you can see in the distance to travel there. Before, distant land answered \"That lies beyond what you can see from here.\"","g":["overworld","distant-land"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-004","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Overworld","t":"Rework","x":"While nearby land is still loading, distant hills fill the gap instead of open sky.","g":["overworld","distant-land"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-005","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Loading","t":"Performance","x":"Loading into the world does less work. The longest freeze while the world is built is about half as long, and the first moments in the world freeze less often: the map of Tamriel is fitted in a fraction of the time, and the roads' travellers are planned faster, thanks to joaomdb3's TRIP-PICKS (#854), carried here.","g":[],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-006","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Trading","t":"Performance","x":"Trading with a large inventory is smooth. A shop or a trade with another player now opens with its item pictures in place, instead of rebuilding the window once per picture for up to minutes. A click on an item answers in about 50 ms where it took up to 0.8 s, and buying or selling a piece takes about 0.1 s where it took up to 3 s. Long lists keep their place while you scroll, whatever the height of each row.","g":["market"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-007","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Performance","t":"Performance","x":"No more freezes while shaders compile. Oblivion Gates (the gate's fire, its veil, the court's telegraphs, blows, crystals and portal), the Elite Gates' fight, the glint on gathering nodes, the sea's effects, spell impacts and the snow on the ground now compile in the background. Before, the game froze for each one, for seconds on some graphics cards. Each effect appears a moment later instead. On most graphics cards, the gate and node effects now start compiling while you load in.","g":["rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10418-008","v":"0.1.10418","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Snowfall","t":"Performance","x":"The weather's snow no longer eats your frame rate. While the snow on the ground was catching up with the weather (after arriving somewhere, or travelling on), it cost about 18 ms a frame and spiked past 60 ms. It now keeps to its 3 ms, and the snowline settles in over a few seconds instead.","g":["weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10425-001","v":"0.1.10425","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Discord Reports","t":"Fix","x":"If you were the only one who entered the breach, the Discord announcement of a tenth Redoubt (10, 20, 30...) now names you and says you did it alone. For example: *Mara took Redoubt 20 of the Battlespire (Hall 100) alone in 40:00, from Redoubt 10*. Before, it said *\"Mara's company took...\"* however many people were in the breach.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10425-002","v":"0.1.10425","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Discord Reports","t":"Fix","x":"A group is still announced as a company. Anyone who stepped through with you counts, even if they fell, went home or left. The announcement now names someone who actually went in, never an opener who stayed outside.","g":["elites","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10425-003","v":"0.1.10425","d":"2026-10-20","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Once the first hall wakes, the company tracker counts only the people who came in. A party member who was called but never stepped through no longer shows as part of your company.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10431-001","v":"0.1.10431","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Rework","x":"In an Athenaeum, the Orrery's six stones now stand in the hall. Each has a dial, a hand showing its hour, and two levers: the right lever turns the stone forward, the left turns it back. Before, each stone was a gold ring on the floor, and you had to search the empty air beside it to find the turn.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10431-002","v":"0.1.10431","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"The door at the end of a span no longer stays shut when you stop to time your jumps. Standing still without moving the mouse made the Spire lose sight of your crossing, and the door would not open for you.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10431-003","v":"0.1.10431","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Elite Gates","t":"QoL","x":"If the door won't let you through, it now tells you why and what to do.","g":["elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10431-004","v":"0.1.10431","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Elite Gates","t":"Fix","x":"Damage numbers on Spire lords and enemies now show the damage each hit actually did, a moment after it lands. Before, they showed what the hit would do to an ordinary enemy, which can be far more than a lord takes. The numbers now add up to the fight's damage chart. Damage over time and Arcane Echo repeats show their numbers too, and a follow-up blow (Open Hand, Many Endings) is counted in its blow's number rather than popping a second one.","g":["elites","combat-visuals"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10435-001","v":"0.1.10435","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Class Skill Swap","t":"Fix","x":"Changing a class skill on the Growth tab could be repeated to push your level far past what any class can reach. One class reached level 223. A skill's training now leaves your class with it. Your level and its progress still never drop, but after you give up a trained skill for a less trained one, your class skills make up the difference before your next level comes any closer.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10435-002","v":"0.1.10435","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Class Skill Swap","t":"UI","x":"The swap form now tells you how many points that is, beside the picks and again when it asks you to confirm.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-001","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"Asking around for work no longer sends you to \"someone named .\" at \"a place called .\" after you've taken (or turned down) a job, or after loading a save. The answer always names a person who has work and the place to find them.","g":["social","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-002","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Townspeople","t":"Fix","x":"A woman with work for you is now \"her\" in those answers, not \"him\".","g":["social","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-003","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A quest that sends you to a temple or a guild hall now always names it. The Orrery of Endings, and other questline steps that began while you were out on the road, used to say things like \"at in Daggerfall\" with the name missing. Quests already in your journal get their names back the next time you load.","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-004","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Quests","t":"Fix","x":"A palace a quest picks while you are on the road now has its proper name (Castle Daggerfall, Castle Wayrest, Castle Sentinel) instead of just \"Palace\".","g":["quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-005","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Hunting","t":"New","x":"You can now skin the Enemy Expansion's animals. Bats give Bat Leather, blood spiders Spider Silk, mountain lions Tiger Pelts and land dreugh Dreugh Shells. Wolves, snow wolves and dogs give the new Wolf Pelt, boars the new Boar Hide, and mudcrabs the new Mudcrab Chitin.","g":["hunting","loot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-006","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Hunting","t":"New","x":"All three new hides cure to Cured Leather, and Wolf Pelts and Boar Hides make Large and Small Skins at the loom.","g":["hunting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-007","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Arcane Essence","t":"Fix","x":"If you take apart a piece you crafted with materials from your pack, its Arcane Essence no longer says \"bought with gold\". It now shows as \"made from pack goods\", and the Reforge with Essence can use it. Essence already in your Stores has been corrected.","g":["enchanting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-008","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Arcane Essence","t":"Fix","x":"The Stores page no longer says Arcane Essence can go to your pack.","g":["enchanting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-009","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Soul Trap","t":"Fix","x":"A Soul Gem holding the soul of one of the Enemy Expansion's creatures (an Ogre, a Goblin, a Troll and the rest) no longer freezes your trading. If trapping one froze yours, that hold and the strikes it added are lifted.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-010","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Player Trade","t":"Fix","x":"In a trade with another player, an item that cannot be traded now tells you so when you offer it. Before, it sat on your side of the table while the other player saw nothing, and a trade could finish without it ever reaching them.","g":["market","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-011","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"When a player dies in the Wrothgarian Mountains, all the gold they drop now shows in their remains. Before, a drop of more than 65,535 gold never appeared, and no one could pick it up.","g":["death-penalty","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-012","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Wrothgarian Zone","t":"Fix","x":"Taking only part of the gold from someone's remains, because your pack can't hold it all, now leaves the rest showing. Before, the pile could show less gold than was really there, or lose it from view.","g":["death-penalty","marks"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-013","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Tab Key","t":"Fix","x":"Pressing Tab no longer moves the keyboard onto the Social button or any other on-screen button.","g":["gamepad"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10454-014","v":"0.1.10454","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Social","t":"Fix","x":"Clicking Social, Chat, Show or \"Play online here\" no longer leaves that button selected, so your next jump no longer opens the friends panel again.","g":["social"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10461-001","v":"0.1.10461","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Overworld","t":"Performance","x":"When you come down from the Overworld, the grass around you no longer freezes the game while it grows back.","g":["overworld","grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10461-002","v":"0.1.10461","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Overworld","t":"Performance","x":"Crossing into a new region (desert, mountains, swamp, snow) no longer stalls the game while its ground is prepared.","g":["overworld","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10461-003","v":"0.1.10461","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Blood","t":"Performance","x":"The first time you take a hit, the blood on your screen no longer causes a freeze.","g":["blood"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10461-004","v":"0.1.10461","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Overworld","t":"Performance","x":"Long journeys hitch less often overall: the grass, the snow on the ground and the weather now create far less garbage, so the game stops much less often to clean it up.","g":["overworld","weather","grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10461-005","v":"0.1.10461","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Grass","t":"Fix","x":"At the edge of a snowline, grass is now buried by snow on the same slopes the snow is drawn on.","g":["grass","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10469-001","v":"0.1.10469","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Snow","t":"Fix","x":"Steep mountainsides keep their snow in winter. The straight green band up snowy ranges is gone: a steep face is now white like the rest of the slope. (Faces steeper than 50° still grow no trees, as in Daggerfall Unity.)","g":["seasons","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10469-002","v":"0.1.10469","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Snow","t":"Fix","x":"Turning \"Weather as places\" or \"Enhanced environments\" on or off mid-game now redraws the ground properly, instead of leaving squares wearing the other setting's season.","g":["seasons","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10469-003","v":"0.1.10469","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Revenant Missions","t":"Rework","x":"Online, a mission keeps real time: it keeps going while you're logged off. A day abroad is 2 real hours. Resting, waiting or traveling still doesn't speed it up.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10469-004","v":"0.1.10469","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Revenant Missions","t":"UI","x":"Online, a mission's time left is shown in real minutes and hours.","g":["revenants","online"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10469-005","v":"0.1.10469","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Hunting","t":"Rework","x":"Making Cured Leather from mixed hides now uses Wolf Pelts and Boar Hides before Bear Hides, so your Bear Hides stay for Ram Kits.","g":["hunting","crafting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10469-006","v":"0.1.10469","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Stores","t":"Fix","x":"The Stores say \"3 Mudcrab Chitin\", like \"3 Scorpion Chitin\".","g":["hunting"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-001","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Sailing","t":"Fix","x":"Sails work again after loading a save. A save made in a dungeon or building kept the indoors' calm, and a load that woke you outdoors (online, a dungeon save always wakes you at a temple or town) brought it out to sea: under sail your ship drifted while the oars still rowed. A load outdoors now has the outdoors' wind.","g":["naval","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-002","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"Fix","x":"\"Under Sail\" counts your voyage in any boat. A slow boat - a rowboat, or a Large Boat in a light wind - had its departure counted from the edge of the harbour instead of the quay, so short trips down the coast never counted. The voyage now counts from where you last lay still.","g":["naval","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-003","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"Fix","x":"Running aground in the next harbour, or leaving the helm as you come in, now counts as making port.","g":["naval","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-004","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"Fix","x":"A voyage survives a reload or a crash between the two ports.","g":["naval","saves"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-005","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"Fix","x":"Pencart's harbour can be reached (its water had all been counted as Longham's).","g":["naval","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-006","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Passage Under Sail","t":"Rework","x":"The harbourmaster now says what counts: the harbour of another port a quarter league off or more. \"The Packet Lanes\" says the same.","g":["naval","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-007","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Lantern","t":"Fix","x":"A lantern lit with O (or Use, or the hotbar) shows in the Lantern slot, where it hangs at your hip - not on the shield's panel.","g":["torch","equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-008","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Lantern","t":"Rework","x":"O lights the lantern in your Lantern slot first, a hung lantern lights with both hands full, and the hotbar's lantern no longer takes your shield off.","g":["torch","quickslot"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-009","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Snowfall","t":"Performance","x":"Fixed a memory leak in winter snow: every map area you travelled through stayed in memory, about 1.8 MB each - long journeys could run the game out of memory.","g":["weather","seasons"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-010","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Loading","t":"Fix","x":"Fixed a rare stall where the world stopped loading new ground for the rest of the session (offline play, about one area in 37).","g":["terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-011","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Desktop App","t":"New","x":"On the desktop app, a game that stops now says so and why, and offers Restart, instead of leaving a black window. A game that stops responding offers Wait or Restart. The reason is kept in crash.log beside your saves - please include it in a bug report.","g":["desktop-app"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10477-012","v":"0.1.10477","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Witches' Festival","t":"Rework","x":"Soul Cakes have a daily limit of 120, and the game now tells you when you reach it and the time more can be found (midnight UTC, shown in your own time). The Wyrd Sister's window shows how many you have found today.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10485-001","v":"0.1.10485","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Nerf","x":"Each wave at a fallen star is now larger, and it grows as the fight goes on. Alone you face 4, 5, 6 and then 7 foes. Every player beside you adds two more. A group of four faces 10 to 13 a wave, a group of eight 18 to 21, and the largest waves reach 24.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10485-002","v":"0.1.10485","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Nerf","x":"The coven's foes are tougher: its waves and the master's circle have twice their usual health. The master is unchanged.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10485-003","v":"0.1.10485","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Rework","x":"The coven's breath between waves is now 5 seconds, down from 12.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10485-004","v":"0.1.10485","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Rework","x":"Waves now gather just outside the crater instead of far beyond it, so they reach you sooner.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10485-005","v":"0.1.10485","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Rework","x":"In a group, a wave you clear quickly now ends when you clear it. Before, a large group could stand in an empty crater for up to a minute.","g":["events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10485-006","v":"0.1.10485","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Fix","x":"The mound of earth around a fallen star's crater is now solid. You can no longer walk through it. You also can't get stuck in it if the crater forms around you.","g":["events","terrain"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-001","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Barbarian: primaries Axe, Blunt Weapon and Critical Strike; majors Long Blade, Dodging and Running (were Jumping, Running and Swimming).","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-002","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Acrobat: gains Short Blade as a primary and Archery as a major.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-003","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Mage and Sorcerer are no longer identical. Both lead with Destruction, the Sorcerer adds Blunt Weapon, and neither spends skill slots on Dragonish or Daedric.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-004","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Healer: Blunt Weapon is now a major.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-005","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Archer: Critical Strike replaces Hand-to-Hand as a primary; Short Blade, Long Blade and Stealth are its majors.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-006","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Warrior, Barbarian: two weapons and Critical Strike as primaries, so every swing trains both the weapon in hand and Critical Strike.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-007","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"No class spends a skill slot on a language. Languages are still learnable.","g":["ascension"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10491-008","v":"0.1.10491","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Premade Classes","t":"Rework","x":"Burglar can now wear leather armour (it is forbidden chain and plate instead of leather and chain).","g":["equipment"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-001","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Enemy Sync","t":"Fix","x":"In busy areas, other players' enemies no longer die for one player and stay alive for another, or vanish when the player who controls them leaves, dies or goes through a door.","g":["online","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-002","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Starfall","t":"Fix","x":"At a crowded Starfall, every player's enemies now reach everyone in turn - including the player who controls the star's waves, whose enemies could go unseen by others before.","g":["online","events"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-003","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Enemy Sync","t":"Fix","x":"Enemies controlled by a slow or lagging player now move smoothly for everyone else instead of freezing and jumping.","g":["online","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-004","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Enemy Sync","t":"Fix","x":"On a slow computer with other players nearby, enemies keep pace with your character instead of moving at half speed - outdoors, in buildings and in dungeons, and the town watch with them.","g":["online","enhanced-ai"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-005","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Ships at Sea","t":"Performance","x":"Ships far out at sea, other players' boats and your own moored boats far away cost much less to draw.","g":["naval","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-006","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Horse","t":"Performance","x":"Horses - other players', strangers' on the road and those standing in towns - are only animated in full when you can see them, and a horse that comes into view is drawn in its current stride.","g":["horse","culling"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10530-007","v":"0.1.10530","d":"2026-10-21","e":"Grass","t":"Performance","x":"Grass no longer stutters while riding or running fast on a slower computer, and fills in around you even when you arrive at speed.","g":["grass"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10536-001","v":"0.1.10536","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Sea","t":"Fix","x":"The ocean no longer stays nearly black after sunrise and before sunset; it brightens along with the sky.","g":["water","sky"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10536-002","v":"0.1.10536","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Guilds","t":"Buff","x":"A guild can now hold 75 members (up from 50).","g":["guild"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10537-001","v":"0.1.10537","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Grass","t":"Rework","x":"Grass sways more gently in the wind. Blades lean less than half as far at a full gust, and gusts roll through the field more softly instead of whipping it.","g":["grass","weather"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10537-002","v":"0.1.10537","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Wisps","t":"Rework","x":"The wind wisps are more transparent and shorter. You can still see which way the wind blows, but they no longer stand out against the scenery.","g":["weather","rendering"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10543-001","v":"0.1.10543","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"Once anyone steps through an Abyss Dungeon's Rift, a portal - the Way Through - opens beside everyone in the dungeon, and beside everyone who enters it afterwards. Use it to go straight to the Shattered Hour.","g":["portals","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10543-002","v":"0.1.10543","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Abyss Dungeons","t":"New","x":"The Way Through closes when the Brass Remnant falls.","g":["portals","elites"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10547-001","v":"0.1.10547","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Online Sign-In","t":"Fix","x":"Signing in, and joining the world, failed for many players for an hour or two after midnight UTC every night. The game no longer has every player's client check in with the server in the same second when the day changes. Each client now waits a random 0–10 minutes past midnight.","g":["online","clock"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10547-002","v":"0.1.10547","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Gathering Nodes","t":"Other","x":"For those few minutes after midnight, the ground's gathering nodes, your profession's day and the town reports stay on the day before's until your client catches up. Nothing is lost.","g":["clock","foraging"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10555-001","v":"0.1.10555","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"A yellow \"!\" over anyone a quest needs, including the townsfolk who've been named as having work for you.","g":["morrowind","quests"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10555-002","v":"0.1.10555","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"An amber coin over merchants: shopkeepers, bankers and innkeepers.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10555-003","v":"0.1.10555","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"A blue gem over guild trainers, spell sellers and quest givers, the witches' coven, and the arena's officers.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null},{"id":"0.1.10555-004","v":"0.1.10555","d":"2026-10-22","e":"Morrowind People","t":"New","x":"Walls hide the markers, and they fade out beyond about 30 metres. Classic sprites don't get one, because their picture already tells you who they are. Turn them off with Morrowind People Marks on the Features page.","g":["morrowind"],"n":null}]);
